INSERT INTO `community_replies` (`id`, `user_id`, `question_id`, `parent_id`, `content`, `image`, `status`, `is_active`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4, 12, 3, NULL, 'Artificial intelligence isn\'t eliminating careers — it\'s redefining what skills matter most within them. Here\'s the real shift happening across industries: 1. Entry-level jobs are evolving, not vanishing  AI now handles repetitive tasks (basic coding, data entry, first drafts), which means freshers need to show judgment and problem-solving, not just execution, to stand out.\r\n\r\n 2. New AI-driven careers are emerging fast  Roles like prompt engineering, AI ethics, ML operations, and AI-assisted design barely existed five years ago — and they\'re growing faster than traditional tech roles.\r\n\r\n 3. \"AI-proof\" careers rely on human trust  Healthcare, skilled trades, teaching, and creative direction are growing because they need human judgment AI can\'t replicate — not despite AI.\r\n\r\n 4. AI literacy is now a core career skill  Across every industry, professionals who know how to use AI tools effectively are outperforming peers who ignore them — regardless of their actual subject expertise. Bottom line: The best career strategy isn\'t avoiding AI — it\'s learning to work alongside it. Choose a field where you can direct AI, not compete with it. What AI tools are you already using in your field of study? Drop them below 👇', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 02:58:48', '2026-06-22 03:06:04'),
(5, 12, 3, NULL, 'Honestly I feel like everyone\'s only talking about the good side of AI when it comes to jobs lol. Like yes new roles are coming up but let\'s be real, most of us aren\'t getting hired for \"AI ethics\" or \"prompt engineering\" roles straight out of college 😅 The bigger problem is entry level jobs are literally vanishing. Companies don\'t wanna hire freshers anymore because AI can do the \"basic\" stuff we used to learn on. So now there\'s this weird gap where you need experience to get experience. Also not everyone has equal access to learn this stuff fast. Some people have time, money, mentors, premium AI tools... others are just trying to pass their semester and don\'t even know where to start. So saying \"just learn AI skills\" sounds easy but isn\'t that simple for everyone. And it\'s not just tech jobs either, even content writing, design, customer support type roles are getting cut down or restructured because of AI. So saying \"AI won\'t replace you, it\'ll just change your role\" feels a bit too optimistic tbh. Not saying AI is bad, just feel like the struggle is way more real than these articles make it sound 🙃 anyone else feel like colleges aren\'t really preparing us for this fast enough?', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 03:04:43', '2026-06-22 03:05:02'),
(6, 11, 3, 5, 'This is the real engagement hook. A student who bookmarks 5 scholarships and returns for deadline reminders is a retained user. This feeds your notification system, re-engagement emails, and eventually shows you which scholarships your users care most about — valuable data for partnerships.', NULL, 'pending', 1, '2026-06-22 03:25:48', '2026-06-22 03:25:48'),
(7, 11, 3, 4, 'This is deliberate and important. Since your data comes from public scraping, you cannot own the application pipeline. Routing students to your counseling/guidance layer is both legally safer and commercially smarter — it becomes a monetizable touchpoint (paid counseling, premium tracking, assisted application service) rather than a dead redirect link.', NULL, 'pending', 1, '2026-06-22 03:26:28', '2026-06-22 03:26:28'),
(8, 12, 2, NULL, 'In my opinion, an MBA is worth it when it helps you achieve a specific career goal rather than just adding another degree to your resume. A good MBA can open doors to leadership roles, better salary packages, stronger professional networks, and career growth opportunities. However, the return on investment depends on factors such as the college, specialization, placements, and your own efforts. In today\'s competitive job market, combining an MBA with practical skills and industry exposure can create a significant advantage. Do you think employers value MBA graduates more than candidates with strong work experience?', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 03:47:03', '2026-06-22 03:47:46'),
(10, 12, 2, NULL, 'The value of an MBA has evolved over the years. Earlier, it was mainly seen as a pathway to management positions, but today it also helps professionals develop strategic thinking, problem-solving abilities, and business leadership skills. Whether it\'s Marketing, Finance, Human Resources, Business Analytics, or Operations, an MBA can provide the knowledge and network needed for long-term success. The real question is not whether an MBA is worth it, but whether the chosen program can deliver strong career outcomes and placement opportunities. What factors would you consider before investing in an MBA program?', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 03:50:16', '2026-06-22 03:50:47'),
(11, 12, 2, NULL, 'While an MBA can be valuable for some careers, I don\'t think it is worth it for everyone. Many students spend lakhs on MBA programs expecting high-paying jobs, but the reality is that placements and salary packages vary significantly across colleges. In today\'s job market, employers often prioritize practical skills, industry experience, certifications, and real-world problem-solving abilities over just having a management degree. Unless the MBA is from a reputed institution with strong industry connections and placement support, the return on investment may not justify the cost. Instead of automatically pursuing an MBA after graduation, students should carefully evaluate their career goals, financial investment, and available alternatives before making a decision.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 03:52:50', '2026-06-22 03:53:07'),
(12, 12, 4, NULL, 'I believe online learning is more effective than offline classes for today\'s generation because it offers flexibility, accessibility, and personalized learning opportunities. Students can learn from top educators, access recorded lectures multiple times, and study at their own pace without being restricted by location. Online learning also helps develop self-discipline, digital skills, and independent problem-solving abilities, which are highly valued in modern workplaces. With advancements in technology, interactive classes, virtual labs, and AI-powered learning tools are making online education more engaging and effective than ever before. In many cases, students can gain better learning outcomes while saving both time and money.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:03:10', '2026-06-22 04:03:38'),
(13, 12, 4, NULL, 'While online education has its advantages, I believe offline classes remain more effective for overall student development. Classroom learning provides direct interaction with teachers, instant doubt resolution, practical activities, and a structured environment that helps students stay focused. Offline education also encourages teamwork, communication skills, networking, and participation in extracurricular activities, all of which contribute to personal and professional growth. The campus experience, peer discussions, and face-to-face mentorship are difficult to replicate online. For students who learn best through engagement and discipline, traditional classroom education continues to be the stronger option.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:04:37', '2026-06-22 04:05:42'),
(14, 12, 4, NULL, 'In my opinion, both online learning and offline classes are effective in their own ways, and the better choice depends on the learner\'s goals and circumstances. Online education provides flexibility, affordability, and access to global learning resources, while offline education offers structured learning, direct faculty interaction, and valuable campus experiences. Instead of viewing them as competitors, they should be seen as complementary approaches to education. A hybrid learning model that combines the convenience of online learning with the engagement of offline classes can deliver the best learning outcomes, helping students gain knowledge, practical skills, and industry readiness simultaneously.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:05:14', '2026-06-22 04:05:35'),
(15, 12, 5, NULL, 'I believe studying abroad is worth the investment for students who are looking for global exposure, high-quality education, and international career opportunities. Beyond earning a degree, students gain access to diverse cultures, advanced research facilities, global networking opportunities, and industry-focused learning environments. Many international universities also offer strong placement support and pathways to work opportunities after graduation. While the cost can be significant, the long-term benefits in terms of career growth, earning potential, and personal development often make studying abroad a valuable investment for the future. The key is choosing the right country, university, and program that align with your career goals.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:20:53', '2026-06-22 04:24:14'),
(16, 12, 5, NULL, 'Studying abroad is not automatically worth the money for every student. Tuition fees, living expenses, accommodation costs, and education loans can create a significant financial burden. In many cases, students can receive quality education, industry-relevant skills, and strong placement opportunities within their home country at a much lower cost. The return on investment depends heavily on the university\'s reputation, the chosen course, job market conditions, and post-study work opportunities. Before making such a large financial commitment, students should carefully compare costs, career prospects, and potential salary outcomes rather than assuming that an international degree guarantees success.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:22:54', '2026-06-22 04:24:23'),
(17, 12, 5, NULL, 'Whether studying abroad is worth the money depends entirely on a student\'s goals, financial situation, and career aspirations. For some, it provides access to world-class education, international exposure, and global job opportunities that may not be easily available elsewhere. For others, the high cost may outweigh the benefits, especially if similar career outcomes can be achieved through local universities, online degrees, or professional certifications. Instead of focusing only on rankings or foreign locations, students should evaluate the return on investment, placement outcomes, scholarship opportunities, and long-term career benefits before making a decision. What matters most is not where you study, but how effectively you use the opportunities available to you.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:23:08', '2026-06-22 04:24:30'),
(18, 13, 5, 16, 'dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf', NULL, 'pending', 1, '2026-06-22 04:25:44', '2026-06-22 04:25:44'),
