(20, 13, 4, 12, 'dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnfdfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf', 'images/community/replies/1782122190_reply.png', 'pending', 1, '2026-06-22 04:26:30', '2026-06-22 04:26:30'),
(21, 13, 2, 11, 'dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf dfhbdfkbdjhfjsdhf ksdjbfjsdfjsdfj   jsdbfjsdjksdf sdjfkjdsfjkdsnf ksdjfnjdsnf', NULL, 'pending', 1, '2026-06-22 04:26:58', '2026-06-22 04:26:58'),
(22, 12, 6, NULL, 'I believe excessive reliance on AI tools for studying can make some students less independent thinkers. When students use AI to generate answers, solve problems, or complete assignments without understanding the underlying concepts, they may miss opportunities to develop critical thinking, creativity, and problem-solving skills. Education is not just about finding the correct answer; it is about learning how to analyze information, evaluate different perspectives, and arrive at conclusions independently. AI should be used as a learning assistant rather than a replacement for genuine effort and intellectual curiosity. If students become too dependent on technology, they may struggle in situations that require original thinking and decision-making.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:58:05', '2026-06-22 04:59:02'),
(23, 12, 6, NULL, 'I disagree with the idea that AI tools make students less independent thinkers. When used correctly, AI can actually encourage self-directed learning by providing instant explanations, personalized feedback, and access to educational resources. Students can explore complex topics, clarify doubts, and learn at their own pace without waiting for classroom assistance. Just as calculators did not eliminate mathematical thinking, AI is unlikely to replace critical thinking if students use it responsibly. Instead, AI can free students from routine tasks and allow them to focus on deeper understanding, creativity, and innovation. The real challenge is learning how to use AI effectively rather than avoiding it altogether.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:58:25', '2026-06-22 04:59:24'),
(24, 12, 6, NULL, 'AI tools are neither inherently good nor bad for independent thinking—the outcome depends on how students use them. If learners depend entirely on AI-generated answers, their analytical and problem-solving abilities may weaken over time. However, when AI is used to explain concepts, provide study guidance, and support research, it can become a powerful educational tool that enhances learning efficiency and understanding. The future of education will likely involve students working alongside AI rather than competing with it. The most successful learners will be those who use AI to expand their knowledge while continuing to question, analyze, and think critically on their own.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 04:58:43', '2026-06-22 04:59:33'),
(25, 12, 7, NULL, 'I believe choosing a high-paying career can be a smart decision, especially in today\'s competitive world where financial stability plays a major role in overall quality of life. A well-paying profession can help individuals achieve personal goals, support their families, reduce financial stress, and create opportunities for future investments. While passion is important, financial security often provides the freedom to explore interests and hobbies without constant economic pressure. The key is to find a career that offers strong earning potential while still aligning with your skills and strengths. After all, career growth, job security, and salary prospects are important factors when planning a successful future.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:08:17', '2026-06-22 05:11:17'),
(26, 12, 7, NULL, 'In my opinion, pursuing a career you are passionate about is more important than focusing solely on salary. When people genuinely enjoy their work, they tend to stay motivated, continuously improve their skills, and achieve long-term success. A high-paying job may provide financial rewards, but if it lacks personal satisfaction, it can lead to stress, burnout, and dissatisfaction over time. Passion often drives innovation, creativity, and commitment, which can eventually result in both career success and financial growth. Choosing a profession that excites and inspires you can make work feel meaningful rather than just a way to earn money.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:09:46', '2026-06-22 05:11:10'),
(27, 12, 7, NULL, 'I don\'t think this decision should be viewed as a choice between money and passion. The ideal career is one that combines both earning potential and personal interest. Instead of asking whether salary or passion is more important, students should look for opportunities where their skills, interests, and market demand intersect. Many successful professionals build rewarding careers by pursuing fields they enjoy while also developing expertise that employers value. A balanced approach can provide financial security, job satisfaction, and long-term career growth. The best career choice is often the one that allows you to wake up motivated while still meeting your financial goals.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:10:46', '2026-06-22 05:11:03'),
(28, 12, 8, NULL, 'In my opinion, every student should learn AI literacy, data analysis, digital communication, and prompt engineering to stay relevant in the future job market. As artificial intelligence continues to automate routine tasks, employers are increasingly looking for candidates who can work alongside AI tools rather than compete with them. Understanding how to use AI effectively, analyze information, and make data-driven decisions will become valuable skills across industries. Students who embrace technology and continuously update their skills will have a significant advantage in future careers.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:27:26', '2026-06-22 05:28:57'),
(29, 12, 8, NULL, 'While AI is transforming education and employment, I believe the most important skills for students are critical thinking, creativity, communication, emotional intelligence, and problem-solving. These are uniquely human abilities that AI cannot easily replicate. Technology can provide information and automate processes, but it still relies on people to ask the right questions, make ethical decisions, and develop innovative solutions. Students who strengthen these skills will remain valuable regardless of how advanced AI becomes', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:27:49', '2026-06-22 05:29:05'),
(30, 12, 8, NULL, 'The students who thrive in the AI era will be those who combine technical knowledge with strong human skills. Learning AI tools, digital technologies, coding basics, and data literacy is important, but so are leadership, adaptability, teamwork, and critical thinking. AI should be viewed as a powerful assistant rather than a replacement for learning. The future belongs to individuals who can leverage technology while continuing to think independently, solve complex problems, and communicate effectively. Which skill do you think will be most valuable in the next decade—AI expertise or human creativity?', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:28:08', '2026-06-22 05:29:12'),
(31, 12, 9, NULL, 'I believe social media is affecting student mental health more than many people realize. Constant exposure to highlight reels, academic achievements, lifestyle comparisons, and unrealistic expectations can increase stress, anxiety, and feelings of inadequacy among students. The pressure to gain likes, followers, and online validation often impacts self-esteem and confidence. While social media offers opportunities for learning and connection, excessive usage can distract students from studies, reduce productivity, and contribute to mental fatigue. Developing healthy digital habits is becoming just as important as academic success in today\'s connected world.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:46:37', '2026-06-22 05:47:51'),
(32, 12, 9, NULL, 'I don\'t think social media should be blamed entirely for student mental health challenges. When used responsibly, it can be a powerful platform for learning, networking, skill development, and staying connected with friends and communities. Students have access to educational content, career guidance, motivational stories, and mental health awareness resources that were not easily available before. The issue is often not social media itself but how it is used. Learning digital balance and responsible online behavior can help students benefit from social media while minimizing its negative effects.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:46:55', '2026-06-22 05:47:59'),
(33, 12, 9, NULL, 'Social media is a tool, and its impact on student mental health depends largely on usage patterns. On one hand, it can create opportunities for learning, collaboration, and community support. On the other hand, excessive screen time, comparison culture, cyberbullying, and information overload can negatively affect emotional well-being and academic performance. Rather than asking whether social media is good or bad, students should focus on using it mindfully and maintaining a healthy balance between online engagement and real-world experiences. The real challenge is learning how to control social media instead of allowing it to control us.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 05:47:17', '2026-06-22 05:48:07'),
(34, 12, 10, NULL, 'I strongly believe every student should complete at least one internship before graduating. While academic knowledge provides a strong foundation, internships help students apply classroom concepts in real-world situations. They offer practical experience, industry exposure, professional networking opportunities, and a better understanding of workplace expectations. Many graduates struggle to secure jobs because employers often seek candidates with hands-on experience. Making internships a mandatory part of higher education can improve employability, bridge the gap between theory and practice, and help students make more informed career decisions before entering the job market.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:15:39', '2026-06-22 06:16:45'),
(35, 12, 10, NULL, 'Although internships provide valuable learning experiences, I do not think they should be compulsory for every student. Different career paths require different forms of preparation. Some students may focus on research, entrepreneurship, competitive examinations, freelancing, or higher studies rather than traditional internships. Making internships mandatory could create unnecessary pressure and may result in students accepting low-quality opportunities simply to meet graduation requirements. Instead of imposing a single pathway, educational institutions should provide flexibility and allow students to choose experiences that align with their career goals and interests.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:16:02', '2026-06-22 06:16:52'),
(36, 12, 10, NULL, 'In my opinion, students should gain practical industry exposure before graduation, but this does not necessarily have to come through a traditional internship. Universities can offer multiple options such as internships, live projects, research programs, startup ventures, community initiatives, or industry-sponsored assignments. The primary objective should be to help students develop workplace skills, problem-solving abilities, communication skills, and professional confidence. A flexible approach would ensure that every student gains real-world experience while pursuing opportunities that best support their future career aspirations. What matters most is not the format of the experience, but the skills and insights gained', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:16:22', '2026-06-22 06:16:59'),
(37, 12, 11, NULL, 'I believe online degrees should be treated equally to traditional degrees by employers, especially when they are offered by accredited and recognized universities. The curriculum, faculty, examinations, and learning outcomes of many online degree programs are often comparable to those of on-campus courses. In today\'s digital economy, online learners demonstrate valuable qualities such as self-discipline, time management, adaptability, and technological proficiency. Employers should focus more on a candidate\'s skills, knowledge, projects, and professional capabilities rather than the mode of education. As remote work and digital learning continue to grow, online degrees are becoming a credible pathway to career advancement and professional success.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:21:47', '2026-06-22 06:23:28'),
(38, 12, 11, NULL, 'While online education has improved significantly, I believe traditional degrees still offer advantages that are difficult to replicate in a virtual environment. On-campus students benefit from face-to-face interactions, networking opportunities, laboratory experiences, extracurricular activities, and direct access to faculty mentors. These experiences often contribute to personal development, communication skills, and professional networking. Employers may view traditional degrees more favorably because they provide a broader educational experience beyond academics. Therefore, while online degrees deserve recognition, treating both formats as completely identical may overlook important differences in the learning journey.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:21:55', '2026-06-22 06:23:21'),
(39, 12, 11, NULL, 'In my opinion, employers should evaluate candidates based on their competencies, achievements, and practical skills rather than automatically favoring one mode of education over another. A high-quality online degree from a recognized university can provide the same academic knowledge as a traditional degree, while a motivated student can gain industry experience through internships, certifications, and projects. At the same time, traditional education offers unique networking and campus experiences that add value to a student\'s profile. The future of hiring should focus on what a candidate can contribute to an organization, not simply whether the degree was earned online or offline.', NULL, 'approved', 1, '2026-06-22 06:22:52', '2026-06-22 06:23:12');

