INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(86, 5, 'NATIONAL ELIGIBILITY-CUM-ENTRANCE TEST NEET (UG) – 2026', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"About exam \",\"name\":\"about_exam_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET (UG) 2026 is India&rsquo;s single national-level entrance examination for undergraduate medical and allied health science education. It acts as the unified selection system through which students gain admission into courses such as MBBS, BDS, and several AYUSH programs after completing their Class 12 education. The examination represents a standardized academic gateway that connects school-level biology and science education&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unlike earlier systems where multiple medical entrance exams existed across states and institutions, NEET (UG) has been designed to bring all admissions under one common evaluation process. The responsibility of conducting this examination lies with the National Testing Agency, which has been entrusted with this role since 2019. The NTA functions as an independent testing body under the Government of India and ensures that large-scale national examinations are conducted in a structured, transparent, and uniform manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The foundation of NEET is strongly rooted in national legislation and judicial direction. It is mandated under major regulatory frameworks such as the National Medical Commission Act, 2019, which makes NEET compulsory for admission into undergraduate medical education in India. Similar provisions extend to dental education and traditional medicine systems, ensuring that admissions across disciplines like Ayurveda, Unani, Siddha, and Homeopathy follow a single merit-based pathway. Over time, the validity and necessity of NEET as a unified entrance system have also been upheld through judicial interpretations, reinforcing its position as the core selection mechanism for medical education in India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scope of NEET (UG) is broad and inclusive, covering admissions to a wide range of undergraduate medical programs. These include MBBS for modern medicine, BDS for dental studies, and AYUSH courses such as BAMS, BUMS, BSMS, and BHMS. Additionally, performance in NEET is required for admission to premier national medical institutions such as the All India Institute of Medical Sciences and the Jawaharlal Institute of Postgraduate Medical Education and Research, which are among the most competitive and prestigious medical institutes in India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The core idea behind introducing a single examination system was to create uniformity in medical admissions across the country. Before NEET, students often had to appear for multiple entrance tests conducted by different states and institutions, leading to inconsistencies in evaluation standards. NEET resolved this by establishing a common merit-based ranking system, where every candidate is assessed through the same question paper, marking scheme, and evaluation process. This approach promotes fairness, reduces duplication of effort, and ensures that selection is based purely on academic performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In terms of operation, NEET (UG) follows a highly organized national testing framework. The entire examination cycle&mdash;from application to result declaration&mdash;is managed centrally by NTA. This includes releasing information bulletins, conducting the exam on a single day across thousands of centers, and publishing results based on standardized evaluation methods. The centralized system ensures transparency and minimizes regional disparities in the admission process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All official and authentic information regarding NEET (UG), including notifications, application procedures, admit cards, answer keys, results, and counselling-related updates, is made available exclusively on the official portal of NTA for NEET. Candidates are advised to rely only on this official source for accurate and updated information, as it serves as the primary communication channel between the examination authority and applicants.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overall, NEET (UG) functions as more than just an entrance test; it is a national academic framework that governs the transition of students from secondary education into professional medical training. By establishing a single, uniform, and merit-driven system, it plays a key role in shaping the future healthcare workforce of India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" NEET (UG)  and Role of NTA\",\"name\":\"_neet_ug_and_role_of_nta\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Authority, Scope of Responsibility &amp; Importance of Official Communication)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET (UG) 2026 examination is the single national-level entrance test for admission into multiple undergraduate medical and AYUSH courses across India. The responsibility for conducting this exam lies with a centralized authority, ensuring uniformity, transparency, and fairness in the admission process.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; This section explains the complete role of NTA, its responsibilities, and why candidates must rely strictly on official sources.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Conducting Authority of NEET (UG) 2026&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; The NEET (UG) 2026 examination is conducted by the<br>National Testing Agency.<\\/h4>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of NTA in NEET<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NTA is responsible for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducting the examination across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Managing application process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issuing admit cards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evaluating answer sheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Declaring results<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NTA&rsquo;s role is limited to conducting the examination and declaring results. It does not handle counselling or admission, which are managed by separate authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Courses Covered Under NEET (UG)&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET serves as the mandatory entrance exam for admission into the following undergraduate courses:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MBBS (Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BDS (Bachelor of Dental Surgery)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BAMS (Ayurveda)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BUMS (Unani)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BSMS (Siddha)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BHMS (Homoeopathy)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Governing Regulatory Bodies<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admissions to these courses are regulated under guidelines issued by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Medical Commission &ndash; for MBBS\\/BDS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Indian System of Medicine &ndash; for BAMS, BUMS, BSMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Homoeopathy &ndash; for BHM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each course follows its own:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">But all require NEET qualification as the entry point<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Official Website &ndash; The Only Trusted Source<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Official NEET Website<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\">https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Website Is Critical<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All official information related to NEET is published only on this platform by the<br>National Testing Agency.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Type of Information Available<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card release<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam schedule<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Answer key notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result announcements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Important instruction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Continuous Updates &amp; Candidate Responsibility<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Information may be updated or modified over tim<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Candidates Must Do<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the official website regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay updated with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li