ate quota<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Respective State AYUSH Portals<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Conducting Authority<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">National Testing Agency<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Conducts NEET (UG) examination, releases application forms, admit cards, results, and official notifications<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\">https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in<\\/a> \\/<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.nta.ac.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/www.nta.ac.in<\\/a><\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Higher Education Ministry<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ministry of Education (MoE), Department of Higher Education<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Provides administrative oversight and policy coordination for national-level entrance examinations&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.education.gov.in\\/\\\">https:\\/\\/www.education.gov.in<\\/a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\\/h4>\\r\\n<h4>&nbsp;<\\/h4>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"Important Instructions \",\"name\":\"important_instructions_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before starting the application process, candidates should first ensure they have a clear understanding of all requirements, procedures, and eligibility conditions associated with the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This initial preparation plays a crucial role in preventing errors during form submission. It helps candidates become familiar with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria and qualification requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Necessary documents and their correct format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Step-by-step application procedures<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Important rules and instructions related to the examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Lack of proper understanding at this stage can lead to serious issues such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting an incorrect qualification or eligibility code<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Providing incomplete or inaccurate information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Facing rejection or disqualification during verification or later stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, candidates are strongly advised to treat this preparatory step as a critical foundation and ensure they are fully informed before proceeding with the application process.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The official Information Bulletin<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The sample (replica) application form<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This step is essential because it provides clarity on eligibility conditions, required documents, application procedures, and rules governing the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to understand these details often results in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incorrect eligibility code selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submission of incomplete or invalid information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification at later stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should treat this document as the primary reference for all decisions related to the application<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Exclusive Online Application Process<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application process for NEET (UG) 2026 is entirely online. This includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Filling of application form<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading of documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment of application fee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Generation of confirmation page&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Applications submitted through any other mode&mdash;such as post, email, fax, or hand delivery&mdash;will not be accepted under any circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are advised to use only the official NEET website to complete the application to ensure authenticity and avoid errors.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Accurate and Careful Completion of Application Form<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application form requires candidates to provide detailed personal, academic, and contact information. All entries must be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Consistent with official documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carefully verified before submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once the application is submitted and the fee is paid:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Most fields become non-editable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only limited corrections may be allowed during a predefined correction window<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Errors such as incorrect name spelling, wrong date of birth, or inaccurate category selection can lead to complications during counselling or even cancellation of candidature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Identity Verification and Use of Aadhaar<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are required to provide valid identity proof. While multiple options are available, the use of an Aadhaar Card is strongly recommended.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Using Aadhaar helps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Simplify the verification process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduce the need for additional documentation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimize the chances of identity-related discrepancies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates using alternative identity proofs may be required to submit additional supporting documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Importance of Valid Mobile Number and Email ID<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must provide a valid and active:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These should belong to the candidate or their parent\\/guardian.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All communication from the examination authority&mdash;including OTP verification, application updates, admit card notifications, and result announcements&mdash;will be sent through these channels.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Providing incorrect or inaccessible contact details may result in missed communications, for which the authorities will not be responsible.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. OTP-Based Authentication Process<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application process includes mandatory OTP verification:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile OTP during registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email OTP before final submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This mechanism ensures the authenticity of the application and prevents unauthorized submissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to complete OTP verification will result in an incomplete application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Final Submission and Data Lock<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After successful submission of the application form and payment of the fee:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The application is considered final<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Most of the entered information becomes non-editable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only specific fields may be modified during a limited correction window, if provided.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must therefore ensure complete accuracy before final submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7. Fee Payment and Completion of Application<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application fee must be paid through online modes such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Net Banking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Credit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">UPI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional charges such as processing fees and taxes may apply.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application is considered successfully submitted only when:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment is completed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirmation page is generated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If payment fails, the application remains incomplete.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">8. Confirmation Page and Document Retention<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After successful submission, a confirmation page is generated. This document serves as proof of application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download the confirmation page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Print multiple copies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preserve it for future reference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Similarly, copies of the admit card and scorecard should also be retained, as they may be available for download only for a limited period.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">9. Selection of Correct Qualification Code<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must select the appropriate qualification code based on their academic status:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Code 01: Candidates appearing in Class 12 in 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Codes 02&ndash;07: Candidates who have already passed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Incorrect selection may result in eligibility issues during verification stages. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 10. Restriction on Multiple Applications &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Candidates are strictly prohibited from submitting more than one application form.If multiple applications are detected:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidature will be cancelled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The case may be treated under unfair means practices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional penalties may be imposed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must ensure that only one valid application is submitted.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">11. Address Details and Exam City Allocation<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must provide complete and accurate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Permanent address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correspondence address with PIN code<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The choice of examination city is influenced by these details. Incorrect information may lead to inconvenience in centre allocation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">12. Photograph and Document Consistency<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should maintain uniformity in photographs by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using recent passport-size photographs with a white background<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keeping multiple copies of the same photograph<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The same photograph should be used across all stages, including application, examination, and counselling, to avoid identity verification issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">13. Examination Day Rules and Security Protocols<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must strictly adhere to examination guidelines.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Prohibited items include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile phones and electronic devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bags, books, and written materials<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any unauthorized items<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Security procedures may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Metal detector checks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric and facial verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to comply may result in denial of entry or disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">14. Admission is Not Guaranteed by Qualification Alone<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Qualifying NEET (UG) 2026 does not automatically ensure admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission depends on multiple factors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank obtained<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat availability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical fitness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must fulfill all conditions prescribed by relevant authorities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">15. Consequences of Providing False Information<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any incorrect, misleading, or fabricated information in the application form may lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of result<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification at any stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Legal action<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are fully responsible for the accuracy and authenticity of the information provided.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">16. Continuous Monitoring of Updates<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must regularly check:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official website<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registered email<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important updates related to the examination, admit card, results, and counselling may be communicated at any stage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">17. Unfair Means and Strict Penalties<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Engaging in activities such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Impersonation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submission of fake documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multiple applications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">May result in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debarment from future examinations (up to three years)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Legal or criminal proceedings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">18. Document Storage and DigiLocker Access<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may be provided access to documents through DigiLocker, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirmation page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scorecard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since these documents may be available only for a limited period, candidates must download and securely store them.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Advisory<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET (UG) 2026 application process demands careful attention and strict compliance with official instructions. Candidates should approach the process with seriousness and responsibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify all details before submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid last-minute errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep all documents ready in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow official guidelines at every step<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A well-filled application ensures a smooth examination and admission journey, while negligence at this stage can have long-term&nbsp;consequences.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><strong id=\\\"docs-internal-guid-2da49752-7fff-747d-fb93-5a81a343bd78\\\"><\\/strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 0, 1, '2026-04-14 00:14:47', '2026-04-14 00:56:34');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(280, 5, 'Instructions for submission of Application Form/ Payment of FEE ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"  Detailed Readiness Guidelines \",\"name\":\"_detailed_readiness_guidelines_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1.&nbsp; Detailed Readiness Guidelines&nbsp;<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before initiating the NEET (UG) 2026 application process, candidates must ensure that they are fully prepared with all required information, documents, and identity details. Proper preparation at this stage is not just a matter of convenience&mdash;it is a critical step that directly impacts the accuracy of the application and reduces the risk of errors that may lead to rejection or complications during verification and admission stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the Application Process and Access<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application for NEET (UG) 2026 is conducted entirely through an online system, which requires candidates to access the official examination portal and complete all steps digitally. This includes registration, form filling, document submission, and fee payment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It is important for candidates to approach this process with clarity and readiness, as the system does not allow unlimited revisions. Once key steps such as submission and payment are completed, most of the entered details become final. Therefore, entering the application portal without preparation can increase the likelihood of mistakes, incomplete entries, or incorrect submissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Comprehensive Preparation Before Filling the Application Form<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before starting the application form, candidates must organize and verify all required information in advance. This preparation ensures a smooth and error-free form-filling experience.&nbsp; Candidates should keep the following details readily available and carefully verified:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal details, including the candidate&rsquo;s name and parents&rsquo; names, must be written exactly as they appear in official records. Even minor spelling differences can create issues during identity verification or counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date of birth should match the official certificate, as this is a key eligibility parameter and cannot be altered later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic records such as Class X and Class XII mark sheets or certificates must be accurate, as they are used to validate eligibility conditions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid identity proof details must be correctly entered, as these are used for authentication throughout the examination process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Address details should be complete and accurate, including permanent and correspondence addresses, as these may influence communication and examination centre allocation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A functional mobile number and email address must be provided, ensuring that the candidate can receive important updates, verification codes, and official communication without interruption.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preparing all of this information in advance helps candidates avoid last-minute confusion, reduces errors, and ensures that the application is completed in a structured and confident manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Importance of Verifying Information Before Entry<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are strongly advised to mentally simulate or review the application structure before entering details into the system. Understanding the type of information required and its format helps in minimizing mistakes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This preparation is particularly important because incorrect or inconsistent entries can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of the application at any stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mismatch during document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delays or issues during counselling and admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since only limited corrections may be allowed later, and not all fields can be edited, this initial verification step becomes crucial in ensuring a successful application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Identity Details Requirement and Selection<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Providing correct identity information is a mandatory part of the application process. Candidates must select and enter valid identity details based on their category.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates who are Indian nationals, acceptable identity options include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aadhaar Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Indian Passport<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PAN Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">DigiLocker credentials<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any other valid government-issued photo identity card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates belonging to other categories:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Non-Resident Indians (NRIs) are required to provide their passport details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Foreign nationals and Overseas Citizens of India (OCI) must also use passport details for identification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The selection of identity proof must be done carefully, ensuring that the document is valid, current, and matches the candidate&rsquo;s personal details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advantage of Using Aadhaar for Verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although multiple identity options are available, using an Aadhaar Card is generally the most efficient choice for candidates who possess it.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choosing Aadhaar simplifies the verification process because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It is widely accepted and easily verifiable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It reduces the need for additional supporting documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It minimizes the chances of discrepancies during identity validation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who opt for other identity documents may be required to submit additional proofs or undergo further verification steps, which can increase the complexity of the application process and the risk of delays or errors.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Preparation Mindset Before Application<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The readiness stage should be approached with a mindset of precision and responsibility. Candidates must understand that the application form is not merely a procedural requirement but a critical document that reflects their identity, eligibility, and intent to appear for the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Being fully prepared before starting the application ensures:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Faster and smoother form completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduced chances of technical or data entry errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Higher confidence in the accuracy of submitted information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A well-prepared application not only prevents rejection but also ensures a seamless experience in later stages such as admit card issuance, examination, and counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Concluding Guidance<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should never rush into filling the application form without preparation. Taking the time to gather, verify, and understand all required details beforehand significantly reduces risks and enhances the overall quality of the application.&nbsp; A careful and well-prepared approach at this stage lays a strong foundation for the entire NEET (UG) 2026 journey, ensuring that candidates can proceed with confidence and without avoidable complications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"  Application Procedure \",\"name\":\"_application_procedure_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Filling the NEET (UG) 2026 application form is a high-responsibility process where accuracy, timing, and understanding of rules play a decisive role. This is not merely a technical submission&mdash;it is the foundation of your eligibility, identity verification, and participation in the entire admission cycle. Any lapse at this stage can create consequences that may not be correctable later, even after qualifying the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This guide explains not only the steps but also the underlying logic, hidden risks, and strategic precautions required to complete the application flawlessly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Foundational Approach Before Starting the Application<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must approach the application process with the understanding that the system is designed to capture final, verifiable data, not provisional or approximate information. While the interface may allow edits within sections, the moment the form is finally submitted and payment is completed, most of the data becomes locked.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A common mistake candidates make is treating the application as a &ldquo;draft stage&rdquo; where corrections can be done later. In reality, the correction window&mdash;if provided&mdash;allows only limited changes and does not cover critical identity or eligibility fields. Therefore, the correct approach is to treat every entry as final at the time of input itself.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Another critical aspect is decision-making during the form, particularly in areas such as question paper medium, category selection, and exam city preference. These are not cosmetic choices&mdash;they directly influence exam experience, eligibility benefits, and logistical convenience.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Registration and Secure Account Creation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The first stage involves registering on the official portal, where the candidate creates a digital identity within the system.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">During this process, candidates provide basic details and generate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A unique application number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A secure password<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A security question and answer&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance of Application Number<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application number is not just a login credential; it becomes the candidate&rsquo;s primary identifier throughout the entire lifecycle of the examination&mdash;from admit card download to counselling and admission. Losing or mishandling this number can delay or complicate access to critical services.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should store this information in multiple secure formats, ensuring it is always accessible when needed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Password Creation &ndash; More Than a Formal Requirement<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The password requirements are designed to enforce security, but candidates often treat them casually. Weak password practices or sharing credentials with others (such as coaching institutes or cyber caf&eacute; operators) introduces serious risks, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Unauthorized modification of application details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accidental or intentional submission errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of control over the application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It is essential to maintain exclusive control over login credentials and log out after every session, especially when using shared devices.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Password Recovery &ndash; Understanding Backup Access<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The system provides multiple recovery mechanisms, including security questions, OTP-based verification, and email reset links. However, these mechanisms depend entirely on the accuracy of previously entered data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate enters incorrect email or mobile details during registration, even password recovery may become difficult. This highlights the importance of accuracy at the very first stage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Detailed Application Form Completion<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is the most extensive and critical stage, where the candidate provides complete personal, academic, and eligibility-related information.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Personal and Academic Information &ndash; Identity Consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All personal details must exactly match official records. Even minor inconsistencies&mdash;such as variation in spelling or format&mdash;can create complications during document verification or counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Academic details, particularly for Class 10 and Class 12, must be entered accurately, as they serve as the basis for eligibility validation. Candidates must also carefully select the correct qualifying code, which reflects their current academic status.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A frequent mistake is incorrect code selection, especially by candidates appearing in Class 12. This can create confusion during eligibility verification and may require additional clarification later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category Selection &ndash; High-Impact Decision<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Selecting the correct category is one of the most sensitive parts of the application. This is not merely informational&mdash;it directly affects reservation benefits, cutoff eligibility, and seat allocation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must ensure that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They genuinely belong to the selected category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their category is recognized under the applicable lists<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They possess valid supporting documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A common and serious error is selecting a reserved category without verifying eligibility under the correct list (especially in the case of OBC-NCL). If the category is found invalid during counselling, the candidate may lose reservation benefits or face disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Examination City Preference &ndash; Strategic Choice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">While selecting examination cities, candidates often choose randomly or based on assumptions. However, this decision should be made strategically, considering:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel convenience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accessibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Familiarity with the location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since the allocation is automated and final, poor choices can result in logistical challenges on the exam day.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Question Paper Medium &ndash; Irreversible Decision<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The selection of the question paper medium must be made with careful consideration. Candidates should choose a language in which they are fully comfortable understanding scientific terminology.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although bilingual papers are provided for certain languages, the English version is treated as the final reference in case of ambiguity. Therefore, candidates relying solely on translation without strong English comprehension may face difficulties. &nbsp; This decision cannot be changed later, making it one of the most critical choices in the application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Document Upload &ndash; Most Error-Prone Stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This stage is where a large number of applications face rejection due to non-compliance with specifications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Photograph &ndash; Identity Representation<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The photograph must clearly represent the candidate&rsquo;s identity. Common mistakes include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using edited or filtered images<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading unclear or low-resolution photos<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using outdated or mismatched photographs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any mismatch between the uploaded photograph and the candidate&rsquo;s appearance during the exam or verification stages can create serious issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Signature and Biometric Impressions &ndash; Verification Tools<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The signature and finger\\/thumb impressions are used for authentication. Poor quality or unclear uploads may result in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Difficulty in verification at exam centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must ensure proper scanning and clarity.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Documents &ndash; Accuracy and Relevance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must upload all required documents in the correct format and size. Uploading incorrect, incomplete, or irrelevant documents can delay verification or lead to rejection.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates using identity methods other than Aadhaar, additional documentation may be required to establish authenticity.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Live Photograph Capture &ndash; Real-Time Verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The live photograph feature is a critical security measure. It ensures that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The person filling the form matches the identity records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fake or proxy applications are prevented<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If the captured image does not match identity records, candidates may be required to submit certified verification documents. Failure to do so correctly can delay or jeopardize the application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3: Fee Payment and Final Submission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The final stage completes the application process and confirms candidature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Payment Verification &ndash; Understanding the System<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A common misconception is that deduction of money from the bank account confirms submission. In reality, the application is considered successful only when:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment status is confirmed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirmation page is generated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If the confirmation page is not generated, the application is incomplete, regardless of whether the amount has been deducted.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Handling Failed or Duplicate Transactions<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must carefully monitor payment status. In case of failure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A new payment must be initiated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The previous amount (if deducted) is usually refunded later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Multiple payments may occur due to confusion, but these are generally reconciled and refunded after the process is completed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Submission &ndash; Point of No Return<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once payment is successful and the confirmation page is generated:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The application is officially submitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Most details become non-editable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must download and securely store the confirmation page, as it serves as official proof of submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Mistakes That Can Lead to Rejection<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entering incorrect personal or academic details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting wrong category or qualification code<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading unclear or incorrect documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using someone else&rsquo;s photograph or details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Failing to complete payment successfully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submitting multiple application forms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These errors are often irreversible and can lead to rejection at any stage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" CHECK LIST FOR FILLING THE ONLINE APPLICATION FORM\",\"name\":\"_check_list_for_filling_the_online_application_form\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before submitting the NEET (UG) 2026 application form, candidates must conduct a thorough and structured verification of all entered details and uploaded documents. This stage acts as the final quality check, ensuring that the application is not only complete but also accurate, compliant, and free from errors that could lead to rejection, disqualification, or complications during counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unlike earlier stages where minor corrections may still be possible, this checklist phase must be treated as a final validation step, where every critical detail is reviewed with precision and responsibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verification of Eligibility Conditions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The first and most fundamental requirement is confirming that the candidate fully satisfies all eligibility criteria applicable to the examination. This includes academic qualifications, subject requirements, and other prescribed conditions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This step is crucial because eligibility is not just checked at the time of application&mdash;it is verified again during counselling and admission. Candidates who apply without meeting the required criteria may be allowed to appear in the examination provisionally, but their candidature can be cancelled at a later stage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A common high-impact mistake is assuming eligibility without careful verification, especially in cases involving qualifying examination status or subject combinations. Therefore, candidates must ensure complete clarity before proceeding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Accuracy in Personal Identity Details<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must ensure that essential personal details such as gender are selected correctly. While this may appear to be a simple field, incorrect selection can create inconsistencies with official records and may lead to complications during identity verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application system relies heavily on consistency across documents, biometric data, and submitted information. Even seemingly minor discrepancies can raise flags during verification processes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Correct Selection of Category and Reservation Status<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category selection is one of the most sensitive and high-impact fields in the application form. Candidates must ensure that they have selected the correct category&mdash;General, General-EWS, OBC-NCL, SC, or ST&mdash;based strictly on their eligibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This decision directly affects:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation benefits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cut-off eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allocation during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A critical mistake observed among candidates is selecting a reserved category without verifying whether they meet the exact criteria under the applicable category lists. If the category claim is found invalid during document verification, the candidate may lose reservation benefits or face disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, candidates must ensure that their category selection is accurate and supported by valid documentation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disability) Declaration<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who belong to the PwBD category must ensure that they have correctly filled the relevant section in the application form. Only those candidates who meet the defined benchmark disability criteria should select this option.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who do not fall under this category must leave this field blank. Incorrectly marking this option can lead to unnecessary scrutiny, document verification issues, and possible rejection of the claim during counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Confirmation Page and Record Maintenance<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After successful submission, candidates must ensure that they have downloaded and securely stored the confirmation page of the application form. This document serves as official proof of submission and may be required during future stages such as counselling and admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to retain this document can create unnecessary complications, especially if verification or reference is required later. Candidates should maintain multiple copies, both digital and printed, for safety.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Requirements for PwD\\/PwBD Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates belonging to the PwD\\/PwBD category must ensure that their disability-related documentation is accurate, valid, and verifiable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The details provided in the application may be cross-verified with official databases. In cases where a unique disability identification document is not available, candidates must upload the appropriate certificate in the prescribed format. This certificate may be verified with the issuing authority, making accuracy and authenticity essential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates who intend to use the assistance of a scribe, providing identification details of the scribe during the application stage can help avoid additional documentation requirements later. This proactive step simplifies the verification process during the examination and counselling stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Authenticity of Uploaded Photographs and Documents<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must ensure that all uploaded materials&mdash;including photographs, signatures, biometric impressions, and certificates&mdash;are their own, recent, and authentic.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is a critical compliance requirement because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The system uses these materials for identity verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any mismatch or inconsistency may be treated as suspicious<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Uploading someone else&rsquo;s photograph or using altered or fabricated documents is considered a serious violation. Such actions can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediate rejection of the application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Classification under unfair means practices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Possible legal consequences<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the most serious risks in the application process and must be strictly avoided.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Pre-Application Document Readiness and Updates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are strongly advised to ensure that all key documents are updated and accurate before applying. This proactive preparation helps prevent discrepancies, delays, or rejection at later stages.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Aadhaar and Identity Information Accuracy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should verify that their identity details are fully updated and consistent across records. This includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date of birth<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gender<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any mismatch between identity records and application details can create verification issues. Candidates should complete necessary updates well in advance to avoid last-minute complications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Disability Documentation (if applicable)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates belonging to the PwD\\/PwBD category must ensure that their disability identification documents are valid, updated, and compliant with requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In particular, permanent disability identification may be required during counselling for physical verification. Failure to produce valid documentation at that stage may result in rejection of the claim.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category Certificate Validity<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates applying under reserved categories must ensure that their category certificates are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Updated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issued in the correct format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Certificates that are outdated, invalid, or incorrectly issued may not be accepted during counselling, leading to loss of reservation benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Verification and Authority Oversight<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All information submitted by candidates, including personal details and uploaded documents, may be subject to verification by the examination authority.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must understand that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submitted data is not merely recorded&mdash;it is verified<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any inconsistency may lead to further scrutiny<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final acceptance depends on successful verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This reinforces the importance of accuracy, honesty, and consistency in every part of the application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Responsible Use of Submitted Data<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The information provided during the application process may be used for legitimate administrative purposes such as analysis, research, and system improvement. Candidates should be aware that their data becomes part of an official system and must therefore be submitted responsibly and accurately.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 1, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 02:14:11');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(281, 5, ' Examination Scheme     ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"Syllabus of the test \",\"name\":\"syllabus_of_the_test_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The syllabus for NEET (UG) 2026 defines the complete academic scope of the examination and acts as the foundation for preparation. It is carefully structured to assess a candidate&rsquo;s understanding of core scientific concepts, their ability to apply knowledge, and their problem-solving skills across Physics, Chemistry, and Biology.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, simply knowing the syllabus is not enough. What truly differentiates high-performing candidates is their ability to interpret the syllabus strategically, identify high-impact areas, and prepare with clarity, depth, and consistency.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This guide not only explains the syllabus but also provides a subject-wise breakdown, important topics, preparation strategy, and critical mistakes to avoid, making it a complete preparation framework.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the Nature of the Syllabus<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET syllabus is aligned with senior secondary education (Class 11 and Class 12), but the level of questions is designed to test more than basic knowledge. The exam focuses on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conceptual clarity rather than rote learning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application of theory in unfamiliar situations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interlinking of topics across chapters<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Speed and accuracy under time pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A major mistake candidates make is treating the syllabus as a checklist. In reality, it should be treated as a conceptual map, where each topic is connected and builds toward deeper understanding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Subject-Wise Syllabus with Important Topics and Strategic Focus<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To make preparation practical and focused, the syllabus must be understood subject-wise along with high-yield topics and their importance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Biology &ndash; Core Scoring Subject<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Biology carries the highest weightage in NEET, making it the most scoring subject. However, scoring well requires more than memorization&mdash;it demands clarity of concepts and precise understanding of NCERT-based content.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Topics in Biology<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Human Physiology<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the most important and consistently asked areas:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Digestion and absorption<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Respiratory system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Circulatory system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Excretory system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Nervous system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Endocrine system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<br>Questions are often conceptual and process-based. Understanding mechanisms is more important than memorizing facts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Genetics and Molecular Biology<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A concept-heavy but high-scoring unit:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mendelian genetics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">DNA structure and replication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Transcription and translation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Genetic disorders<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evolution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk:<br>Superficial learning leads to confusion in application-based questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ecology and Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A relatively easier and scoring section:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ecosystems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biodiversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Environmental issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Advantage:<br>This section can be mastered quickly and used to improve overall score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Plant Physiology<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photosynthesis<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Respiration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Plant growth and hormones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistake:<br>Ignoring cycles and diagrams, which are frequently tested.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reproduction<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sexual reproduction in plants<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Human reproduction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reproductive health<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Important:<br>Frequently asked with both direct and conceptual questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry &ndash; Balanced and Scoring with Right Strategy<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry requires a balanced approach involving conceptual understanding, numerical practice, and memorization. It is divided into three parts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physical Chemistry &ndash; Concept + Numerical Application<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Topics:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mole concept<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Thermodynamics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Equilibrium<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electrochemistry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chemical kinetics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<br>Regular practice is essential. Weak concepts lead to errors under time pressure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Organic Chemistry &ndash; Logic and Reaction Mechanisms<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Topics:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General organic chemistry (GOC)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hydrocarbons<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Alcohols, phenols, ethers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aldehydes and ketones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carboxylic acids<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biomolecules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk:<br>Memorizing reactions without understanding mechanisms leads to mistakes in indirect questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Inorganic Chemistry &ndash; Memory with Conceptual Base<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Topics:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chemical bonding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Periodic table<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Coordination compounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">p-block elements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">d and f block elements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistake:<br>Ignoring NCERT facts and exceptions, which are frequently tested.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physics &ndash; Conceptual and Analytical Section<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physics is often the most challenging subject due to its numerical and conceptual depth. Success depends on strong fundamentals and consistent problem-solving practice.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Weightage Topics in Physics<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mechanics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Laws of motion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work, energy, and power<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rotational motion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gravitation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Critical:<br>Forms the foundation for many other topics.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Thermodynamics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Laws of thermodynamics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Heat and energy transfer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Insight:<br>Concept clarity is more important than formula memorization.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Electrodynamics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electrostatics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Current electricity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Magnetism<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electromagnetic induction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistake:<br>Avoiding this section due to difficulty, despite high scoring potential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Optics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ray optics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wave optics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Importance:<br>Conceptual + formula-based questions are common.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Modern Physics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photoelectric effect<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Atoms and nuclei<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Semiconductors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Advantage:<br>Easier to master and highly scoring.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Use the Syllabus Strategically<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The syllabus should guide your preparation, not overwhelm it. A smart strategy includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prioritizing high-weightage topics first<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strengthening concept-heavy areas early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Practicing application-based questions regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintaining continuous revision cycles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Top-performing candidates do not study everything equally&mdash;they focus on impact and efficiency.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common High-Impact Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Treating the syllabus as a checklist instead of a concept map<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring difficult topics instead of improving them<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Over-relying on memorization without understanding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Neglecting revision<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Skipping practice of application-based questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes significantly reduce performance despite hard work.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"  Exam Pattern  \",\"name\":\"_exam_pattern_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the NEET (UG) 2026 exam pattern is essential for building an effective preparation and test-taking strategy. The pattern defines not only the structure of the question paper but also how candidates should manage time, prioritize subjects, and attempt questions during the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The test is designed to evaluate a candidate&rsquo;s conceptual understanding, accuracy, and speed under a fixed time constraint. Therefore, a clear understanding of the pattern can significantly influence overall performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overall Structure of the Examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET (UG) 2026 examination consists of three core subjects:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Physics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chemistry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biology (Botany and Zoology combined)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The paper contains a total of 180 compulsory questions, all of which must be attempted within a duration of 180 minutes (3 hours). This creates a direct time-pressure scenario where, on average, candidates get 1 minute per question, making speed and accuracy equally important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Subject-Wise Distribution of Questions and Marks<\\/h3>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"179\\\"><col width=\\\"240\\\"><col width=\\\"145\\\"><col width=\\\"59\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Subject<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Type of Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Number of Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCQs (4 options, single correct answer)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">45<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">180<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCQs (4 options, single correct answer)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">45<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">180<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Biology (Botany &amp; Zoology)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCQs (4 options, single correct answer)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">90<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">360<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&mdash;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">180<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">720<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Nature of Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All questions in NEET are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each question has four options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only one correct or best answer must be selected<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This format emphasizes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conceptual clarity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Elimination skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Precision in selecting the correct option<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time Duration and Exam Schedule<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Total Duration: 180 minutes (3 hours)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam Timing: 2:00 PM to 5:00 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must complete the entire paper within this fixed duration, with no sectional time limits. This means candidates have full flexibility in choosing the order of attempting subjects.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Marking Scheme (Critical for Strategy)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although not explicitly shown in the table, the standard marking scheme followed is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">+4 marks for each correct answer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">-1 mark for each incorrect answer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">0 marks for unattempted questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strategic Implication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Negative marking makes blind guessing risky. Candidates must balance:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accuracy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempt rate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Risk-taking ability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Subject-Wise Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Biology &ndash; Highest Weightage (50% of Paper)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">With 90 questions and 360 marks, Biology dominates the paper. A strong performance in this section can significantly boost overall score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Insight:<br>Candidates should aim for high accuracy in Biology, as it is relatively more scoring compared to Physics.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry &ndash; Moderate Difficulty, High Scoring Potential<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry often acts as a scoring bridge between Biology and Physics.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Insight:<br>A well-prepared candidate can maximize marks here with balanced preparation across Physical, Organic, and Inorganic Chemistry.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physics &ndash; Most Challenging Section<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Physics is generally considered the most time-consuming and conceptually demanding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategy Insight:<br>Efficient time allocation and strong problem-solving skills are crucial to avoid losing marks due to time pressure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time Management Strategy Based on Pattern<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Given the structure of the paper, candidates must develop a personalized attempt strategy. A commonly effective approach includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Starting with Biology to secure quick and accurate marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Moving to Chemistry for moderate difficulty questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting Physics with remaining time and focused attention<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, this strategy may vary depending on individual strengths.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Make<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Spending too much time on difficult Physics questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting guesses without elimination (leading to negative marking)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring time tracking during the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not practicing full-length mock tests based on actual pattern<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes often reduce overall score despite good preparation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" IMPORTANT POINTS \",\"name\":\"_important_points_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the marking scheme of NEET (UG) 2026 is critical because it directly determines how your attempts translate into your final score. Unlike many exams where attempting more questions increases chances of scoring higher, NEET follows a precision-based evaluation system, where accuracy is as important as knowledge.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A well-prepared candidate who understands the marking rules can significantly improve their score simply by making smarter decisions during the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Standard Marking Scheme &ndash; Core Evaluation System<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each question in NEET follows a fixed marking structure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct Answer: +4 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incorrect Answer: -1 mark<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Unattempted Question: 0 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This creates a high-risk, high-reward system, where:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accurate attempts lead to strong score gains<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Careless or blind attempts lead to negative marking and score reduction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Meaning of the Marking Scheme<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The presence of negative marking changes the entire exam strategy. Candidates must understand that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting every question is not always beneficial<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guessing without elimination can reduce overall score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selective and intelligent attempts often outperform aggressive attempts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Example Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate randomly guesses multiple questions, even a few incorrect answers can cancel out marks gained from correct ones. This makes accuracy more valuable than attempt volume.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Evaluation Rules for Exceptional Cases<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">While the exam is designed to have one correct answer per question, there are rare situations where discrepancies may occur. The evaluation system includes predefined rules to ensure fairness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Case 1: More Than One Correct Option<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a question is found to have multiple correct answers:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates who have selected any of the correct options will receive full marks (+4)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates who selected incorrect options will not receive marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<br>This benefits candidates who rely on strong conceptual understanding rather than memorization, as they are more likely to identify correct alternatives.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Case 2: All Options Are Correct<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If all answer options are found to be correct:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Every candidate who has attempted the question will be awarded full marks (+4)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Advantage:<br>Even partial understanding can result in full marks in such rare scenarios, making it beneficial to attempt questions where you have reasonable confidence.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Case 3: No Correct Option or Question Error<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a question is found to be incorrect, ambiguous, or invalid:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All candidates who appeared in the examination will receive +4 marks, regardless of whether they attempted the question or not<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<br>This ensures fairness and protects candidates from errors in the question paper.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistakes Students Make<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Despite knowing the marking scheme, many candidates lose marks due to poor execution:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blind guessing without eliminating options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Changing correct answers due to overthinking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Spending too much time on uncertain questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting questions under pressure without clarity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes often lead to unnecessary negative marking, which significantly affects the final score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Attempt Strategy Based on Marking Scheme<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To maximize marks, candidates should adopt a balanced approach:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempt questions with clear confidence first<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use elimination techniques before attempting doubtful questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid random guessing when unsure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mark and revisit difficult questions if time permits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This approach ensures that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accuracy remains high<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Negative marking is minimized<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall score is optimized<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Examination Mode\",\"name\":\"_examination_mode\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET (UG) 2026 will be conducted in a single day and single shift using the traditional pen-and-paper (offline) mode. This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates will receive a printed question paper booklet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Answers must be marked on a physical OMR (Optical Mark Recognition) sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No computer-based interface will be used<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This format continues the same approach followed in the previous session, ensuring consistency in the examination process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Standard Duration\",\"name\":\"_standard_duration\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The total duration of the NEET (UG) 2026 examination is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">3 hours (180 minutes)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Within this time, candidates are required to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read and understand 180 questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Solve them accurately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mark responses carefully on the OMR sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This creates a high-pressure environment, where candidates must maintain both speed and accuracy consistently throughout the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Medium of Question Paper\",\"name\":\"_medium_of_question_paper\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The medium of the question paper in NEET (UG) 2026 is a crucial decision that directly impacts a candidate&rsquo;s comprehension, accuracy, and overall performance. Since the examination involves complex scientific concepts, choosing the right language can significantly influence how effectively a candidate understands and interprets questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains the available languages, rules for selection, regional availability, and important strategic insights that candidates must consider before finalizing their choice.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Available Languages for NEET (UG) 2026<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET (UG) 2026 will be conducted in 13 different languages, allowing candidates from diverse linguistic backgrounds to attempt the exam comfortably.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">List of Available Mediums:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hindi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assamese<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bengali<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gujarati<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Kannada<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Malayalam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marathi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Odia<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Punjabi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tamil<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Telugu<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Urdu<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Language Selection &ndash; Critical Rules<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choosing the medium is not just a preference&mdash;it is a binding decision with long-term implications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The option must be selected carefully during the application process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Once chosen, the medium cannot be changed under any circumstances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The selected language determines how the question paper will be presented on exam day<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students choose a regional language for comfort but later face difficulty with scientific terminology. Therefore, the choice must balance comfort + clarity of concepts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Format of Question Paper Based on Language Choice<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The structure of the question paper varies depending on the selected medium:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">English Medium:<br>Question paper will be provided only in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hindi Medium:<br>Question paper will be bilingual (English + Hindi)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Regional Languages:<br>Question paper will be bilingual (English + selected regional language)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In case of any confusion, discrepancy, or error in translation, the English version will be considered final and authoritative.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why English Version is Considered Final<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even though multiple languages are provided, the original question paper is designed in English. Translations are secondary versions, and minor variations in wording may occur.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Implication:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates relying only on regional language may face confusion in rare cases<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cross-checking with English (if possible) can reduce errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medium vs Eligibility for Admission<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The language chosen for the exam does not affect eligibility for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Quota (AIQ) seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State quota admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Selection is purely based on:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medium of examination has no role in admission process, only performance matters.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Region-Wise Availability of Question Paper Medium<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The availability of language options depends on the location of the examination centre. Candidates can only select from languages permitted in their chosen exam region.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medium vs Examination Centre &ndash; Detailed Table<\\/h3>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"201\\\"><col width=\\\"362\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medium of Question Paper<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Examination Centres Where Available<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All centres in India and outside India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English &amp; Hindi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All examination centres in India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Assamese<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Assam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Bengali<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">West Bengal, Tripura, Andaman &amp; Nicobar Islands<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Gujarati<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Gujarat, Daman &amp; Diu, Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Kannada<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Karnataka<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Malayalam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Kerala, Lakshadweep<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Marathi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Maharashtra<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Odia<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Odisha<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Punjabi<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Punjab, Chandigarh, Delhi\\/NCR region<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Tamil<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Tamil Nadu, Puducherry, Andaman &amp; Nicobar Islands<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Telugu<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Andhra Pradesh, Telangana<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">English, Hindi &amp; Urdu<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Examination centres across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistakes Students Make<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choosing a regional language without strong familiarity with scientific terms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring the importance of English as the reference version<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting a medium based on comfort rather than exam strategy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not practicing mock tests in the chosen language<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes can lead to confusion during the exam, especially in concept-based questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr>\\r\\n<p><strong>Smart Strategy for Choosing Medium<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should finalize their medium based on:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Language in which they studied core subjects (Physics, Chemistry, Biology)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Comfort in understanding technical terms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ability to quickly interpret questions under time pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Recommendation:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate is comfortable with English, it is often the safest option due to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Original question framing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No translation ambiguity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Better alignment with study material&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 2, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 02:48:53');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(282, 5, '  Exam Centres – City Selection', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"Exam centres \",\"name\":\"exam_centres_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The selection and allocation of exam centres for NEET (UG) 2026 is a critical step in the application process. While it may seem like a simple preference-based choice, it involves multiple administrative and logistical factors that candidates must clearly understand to avoid inconvenience on the exam day.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The exam centre allotted to a candidate is not entirely dependent on personal choice&mdash;it is influenced by availability, demand, and operational feasibility. Therefore, candidates must approach this step with careful planning and awareness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Instructions for Selecting Exam Cities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates are required to select three preferred cities while filling out the application form, based on their convenience and accessibility. These preferences must be arranged in order of priority, as they guide the allotment process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The available list of cities (along with city codes) is predefined, and candidates must choose only from the officially provided options.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">In certain cases, depending on the candidate&rsquo;s address details, the system may restrict choices to one or two cities instead of three.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Restrictions Based on Address Criteria<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates can select exam cities only within the State of their Permanent Address or Present Address.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selection of cities outside these states is not permitted, ensuring that candidates are allotted centres within a reasonable geographic range.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are strongly advised to choose:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their own city, or<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Nearby cities within the same state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting distant or inconvenient locations can lead to avoidable travel challenges, for which the examination authority will not be responsible.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Centre Allotment Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The allotment of exam centres is done through a computer-based automated system, ensuring fairness and eliminating human intervention.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">While efforts are made to allot a centre in one of the preferred cities, final allocation depends on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Administrative feasibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Technical capacity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Number of candidates opting for a particular city<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The examination authority reserves the full right to allot any city\\/centre, even if it is not among the candidate&rsquo;s preferences.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Situations Where Preferred City May Not Be Allotted<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If the number of candidates in a selected city is too low, that city may be merged with another nearby city.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If the number of candidates opting for a specific regional language in a city is insufficient, candidates may be allotted a centre in a different city.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Due to logistical constraints, candidates may be required to travel to another city, even within the same state.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rules Regarding Exam Centres<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The final details of the exam centre (city and exact location) will be mentioned in the Admit Card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Once allotted, no request for change of exam centre or city will be entertained under any circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The examination authority may:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Add new centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancel existing centres<br>based on operational requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidate Responsibility and Travel Considerations<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must appear at the exam centre at their own cost and risk.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The examination authority will not be responsible for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel inconvenience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal injury<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of belongings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No travel allowance (TA\\/DA) will be provided to any candidate, including those from reserved categories.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting cities without considering distance and travel feasibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming that the first preference will always be allotted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring address-based restrictions while choosing cities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not planning travel arrangements in advance after admit card release<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes can lead to unnecessary stress and logistical challenges on exam day.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice for Smart City Selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choose cities that are easily accessible and familiar<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prefer locations with reliable transportation options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid selecting far-off cities just for preference without practical feasibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep a backup plan for travel once the admit card is released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', 3, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 02:55:10'),
(283, 5, ' ELIGIBILITY', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" ELIGIBILITY\",\"name\":\"_eligibility\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The eligibility criteria for NEET (UG) 2026 define who is permitted to appear for the examination and are strictly governed by regulatory authorities. Understanding these conditions is essential because failure to meet even a single requirement can lead to disqualification, regardless of preparation level or exam performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section provides a detailed and structured explanation of age requirements, nationality conditions, and critical eligibility rules, along with important insights that candidates often overlook.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Age Requirement<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To be eligible for NEET (UG) 2026, a candidate must fulfill the following age condition:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><span style=\\\"background-color: #fbeeb8;\\\">The candidate must have completed 17 years of age on or before 31st December 2026<\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Birth Date Criteria<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must be born on or before 31st December 2009<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This applies to:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General (UR) category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General-EWS category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC \\/ ST \\/ OBC-NCL categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD \\/ PwBD candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This rule ensures that candidates have reached a minimum level of academic and personal maturity required for medical education. Any candidate not meeting this age requirement will not be permitted to appear in the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Upper Age Limit &ndash; <span style=\\\"background-color: #fbeeb8;\\\">REMOVED<\\/span>&nbsp;<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">There is no upper age limit for appearing in NEET (UG) 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This allows:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Drop-year students<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Repeat aspirants<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates switching career paths<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">to attempt NEET without any restriction based on age.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Nationality Criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates belonging to the following categories are eligible to appear for NEET (UG) 2026:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Indian Citizens<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overseas Citizens of India (OCI)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Non-Resident Indians (NRIs)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Foreign Nationals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility for Studying Abroad<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Indian Citizens and OCI candidates who wish to pursue undergraduate medical or dental courses in foreign institutions are also required to qualify NEET (UG) 2026&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistakes Students Make<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Misinterpreting the minimum age cutoff date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming different age limits for different categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Believing there is still an upper age restriction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring NEET requirement for studying medicine abroad<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such misunderstandings can lead to serious eligibility issues at later stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Advisory<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Age eligibility is verified through official documents such as date of birth certificates and Class 10 records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any mismatch or incorrect information can lead to cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must ensure that all personal details are accurate and consistent across documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Eligibility for NRI, OCI & Foreign Nationals\",\"name\":\"_eligibility_for_nri_oci__foreign_nationals\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The eligibility framework for Non-Resident Indians (NRIs), Overseas Citizens of India (OCI), and Foreign Nationals in NEET (UG) 2026 is more complex than that of Indian residents. It involves not only qualifying the examination but also complying with multiple layers of documentation, nationality verification, and admission regulations defined by different authorities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates belonging to these categories must clearly understand that eligibility to appear in NEET and eligibility for admission are two separate aspects, both of which must be satisfied to secure a medical seat.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Overall Eligibility Framework<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates classified as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Non-Resident Indians (NRIs)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overseas Citizens of India (OCI)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Foreign Nationals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">are permitted to appear for NEET (UG) 2026 and are eligible for admission to medical and dental colleges. However, this eligibility is not absolute and is subject to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Regulations of the Government of India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rules defined by respective State Governments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Policies of individual institutions and counselling authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Qualifying NEET alone does not guarantee admission. Candidates must also meet specific institutional and state-level eligibility conditions, which may vary.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Documentation Requirements<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A critical aspect of eligibility for these candidates is submission of valid proof of nationality and status during the application process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For NRI and OCI Candidates<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must upload a valid certificate issued by the Indian Diplomatic Mission (Embassy\\/Consulate) in their country of residence.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This certificate serves as official proof of:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NRI status, or<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OCI status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The document must be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploaded during the online application process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preserved in original form for verification during counselling\\/admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to provide this certificate or submission of incorrect\\/invalid documentation can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification during counselling stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For Foreign National Candidates<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Foreign applicants must upload documentary proof of their nationality, which may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Relevant pages of a valid passport<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official certificate issued by a competent authority in their country confirming citizenship<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">These documents must be submitted during application and verified later during admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Nationality verification is strict and non-negotiable. Any discrepancy between submitted documents and actual identity can result in cancellation of candidature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Advisory for Foreign Candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Foreign nationals are strongly advised to:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Independently verify their eligibility with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling bodies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Participating institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is important because admission rules, seat availability, and reservation policies may differ significantly across states and institutions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility Status of OCI Candidates &ndash; Important Clarification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OCI candidates have a unique position in the eligibility framework due to legal developments.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OCI candidates are eligible to participate in NEET (UG) 2026 for admission to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dental<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH courses (Ayurveda, Siddha, Unani, Homoeopathy)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their eligibility is governed by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Policies of Government of India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional and state-level regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Legal Position and Rights of OCI Candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">As per the prevailing legal position:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OCI candidates continue to enjoy rights and privileges equivalent to those granted prior to regulatory changes made in 2021, based on judicial direction.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This ensures that OCI candidates:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Are not unfairly restricted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Can participate in admission processes under conditions similar to earlier frameworks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, practical implementation may still vary depending on counselling authorities, making verification essential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes and Risks to Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates in these categories often face issues due to:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not uploading proper embassy or nationality certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming NEET qualification alone ensures admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring state-specific eligibility rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Failing to preserve original documents for verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes can result in rejection even after qualifying the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Strategy for NRI \\/ OCI \\/ Foreign Candidates<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To ensure a smooth process, candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepare all required documents well in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify eligibility conditions for each target state or institution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure consistency across all identity and nationality documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep both digital and physical copies ready for future stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 4, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 03:03:06');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(284, 5, ' Counselling & Reservation', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Admission Procedure\",\"name\":\"_admission_procedure\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The counselling and admission process after NEET (UG) 2026 is a multi-layered system involving central and state authorities, multiple quotas, and strict merit-based selection. Qualifying NEET is only the first step&mdash;actual admission depends on how candidates navigate counselling, understand quota systems, and fulfill verification requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section provides a comprehensive and structured explanation of how seats are allocated, who conducts counselling, and how merit and reservation policies are applied across different courses and institutions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission Through NEET &ndash; The Only Gateway<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to undergraduate courses such as:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MBBS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BDS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BAMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BUMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BSMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BHMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">B.Sc. Nursing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">is done exclusively through NEET (UG) 2026.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No separate entrance exam is conducted for these courses. NEET score is the single qualifying and ranking criterion, making it the central pillar of the entire admission process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Types of Seats Available Under Different Quotas<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET counselling covers a wide range of seat categories across India. Understanding these categories is essential because eligibility, competition level, and counselling authority differ for each.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Major Seat Categories Include:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Quota (AIQ) Seats (15%)<br>Available across government medical colleges in India, filled on a national merit basis.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Government Quota Seats (85%)<br>Reserved for candidates belonging to a particular state, filled through state counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Institutions \\/ Universities Seats<br>Includes institutions under central government control.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities Seats<br>Private institutions with autonomous status, offering admissions through centralized counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Private Medical\\/Dental Colleges Seats<br>Includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Management quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NRI quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Self-financed seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Pool Quota Seats<br>Reserved for specific categories as defined by government policies.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutes of National Importance<br>Includes premier institutions like:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AIIMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">JIPMER<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Counselling Authorities &ndash; Who Conducts Admission?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The counselling process is divided between central-level and state-level authorities, each responsible for specific seat categories.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Central Counselling Authority (MCC\\/DGHS)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Medical Counselling Committee (MCC) under the Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS) conducts counselling for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">15% All India Quota (AIQ) seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">100% seats in Central Institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AIIMS and JIPMER institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MCC also handles registration for certain institutions like AFMC but may forward data to respective authorities for final admission processing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">State Counselling Authorities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Governments and Union Territories conduct counselling for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">85% State quota seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State medical colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Private colleges within the state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each state has its own rules, eligibility criteria, domicile requirements, and reservation policies. Candidates must carefully follow state-specific notifications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of NEET Result in Other Courses<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET (UG) 2026 results are not limited to MBBS and BDS. They are also used for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">B.Sc. (Hons.) Nursing admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Veterinary courses (BVSc &amp; AH) under specific quotas<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shortlisting candidates for Military Nursing Service (MNS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Different institutions may apply their own eligibility criteria even while using NEET scores.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">AYUSH Courses Counselling Authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For traditional medicine courses:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AACCC (All India Ayush Central Counselling Committee) conducts counselling for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BAMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BUMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BSMS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BHMS&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Strategic Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">AYUSH counselling is separate from MBBS\\/BDS counselling and requires separate registration and participation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Merit List and Admission Basis<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">An All India Merit List is prepared based on NEET (UG) 2026 scores<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates are assigned an All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NTA only provides the AIR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling authorities prepare final merit lists based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AIR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Admission Criteria:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission is granted strictly based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat availability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Document Verification and Eligibility Check<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">During counselling, candidates must undergo strict verification of:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploaded documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity and category claims<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic qualifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any mismatch, incorrect declaration, or invalid document can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediate disqualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Policy &ndash; How It Applies<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation in NEET counselling is applied as per:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government of India rules (for AIQ seats)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State government policies (for state quota seats)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This includes categories such as:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OBC-NCL<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD\\/PwBD<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation benefits vary significantly between central and state quotas, making it essential to understand applicable rules before participating in counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming NEET qualification guarantees admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not participating in counselling rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring state-specific eligibility rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missing document verification requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confusing AIQ and state quota processes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes often result in loss of seats despite good ranks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"Admission in State Medical Colleges & Private Institutions (Beyond 15% All India Quota)\",\"name\":\"admission_in_state_medical_colleges__private_institutions_beyond_15_all_india_quota\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to medical seats outside the 15% All India Quota is governed entirely by State\\/Union Territory counselling systems, making this pathway highly dependent on regional policies, eligibility conditions, and reservation frameworks. Candidates must clearly understand that rules applicable in one state may not apply in another, and overlooking these variations is one of the most common reasons for admission failure despite qualifying NEET.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">State Quota Admissions &ndash; Policy-Driven and State-Specific<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Seats under the State Quota (generally 85%) in government medical colleges are filled by respective State\\/UT counselling authorities. Admission in these seats is not uniform across India and is strictly based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State-specific eligibility conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Domicile requirements (in most cases)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation policies defined by the state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each state releases its own counselling notification, and candidates must comply with those rules independently. Simply qualifying NEET does not automatically make a candidate eligible for every state.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Policies &ndash; Vary Across States<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation for categories such as:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OBC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD\\/PwBD<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">is applied based on laws and regulations of the respective State\\/UT.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Understanding:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The percentage of reservation and category definitions may differ from central policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some states may have additional sub-categories or local quotas<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates often assume central reservation rules apply everywhere, which can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incorrect category claims<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection during document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission in Private Medical Colleges<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Private medical colleges follow a combination of national and state-level regulations, and their admission process is also conducted through state counselling authorities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These institutions may offer:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Management quota seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NRI quota seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Self-financed seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although NEET qualification is mandatory, admission policies in private colleges are influenced by:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State government regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee structures and seat distribution norms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Governing Authorities and Decision Framework<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admissions under this category are controlled by:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Governments \\/ UT Administrations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State counselling authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Regulatory guidelines issued by Government of India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No centralized authority (like MCC) controls these seats. Each state independently manages:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Merit list preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Considerations for Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To maximize chances of admission under State Quota or Private Colleges, candidates must:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carefully check state-wise eligibility and domicile rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Understand applicable reservation policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Participate in multiple state counselling processes if eligible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepare all required documents in advance for verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming eligibility across all states without checking domicile rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring state counselling registration deadlines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Misunderstanding reservation criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not exploring private college options strategically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These errors can result in missed opportunities even for candidates with good ranks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Admission Through 15% All India Quota & Central Institutions\",\"name\":\"_admission_through_15_all_india_quota__central_institutions\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to top medical institutions and the 15% All India Quota (AIQ) seats is conducted through a centralized counselling system managed by the Medical Counselling Committee (MCC) under the Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS). This process is highly competitive, strictly merit-based, and governed by national-level regulations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding how this system works is essential because it includes India&rsquo;s most prestigious institutions and offers opportunities beyond state boundaries.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scope of MCC Counselling &ndash; Which Institutions Are Covered?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC counselling is responsible for admissions to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">15% All India Quota (AIQ) seats in government medical colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AIIMS institutes across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">JIPMER institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Universities, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delhi University (DU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Banaras Hindu University (BHU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aligarh Muslim University (AMU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guru Gobind Singh Indraprastha University (GGSIPU) medical colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ESIC Medical Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PGIMER and other central institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This system allows candidates to compete at a national level, irrespective of their state of domicile, making it one of the most important admission pathways.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Registration for MCC Counselling<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Qualifying NEET alone is not sufficient. Candidates must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Register separately on the official MCC counselling portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Participate in counselling rounds based on their All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Understanding:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate fails to register on the MCC platform after results are declared, they will not be considered for any of these seats, regardless of their rank.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission Process &ndash; Merit and Regulatory Framework<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admissions through MCC are governed by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET (UG) 2026 All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Regulations defined by national authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional policies of respective universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Seat allotment is strictly based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Availability of seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">There is no manual intervention, ensuring transparency and fairness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Case: Admission to Armed Forces Medical College (AFMC), Pune<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to AFMC follows a distinct process, even though initial registration is done through MCC.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Points:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must first register through MCC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data is then forwarded to AFMC authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shortlisted candidates must undergo:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A second-stage screening process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional evaluation as per defence requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to AFMC is not solely based on NEET rank. It involves:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional screening<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical fitness standards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional selection criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of MCC &ndash; What It Does and What It Does Not Do<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC functions as a counselling execution authority, meaning:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What MCC Does:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducts counselling rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Allots seats based on merit and preferences<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Publishes results and schedules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What MCC Does NOT Do:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Modify or correct candidate data<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Change personal details such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date of Birth<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Contact information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All data used in counselling is directly taken from the application submitted earlier. Any mistake made during application will:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reflect during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cannot be corrected at this stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Counselling Rounds and Eligibility Rules<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC counselling is conducted in multiple rounds, and eligibility for each round depends on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Previous seat allotment status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Participation in earlier rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rules designed to prevent seat blocking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Regulation Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who are allotted a seat in earlier rounds may:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Become ineligible for subsequent rounds under certain conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lose the opportunity to upgrade if rules are not properly understood<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutional and Legal Framework<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admissions are governed by:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National medical education regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional rules of universities and colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Judicial decisions and policy guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Understanding:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even within MCC counselling, institution-specific rules may apply, especially in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not registering for MCC counselling after NEET results<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming AIQ participation is automatic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring rules related to counselling rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entering incorrect data during application stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding AFMC&rsquo;s separate admission process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Reservation Policy for MBBS, BDS & B.Sc. Nursing\",\"name\":\"_reservation_policy_for_mbbs_bds__bsc_nursing\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The reservation system under MCC (DGHS) counselling for NEET (UG) 2026 is a structured, legally governed framework designed to ensure equitable access to medical education across different socio-economic and social categories. However, this system is not just about percentages&mdash;it involves strict eligibility conditions, documentation requirements, and category-specific rules, which candidates must understand in depth to avoid disqualification during counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains the reservation policy in a comprehensive and strategic manner, including category definitions, eligibility conditions, and high-impact mistakes that candidates must avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Central Reservation Framework &ndash; Applicable Scope<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The reservation policy discussed here applies to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">15% All India Quota (AIQ) seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Universities and Institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutions where counselling is conducted by MCC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This reservation system is based on Government of India norms, and it may differ from reservation policies followed in State Quota counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category-Wise Reservation Distribution<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The following reservation percentages are applicable across courses:<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"312\\\"><col width=\\\"252\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">General-EWS (Economically Weaker Section)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OBC-NCL (Non-Creamy Layer)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">27%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scheduled Caste (SC)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">15%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scheduled Tribe (ST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7.5%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disabilities)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5% (Horizontal across all categories)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">General &ndash; Economically Weaker Section (GEN-EWS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The GEN-EWS category is meant for candidates from the general category who fall under economically weaker sections as defined by the Government of India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility Conditions:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate must satisfy income and asset criteria defined by central government norms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must possess a valid and current EWS certificate issued by a competent authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only candidates who strictly meet financial eligibility conditions are entitled to this benefit. Incorrect claims or outdated certificates will lead to rejection during verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Other Backward Classes &ndash; Non-Creamy Layer (OBC-NCL)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OBC-NCL reservation is available only to candidates who belong to the non-creamy layer of OBC categories listed in the Central List.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Conditions:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate&rsquo;s caste must be present in the Central OBC list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State OBC list alone is not sufficient<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate must fall under non-creamy layer criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarifications:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates from the creamy layer are NOT eligible for reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Such candidates are treated as General (Unreserved)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates incorrectly assume that being OBC in their state guarantees eligibility. If the caste is not in the central list, the reservation claim will be rejected.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scheduled Caste (SC) Category<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation: 15%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must provide a valid SC certificate as per Government of India guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The certificate must be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issued by a competent authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">In the prescribed format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid at the time of counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scheduled Tribe (ST) Category<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation: 7.5%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Similar documentation requirements as SC category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Understanding:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verification of ST status is strict, and any inconsistency in documentation can lead to cancellation of candidature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Persons with Benchmark Disabilities (PwBD) &ndash; Horizontal Reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwBD reservation is applied across all categories, meaning:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">5% seats are reserved within each category (GEN, EWS, OBC, SC, ST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility Requirements:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate must meet disability criteria defined under NMC guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must possess a valid PwBD\\/UDID certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is a horizontal reservation, not a separate category. It works within existing categories.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Documentation Requirements &ndash; A Crucial Step<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For each category, candidates must provide:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid and updated certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Documents in prescribed format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Certificates issued by authorized authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if a candidate has a valid rank, failure to produce correct documentation will result in loss of reserved seat benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation in State Quota &ndash; A Different System<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For seats under State Quota:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation policies are governed by respective State Governments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentage and criteria may differ significantly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A candidate eligible for reservation under AIQ may not necessarily be eligible under a particular state&rsquo;s rules, and vice versa.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using outdated or invalid category certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Claiming OBC status based only on state list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding creamy layer exclusion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming PwBD applies as a separate category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring differences between central and state reservation systems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes often lead to rejection at the counselling stage, even after achieving a good NEET rank.&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Provisions for Persons with Disability (PwD) \\/ Persons with Benchmark Disability (PwBD) in NEET (UG) \",\"name\":\"_provisions_for_persons_with_disability_pwd__persons_with_benchmark_disability_pwbd_in_neet_ug_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The provisions for candidates with disabilities in NEET (UG) 2026 are governed by a comprehensive legal and procedural framework, primarily based on The Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016, along with subsequent government guidelines. These provisions are designed to ensure equal opportunity, accessibility, and fairness during the examination process. However, availing these benefits requires strict compliance with defined criteria, certification standards, and procedural requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding these provisions in depth is essential, as incorrect claims or documentation errors can lead to serious consequences, including disqualification even after qualification or admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Legal Foundation &ndash; Understanding Disability Classification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The eligibility and facilities for PwD\\/PwBD candidates are rooted in legal definitions that determine who qualifies for what benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Definitions:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Person with Disability (PwD):<br>A candidate with a long-term physical, mental, intellectual, or sensory impairment that affects their ability to participate fully in society.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Person with Benchmark Disability (PwBD):<br>A candidate with at least 40% of a specified disability, certified by an authorized medical authority.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Specified Disability:<br>Disabilities recognized under the official schedule of the law, forming the basis for eligibility and benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The distinction between PwD and PwBD is crucial because most examination benefits (like scribe and compensatory time) are directly linked to benchmark disability status or certified writing limitations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scribe Facility &ndash; Eligibility and Conditions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The provision of a scribe (writer\\/assistant) is one of the most important support mechanisms for candidates who face difficulty in writing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Who Can Avail a Scribe?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates with benchmark disabilities (PwBD) who have writing limitations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates with specific conditions such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blindness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Severe locomotor disability (both arms affected)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cerebral palsy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates with less than 40% disability but certified difficulty in writing (with valid medical proof)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Conditions for Availing a Scribe:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A valid certificate must confirm:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Physical limitation in writing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Necessity of a scribe<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Certificate must be issued by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government medical authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authorized medical board<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Using Own Scribe:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are allowed to bring their own scribe, subject to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The scribe&rsquo;s qualification must be lower than the candidate&rsquo;s qualification level<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Proper declaration and documentation must be submitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Restriction:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scribe is only allowed to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Write answers as dictated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scribe is strictly prohibited from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Explaining questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Suggesting answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Compensatory Time &ndash; Extra Time Provision<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To ensure fairness, candidates eligible for assistance are granted compensatory time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Standard Provision:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum 20 minutes per hour of examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">For a 3-hour exam, at least 1 additional hour is provided<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This benefit applies even if the candidate does not use a scribe (if eligible)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time is calculated proportionally for shorter durations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should plan their exam strategy accordingly, as compensatory time can significantly impact performance when used effectively.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates with Less Than 40% Disability<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who do not meet the 40% benchmark but still face difficulty in writing are not automatically eligible for benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Conditions to Avail Support:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must provide certification from a multi-member medical board, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chief Medical Officer \\/ Civil Surgeon<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Specialists (Orthopaedic, Neurologist, Psychologist, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Certificate must clearly state:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing limitation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Need for a scribe or additional time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This category undergoes stricter verification, and approval is not guaranteed without proper documentation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of Exam Authority in Providing Scribe<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates can either:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bring their own scribe<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Request the examination authority to provide one<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If provided by the authority:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates may be given an opportunity to meet the scribe before the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Document Requirements and Verification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must upload:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disability Certificate or UDID (Unique Disability ID)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Supporting documents as required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If UDID is provided and verified, certificate upload may not be required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All documents must be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Legible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issued by competent authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rules on Misuse of Benefits<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The system has zero tolerance for misuse of disability provisions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Consequences of False Claims:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If at any stage it is found that a candidate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Did not actually have the claimed disability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Used a scribe without eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submitted false or fabricated documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Then:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The candidate will be removed from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evaluation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ranking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If already admitted:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission will be cancelled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Risk:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This applies even after admission, making accuracy and honesty absolutely critical.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Accessibility and Examination Support<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Beyond scribes and time, additional provisions include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use of assistive devices (where permitted)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accessible seating arrangements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Barrier-free examination centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These measures aim to ensure a fair testing environment for all candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category Selection &ndash; A Non-Editable Decision<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must carefully select their PwD\\/PwBD status while filling the application form.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No changes will be allowed after submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category cannot be modified after result declaration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Incorrect selection at the application stage can permanently affect eligibility for benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation vs Examination Support &ndash; Key Distinction<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation benefits (seat allocation) depend on category eligibility and verification during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Examination support (scribe\\/time) depends on certified disability and functional limitation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Understanding:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A candidate may qualify for one but not necessarily the other.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Reservation Policy in Central Institutions and State Quota\",\"name\":\"_reservation_policy_in_central_institutions_and_state_quota\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding how reservation works is extremely important because it directly affects your admission chances, cutoff scores, and college allocation strategy. Many students ignore the depth of reservation rules and later face confusion during counselling. This section explains both Central-level reservation and State-level reservation in a clear, structured, and practical way.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation in Central Universities and Institutions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For admissions conducted under central authorities (such as All India Quota seats, AIIMS, JIPMER, Central Universities, and other centrally governed institutions), a uniform reservation policy defined by the Government of India is followed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The seat distribution across categories is fixed and applies consistently across these institutions:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"169\\\"><col width=\\\"122\\\"><col width=\\\"333\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Explanation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">GEN-EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For economically weaker candidates from the General category who meet income and asset criteria defined by the government<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OBC-NCL<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">27%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates belonging to Other Backward Classes under the Non-Creamy Layer (as per central list)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">SC (Scheduled Caste)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">15%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reserved for candidates from Scheduled Caste communities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">ST (Scheduled Tribe)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7.5%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reserved for candidates from Scheduled Tribe communities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disabilities)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5% (Horizontal)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Applied across all categories (GEN, EWS, OBC, SC, ST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Concept: Horizontal vs Vertical Reservation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A key concept that students often misunderstand is the difference between vertical and horizontal reservation:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Vertical Reservation (GEN-EWS, OBC-NCL, SC, ST):<br>These are category-based seat divisions. Each category gets a fixed percentage of total seats.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Horizontal Reservation (PwBD):<br>This is applied within each category, not separately.<br>For example, 5% PwBD seats are distributed across GEN, EWS, OBC, SC, and ST categories.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why this matters:<br>A PwBD candidate competes within their category first and then benefits from additional reservation, which can significantly improve admission chances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Conditions for Availing Reservation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Simply selecting a category is not enough. To actually benefit from reservation:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must have valid and up-to-date certificates as per Government of India norms.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">For OBC-NCL, your name must be in the Central List, not just the State List.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">For EWS, income and asset criteria must strictly match official guidelines.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">For SC\\/ST, certificates must follow the prescribed format and issuing authority rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">For PwBD, disability must meet the defined benchmark and be verified through proper medical certification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to meet these conditions leads to:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of category claim<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conversion to General category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of reserved seat advantage during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation in State Quota Seats<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">While central institutions follow a uniform system, State Quota seats operate differently.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For admissions under:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Government Medical Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Private Medical Colleges under State jurisdiction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The reservation policy is decided entirely by the respective State Government or Union Territory.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Differences in State Reservation<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each state has its own reservation percentages, which may differ significantly from central rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some states include additional categories, such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State-specific OBC lists<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Local domicile quotas<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Special categories (e.g., rural, defence, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility conditions like domicile requirements may apply.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight for Students<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is where smart planning becomes important:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A student may qualify under a category at the central level but not at the state level, or vice versa.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cutoffs vary significantly between:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Quota (AIQ)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State Quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some states offer better chances due to lower competition or higher reservation percentages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates lose opportunities due to avoidable errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming state and central reservation rules are the same<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting the wrong category without verifying eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading outdated or incorrect certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring domicile rules for state counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding how PwBD reservation is applied<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Guidelines for PwBD Candidates\",\"name\":\"_guidelines_for_pwbd_candidates\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For candidates applying under the Persons with Benchmark Disabilities (PwBD) category, the admission process involves strict legal, medical, and verification-based procedures. This is not just a reservation benefit&mdash;it is a multi-stage eligibility validation system, and misunderstanding it can lead to rejection even after qualifying NEET.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains the complete framework in a detailed and practical manner so that candidates clearly understand what qualifies them, what documents are required, and what risks must be avoided.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Framework for PwBD Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">As per the provisions of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016, candidates with benchmark disabilities are eligible for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">5% reservation in total seats in medical courses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This reservation is horizontal, meaning it is applied within each category (General, EWS, OBC, SC, ST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, simply having a disability does not automatically guarantee admission under this quota. The candidate must satisfy both:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Legal eligibility (as per disability definition and percentage)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Functional eligibility (ability to pursue a medical course)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Rule for AIIMS and Similar Institutes<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For institutions like AIIMS and other top central institutes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even if a candidate qualifies under PwBD category,<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final eligibility is subject to assessment by the institute&rsquo;s Medical Board<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why this matters:<br>A candidate may be eligible on paper but can still be declared unfit for medical education if the disability is considered incompatible with course requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Pre-Application Medical Validation (Highly Critical)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who believe they fall under PwBD category should not assume eligibility. Instead, they must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Get themselves examined at a:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government Medical College<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">District Hospital<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government Hospital<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Obtain a Disability Certificate issued as per:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official assessment guidelines notified by the Government of India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reality Most Students Miss<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The disability certificate obtained at this stage:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only confirms whether you are eligible to apply under PwBD category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Does NOT guarantee admission under PwBD quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the biggest misconceptions among candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Document Requirements During Counselling<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After qualifying NEET, PwBD candidates must undergo strict verification during counselling, where the following documents are mandatory:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. UDID Card (Unique Disability ID)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issued by authorized government medical authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Acts as a centralized and verifiable proof of disability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Self-Certified Affidavit<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must be submitted in the prescribed format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirms that the candidate is declaring correct disability details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Medical Board Verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate must appear before a designated medical board<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The board will:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assess actual disability condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirm whether the candidate is eligible for admission under PwBD quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Multi-Level Verification: Why It Exists<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The system is designed to prevent misuse and ensure fairness. Therefore, PwBD eligibility is checked at multiple levels:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Initial Certification (before applying)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document submission during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final medical board assessment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure at any stage can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of PwBD status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shift to General category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of admission (even after seat allotment)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Risk Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates lose their PwBD benefit due to avoidable errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming disability automatically qualifies for reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not getting certification from authorized government medical institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading incorrect or incomplete documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not obtaining UDID card in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Providing false or exaggerated disability claims<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring final medical board verification requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight: Functional Fitness Matters<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medical education is physically and mentally demanding. Therefore:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authorities evaluate not just the percentage of disability, but also<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Whether the candidate is capable of performing essential medical duties<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is why final approval is given only after functional assessment by experts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"  MCC Counselling Process for MBBS and BDS Admission    \",\"name\":\"_mcc_counselling_process_for_mbbs_and_bds_admission_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The counselling process is the final and most decisive stage in securing a medical or dental seat after qualifying NEET. Many candidates with good ranks lose opportunities not due to marks, but due to lack of clarity about counselling structure, quotas, and decision-making strategy. This section explains the entire process in a structured and practical manner to help you navigate it effectively.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Who Conducts Counselling and Where to Access It<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All counselling for major national-level seats is conducted by the Medical Counselling Committee, which operates under the Directorate General of Health Services.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The entire process is conducted online<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All official updates, schedules, and registration links are available only on the MCC portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must regularly track updates because missing a deadline can directly lead to loss of admission opportunity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Scope of MCC Counselling: Which Seats Are Covered<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC counselling is not limited to a single quota&mdash;it covers a wide range of institutions and seat categories across India. Understanding this scope is crucial for making informed choices.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. All India Quota (AIQ) Seats<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">15% MBBS\\/BDS seats in government medical and dental colleges across states<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open to candidates from all states based on All India Rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Central Universities and Institutions<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC handles 100% seats in major central institutions, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Banaras Hindu University (BHU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aligarh Muslim University (AMU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">University of Delhi (DU)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Jamia Millia Islamia<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These may include both:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open seats (All India)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Internal\\/domicile-based seats (for specific categories)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. National Institutes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MCC conducts counselling for top national-level institutes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) &ndash; 100% MBBS seats across all AIIMS campuses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Jawaharlal Institute of Postgraduate Medical Education and Research (JIPMER) &ndash; Puducherry and Karaikal campuses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Special Institutions and Quotas<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Employees\' State Insurance Corporation Medical Colleges (including insured persons quota)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Armed Forces Medical College<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MCC only handles registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final selection involves additional screening by AFMC authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Deemed Universities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MCC conducts counselling for 100% seats in deemed universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NRI quota seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minority institution seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Nursing and Other Courses<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MCC also handles admission for selected central B.Sc. Nursing institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Policy in MCC Counselling (Central Level)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For All India Quota and central institutions, a uniform reservation policy is followed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"155\\\"><col width=\\\"252\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">SC (Scheduled Caste)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">15%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">ST (Scheduled Tribe)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7.5%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OBC-NCL<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">27% (only if in Central List)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">GEN-EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwBD<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5% (Horizontal across all categories)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Reservation Rules for Deemed Universities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Deemed universities follow a slightly different structure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NRI Quota Seats available for eligible candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minority-based reservations such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Jain Minority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Muslim Minority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These rules vary by institution and must be carefully reviewed before choice filling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Rule for OBC Candidates (High Impact)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A common mistake occurs in the OBC category:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only candidates listed in the Central OBC-NCL list are eligible for reservation in MCC counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If a candidate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Belongs to OBC in state list but not in central list, OR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Falls under creamy layer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&rarr; They must select General (Unreserved) category<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Consequence of mistake:<br>Incorrect category selection can lead to:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of allotted seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification during document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How the MCC Counselling Process Works (Strategic Flow)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although technical steps may appear simple, the process requires strategic thinking:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration on MCC portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choice filling and locking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment based on rank, category, and choices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reporting to allotted institute or opting for upgrade<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multiple rounds (Round 1, Round 2, Mop-up, Stray Vacancy)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Impact Mistakes Candidates Must Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students with good ranks lose seats due to avoidable errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding which seats MCC controls<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Filling limited or poorly researched choices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring previous year cutoffs and trends<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting wrong category (especially OBC\\/EWS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missing deadlines for registration or reporting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding upgrade and exit rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight for Better Outcomes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Treat counselling as a decision-making process, not a formality<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Always fill maximum possible choices to avoid losing a seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prioritize colleges based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank feasibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Location preference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Infrastructure and exposure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep backup options ready (Deemed universities, lower preference colleges)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 5, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 03:44:06');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(285, 5, ' Merit list and Qualifying Criteria', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Qualifying Criteria for NEET UG\",\"name\":\"_qualifying_criteria_for_neet_ug\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The qualifying criteria for NEET UG are not just entry conditions&mdash;they are the foundation for ranking, eligibility determination, and admission eligibility across all medical and allied health courses in India. The National Testing Agency (NTA) prepares the merit list strictly based on these rules, along with guidelines issued by multiple regulatory bodies governing medical, dental, and AYUSH education.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding this section clearly is essential because even a small misunderstanding can lead to ineligibility for counselling despite appearing in the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Merit List and Rank Preparation Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The National Testing Agency is responsible for preparing the:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Merit List<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category-wise ranking list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These are prepared strictly based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Performance in NEET UG exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility norms defined by regulatory authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation and category rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic and document verification standards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The final data is shared with counselling authorities and used for seat allocation across India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Qualifying Percentile Requirement<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To be considered eligible for admission, candidates must secure a minimum percentile score, not just marks. This percentile system ensures relative performance-based selection.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. General and EWS Category<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum requirement: 50th percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicable to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General category candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General-EWS candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. SC \\/ ST \\/ OBC-NCL Categories<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum requirement: 40th percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicable to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduled Caste (SC)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduled Tribe (ST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other Backward Classes &ndash; Non-Creamy Layer (OBC-NCL)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. PwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disabilities)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">General \\/ EWS PwBD candidates: 45th percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC \\/ ST \\/ OBC-NCL PwBD candidates: 40th percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Concept: How Percentile is Calculated<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Percentile is not a fixed mark; it depends on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Highest score achieved in NEET UG that year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall performance of all candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Relative ranking position in the merit list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even if paper difficulty changes, qualifying benchmark adjusts automatically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission eligibility remains fair across different exam years<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Relaxation of Minimum Qualifying Criteria (Special Provision)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In certain situations, if a large number of candidates fail to meet the minimum qualifying percentile, the Central Government may revise the cutoff.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This decision is taken in consultation with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical education regulatory bodies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dental education authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH governing councils<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such relaxation is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicable only for that specific academic year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not permanent<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issued to ensure sufficient candidate availability for admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Subject-Specific Eligibility for AYUSH Courses<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some courses require additional subject-specific qualifications, especially in traditional medicine systems.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">BUMS (Bachelor of Unani Medicine and Surgery)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must have:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Studied Urdu, Arabic, or Persian at 10th standard level<br>OR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Passed a recognized Urdu proficiency test (if applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">BSMS (Bachelor of Siddha Medicine and Surgery)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must have:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Studied Tamil at 10th standard or higher secondary level<br>OR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Study Tamil as a subject during the first professional year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why this matters:<br>These language requirements ensure students can understand classical medical texts and traditional diagnostic systems effectively.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Provision for Students Awaiting Results<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who have:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appeared for qualifying examination (Class 12 or equivalent)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not yet received results<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">are allowed to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appear for NEET UG provisionally<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, admission is granted only if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They later meet all eligibility conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Required marks and subject criteria are fulfilled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If eligibility is not met later, admission is automatically cancelled.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Regulatory Framework<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility rules are governed by multiple authorities, including:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National medical education regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dental education standards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH and traditional medicine councils<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State and central counselling bodies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This ensures that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission standards remain uniform nationwide<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only eligible candidates proceed to counselling&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Inter-Se-Merit (Tie-Breaking Criteria)\",\"name\":\"_inter-se-merit_tie-breaking_criteria\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In competitive exams like NEET UG, it is quite common for two or more candidates to secure exactly the same marks or percentile score. Since ranks must still be assigned uniquely for counselling and seat allocation, a structured tie-breaking system (Inter-Se-Merit rule) is used.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This system ensures fairness by evaluating candidates step-by-step based on subject performance and accuracy levels.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Priority Based on Biology Performance<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The first and most important deciding factor is Biology (Botany &amp; Zoology).<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The candidate who scores higher marks in Biology is given a better rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biology carries the highest weightage in NEET, so it is prioritized first<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why this matters:<br>Since Biology is most relevant for medical courses, it acts as the strongest indicator of suitability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Chemistry Score as Second Preference<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Biology marks are also equal, the next deciding factor is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Higher marks in Chemistry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Chemistry is considered next because it forms the core bridge between Biology and Physics in medical sciences, especially in pharmacology and biochemical understanding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3: Physics Score as Third Preference<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If both Biology and Chemistry scores are identical:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Higher marks in Physics are considered<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although Physics has lower weightage in MBBS selection compared to Biology, it is still important for scientific and analytical reasoning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 4: Accuracy-Based Evaluation (Overall Performance)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If subject-wise marks remain identical, the system shifts to accuracy analysis across the entire exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Here, the candidate with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A lower proportion of incorrect answers compared to correct answers (overall subjects combined)<br>is ranked higher.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Meaning:<br>This step rewards candidates who:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempted questions carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintained higher accuracy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoided guesswork or negative marking impact<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 5: Subject-Wise Accuracy in Biology<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If tie still persists, the system evaluates accuracy specifically in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biology (Botany &amp; Zoology)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The candidate with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fewer incorrect attempts relative to correct answers in Biology<br>gets the advantage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 6: Subject-Wise Accuracy in Chemistry<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If still unresolved:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chemistry accuracy is considered next<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Better precision and fewer wrong answers in Chemistry<br>are ranked higher<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 7: Subject-Wise Accuracy in Physics<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If the tie still continues:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Physics accuracy is evaluated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lower incorrect-to-correct ratio gives advantage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 8: Random Selection (Final Stage)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If all above criteria fail to break the tie:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A random selection process is conducted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This is done under the supervision of an independent expert committee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Purpose of this step:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">To ensure final fairness when all measurable academic parameters are identical<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">To eliminate bias or subjective decision-making<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight: How Tie-Breaking Actually Impacts Rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although rare, tie-breaking can significantly affect:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">College allocation during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat category distribution (especially in borderline ranks)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even a small difference in Biology marks or accuracy can shift a candidate thousands of ranks ahead.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Understanding for Students<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To minimize risk in tie situations, candidates should focus on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strengthening Biology accuracy (highest priority factor)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reducing negative marking in all subjects<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoiding blind guessing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Improving conceptual clarity instead of memorization-based attempts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Merit List for Counselling under 15% All India Quota\",\"name\":\"_merit_list_for_counselling_under_15_all_india_quota\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The 15% All India Quota (AIQ) is one of the most important admission pathways in NEET UG counselling. It allows candidates from any state in India to compete for a fixed percentage of seats in government medical and dental colleges across the country. The preparation and handling of the merit list for these seats is done in a highly structured and centralized manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preparation of AIQ Merit List<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The National Testing Agency is responsible for preparing the official merit list for candidates applying under the 15% All India Quota.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This merit list is created strictly on the basis of:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marks obtained in NEET UG&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria prescribed for the examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category and reservation rules (where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tie-breaking rules in case of equal scores<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only those candidates who:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Qualify NEET UG<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Opt for All India Quota during counselling<br>are included in this list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How Candidates Are Selected for the Merit List<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The selection process is straightforward but strictly merit-based:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates are arranged according to their All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Higher rank candidates are placed above lower rank candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category-wise classification is also maintained for counselling purposes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This ensures a transparent and rank-driven admission process, where performance in the entrance exam is the sole deciding factor.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of the Merit List in Counselling Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The merit list is not just a ranking document&mdash;it acts as the foundation for seat allocation under AIQ counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once prepared, it is forwarded to the official counselling authority:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical Counselling Committee<br>(under the Directorate General of Health Services, Ministry of Health and Family Welfare)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This authority uses the merit list for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Online registration verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choice filling and locking process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment in multiple counselling rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Distribution of Merit List to Regulatory Bodies<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After preparation, the merit list is shared with multiple national regulatory and counselling bodies responsible for different streams of medical education:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical and Dental counselling authorities under MCC\\/DGHS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Indian System of Medicine (NCISM)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Homoeopathy (NCH)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ministry of AYUSH (for AYUSH-related admissions where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This ensures that the same NEET UG result is used across:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MBBS and BDS admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH courses (where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other allied medical education streamsImportance of AIQ Merit List in Admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The 15% AIQ merit list plays a crucial role because:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It provides nationwide competition, not state-limited selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It allows candidates to apply for top government colleges across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It ensures admission based purely on national ranking and merit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It removes state domicile restrictions for AIQ seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Understanding<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The merit list for the 15% All India Quota is a centralized and highly competitive ranking system that determines admission to some of the most sought-after medical and dental seats in India. Prepared by NTA and used by MCC and other authorities, it ensures that:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only NEET UG performance matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission is strictly rank-based<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling is conducted in a transparent and uniform manner<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A strong position in this merit list significantly increases the chances of securing a top medical college under the All India Quota system.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"   MERIT LIST FOR SEATS OTHER THAN 15% ALL INDIA QUOTA\",\"name\":\"_merit_list_for_seats_other_than_15_all_india_quota\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The preparation of merit lists for medical admissions beyond the 15% All India Quota is carried out in a structured and centralized manner to ensure fairness, transparency, and uniformity across different states and institutions. In this system, the National Testing Agency (NTA) plays a key role in generating the All India Rank based purely on the performance of candidates in NEET (UG) - 2026.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once the results are declared, the NTA does not conduct counselling itself for these seats. Instead, it shares the complete database of qualified candidates along with their ranks with the relevant authorities. These authorities include the Directorate General of Health Services under the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, along with the Ministry of AYUSH and regulatory bodies such as NCISM and NCH. This ensures that all streams of medical education, including modern medicine and Indian systems of medicine, receive standardized result data for further admission processing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After receiving this data, counselling authorities at the state or institutional level take responsibility for the next stage. They invite eligible candidates to participate in counselling registration as per their own published schedules and admission rules. This step ensures that candidates are considered under the specific rules of each state or institution, including reservation policies, eligibility conditions, and seat availability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 6, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 04:28:35');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(286, 5, ' Eligibility Criteria/Quota of Seats/Reservation/Result Criteria/Counselling for admission to BAMS/BSMS/BUMS/BHMS Courses ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Admission to BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS Courses Through NEET (UG)\",\"name\":\"_admission_to_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_courses_through_neet_ug\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to undergraduate courses in traditional systems of medicine&mdash;Ayurveda (BAMS), Siddha (BSMS), Unani (BUMS), and Homoeopathy (BHMS)&mdash;is strictly regulated and centralized through the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) 2026. This means that no separate entrance exam is conducted for these courses, and every candidate must qualify NEET to secure a seat in any recognized college across India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Role of NEET (UG) 2026 in Admission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET (UG) 2026 acts as the single gateway for admission into all government, private, and deemed institutions offering these AYUSH courses. This centralized system ensures fairness, transparency, and uniform academic standards across the country.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Without qualifying NEET:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A candidate cannot participate in counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No admission is possible, even in private colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State-level or college-level admissions do not override NEET eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This makes NEET not just an entrance exam, but a legal requirement for entry into these courses.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Courses Covered Under NEET-Based Admission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The following undergraduate medical courses fall under this system:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BAMS (Bachelor of Ayurvedic Medicine and Surgery) &ndash; Focuses on Ayurveda, India&rsquo;s traditional holistic healing system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BSMS (Bachelor of Siddha Medicine and Surgery) &ndash; Based on Siddha, primarily practiced in South India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BUMS (Bachelor of Unani Medicine and Surgery) &ndash; Derived from Greco-Arabic medical traditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BHMS (Bachelor of Homoeopathic Medicine and Surgery) &ndash; Based on the principle of &ldquo;like cures like&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each course is governed by strict academic and professional standards to ensure quality education and patient safety.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Regulatory Authorities and Their Role<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admissions and academic standards for these courses are governed by two key national bodies:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Indian System of Medicine (NCISM)<br>Responsible for regulating Ayurveda, Siddha, and Unani education. It sets rules related to curriculum, infrastructure, faculty standards, and admission processes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Homoeopathy (NCH)<br>Oversees Homoeopathy education, ensuring uniform standards in BHMS programs across India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Both these bodies function under the Ministry of AYUSH, which is responsible for promoting and regulating traditional systems of medicine in India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why These Regulations Matter for Students<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the regulatory framework is important because it directly affects your admission and future career:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Uniform Standards Across India<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All colleges must follow the same minimum standards for teaching, infrastructure, and training. This ensures that your degree holds equal value regardless of the state or institution.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Protection from Invalid Admissions<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only colleges approved by NCISM or NCH can offer these courses. Taking admission outside this regulated system can result in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invalid degree<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ineligibility for practice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of time and money<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Centralized Merit-Based Selection<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since NEET is the only entrance test, admissions are purely merit-based. This reduces bias and increases competition, making preparation strategy extremely important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Insight: What Most Students Overlook<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students assume that AYUSH courses are easier to enter compared to MBBS, but this is a critical misconception.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cut-offs for top government AYUSH colleges are rising every year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Competition is increasing due to growing awareness and career scope<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Poor NEET preparation often leads to limited college options or high private fees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">So, even if your primary target is AYUSH, your NEET preparation must be serious and strategic, not casual.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Eligibility Criteria for Admission to BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS Courses\",\"name\":\"_eligibility_criteria_for_admission_to_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_courses\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding eligibility is one of the most critical steps before preparing for admission into AYUSH courses. Many students lose opportunities not because of low marks, but due to misunderstanding eligibility rules. Below is a complete, deeply explained breakdown to help you avoid such mistakes and plan confidently.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Academic Qualification Requirement (Class 12 Criteria)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To be eligible for admission into BAMS, BSMS, BUMS, or BHMS courses, a candidate must have completed 10+2 (or equivalent qualification) with the following core subjects:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Physics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chemistry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biology or Biotechnology<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These subjects are mandatory because they form the scientific foundation required for medical education.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarifications Most Students Miss<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biology is non-negotiable: Without Biology\\/Biotechnology, you are not eligible under any circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Equivalent qualification is accepted: Students from recognized boards (CBSE, ICSE, State Boards, or equivalent) are eligible.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NIOS (National Institute of Open Schooling) students are also eligible, provided they meet subject requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Students appearing for Class 12 in 2026 are also eligible, but admission will be confirmed only after passing the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">AYUSH courses are medical programs requiring a strong understanding of life sciences. If your foundation in PCB is weak, it directly impacts your performance in both NEET and the course itself.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory NEET (UG) Qualification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to all AYUSH undergraduate courses is strictly through NEET (UG) 2026. This is not just a formality&mdash;it is a legal and compulsory requirement.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Points to Understand<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must appear and qualify NEET to be considered for admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Simply passing Class 12 is not enough<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even private colleges cannot admit you without NEET qualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your NEET score determines your eligibility for counselling and seat allotment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students wrongly assume that AYUSH courses have relaxed entry requirements. In reality:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET cut-offs for top AYUSH colleges are increasing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A low NEET score limits your options to expensive private colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A good score gives you access to better colleges and lower fees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Age Requirement<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A candidate must meet the following age condition:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must have completed 17 years of age on or before 31st December 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Meaning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If you turn 17 anytime before 31 December 2026, you are eligible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If you are still 16 on that date, you cannot take admission that year, even if you qualify NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Rule Exists<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Medical education involves clinical exposure and patient interaction. The minimum age ensures a basic level of maturity and responsibility before entering professional training.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risks and Common Mistakes<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Ignoring Subject Requirements<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some students take PCB lightly or switch streams late. Without PCB, admission is impossible&mdash;no exceptions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Assuming NEET is Optional for Private Colleges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is a major myth. NEET is compulsory for all colleges, including private and deemed universities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Misjudging Age Eligibility<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students sometimes prepare for NEET without checking age criteria, leading to wasted attempts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Overlooking Qualification Proof<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">At counselling and admission, you must provide valid documents. Any mismatch or missing proof can lead to cancellation of your seat.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Guidance for Students<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Always verify your subject combination early (before Class 12)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Treat NEET preparation as your primary focus, not a backup<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep track of your date of birth eligibility carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain proper documentation (marksheets, certificates) to avoid last-minute issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Quota of Seats for Admission to BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS Courses\",\"name\":\"_quota_of_seats_for_admission_to_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_courses\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission to AYUSH courses is not done through a single uniform pool of seats. Instead, seats are divided into multiple quotas, each with its own eligibility rules, competition level, fee structure, and counselling authority. Understanding these quotas is extremely important because your strategy, chances of selection, and financial planning depend heavily on which quota you target.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Below is a deeply explained breakdown of each quota to help you make informed and strategic decisions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. All India Quota (AIQ) &ndash; Government Colleges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This quota consists of seats in government AYUSH colleges that are open to students from across the country, regardless of their state of domicile.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Typically includes 15% of seats in government colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open to candidates from any state in India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission is based on All India Rank (AIR) in NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling is conducted centrally (not by states)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Quota Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Offers high-quality education at very low fees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provides opportunity to study in top colleges outside your home state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Highly competitive due to nationwide participation&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If your NEET score is strong, this quota gives you maximum flexibility and best return on investment (low fees + good colleges).<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. All India Quota &ndash; Government Aided Colleges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Government-aided colleges are privately managed institutions that receive partial funding from the government.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A portion of their seats is available under All India Quota<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees are moderate (higher than government, lower than private)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open to candidates from all states<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Students Often Miss<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">These colleges can offer good infrastructure and faculty<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They are often overlooked, leading to less competition compared to pure government colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. All India Quota &ndash; Private Colleges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Private colleges also allocate a certain number of seats under All India Quota.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open to all India candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees are significantly higher<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission strictly through NEET rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students treat private AIQ as a backup, but:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees can be financially challenging<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Quality varies widely between colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always research the college&rsquo;s recognition, clinical exposure, and reputation before choosing this option.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. State Government Quota \\/ Institutional Quota<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is the largest pool of seats and is controlled by individual state authorities or institutions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Usually 85% of seats in government colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preference given to state domicile students<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling conducted by state authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each state has its own eligibility rules, including domicile requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some private colleges also have an institutional quota, giving preference to local or internal candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Crucial<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For many students, this quota offers the highest chance of admission, especially if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their NEET score is moderate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They have valid state domicile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Central Universities \\/ National Institutes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These are prestigious institutions run by the central government.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Limited number of seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission through All India basis<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Generally better infrastructure, faculty, and research opportunities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Highly preferred due to reputation and career value<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cut-offs are usually higher due to limited seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Deemed-to-be Universities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These are autonomous institutions with the authority to conduct their own admissions under NEET-based counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open to students from all over India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees are high and vary significantly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centralized counselling is usually conducted separately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What You Must Understand<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They offer more flexibility in seat availability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">However, cost can be a major limiting factor<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often rush into deemed universities due to lower cut-offs, but:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Total course cost can be very high<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Return on investment must be evaluated carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7. Self-Financed \\/ Management \\/ NRI Quota<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This quota exists mainly in private and deemed universities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Includes management quota and NRI quota seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees are highest among all quotas<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission still requires NEET qualification, but cut-offs are lower<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ground Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">These seats are often used as a last option by students with low NEET scores<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Financial burden can be extremely high<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choosing this quota without proper planning can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Long-term financial stress<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Limited return if college quality is not strong<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How Quotas Affect Your Admission Strategy<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding quotas is not just theoretical&mdash;it directly impacts your decisions:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">High NEET score &rarr; Target AIQ Government &amp; Central Institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Moderate score &rarr; Focus on State Quota &amp; Government-Aided Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lower score &rarr; Carefully evaluate Private\\/Deemed options (avoid impulsive decisions)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Reservation of Seats for BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS Courses \",\"name\":\"_reservation_of_seats_for_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_courses_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation plays a crucial role in medical admissions, especially in AYUSH courses. It is designed to ensure fair representation of different social and economic groups, but many students misunderstand how it actually works. A clear and deep understanding of reservation policies is essential because it directly affects your cut-off, rank advantage, and admission chances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains the reservation system in a structured and practical way, going beyond basic percentages to help you understand its real impact.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Under All India Quota (AIQ) &ndash; Central Government Policy<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For seats under All India Quota (AIQ) in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government-Aided Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">the reservation policy is determined by the Central Government and is applied uniformly across India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category-wise Reservation Distribution<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduled Caste (SC) &ndash; 15%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduled Tribe (ST) &ndash; 7.5%<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other Backward Classes &ndash; Non-Creamy Layer (OBC-NCL) &ndash; 27% (only in Central Universities &amp; National Institutes)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Economically Weaker Section (EWS) &ndash; 10% (only in Central Universities &amp; National Institutes)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Persons with Benchmark Disabilities (PwBD) &ndash; 5% (horizontal reservation across all categories)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding Vertical vs Horizontal Reservation (Critical Concept)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the most misunderstood areas, yet extremely important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Vertical Reservation (Category-Based)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OBC-NCL<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These categories have fixed percentage of seats reserved exclusively for them.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Horizontal Reservation (Across All Categories)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwBD (5%) falls under horizontal reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwBD seats are distributed within each category (General, SC, ST, OBC, EWS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It does not create separate seats, but overlaps existing categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often assume PwBD adds extra seats&mdash;it does not. It adjusts seats within categories, which can impact cut-offs and availability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Conditions for OBC-NCL and EWS Categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">OBC-NCL (Non-Creamy Layer)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicable only in Central Universities and National Institutes under AIQ<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Requires valid Non-Creamy Layer certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Creamy layer candidates are treated as General category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">EWS (Economically Weaker Section)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Also applicable only in Central Universities and National Institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Requires fulfilling income and asset criteria defined by the government<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must provide valid EWS certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Apply under OBC\\/EWS without valid certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Or submit incorrect\\/expired documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of reserved category benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Automatic shift to General category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of admission opportunity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation for PwBD (Persons with Benchmark Disabilities)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">5% reservation across all categories (horizontal)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicable only for candidates with specified benchmark disabilities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility is strictly defined under the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical fitness and disability type must match approved criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Certification must be from authorized medical boards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not all disabilities are eligible for medical courses. Some conditions may disqualify candidates from clinical practice, even if reservation exists.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation in State Quota Seats (85% Seats)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For State Quota seats, reservation is not controlled by the central government.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each state follows its own reservation policy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentages for SC, ST, OBC, EWS, etc., may vary from state to state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Example of Variation<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some states have higher OBC reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some include additional local categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some have different EWS implementation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Important<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your chances of admission can significantly improve or decrease depending on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your state of domicile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your category within that state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Disability Guidelines for AYUSH Courses<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission of candidates with disabilities is governed by strict medical and academic regulations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Points<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only &ldquo;specified disabilities&rdquo; are allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must meet functional ability requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guidelines differ slightly between:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ayurveda, Siddha, Unani courses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Homoeopathy (BHMS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even within PwBD:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some candidates may qualify for reservation but fail medical fitness tests later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This can result in seat cancellation after allotment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Make<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Assuming Reservation Guarantees Admission<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation improves chances but does not eliminate competition. You still need a qualifying NEET score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Ignoring Certificate Validity<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Incorrect format, expired certificates, or missing documents can lead to rejection of category benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Confusion Between Central and State Policies<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often assume the same reservation rules apply everywhere, which is incorrect.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Misunderstanding PwBD Reservation<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many think it adds extra seats, but it actually redistributes existing seats.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice for Students<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Always prepare for NEET aiming above minimum cut-off, even with reservation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify your category certificate format and validity early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Understand both AIQ and State quota reservation rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid relying completely on reservation&mdash;use it as an advantage, not a backup<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Percentage Criteria for Result Qualification & Ranking in BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS \",\"name\":\"_percentage_criteria_for_result_qualification__ranking_in_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"101\\\" data-end=\\\"459\\\">Qualifying NEET is not based on fixed marks&mdash;it is based on <strong data-start=\\\"160\\\" data-end=\\\"181\\\">percentile scores<\\/strong>, which makes the system dynamic and often confusing for students. For admission into AYUSH courses like BAMS, BSMS, BUMS, and BHMS, understanding this percentile-based eligibility is absolutely critical because it determines whether you can even <strong data-start=\\\"428\\\" data-end=\\\"458\\\">participate in counselling<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"461\\\" data-end=\\\"615\\\">This section explains the concept in a clear, detailed, and practical way so you can avoid common misunderstandings and plan your preparation effectively.<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"617\\\" data-end=\\\"620\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1lc5a17\\\" data-start=\\\"622\\\" data-end=\\\"662\\\">What Does &ldquo;Percentile&rdquo; Actually Mean?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"664\\\" data-end=\\\"738\\\">Before looking at the criteria, it is important to understand the concept:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"740\\\" data-end=\\\"838\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1gkxxjf\\\" data-start=\\\"740\\\" data-end=\\\"776\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"742\\\" data-end=\\\"774\\\">Percentile is not your marks<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"mdudt7\\\" data-start=\\\"777\\\" data-end=\\\"838\\\">It shows how you performed <strong data-start=\\\"806\\\" data-end=\\\"838\\\">relative to other candidates<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1r9ltvf\\\" data-start=\\\"840\\\" data-end=\\\"862\\\">Simple Explanation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"864\\\" data-end=\\\"1007\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"j8iz1d\\\" data-start=\\\"864\\\" data-end=\\\"935\\\">50th percentile means you performed <strong data-start=\\\"902\\\" data-end=\\\"935\\\">better than 50% of candidates<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"9r79gh\\\" data-start=\\\"936\\\" data-end=\\\"1007\\\">40th percentile means you performed <strong data-start=\\\"974\\\" data-end=\\\"1007\\\">better than 40% of candidates<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"181lajy\\\" data-start=\\\"1009\\\" data-end=\\\"1029\\\">Why This Matters<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1031\\\" data-end=\\\"1257\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"k18w0b\\\" data-start=\\\"1031\\\" data-end=\\\"1111\\\">Cut-offs <strong data-start=\\\"1042\\\" data-end=\\\"1063\\\">change every year<\\/strong> depending on difficulty level and competition<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"aejxcl\\\" data-start=\\\"1112\\\" data-end=\\\"1192\\\">You cannot predict qualification using fixed marks (like &ldquo;I need 300 marks&rdquo;)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ssmsyd\\\" data-start=\\\"1193\\\" data-end=\\\"1257\\\">A score that qualified last year may <strong data-start=\\\"1232\\\" data-end=\\\"1257\\\">not qualify this year<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"1259\\\" data-end=\\\"1262\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"hssd2a\\\" data-start=\\\"1264\\\" data-end=\\\"1312\\\">Minimum Percentile Required for AYUSH Courses<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1314\\\" data-end=\\\"1458\\\">To be eligible for admission into BAMS, BSMS, BUMS, and BHMS courses, candidates must achieve the following minimum percentiles in NEET UG 2026:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1fdmtja\\\" data-start=\\\"1460\\\" data-end=\\\"1485\\\">General Category (UR)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1487\\\" data-end=\\\"1508\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1d7ajii\\\" data-start=\\\"1487\\\" data-end=\\\"1508\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"1489\\\" data-end=\\\"1508\\\">50th Percentile<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1510\\\" data-end=\\\"1588\\\">This is the standard eligibility threshold for candidates without reservation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"1590\\\" data-end=\\\"1593\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"6sqpsc\\\" data-start=\\\"1595\\\" data-end=\\\"1634\\\">SC \\/ ST \\/ OBC (Reserved Categories)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1636\\\" data-end=\\\"1657\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1i4wqx7\\\" data-start=\\\"1636\\\" data-end=\\\"1657\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"1638\\\" data-end=\\\"1657\\\">40th Percentile<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1659\\\" data-end=\\\"1750\\\">This relaxation is provided to ensure fair representation of socially disadvantaged groups.<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"1752\\\" data-end=\\\"1755\\\">\\r\\n<h3>Persons with Benchmark Disabilities (PwBD)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1805\\\" data-end=\\\"1854\\\">This category has a slightly different structure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1856\\\" data-end=\\\"1946\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1j3xav8\\\" data-start=\\\"1856\\\" data-end=\\\"1905\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"1858\\\" data-end=\\\"1885\\\">General-PwBD \\/ EWS-PwBD<\\/strong> &rarr; 45th Percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"7534uk\\\" data-start=\\\"1906\\\" data-end=\\\"1946\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"1908\\\" data-end=\\\"1926\\\">SC\\/ST\\/OBC-PwBD<\\/strong> &rarr; 40th Percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"1948\\\" data-end=\\\"1951\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"4ihfz8\\\" data-start=\\\"1953\\\" data-end=\\\"2000\\\">Critical Insight: Percentile vs Actual Marks<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2002\\\" data-end=\\\"2079\\\">One of the biggest mistakes students make is confusing percentile with marks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"iaed40\\\" data-start=\\\"2081\\\" data-end=\\\"2101\\\">Example Scenario<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2103\\\" data-end=\\\"2221\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"o6b412\\\" data-start=\\\"2103\\\" data-end=\\\"2164\\\">In one year, 50th percentile may correspond to ~140 marks<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"zcdnzm\\\" data-start=\\\"2165\\\" data-end=\\\"2221\\\">In another year, it may drop to ~120 or rise to ~160<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2223\\\" data-end=\\\"2254\\\">This variation happens because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2255\\\" data-end=\\\"2353\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8koq33\\\" data-start=\\\"2255\\\" data-end=\\\"2289\\\">Difficulty of the exam changes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1qh6pgx\\\" data-start=\\\"2290\\\" data-end=\\\"2322\\\">Number of candidates changes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"d8djg\\\" data-start=\\\"2323\\\" data-end=\\\"2353\\\">Overall performance shifts<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>Key Takeaway<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2373\\\" data-end=\\\"2456\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"2373\\\" data-end=\\\"2446\\\">Your target should always be a high score&mdash;not just minimum percentile<\\/strong>, because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2457\\\" data-end=\\\"2540\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1fw0ume\\\" data-start=\\\"2457\\\" data-end=\\\"2505\\\">Minimum percentile only makes you <em data-start=\\\"2493\\\" data-end=\\\"2503\\\">eligible<\\/em><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dgbyx1\\\" data-start=\\\"2506\\\" data-end=\\\"2540\\\">It does <strong data-start=\\\"2516\\\" data-end=\\\"2540\\\">not guarantee a seat<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"2542\\\" data-end=\\\"2545\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"hm5itf\\\" data-start=\\\"2547\\\" data-end=\\\"2597\\\">Eligibility vs Admission: A Critical Difference<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2599\\\" data-end=\\\"2644\\\">Many students misunderstand this distinction:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"1pb57zj\\\" data-start=\\\"2646\\\" data-end=\\\"2679\\\">Eligibility (Qualifying NEET)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2681\\\" data-end=\\\"2754\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jfzuoa\\\" data-start=\\\"2681\\\" data-end=\\\"2714\\\">Achieving required percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"r0kgil\\\" data-start=\\\"2715\\\" data-end=\\\"2754\\\">Allows participation in counselling<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"1yhfnce\\\" data-start=\\\"2756\\\" data-end=\\\"2786\\\">Admission (Getting a Seat)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2788\\\" data-end=\\\"2907\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ovuhbf\\\" data-start=\\\"2788\\\" data-end=\\\"2907\\\">Depends on:\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2804\\\" data-end=\\\"2907\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1lim5wk\\\" data-start=\\\"2804\\\" data-end=\\\"2817\\\">NEET rank<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ydyvmy\\\" data-start=\\\"2820\\\" data-end=\\\"2844\\\">Cut-offs of colleges<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"302y2e\\\" data-start=\\\"2847\\\" data-end=\\\"2868\\\">Quota (AIQ\\/State)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1e0942g\\\" data-start=\\\"2871\\\" data-end=\\\"2883\\\">Category<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"17iivu\\\" data-start=\\\"2886\\\" data-end=\\\"2907\\\">Seat availability<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"1dsm4eq\\\" data-start=\\\"2909\\\" data-end=\\\"2927\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2929\\\" data-end=\\\"2979\\\">Thousands of students qualify NEET every year but:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2980\\\" data-end=\\\"3053\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"111n4jm\\\" data-start=\\\"2980\\\" data-end=\\\"3003\\\">Do <strong data-start=\\\"2985\\\" data-end=\\\"3003\\\">not get a seat<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"167g1jj\\\" data-start=\\\"3004\\\" data-end=\\\"3053\\\">Or get only <strong data-start=\\\"3018\\\" data-end=\\\"3053\\\">low-preference\\/private colleges<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"3055\\\" data-end=\\\"3058\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"tjmmte\\\" data-start=\\\"3060\\\" data-end=\\\"3094\\\">Impact of Percentile on Ranking<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3096\\\" data-end=\\\"3157\\\">Percentile directly influences your <strong data-start=\\\"3132\\\" data-end=\\\"3156\\\">All India Rank (AIR)<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3159\\\" data-end=\\\"3257\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"27pd26\\\" data-start=\\\"3159\\\" data-end=\\\"3194\\\">Higher percentile &rarr; Better rank<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"pqxd0o\\\" data-start=\\\"3195\\\" data-end=\\\"3257\\\">Better rank &rarr; Higher chances of admission in good colleges<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"tvpyju\\\" data-start=\\\"3259\\\" data-end=\\\"3286\\\">Strategic Understanding<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3288\\\" data-end=\\\"3318\\\">Even within the same category:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3319\\\" data-end=\\\"3484\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1l7jsdl\\\" data-start=\\\"3319\\\" data-end=\\\"3404\\\">A student at 90th percentile has a <strong data-start=\\\"3356\\\" data-end=\\\"3374\\\">huge advantage<\\/strong> over one at 50th percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1v2zuvm\\\" data-start=\\\"3405\\\" data-end=\\\"3484\\\">Both are &ldquo;qualified,&rdquo; but their admission outcomes are completely different<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"3486\\\" data-end=\\\"3489\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1l2cwzh\\\" data-start=\\\"3491\\\" data-end=\\\"3536\\\">Special Considerations for PwBD Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3538\\\" data-end=\\\"3583\\\">Candidates under the PwBD category must meet:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3585\\\" data-end=\\\"3696\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1xh4uks\\\" data-start=\\\"3585\\\" data-end=\\\"3643\\\">Required percentile (45% or 40% depending on category)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"2ais74\\\" data-start=\\\"3644\\\" data-end=\\\"3696\\\">Medical eligibility as per disability guidelines<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"lgxe1v\\\" data-start=\\\"3698\\\" data-end=\\\"3716\\\">Important Risk<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3718\\\" data-end=\\\"3753\\\">Even if percentile criteria is met:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3754\\\" data-end=\\\"3894\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"20txt\\\" data-start=\\\"3754\\\" data-end=\\\"3829\\\">A candidate may still be <strong data-start=\\\"3781\\\" data-end=\\\"3829\\\">declared medically unfit for certain courses<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"182jn8k\\\" data-start=\\\"3830\\\" data-end=\\\"3894\\\">This can result in <strong data-start=\\\"3851\\\" data-end=\\\"3894\\\">loss of admission despite qualification<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"3896\\\" data-end=\\\"3899\\\">\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1xvt1dz\\\" data-start=\\\"3901\\\" data-end=\\\"3939\\\">Common Mistakes Students Must Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"18zuv69\\\" data-start=\\\"3941\\\" data-end=\\\"3983\\\">1. Targeting Only Minimum Percentile<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3984\\\" data-end=\\\"4069\\\">This is the biggest strategic error. Minimum qualification does not ensure admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"zar2wx\\\" data-start=\\\"4071\\\" data-end=\\\"4110\\\">2. Relying on Previous Year Marks<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4111\\\" data-end=\\\"4173\\\">Cut-offs vary every year&mdash;blindly following past data is risky.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"pijnk\\\" data-start=\\\"4175\\\" data-end=\\\"4220\\\">3. Ignoring Category Advantage Planning<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4221\\\" data-end=\\\"4300\\\">Students often fail to understand how their category impacts realistic targets.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"yrq9gq\\\" data-start=\\\"4302\\\" data-end=\\\"4343\\\">4. Assuming Qualification = Success<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4344\\\" data-end=\\\"4407\\\">Qualifying NEET is just the <strong data-start=\\\"4372\\\" data-end=\\\"4386\\\">first step<\\/strong>, not the final goal.<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"4409\\\" data-end=\\\"4412\\\">\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"avs1fx\\\" data-start=\\\"4414\\\" data-end=\\\"4445\\\">Smart Strategy for Aspirants<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4447\\\" data-end=\\\"4710\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"41zohw\\\" data-start=\\\"4447\\\" data-end=\\\"4520\\\">Aim for a score that places you <strong data-start=\\\"4481\\\" data-end=\\\"4518\\\">well above the minimum percentile<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tokqz6\\\" data-start=\\\"4521\\\" data-end=\\\"4590\\\">Track <strong data-start=\\\"4529\\\" data-end=\\\"4588\\\">expected cut-offs for your category and target colleges<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"180yw2z\\\" data-start=\\\"4591\\\" data-end=\\\"4648\\\">Focus on <strong data-start=\\\"4602\\\" data-end=\\\"4622\\\">rank improvement<\\/strong>, not just qualification<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bu0zrw\\\" data-start=\\\"4649\\\" data-end=\\\"4710\\\">Always have <strong data-start=\\\"4663\\\" data-end=\\\"4708\\\">backup options across quotas and colleges<\\/strong><\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Counselling Provisions for Admission to BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS Courses\",\"name\":\"_counselling_provisions_for_admission_to_bams_bsms_bums__bhms_courses\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Counselling is the most decisive stage in the entire admission process for AYUSH courses. Even with a good NEET score, a lack of clarity about counselling rules can lead to poor seat choices, missed opportunities, or even disqualification. This section explains the complete counselling framework for All India Quota (AIQ) seats in a detailed and practical manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preparation of All India Merit List: The Foundation of Counselling<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The entire counselling process begins with the preparation of an All India Merit List, which is based purely on your All India Rank (AIR) in NEET UG 2026.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How It Works<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only candidates who qualify NEET are included<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ranking is determined strictly by NEET performance (percentile + marks)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admissions to all AIQ seats in AYUSH courses are done only from this merit list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Critical<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your AIR directly determines your position in counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A better rank gives you:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Higher priority in seat selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Better college options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Greater control over choices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">There is no separate entrance or ranking system for AYUSH&mdash;everything depends on NEET. This makes your NEET preparation the single most important factor in the entire admission journey.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Counselling Authorities: Who Conducts the Process?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Different authorities handle counselling depending on the type of institution. Understanding this avoids confusion and helps you apply in the correct place.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. All India Quota Counselling Authority<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducted by Ayush Admissions Central Counselling Committee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Responsible for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government-Aided Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deemed Universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Private College AIQ Counselling<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducted by an authority designated by the Central Government<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Process may differ slightly depending on institutional structure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. State Quota Counselling<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducted by respective State Government counselling authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applies to 85% state quota seats and varies by state rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step-by-Step Understanding of the Counselling Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Although the process may look simple, each step has strategic importance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Registration<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must register on the official counselling portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provide NEET details, personal information, and preferences<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Choice Filling and Locking<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Select preferred:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Courses (BAMS, BHMS, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Locations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3: Seat Allotment<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preferences filled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat availability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 4: Reporting to Allotted Institute<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee payment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final admission confirmation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Rule: No Change in Category During Counselling<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the most important and often ignored rules:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The details filled in your NEET application form (such as category, phone number, email) are considered final for AIQ counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You cannot change your category later, even if you have valid documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any mistake during NEET registration can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Remove your reservation benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Affect your admission chances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fill incorrect category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forget to update certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assume correction will be allowed later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This can lead to permanent loss of category advantage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of NTA in Counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The National Testing Agency (NTA):<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducts NEET examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepares and declares results<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NTA has no role in counselling or admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any issue related to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">College selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">must be addressed to the counselling authority, not NTA<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Authorities for Counselling Support<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you face issues or need clarification, the following bodies are responsible:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. National Commission for Indian System of Medicine<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Handles academic and regulatory issues for Ayurveda, Siddha, Unani<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Ayush Admissions Central Counselling Committee<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Main authority for AIQ counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Handles seat allotment, registration, and process-related queries<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. State AYUSH Counselling Authorities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Handle state quota admissions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rules and procedures vary by state<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Insights Most Students Miss<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Rank Is Only Half the Game<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students focus only on NEET score, but:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Poor choice filling can waste a good rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smart preference order can secure better colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Counselling Is Multi-Round<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multiple rounds are conducted (Round 1, Round 2, Mop-Up, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not getting a seat in early rounds does not mean failure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Backup Planning Is Essential<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Always include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Safe options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Moderate options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dream colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Document Readiness Is Crucial<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Missing or incorrect documents can result in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of allotted seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification from further rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes That Cost Students Seats<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Filling limited or unrealistic choices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring state counselling alongside AIQ<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not locking choices properly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missing deadlines for reporting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming counselling is automatic after NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ayush Admissions Central Counselling Committee (Primary Counselling Authority)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is the main authority for All India Quota (AIQ) counselling for BAMS, BSMS, BUMS, and BHMS courses.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email: counseling-ayush@gov.in<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official Website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/aaccc.gov.in\\/aacccug\\/home\\/homepage\\\"> https:\\/\\/aaccc.gov.in\\/aacccug\\/home\\/homepage<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When to Contact AACCC<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration and choice filling issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment queries<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling schedule and rounds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AIQ admission-related problems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. National Commission for Indian System of Medicine (Regulatory Support)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Handles academic and administrative issues related to Ayurveda, Siddha, and Unani courses.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email: helpdesk@ncismindia.org<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/aaccc.gov.in\\/aacccug\\/home\\/homepage\\\"> https:\\/\\/aaccc.gov.in\\/aacccug\\/home\\/homepage<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When to Contact NCISM<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Course regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility-related clarifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional or academic issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Important Information for the Application Process (BAMS, BSMS, BUMS & BHMS \\u2013 NEET UG \",\"name\":\"_important_information_for_the_application_process_bams_bsms_bums__bhms__neet_ug_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application process for AYUSH courses is not limited to just filling a NEET form. It is a multi-layered system governed by multiple authorities, rules, and official documents. Many students focus only on basic steps and ignore deeper instructions&mdash;this often leads to mistakes that can affect eligibility, counselling, or even final admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains every important aspect of the application process in a detailed, practical, and student-focused manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the Scope of the Application Process<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The application process includes much more than just NEET registration. It involves:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Filling the NEET application form correctly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Understanding eligibility and reservation rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Following counselling procedures<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Complying with official guidelines issued by authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your admission depends not only on your marks but also on how accurately you follow official instructions across all stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Importance of Referring to Complete Information Sources<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are advised to carefully review all relevant sections, chapters, and appendices provided in official guidelines.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means Practically<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You should not rely on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Partial information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Social media updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assumptions based on previous years<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Instead, you must understand:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling procedures<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Documentation requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students who skip detailed instructions often:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fill incorrect details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Miss important steps<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Become ineligible during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Authorities Governing the Application and Admission Process<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Multiple national bodies are involved in regulating AYUSH admissions. Each has a specific role, and understanding them helps you know where to refer in case of confusion.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Ministry of AYUSH<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is the central government body responsible for overall policy-making and governance of traditional medical systems.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role in Application Process<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issues major policies and notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Defines broad admission frameworks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Oversees all AYUSH-related institutions and systems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why It Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any major change in rules (like reservation, counselling structure, or eligibility) originates from this ministry.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Ayush Admissions Central Counselling Committee<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is the primary authority for AIQ counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role in Application Process<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducts All India Quota counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Releases counselling schedules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Handles seat allotment and registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After NEET, your interaction shifts mainly to AACCC for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choice filling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. National Commission for Indian System of Medicine<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Regulates education for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ayurveda (BAMS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Siddha (BSMS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Unani (BUMS)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role in Application Process<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sets academic standards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Defines eligibility and course structure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issues regulations for institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Students Must Care<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a college is not approved by NCISM:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your degree may become invalid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You may not be allowed to practice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. National Commission for Homoeopathy<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Responsible for regulating BHMS (Homoeopathy) education.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sets curriculum and academic standards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Approves colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Defines admission-related guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Central Council of Indian Medicine (Legacy Reference)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This was the earlier regulatory body for Ayurveda, Siddha, and Unani before NCISM.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why It Is Still Mentioned<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Older regulations and notifications may still be referenced<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some guidelines are historically linked to CCIM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Central Council of Homoeopathy (Legacy Reference)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Earlier governing body for Homoeopathy before NCH.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Some previous rules and standards still trace back to this body<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Multiple Guidelines and Documents Are Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not all rules are available in a single place. Instead, they are spread across:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Circulars<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What You Must Do<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a rule is not clearly mentioned in one section:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Refer to official notifications issued by authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check updated circulars and guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Example Situations<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You may need to refer external guidelines for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disability eligibility rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation certificate formats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling procedures<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institutional eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight: &ldquo;What Is Not Written Here Still Applies&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the most important points students overlook:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if a rule is not mentioned in a specific section, it still applies if issued by the relevant authority.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Real Impact<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You cannot claim ignorance of rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authorities follow latest official notifications, not just one document<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Makes<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Depending on Incomplete Information<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often read only summaries and miss detailed rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Ignoring Official Updates<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Rules may change through circulars&mdash;ignoring them can lead to mistakes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Confusing Authorities<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not knowing which body controls what leads to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong queries<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delayed problem resolution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Not Verifying College Recognition<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Admission into unapproved colleges can destroy your career path.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for a Safe Application Process<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Always cross-check information from official authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow updates from counselling bodies regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep all documents ready in correct format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Understand both NEET and counselling rules together<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Never assume&mdash;always verify<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 7, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 05:02:50');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(287, 5, ' ADMIT CARD', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"admit card \",\"name\":\"admit_card_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card is one of the most important documents in the NEET examination process. However, many students misunderstand its role and importance. It is not just an entry pass&mdash;it is a provisional authorization document, which means your eligibility is still subject to verification at later stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains every rule, instruction, and hidden implication related to the admit card in a clear, detailed, and student-focused manner.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Provisional Nature of the Admit Card (Most Important Concept)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card is issued provisionally, which means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It allows you to appear in the examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">But it does not confirm your final eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means Practically<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if you:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Successfully download the admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appear for the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your eligibility can still be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verified later during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejected if you do not meet required criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students assume:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&ldquo;I got the admit card, so I am fully eligible&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is incorrect. If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your documents are invalid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You don&rsquo;t meet eligibility conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your admission can be cancelled later, even after qualifying NEET.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Download the Admit Card<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must download their admit card from the official website of<br>National Testing Agency:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card will be available online only<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No physical copy will be sent by post<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must print it and carry it to the exam centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download it early to avoid last-minute technical issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Take multiple printouts as backup<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Centre, Date, and Timing &ndash; Strict Compliance Required<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card clearly specifies:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam centre location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entry closing time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You must appear:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only at the assigned centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Only on the given date and time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Warning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You cannot request a change in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Timing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Late entry or wrong centre = No entry allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What to Do If You Cannot Download the Admit Card<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you face issues while downloading:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Contact the NTA helpline between 10:00 AM to 5:00 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Or email: neetug2026@nta.ac.in<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Immediate Action Is Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Delays can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prevent you from appearing in the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leave no time for resolution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Instructions to Be Followed During Examination<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must carefully read:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Instructions given in the official guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Instructions printed on the admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to follow instructions may lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Denial of entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Examples of Critical Instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reporting time compliance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Allowed\\/prohibited items<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dress code rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Handling Discrepancies in Admit Card<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you notice any error in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You must immediately contact NTA helpline.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are still allowed to appear in the exam with the existing admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Corrections will be made later in official records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ignoring discrepancies can cause:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Issues during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document mismatch problems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission delays or rejection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rules and Restrictions (Must Follow Strictly)<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. No Admit Card by Post<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card will only be available online<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No offline delivery under any circumstances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. No Duplicate Admit Card at Exam Centre<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If you forget or lose it, you will not get another copy at the centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">This can result in denial of entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Do Not Damage or Alter the Admit Card<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tear<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Write on it<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Modify any details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Tampered admit cards may be treated as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invalid documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Suspected malpractice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Preserve Admit Card After Exam<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You must keep the admit card safe even after the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why It Is Needed Later<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission formalities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Admit Card Will Not Be Issued in Certain Cases<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You will not receive an admit card if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application form is incomplete<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph is unclear or doubtful<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signature is missing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility criteria is not fulfilled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students lose their attempt due to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Careless form filling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading incorrect images<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Verification of Eligibility Happens Later<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even after:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Receiving admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appearing in exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Qualifying NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your eligibility will still be verified during counselling and admission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is Checked Later<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Educational qualifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity proof<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Warning<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If any mismatch or false information is found:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your candidature can be cancelled at any stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Must Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Downloading admit card at the last moment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not checking details carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring discrepancies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgetting to carry admit card to centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming admit card = confirmed eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Students<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download and print multiple copies early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify all details immediately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep it safe in good condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read all instructions thoroughly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepare all documents in advance for future stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 8, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 05:16:42'),
(288, 5, '  Barred Items and Dress Code for NEET UG', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Barred Items (What You Cannot Carry Inside the Exam Centre)\",\"name\":\"_barred_items_what_you_cannot_carry_inside_the_exam_centre\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before entering the exam centre, every candidate undergoes compulsory and extensive frisking using highly sensitive metal detectors. The purpose is to ensure that no candidate carries any item that could be used for cheating or unfair practices.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you are found carrying any prohibited item, you may be denied entry or disqualified, regardless of your preparation level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category-Wise List of Prohibited Items<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Study Materials and Writing Tools<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You are not allowed to carry:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Printed or handwritten notes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bits of paper<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Geometry box \\/ pencil box<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Plastic pouch<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing pad<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Calculator, log tables<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eraser, scale, pen drives<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electronic pen or scanner<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Rule Exists<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even small items like paper bits can be used for cheating. Therefore, zero tolerance policy is followed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Electronic and Communication Devices<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strictly prohibited:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile phones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bluetooth devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Earphones \\/ microphones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smart bands \\/ health bands<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pager or any wireless device<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if the device is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Switched off<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not being used<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It is still not allowed and can lead to disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Personal Accessories<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not allowed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wallets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Handbags<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Goggles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Caps<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Belts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often forget items like wallets or belts and are forced to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leave them outside (at their own risk)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Or face entry denial<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Watches and Recording Devices<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strictly banned:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wristwatches<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bracelets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cameras<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Watches Are Banned<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even simple watches can be modified into smart devices, so all types are prohibited.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Jewellery and Metallic Items<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chains<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Earrings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any metallic ornaments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even small jewellery items can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Trigger metal detectors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delay entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lead to additional checking or inconvenience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Food Items and Water Bottles<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No packaged or unpackaged food allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No personal water bottles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Tip<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eat before entering the centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow centre-specific instructions if any arrangement is provided<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7. Suspicious or Concealable Devices<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any item that can hide:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Microchips<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cameras<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bluetooth devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Understanding<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if the item looks harmless, if it can potentially hide a device, it will be confiscated or banned.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No Storage Facility at Exam Centres<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam centres do not provide any facility to store your belongings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Real Consequence<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If you bring restricted items, you may have to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leave them outside (risk of loss)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Or miss your exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Case: Religious or Cultural Items<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates wearing items of faith (religious\\/cultural) are allowed, but with conditions:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must report at least 2 hours before reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Will undergo detailed frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Condition<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If any suspicious device is found:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You may be asked to remove the item<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Or not allowed to enter with it<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Dress Code &ndash; What You Should Wear<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The dress code is designed to simplify frisking and prevent concealment of devices.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" General Dress Code Rules\",\"name\":\"_general_dress_code_rules\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Avoid Heavy Clothes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No thick or layered clothing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Long sleeves are discouraged<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Rule Exists<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Heavy clothes can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hide devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Slow down frisking process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Cultural or Customary Dress<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Allowed, but:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must report at least 1 hour before reporting time (12:30 PM)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional frisking will be conducted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Footwear Guidelines<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preferred:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Slippers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sandals with low heels<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Avoid:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shoes with thick soles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Covered footwear<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Special Cases (Medical or Other Reasons)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you need to wear something unusual due to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any unavoidable reason<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You must take prior approval from<br>National Testing Agency before admit card issuance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Compliance with Instructions<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must strictly follow all instructions issued by NTA.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict compliance helps:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smooth entry process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid delays or rejection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain fairness in examination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Security and Verification Process at Exam Centre<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before entering the exam hall, candidates will undergo:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Metal detector frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Face authentication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Videography<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your identity and belongings are thoroughly checked<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any mismatch or suspicious activity can lead to immediate action<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Provisions for Female Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NTA ensures respectful and sensitive checking:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Frisking is done inside a closed enclosure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducted only by female staff<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintains privacy and dignity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensures comfort while following strict security rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Must Avoid<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying mobile phone &ldquo;just in case&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wearing jeans with metal accessories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgetting to remove jewellery<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bringing bags or wallets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring dress code and arriving late<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Exam Day<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carry only:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Required documents (as per instructions)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wear:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Light clothes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Simple slippers\\/sandals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reach early to handle:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 9, 1, '2026-04-14 01:29:11', '2026-04-14 05:58:18');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(339, 5, ' Important Information for Parents/Guardians – NEET (UG) ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"INSTRUCTIONS \",\"name\":\"instructions_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The role of parents and guardians in NEET is far more important than most people realize. At this stage, even small mistakes&mdash;like reaching late, carrying a prohibited item, or missing an instruction&mdash;can result in denial of entry or disqualification, regardless of the student&rsquo;s preparation level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains every instruction in detail so that parents can actively guide their ward and ensure a smooth, stress-free, and rule-compliant exam experience.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Entry Timing and Travel Planning &ndash; The Most Critical Responsibility<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the strictest rules in NEET is the entry closing time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No candidate will be allowed to enter the examination centre after 01:30 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Parents Must Ensure<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The candidate leaves home well in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel planning must consider:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Traffic conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Distance to exam centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Weather conditions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Possible delays<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A highly recommended strategy is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the exam centre one day before the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exact location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Route options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students miss their exam not because of lack of preparation, but due to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Traffic delays<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong location tracking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Last-minute panic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Discipline and Rule Compliance Inside the Exam Hall<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parents must clearly guide their ward to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow all instructions given by invigilators<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain discipline throughout the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid any behavior that may be considered suspicious<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even minor rule violations can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lead to warnings<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Escalate to disqualification in serious cases<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Prohibition of Unfair Means<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students must be strictly instructed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not to use any unfair means<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not to assist others in cheating<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not to carry any suspicious item<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Responsibility<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If the candidate observes any unfair activity:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It must be immediately reported to the invigilator<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to report or involvement in such activities can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lead to disqualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attract strict penalties<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Documents to Carry (Very Important)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parents must ensure the candidate carries only the required documents&mdash;nothing extra, nothing missing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Required Documents<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit Card with passport-size photograph affixed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One additional passport-size photograph (for attendance sheet)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One postcard-size (4&rdquo;&times;6&rdquo;) color photograph with white background (pasted on proforma)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid original ID proof (Aadhaar, PAN, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwBD certificate (if applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistake<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students often:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forget photographs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bring incorrect photo size<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carry photocopies instead of original ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This can create serious issues during verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Prohibition of Barred Items<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must not carry any prohibited items such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile phones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electronic devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bags, wallets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Notes or papers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parent&rsquo;s Responsibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Double-check before the candidate leaves home<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure only essential documents are carried<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Critical<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No storage facility is provided at centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying such items may lead to denial of entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Cooperation During Frisking and Security Checks<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cooperate fully with staff during frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow instructions without resistance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Happens at Centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Metal detector checks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Physical frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Non-cooperation can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delay entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Raise suspicion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lead to complications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reporting Time and Early Arrival<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reach the centre well before reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Be available for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seating process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Case: Customary Dress<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If wearing cultural\\/religious attire:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Must report by 12:30 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional time is required for checking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Dress Code Compliance<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parents must ensure that the candidate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follows NEET dress code strictly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoids:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Heavy clothes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Full sleeves<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Metallic accessories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Improper dress can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Delay frisking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Create complications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Risk entry denial in extreme cases<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Staying Updated with Official Information<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must regularly check updates from<br>National Testing Agency<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Platforms to Monitor<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registered email<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SMS alerts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parent&rsquo;s Role<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure the student does not miss any important update<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cross-check important announcements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Parent\\/Guardian Contact Details in Application<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">While filling the NEET application form:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Parent\\/guardian mobile number and email ID must be provided<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirmation page is sent to parents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final scorecard is also shared<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Benefit<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Parents can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Track progress<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay informed about important updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Consequences of Rule Violation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate breaches any rule:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Immediate Consequences<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Denied entry into exam centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not allowed to appear in exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Serious Violations<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If involved in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Unfair practices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disruptive behavior<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Then:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate can be debarred from NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">May face legal\\/criminal action<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Checklist for Parents (Practical Guidance)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before the exam day, ensure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All required documents are ready<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No barred items are carried<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel plan is finalized<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dress code is followed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam centre location is confirmed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 10, 1, '2026-04-14 01:44:26', '2026-04-14 06:06:24'),
(340, 5, '  Instructions to Be Followed in the Examination Hall – NEET (UG)  ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"INSTRUCTIONS\",\"name\":\"instructions\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The examination hall rules in NEET are extremely strict and structured. These instructions are not just formalities&mdash;they are legally enforceable conditions. Even a small mistake (like sitting in the wrong seat or leaving early) can result in cancellation of candidature, regardless of your preparation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section provides a complete, deeply explained understanding of every instruction so you can avoid risks and perform confidently.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Entry Timing, Reporting &amp; Exam Schedule<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the timeline is critical because timing violations are one of the most common reasons for disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Complete Exam Day Schedule<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"326\\\"><col width=\\\"158\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Event<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reporting\\/Entry Starts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">11:00 AM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Last Entry Allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">01:30 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Instruction Announcement &amp; Admit Card Check<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">01:30 PM &ndash; 01:45 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Test Booklet Distribution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">01:45 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Filling Details on Booklet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">01:50 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Start Time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">02:00 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam End Time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">05:00 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Duration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3 Hours<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The exam centre opens 3 hours before the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No entry is allowed after 01:30 PM under any condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must sit immediately after the hall opens<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Case<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligible PwBD candidates may get extended time (till 06:00 PM, depending on provisions)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Entry into Examination Hall &ndash; Strict Condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Admit Card Verification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must present their admit card when demanded.<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Without a valid admit card &rarr; No entry allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verification is done by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centre Superintendent<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invigilators during the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card is checked multiple times, not just at entry. Any mismatch may lead to serious consequences.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Seating Arrangement &ndash; Zero Tolerance Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each candidate is assigned:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A specific seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A roll number-based location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must sit only in your allotted seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sitting in another seat or room leads to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediate cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even accidental mistakes (wrong room\\/seat) are treated seriously.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Documents Required Inside the Examination Hall<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must bring only the following documents. Missing any one of these can lead to denial of entry.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Documents Checklist<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Printed Admit Card with passport-size photograph affixed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One additional passport-size photograph (for attendance sheet)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One postcard-size (4&rdquo;&times;6&rdquo;) color photograph (for proforma)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Original valid photo ID (Aadhaar, PAN, Passport, Voter ID, Driving License, DigiLocker, APAAR ID)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwBD certificate (if applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying photocopies instead of original ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgetting photographs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bringing wrong-size photos<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Prohibition of Barred Items<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are not allowed to carry any prohibited items.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Legal Consequence<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Possession of such items can lead to penalties under:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Public Examinations (Prevention of Unfair Means) Act, 2024<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No storage facility is provided<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bringing such items may result in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Denial of entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Conduct During the Examination<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. No Leaving the Exam Hall Early<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must remain seated until the exam ends<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leaving early is strictly prohibited<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Submission of OMR Sheet<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must hand over your OMR sheet to the invigilator<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leaving without submission can invalidate your attempt<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Prohibited Activities Inside the Centre<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smoking is strictly prohibited<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying food, beverages, or snacks is not allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Special Relaxation for Diabetic Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates with diabetes are allowed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sugar tablets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fruits (banana, apple, orange)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Transparent water bottle<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Condition<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prior intimation is required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Packaged foods (chocolate, sandwich, etc.) are not allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Examination Start, Signals &amp; Instructions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before Exam Begins<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invigilators will:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Announce important instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify admit cards<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">During Exam<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signals will be given for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Start of exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Half-time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final warning before en<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Start and stop writing exactly as instructed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Attendance &amp; Identity Verification Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must complete<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Actions<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sign attendance sheet twice:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">At the start<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">At the end (while submitting OMR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provide:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Thumb impression<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This ensures:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prevention of impersonation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Test Booklet Verification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before starting the exam:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check total number of pages in the test booklet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure it matches what is mentioned on the cover<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If pages are missing and not reported:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You may lose marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No correction will be entertained later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No Retest Policy (Very Important)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate misses the exam due to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Illness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Travel issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any personal reason<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No re-exam will be conducted under any circumstances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Videography &amp; Surveillance During Exam<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The entire exam process is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Videographed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Monitored for identity verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidate Responsibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep head upright<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Face the camera when required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Agree to videography<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cooperate fully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Invigilator&rsquo;s Role During Exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Invigilators will:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify identity through admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sign answer sheets and attendance sheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Monitor conduct and compliance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes That Lead to Disqualification<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reaching after 01:30 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sitting in the wrong seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying prohibited items<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leaving exam early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not signing attendance sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Students<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reach centre before 12:00 PM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Double-check documents before leaving home<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carefully locate your seat before sitting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read instructions calmly before starting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay focused and avoid panic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 11, 1, '2026-04-14 01:44:26', '2026-04-14 06:12:18');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(341, 5, '  Unfair Means Practices & Breach of Examination Rules – NEET (UG)', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Definition\",\"name\":\"_definition\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unfair Means (UFM) in NEET is treated with zero tolerance. The rules are not just disciplinary&mdash;they are backed by legal provisions under the Public Examinations (Prevention of Unfair Means) Act, 2024, making violations serious enough to result in exam cancellation, multi-year bans, and even criminal action.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains every aspect in depth so you clearly understand what counts as unfair means, its consequences, and how to completely avoid risk.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What is &ldquo;Unfair Means&rdquo;? (Concept You Must Clearly Understand)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unfair means refers to any action&mdash;intentional or accidental&mdash;that gives a candidate an unfair advantage over others or disrupts the fairness of the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if you are not actively cheating, simply being in possession of a prohibited item or violating a rule can be treated as unfair means.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Intent does not always matter<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Possession or behavior alone can lead to punishment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Complete List of Unfair Means Practices (Explained in Detail)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Below is a structured explanation of all activities considered as unfair means, along with their real implications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Possession of Prohibited Items<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Includes carrying:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Notes, papers, study material<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electronic devices (mobile, Bluetooth, etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accessories, eatables, ornaments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any material related or unrelated to the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The item is unused<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You forgot it in your pocket<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You can still be booked under UFM.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Impersonation &amp; Proxy Writing<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Asking someone else to write the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing on behalf of another candidate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preparing cheating material in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Consequence<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is considered a serious criminal-level offence, not just exam misconduct.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Violation of Official Instructions<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring rules issued by National Testing Agency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disobeying invigilator instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even small violations (like ignoring seating rules) can fall under UFM.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Assisting or Receiving Help<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Helping another candidate cheat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Taking help directly or indirectly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting to exchange information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even attempting (not succeeding) is punishable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Writing Outside the Answer Sheet<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing answers or questions on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hands<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Clothes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any material other than official OMR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Banned<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It creates opportunities for copying or later manipulation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. Damage to Official Documents<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tearing or defacing:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OMR sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Test booklet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even careless handling can be misinterpreted as intentional damage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7. Unauthorized Communication<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Talking to other candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signalling or gesturing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Contacting anyone except exam staff<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">8. Taking Away Exam Materials<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Removing OMR sheet (original or office copy)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Taking question paper or parts outside<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is a serious violation and treated strictly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">9. Smuggling Exam Content<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Taking out question paper<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Taking out answer sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is considered high-level malpractice.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10. Threatening or Misconduct<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Threatening:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invigilators<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Staff<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Consequence<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Leads to immediate action and possible legal consequences.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">11. Use of Any Undesirable Method<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any creative or indirect cheating method<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any attempt to bypass rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">12. Manipulation of Documents<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fake or altered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank letter<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Self-declaration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">13. Forceful Entry or Exit<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entering or leaving the exam hall forcibly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not following entry\\/exit rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">14. Use of Electronic Devices<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using or attempting to use any device after entering the centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even possession alone is enough for punishment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">15. Fake or Morphed Photographs<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploading incorrect or edited photos in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application form<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">16. Tampering with OMR Sheet<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Erasing printed information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overwriting details like:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Roll number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">17. Manipulating OMR After Exam<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Trying to change responses after exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tampering with uploaded answer sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">18. Creating Disturbance<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disrupting exam process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Creating obstacles for smooth conduct<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">19. Any Other Declared Malpractice<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any activity declared unfair by NTA<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Any act covered under the Public Examinations (Prevention of Unfair Means) Act, 2024<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Punishment for using unfair means practices \",\"name\":\"_punishment_for_using_unfair_means_practices_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The consequences are extremely serious and long-term.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Found Guilty<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate will be booked under Unfair Means (UFM) case<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Major Penalties<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debarred up to 3 years from NTA exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result cancellation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Criminal action under law<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional penalties depending on severity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Punishment is based on:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Severity of violation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Type of malpractice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Cancellation of Result \\u2013 Immediate Impact\",\"name\":\"_cancellation_of_result__immediate_impact\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. If Unfair Means is Detected<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result will be cancelled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marks will not be declared<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Specific Situations Leading to Cancellation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appearing from a centre other than allotted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing on another candidate&rsquo;s OMR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Allowing someone else to write on your sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Reality<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if you perform well:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your result becomes completely invalid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Make (High-Risk Errors)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying mobile phone unknowingly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Writing rough work on hand or desk<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Talking casually during exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Filling OMR details incorrectly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring small instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy to Stay 100% Safe<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carry only required documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not bring anything extra<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow every instruction strictly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid any unnecessary movement or communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay calm and focused<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 12, 1, '2026-04-14 01:44:26', '2026-04-14 06:23:58');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(342, 5, ' Post-Examination Activities & Declaration of Result – NEET (UG) ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Display of OMR Answer Sheets & Recorded Responses\",\"name\":\"_display_of_omr_answer_sheets__recorded_responses\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After the exam is completed, the National Testing Agency takes an important step to ensure transparency.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What NTA Provides<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scanned images of your OMR Answer Sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Machine-recorded responses (what the system captured)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where It Is Available<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When It Is Released<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The exact date is announced after the exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates must regularly check the website for updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Step Is Extremely Important<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This stage allows you to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify whether your answers were correctly recorded<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identify:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OMR filling mistakes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Technical scanning errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cross-check your expected score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students skip this step, assuming everything is correct. However:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even a minor marking error can change your rank significantly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Early verification gives you a chance to correct official records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Challenging the OMR Grading (Correction Opportunity)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NTA provides a formal mechanism to challenge any discrepancy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What You Can Challenge<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incorrect recording of answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OMR grading issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Challenge<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submit a representation through the official process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pay a non-refundable fee of \\u20b9200 per question<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Financial Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">\\u20b9200 per question is non-refundable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even if your challenge is correct, the fee is not returned<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not challenge blindly. Only raise objections when:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are fully confident of an error<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You have verified your response carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verification Process by NTA<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once you submit a challenge:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NTA cross-checks your claim with actual OMR records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">If your challenge is found valid:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Necessary corrections are made in official data<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight Most Students Miss<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You will NOT receive individual confirmation of acceptance or rejection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Corrections are directly reflected in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check final results carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not expect personal communication from NTA<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Accessing and Downloading Your OMR Sheet<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are strongly advised to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the official website regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download and save their OMR sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Acts as proof of your responses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Helps in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Score estimation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Future reference during counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr>\\r\\n<p><strong>Common Mistakes Students Make in This Stage<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Not Checking OMR Sheet<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates ignore this step and miss potential corrections<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Filing Random Challenges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unnecessary challenges lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Loss of money<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Missing Deadlines<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Challenge window is limited&mdash;late submissions are not accepted<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Post-Exam Phase<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediately check OMR when released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Compare responses with answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identify only genuine discrepancies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge carefully and strategically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Save all documents for future use<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Display of Answer Key & Challenge Process \\u2013 NEET (UG)\",\"name\":\"_display_of_answer_key__challenge_process__neet_ug\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After the examination, one of the most critical stages begins&mdash;the release of the Answer Key. This stage directly influences your final marks, rank, and admission outcome, because it determines how your responses will be evaluated.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unlike many exams, NEET provides a structured challenge mechanism, allowing candidates to question the official answers before results are finalized. Understanding this process properly can give you a strategic advantage and prevent loss of marks due to incorrect keys<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Provisional Answer Key &ndash; First Official Evaluation Step<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The National Testing Agency initially releases a Provisional Answer Key.<br><br><\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What It Includes<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official answers to all NEET questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Basis for initial evaluation of responses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where It Is Released<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When It Is Released<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date is not fixed in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Announced after the examination via official notice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why the Provisional Answer Key Matters<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is your first opportunity to verify correctness of answers used for evaluation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What You Should Do<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Compare your responses with the answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identify:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incorrect answers in key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ambiguous or disputed questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even top-performing students can lose marks if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">The answer key contains errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They do not challenge incorrect answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Answer Key Challenge Process (Objection System)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NTA allows candidates to challenge the provisional answer key if they find any discrepancy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Challenge<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submit objections through the official portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pay a non-refundable fee of \\u20b9200 per question<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Financial Rule<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee is charged per question challenged<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee is non-refundable, regardless of outcome<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not challenge randomly. Only challenge when:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You have strong conceptual clarity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are confident the official answer is incorrect<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Verification of Challenges<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once challenges are submitted:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NTA sends them to a panel of subject experts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Experts review:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scientific correctness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conceptual accuracy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Validity of objections<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Happens After Verification<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Challenge Is Found Correct<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Answer key is revised<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correction is applied to all candidates, not just the one who challenged<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Challenge Is Incorrect<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No change is made<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee remains non-refundable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Insight Most Students Miss<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You will NOT be informed individually whether your challenge is accepted or rejected<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Changes are reflected only in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final result<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Answer Key &ndash; The Basis of Result<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After all valid challenges are processed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NTA releases the Final Answer Key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Features<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It is final and binding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No further challenges are accepted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Used to calculate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Rank<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Impact on Result Preparation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Results are prepared strictly based on the Final Answer Key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even a single corrected question can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Increase your marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Improve your rank significantly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Timeline Overview (Simplified Flow)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam conducted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provisional Answer Key released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge window opens<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Expert verification of objections<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final Answer Key released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result declared<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Make<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Ignoring Answer Key<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students skip this step and miss correction opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Filing Blind Challenges<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Challenging without proper justification leads to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Financial loss<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Missing Deadline<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Challenge window is short&mdash;late submissions are not accepted.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for This Stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check answer key immediately after release<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Match responses carefully with your OMR<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge only high-confidence errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Focus on accuracy, not quantity of challenges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Declaration of Result \\u2013 NEET (UG) \",\"name\":\"_declaration_of_result__neet_ug_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Evaluation Process, Scorecard Access, Merit List &amp; Continuous Monitoring Strategy)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The declaration of the NEET result is not just the announcement of marks&mdash;it is the foundation for your All India Rank (AIR), counselling eligibility, and final admission. This stage connects your performance in the exam to actual college allocation, making it one of the most critical phases in the entire NEET journey.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains the complete process in a detailed, structured, and strategic way so you understand not only what happens, but also how it impacts your future decision&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Evaluation of Answer Sheets &amp; Result Publication<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After completing all post-exam processes (OMR verification and answer key finalization), the National Testing Agency evaluates answer sheets using a standardized and automated procedure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Points About Evaluation<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evaluation is done based on the final answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Responses are checked through machine-based processing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensures:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accuracy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uniformity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fairness across all candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where and How Result is Declared<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Official Platform<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Website:<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/neet.nta.nic.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Candidates Must Do<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the website regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download their Scorecard once released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Your Scorecard Contains<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your NEET scorecard is a crucial document that includes:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Total marks obtained<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Subject-wise marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentile score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All India Rank (AIR)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category rank (if applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Qualifying status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This document is not just informational&mdash;it is required during:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preparation of Merit List &amp; All India Rank (AIR)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After evaluation, NTA prepares a Merit List and All India Rank (AIR).<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How AIR is Determined<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">AIR is calculated based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Your NEET score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Qualifying percentile criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tie-breaking rules (if required)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Governing Bodies Involved in Result &amp; Admission Process<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The ranking and admission process is aligned with guidelines issued by multiple authorities, ensuring standardized and regulated admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Authorities Include<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Medical Commission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Directorate General of Health Services<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical Counselling Committee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ministry of AYUSH<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Indian System of Medicine<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Commission for Homoeopathy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Central Council of Homoeopathy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH Admissions Central Counseling Committee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each authority plays a role in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Defining eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducting counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Allocating seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Continuous Monitoring After Result &ndash; A Critical Requirement<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the most overlooked aspects is post-result tracking.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Platforms to Check Regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must stay updated through:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National Testing Agency &ndash; Result &amp; exam updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ministry of Health &amp; Family Welfare &ndash;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.mohfw.gov.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/www.mohfw.gov.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ministry of AYUSH &ndash;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.ayush.gov.in\\/\\\"> https:\\/\\/www.ayush.gov.in\\/<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Directorate General of Health Services &ndash; Policy updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Medical Counselling Committee &ndash; AIQ counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH Admissions Central Counseling Committee &ndash; AYUSH counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Respective State counselling authorities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Continuous Monitoring Is Crucial<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After result declaration:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling schedules are released<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration windows open (short duration)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat allotment rounds begin<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If you miss any update:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You may lose your chance in that counselling round<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Even a good rank becomes useless without participation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of Result in Counselling &amp; Admission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your NEET result directly determines:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eligibility for counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Type of colleges you can apply to<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Chances of securing:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Private seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">AYUSH seat<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Strategic Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rank matters more than marks in counselling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Small score differences can lead to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Huge rank gaps<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Different college options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Students Make After Result<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not downloading scorecard immediately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring counselling updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missing registration deadlines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not understanding rank vs college mapping<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy After Result Declaration<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download and securely save your scorecard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Track counselling notifications daily<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepare required documents in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Understand your rank position realistically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Participate in counselling without delay<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Re-Checking \\/ Re-Evaluation of Answer Sheets \\u2013 NEET (UG)\",\"name\":\"_re-checking__re-evaluation_of_answer_sheets__neet_ug\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">(Why It Is Not Allowed, System Reliability &amp; What It Means for Candidates)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the most important rules in NEET that candidates must clearly understand is that re-checking or re-evaluation of answer sheets is not permitted under any circumstances. This often creates confusion and concern among students, especially after result declaration. However, this policy is based on a highly standardized, transparent, and multi-layered evaluation system designed to eliminate human error.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains not just the rule, but the logic behind it, its implications, and the correct approach students should follow instead.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No Provision for Re-Checking or Re-Evaluation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Official Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET answer sheets cannot be re-checked or re-evaluated<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No requests, applications, or appeals are accepted for this purpose<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Once your result is declared, it is considered final and binding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You cannot request:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-totaling of marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Manual re-evaluation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-checking of responses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How Answer Sheets Are Evaluated (Why Errors Are Highly Unlikely)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The evaluation process is conducted by the National Testing Agency using a machine-based system, which ensures high accuracy and fairness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Machine-Gradable OMR System<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET uses OMR (Optical Mark Recognition) sheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">These are checked using:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Specialized scanning machines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Dedicated evaluation software<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Advantage<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eliminates human bias<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensures uniform evaluation for all candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Multiple-Level Scrutiny<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OMR sheets are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carefully scanned<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-verified through system checks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The process is designed to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Detect scanning errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure accurate data capture<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Software-Based Evaluation<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evaluation is done through pre-programmed algorithms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">These systems are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Consistent<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Error-minimized<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Impartial<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Re-Evaluation Is Not Allowed (Core Reasons Explained)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The policy exists because NEET already provides two major correction opportunities before result declaration.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. OMR Response Verification Opportunity<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">View their scanned OMR sheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check recorded responses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge discrepancies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Answer Key Challenge System<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge incorrect answers in the answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Get corrections applied (if valid)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Combined Effect<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Because these two systems exist:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Errors can be corrected before final evaluation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final result is already verified and refined<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Conclusion<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Re-evaluation is unnecessary because correction opportunities are provided earlier in the process.<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No Correspondence Policy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strict Rule<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No communication regarding:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-checking requests<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-evaluation appeals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Emails, letters, or complaints on this matter:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Will not be entertained<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Will not lead to any change<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Misconceptions Students Have<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&ldquo;There might be calculation mistakes&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&rarr; Not possible due to automated system<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&ldquo;Manual rechecking can increase marks&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&rarr; No manual checking exists in NEET<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&ldquo;I can request re-evaluation later&rdquo;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&rarr; Completely false<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Risk Most Students Ignore<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Skip OMR verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignore answer key challenge<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Later, they:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Try to request re-evaluation (which is not allowed)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Result<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lost opportunity to correct genuine errors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since re-evaluation is not allowed, you must:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Focus on Pre-Result Stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carefully check your OMR sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Challenge any incorrect answer key<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Act within given deadlines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Post-Result Approach<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accept result as final<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Focus on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Counselling strategy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">College selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" Use of NEET (UG) 2026 Result by Other Organizations\",\"name\":\"_use_of_neet_ug_2026_result_by_other_organizations\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">(Expanded Scope Beyond MBBS, Nursing, Veterinary &amp; Special Institutional Uses)<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The NEET (UG) result is not limited to MBBS or BDS admissions. It has evolved into a multi-purpose national eligibility score that is used by various central and state-level institutions for admission into multiple healthcare-related courses. Understanding this broader usage is essential because it opens additional career pathways and strategic options for students.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section explains in detail how different organizations use NEET scores, what it means for candidates, and the important conditions attached to each use.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Multi-Agency Use of NEET Result &ndash; Core Concept<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The National Testing Agency conducts NEET and publishes results, but these results are shared with multiple authorities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Principle<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET provides a common eligibility score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Individual organizations apply:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their own eligibility criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their own admission rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Their own counselling processes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This System Exists<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduces multiple entrance exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Standardizes merit evaluation across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensures transparency and fairness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use of NEET Result by Central &amp; State Government Entities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Various government bodies use NEET scores for admissions in different courses.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Understanding<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each authority:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Defines its own eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">May have additional requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means for Students<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Same NEET score &rarr; can be used for multiple admission opportunities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You must carefully track different counselling processes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use of NEET for B.Sc. (Hons.) Nursing Courses<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NEET scores are also used for admission into B.Sc. (Hons.) Nursing programs.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Governing Authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ministry of Health and Family Welfare<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Points<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission is based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NEET score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"2\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Specific eligibility criteria of institutions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insig