ata-end=\\\"2848\\\">SC<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1j4cl8v\\\" data-start=\\\"2849\\\" data-end=\\\"2855\\\">ST<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"12ljjpk\\\" data-start=\\\"2856\\\" data-end=\\\"2877\\\">PwD (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1x4vv67\\\" data-start=\\\"2879\\\" data-end=\\\"2917\\\">Why Category Selection Is Important<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2919\\\" data-end=\\\"2944\\\">Your category may affect:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2946\\\" data-end=\\\"3055\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1653o38\\\" data-start=\\\"2946\\\" data-end=\\\"2970\\\">Reservation benefits<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1a6r4rn\\\" data-start=\\\"2971\\\" data-end=\\\"3004\\\">Eligibility under quota seats<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16d0zn7\\\" data-start=\\\"3005\\\" data-end=\\\"3029\\\">Shortlisting process<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"b3d332\\\" data-start=\\\"3030\\\" data-end=\\\"3055\\\">Document verification<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3057\\\" data-end=\\\"3129\\\">Choose only the category for which you possess valid official documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ltwvdg\\\" data-start=\\\"3136\\\" data-end=\\\"3180\\\">Additional Details for Reserved Categories<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3182\\\" data-end=\\\"3243\\\">Candidates selecting reserved categories may need to provide:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3245\\\" data-end=\\\"3360\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"18rvlhs\\\" data-start=\\\"3245\\\" data-end=\\\"3271\\\">Certificate Issue Date<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"13mfq4m\\\" data-start=\\\"3272\\\" data-end=\\\"3309\\\">Certificate Number \\/ Entry Number<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1mwpuaz\\\" data-start=\\\"3310\\\" data-end=\\\"3337\\\">State \\/ Union Territory<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1vh4td4\\\" data-start=\\\"3338\\\" data-end=\\\"3360\\\">Caste \\/ Tribe Name<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3362\\\" data-end=\\\"3420\\\">These details should exactly match the issued certificate.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3422\\\" data-end=\\\"3488\\\">Even small spelling mistakes can create verification issues later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"18jsq5a\\\" data-start=\\\"3495\\\" data-end=\\\"3531\\\">CAT Reservation Certificate Upload<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3533\\\" data-end=\\\"3626\\\">Candidates claiming reservation benefits may need to upload valid certificates in PDF format.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3628\\\" data-end=\\\"3645\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3647\\\" data-end=\\\"3727\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"gd2r0c\\\" data-start=\\\"3647\\\" data-end=\\\"3666\\\">EWS Certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1rzwsgj\\\" data-start=\\\"3667\\\" data-end=\\\"3689\\\">NC-OBC Certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1hd3dv1\\\" data-start=\\\"3690\\\" data-end=\\\"3708\\\">SC Certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1puw7zu\\\" data-start=\\\"3709\\\" data-end=\\\"3727\\\">ST Certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1x62y0t\\\" data-start=\\\"3729\\\" data-end=\\\"3746\\\">Important Tips<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3748\\\" data-end=\\\"3777\\\">Upload certificates that are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3779\\\" data-end=\\\"3879\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1e9wf6q\\\" data-start=\\\"3779\\\" data-end=\\\"3801\\\">Clear and readable<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"9pizpo\\\" data-start=\\\"3802\\\" data-end=\\\"3819\\\">Fully visible<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1if9zgn\\\" data-start=\\\"3820\\\" data-end=\\\"3840\\\">Properly scanned<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1r42pc6\\\" data-start=\\\"3841\\\" data-end=\\\"3879\\\">Valid as per official requirements<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3881\\\" data-end=\\\"3925\\\">Avoid uploading blurry or cropped documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1xq269j\\\" data-start=\\\"3932\\\" data-end=\\\"3959\\\">CAT PwD Details Explained<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3961\\\" data-end=\\\"4075\\\">Candidates applying under <strong data-start=\\\"3987\\\" data-end=\\\"4019\\\">Person with Disability (PwD)<\\/strong> category may need to provide extra information such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4077\\\" data-end=\\\"4244\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bp66g\\\" data-start=\\\"4077\\\" data-end=\\\"4113\\\">Whether disability is measurable<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"10jlxph\\\" data-start=\\\"4114\\\" data-end=\\\"4142\\\">Percentage of disability<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"xwrqdw\\\" data-start=\\\"4143\\\" data-end=\\\"4162\\\">PwD UDID Number<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"7jdg3o\\\" data-start=\\\"4163\\\" data-end=\\\"4186\\\">Disability category<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1sszkze\\\" data-start=\\\"4187\\\" data-end=\\\"4221\\\">Wheelchair support requirement<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"x1r36j\\\" data-start=\\\"4222\\\" data-end=\\\"4244\\\">Scribe requirement<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4246\\\" data-end=\\\"4304\\\">This information helps arrange required facilities fairly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1iprjlg\\\" data-start=\\\"4311\\\" data-end=\\\"4347\\\">PwD Certificate Upload in CAT Form<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4349\\\" data-end=\\\"4474\\\">Candidates claiming PwD benefits may need to upload a valid disability certificate issued by an authorized medical authority.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4476\\\" data-end=\\\"4499\\\">Ensure the certificate:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4501\\\" data-end=\\\"4604\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8of0qu\\\" data-start=\\\"4501\\\" data-end=\\\"4528\\\">Matches entered details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"w5i5sa\\\" data-start=\\\"4529\\\" data-end=\\\"4544\\\">Is readable<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"6kgc4a\\\" data-start=\\\"4545\\\" data-end=\\\"4581\\\">Contains official seal\\/signature<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15wipi0\\\" data-start=\\\"4582\\\" data-end=\\\"4604\\\">Is currently valid<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"gvxowp\\\" data-start=\\\"4611\\\" data-end=\\\"4632\\\">CAT Scribe Facility<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4634\\\" data-end=\\\"4675\\\">Candidates who need a scribe may have to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4677\\\" data-end=\\\"4834\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1n1iobm\\\" data-start=\\\"4677\\\" data-end=\\\"4726\\\">Arrange the scribe as per official guidelines<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1fx1bym\\\" data-start=\\\"4727\\\" data-end=\\\"4781\\\">Complete the required affidavit \\/ declaration form<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"53pmam\\\" data-start=\\\"4782\\\" data-end=\\\"4834\\\">Follow instructions available on the CAT website<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4836\\\" data-end=\\\"4920\\\">It is better to complete this process early rather than waiting until the last date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"y1uct3\\\" data-start=\\\"4927\\\" data-end=\\\"4972\\\">Communication Address and Permanent Address<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4974\\\" data-end=\\\"5011\\\">Candidates usually need to fill both:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5013\\\" data-end=\\\"5070\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1e5eynu\\\" data-start=\\\"5013\\\" data-end=\\\"5048\\\">Present \\/ Communication Address<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dzqt0k\\\" data-start=\\\"5049\\\" data-end=\\\"5070\\\">Permanent Address<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5072\\\" data-end=\\\"5152\\\">These details may be used for official communication during the admission cycle.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"4ddllh\\\" data-start=\\\"5154\\\" data-end=\\\"5171\\\">Fill Carefully<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5173\\\" data-end=\\\"5181\\\">Include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5183\\\" data-end=\\\"5266\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"x4lydr\\\" data-start=\\\"5183\\\" data-end=\\\"5199\\\">House number<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"2624cv\\\" data-start=\\\"5200\\\" data-end=\\\"5221\\\">Street \\/ locality<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1usr2y7\\\" data-start=\\\"5222\\\" data-end=\\\"5230\\\">City<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bme9am\\\" data-start=\\\"5231\\\" data-end=\\\"5243\\\">District<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ph1p8f\\\" data-start=\\\"5244\\\" data-end=\\\"5253\\\">State<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1t01aya\\\" data-start=\\\"5254\\\" data-end=\\\"5266\\\">PIN code<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5268\\\" data-end=\\\"5322\\\">Wrong address details may create communication issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1ffpjvf\\\" data-start=\\\"5329\\\" data-end=\\\"5374\\\">Alternate Email and Emergency Mobile Number<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5376\\\" data-end=\\\"5412\\\">Candidates may also need to provide:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5414\\\" data-end=\\\"5464\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ez7ncp\\\" data-start=\\\"5414\\\" data-end=\\\"5436\\\">Alternate Email ID<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1skcv6q\\\" data-start=\\\"5437\\\" data-end=\\\"5464\\\">Emergency Mobile Number<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5466\\\" data-end=\\\"5602\\\">The emergency contact number should be different from your main number and preferably belong to a close family member or trusted person.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"5j1mmo\\\" data-start=\\\"5609\\\" data-end=\\\"5647\\\">Why Emergency Contact Details Matter<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5649\\\" data-end=\\\"5725\\\">Emergency contact information may be useful in urgent situations related to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5727\\\" data-end=\\\"5799\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"zxq2qq\\\" data-start=\\\"5727\\\" data-end=\\\"5751\\\">Communication issues<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"nt211f\\\" data-start=\\\"5752\\\" data-end=\\\"5773\\\">Admission updates<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"z4ihe\\\" data-start=\\\"5774\\\" data-end=\\\"5799\\\">Candidate emergencies<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5801\\\" data-end=\\\"5848\\\">Always provide an active and reachable contact.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"h8p8ea\\\" data-start=\\\"5855\\\" data-end=\\\"5879\\\">CAT Photo Upload Rules<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5881\\\" data-end=\\\"5942\\\">Candidates usually need to upload a passport-size photograph.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"x7h65s\\\" data-start=\\\"5944\\\" data-end=\\\"5971\\\">Mentioned Specifications<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5973\\\" data-end=\\\"6164\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"oq0036\\\" data-start=\\\"5973\\\" data-end=\\\"6007\\\">Dimensions: 1200 x 1200 pixels<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ryeraz\\\" data-start=\\\"6008\\\" data-end=\\\"6030\\\">Format: JPG \\/ JPEG<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15zl6oo\\\" data-start=\\\"6031\\\" data-end=\\\"6059\\\">Maximum file size: 80 KB<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ptd27p\\\" data-start=\\\"6060\\\" data-end=\\\"6095\\\">Minimum resolution: 150 px\\/inch<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"yvycg1\\\" data-start=\\\"6096\\\" data-end=\\\"6116\\\">White background<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"f5i82d\\\" data-start=\\\"6117\\\" data-end=\\\"6164\\\">Recent photograph (not older than six months)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1yz2xhq\\\" data-start=\\\"6166\\\" data-end=\\\"6182\\\">Important Tip<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6184\\\" data-end=\\\"6285\\\">Use a clear recent photo with full face visibility. Keep extra printed copies of the same photograph.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"20yj6y\\\" data-start=\\\"6292\\\" data-end=\\\"6320\\\">CAT Signature Upload Rules<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6322\\\" data-end=\\\"6377\\\">Candidates may also need to upload a scanned signature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"tr5642\\\" data-start=\\\"6379\\\" data-end=\\\"6404\\\">Mentioned Requirements<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6406\\\" data-end=\\\"6500\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"4wzdlz\\\" data-start=\\\"6406\\\" data-end=\\\"6435\\\">Dimensions: 80 mm x 35 mm<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1be7l5t\\\" data-start=\\\"6436\\\" data-end=\\\"6457\\\">JPG \\/ JPEG format<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1n9t3bq\\\" data-start=\\\"6458\\\" data-end=\\\"6473\\\">Clear image<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ogq0kx\\\" data-start=\\\"6474\\\" data-end=\\\"6500\\\">Proper signature style<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6502\\\" data-end=\\\"6553\\\">Use your regular running signature, not typed text.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"11im936\\\" data-start=\\\"6560\\\" data-end=\\\"6629\\\">Documents to Keep Ready Before Filling CAT Personal Details Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6631\\\" data-end=\\\"6656\\\">Prepare these in advance:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6658\\\" data-end=\\\"6875\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jit5zm\\\" data-start=\\\"6658\\\" data-end=\\\"6682\\\">Class 10 certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1l6qwl6\\\" data-start=\\\"6683\\\" data-end=\\\"6701\\\">Identity proof<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"14qiub2\\\" data-start=\\\"6702\\\" data-end=\\\"6742\\\">Category certificate (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"d51swt\\\" data-start=\\\"6743\\\" data-end=\\\"6778\\\">PwD certificate (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5tdwx1\\\" data-start=\\\"6779\\\" data-end=\\\"6807\\\">Passport size photograph<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1opne43\\\" data-start=\\\"6808\\\" data-end=\\\"6826\\\">Signature scan<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15di1ss\\\" data-start=\\\"6827\\\" data-end=\\\"6846\\\">Address details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"vjjghu\\\" data-start=\\\"6847\\\" data-end=\\\"6875\\\">Emergency contact number<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6877\\\" data-end=\\\"6930\\\">This makes the form filling process faster and safer.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"shykcn\\\" data-start=\\\"6937\\\" data-end=\\\"6992\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid in CAT Personal Details Form<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1g8b347\\\" data-start=\\\"6994\\\" data-end=\\\"7016\\\">Wrong Name Spelling<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7018\\\" data-end=\\\"7058\\\">Can create mismatch during verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"meekli\\\" data-start=\\\"7060\\\" data-end=\\\"7087\\\">Incorrect Category Claim<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7089\\\" data-end=\\\"7135\\\">May lead to rejection of reservation benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1wov65k\\\" data-start=\\\"7137\\\" data-end=\\\"7159\\\">Blurry Photo Upload<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7161\\\" data-end=\\\"7202\\\">Can create admit card or identity issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1x09zfp\\\" data-start=\\\"7204\\\" data-end=\\\"7227\\\">Wrong Contact Number<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7229\\\" data-end=\\\"7254\\\">May cause missed updates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"19w40n6\\\" data-start=\\\"7256\\\" data-end=\\\"7285\\\">Invalid Certificate Upload<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7287\\\" data-end=\\\"7329\\\">Can delay or reject category verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1aezekl\\\" data-start=\\\"7331\\\" data-end=\\\"7352\\\">Signature Mismatch<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7354\\\" data-end=\\\"7390\\\">May create future identity problems.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" ACADEMICS \",\"name\":\"_academics_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"108\\\" data-end=\\\"475\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"112\\\" data-end=\\\"137\\\">CAT Academics section<\\/strong> is one of the most important parts of the CAT application form because it builds your complete educational profile. Your academic records are not only used for eligibility verification, but they may also play an important role during shortlisting, profile evaluation, interview calls, and final admission processes at various institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"477\\\" data-end=\\\"758\\\">Many candidates make mistakes while entering marks, CGPA conversion, passing year, degree type, or course details. Even small errors can create confusion later during document verification. Therefore, the CAT Academics section should be filled with complete attention and accuracy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"760\\\" data-end=\\\"980\\\">This detailed guide explains how to fill the <strong data-start=\\\"805\\\" data-end=\\\"830\\\">CAT Academics section<\\/strong>, including Class 10, Class 12, diploma, graduation, multiple degrees, master&rsquo;s degree, professional qualifications, and percentage calculation rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"173ushy\\\" data-start=\\\"987\\\" data-end=\\\"1035\\\">What Is Included in the CAT Academics Section?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1037\\\" data-end=\\\"1128\\\">Candidates may need to enter educational details for all qualifications applicable to them.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1130\\\" data-end=\\\"1166\\\">The main sections generally include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1168\\\" data-end=\\\"1430\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"hxewxk\\\" data-start=\\\"1168\\\" data-end=\\\"1203\\\">SSC \\/ 10th \\/ Equivalent Details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8mral8\\\" data-start=\\\"1204\\\" data-end=\\\"1249\\\">HSC \\/ 12th \\/ Equivalent \\/ Diploma Details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"13kvk4y\\\" data-start=\\\"1250\\\" data-end=\\\"1285\\\">First Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree Details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"vuxxvf\\\" data-start=\\\"1286\\\" data-end=\\\"1338\\\">Second Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree Details (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"n1crv\\\" data-start=\\\"1339\\\" data-end=\\\"1382\\\">Master&rsquo;s Degree Details (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1hd5kwm\\\" data-start=\\\"1383\\\" data-end=\\\"1430\\\">Professional Degree Details (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1432\\\" data-end=\\\"1519\\\">Every candidate should fill only the sections relevant to their educational background.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1r4wf0s\\\" data-start=\\\"1526\\\" data-end=\\\"1570\\\">Why the CAT Academics Section Is Important<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1572\\\" data-end=\\\"1610\\\">Your academic details may be used for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1612\\\" data-end=\\\"1792\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"qkkbh8\\\" data-start=\\\"1612\\\" data-end=\\\"1640\\\">Eligibility verification<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"byqgbz\\\" data-start=\\\"1641\\\" data-end=\\\"1671\\\">Profile-based shortlisting<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"z143fb\\\" data-start=\\\"1672\\\" data-end=\\\"1699\\\">Interview consideration<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"18h2xwc\\\" data-start=\\\"1700\\\" data-end=\\\"1730\\\">Admission merit parameters<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"b3d332\\\" data-start=\\\"1731\\\" data-end=\\\"1756\\\">Document verification<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ie2i74\\\" data-start=\\\"1757\\\" data-end=\\\"1792\\\">Reservation \\/ degree validation<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1794\\\" data-end=\\\"1900\\\">That is why marks, years, board names, university names, and degree information must be entered correctly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1g8ldyw\\\" data-start=\\\"1907\\\" data-end=\\\"1959\\\">Important Rule for Marks and Percentage Conversion<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1961\\\" data-end=\\\"2164\\\">Many students receive grades, CGPA, or letter marks instead of direct percentages. In such cases, candidates should use the official conversion method provided by their board, university, or institution.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2166\\\" data-end=\\\"2249\\\">If the institution provides no conversion formula, percentage may be calculated by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2251\\\" data-end=\\\"2280\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"2251\\\" data-end=\\\"2280\\\">CGPA &divide; Maximum CGPA &times; 100<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2282\\\" data-end=\\\"2290\\\">Example:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2292\\\" data-end=\\\"2315\\\">If CGPA = 8.2 out of 10<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2317\\\" data-end=\\\"2333\\\">Then percentage:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2335\\\" data-end=\\\"2355\\\">8.2 &divide; 10 &times; 100 = 82%<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2357\\\" data-end=\\\"2451\\\">Candidates may need original conversion proof during later verification stages if shortlisted.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1gu0gve\\\" data-start=\\\"2458\\\" data-end=\\\"2498\\\">How Percentages Are Usually Considered<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"b8dt2v\\\" data-start=\\\"2500\\\" data-end=\\\"2528\\\">For Class 10 and Class 12<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2530\\\" data-end=\\\"2646\\\">Total marks of all subjects shown in the marksheet may be considered, irrespective of board-specific internal rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"z4zovh\\\" data-start=\\\"2648\\\" data-end=\\\"2684\\\">For Graduation and Postgraduation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2686\\\" data-end=\\\"2825\\\">Aggregate percentage awarded by the university is generally used. If no final aggregate is given, marks of all semesters\\/years may be used.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2827\\\" data-end=\\\"2873\\\">This makes accurate entry extremely important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"qdebh8\\\" data-start=\\\"2880\\\" data-end=\\\"2907\\\">1. CAT SSC \\/ 10th Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2909\\\" data-end=\\\"2985\\\">Candidates need to enter their Class 10 or equivalent qualification details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2987\\\" data-end=\\\"3004\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3006\\\" data-end=\\\"3150\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1yfhdzp\\\" data-start=\\\"3006\\\" data-end=\\\"3020\\\">Board name<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tdiyx9\\\" data-start=\\\"3021\\\" data-end=\\\"3047\\\">School name (if asked)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"4lx9va\\\" data-start=\\\"3048\\\" data-end=\\\"3064\\\">Passing year<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1plf1qs\\\" data-start=\\\"3065\\\" data-end=\\\"3081\\\">Marks \\/ CGPA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5bhpyp\\\" data-start=\\\"3082\\\" data-end=\\\"3106\\\">Aggregate percentage<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1iqev7v\\\" data-start=\\\"3107\\\" data-end=\\\"3150\\\">Stream \\/ examination type (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1yz2xhq\\\" data-start=\\\"3152\\\" data-end=\\\"3168\\\">Important Tip<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3170\\\" data-end=\\\"3231\\\">Enter percentage up to the allowed decimal limit if required.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3>Special Provision for 2020 \\/ 2021 Pass-Outs<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3281\\\" data-end=\\\"3450\\\">Where official forms permit, candidates promoted or passed without marks during specific academic disruptions may need to use the designated option provided in the form.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"16o1u0f\\\" data-start=\\\"3457\\\" data-end=\\\"3501\\\">2. CAT 12th \\/ Equivalent \\/ Diploma Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3503\\\" data-end=\\\"3549\\\">Candidates must choose whether they completed:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3551\\\" data-end=\\\"3599\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1nu1aqa\\\" data-start=\\\"3551\\\" data-end=\\\"3582\\\">12th \\/ HSC \\/ Equivalent, or<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ea6udj\\\" data-start=\\\"3583\\\" data-end=\\\"3599\\\">Diploma Course<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"gcpxl4\\\" data-start=\\\"3601\\\" data-end=\\\"3623\\\">When to Choose 12th<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3625\\\" data-end=\\\"3683\\\">If you followed the standard school system after Class 10.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1ll3539\\\" data-start=\\\"3685\\\" data-end=\\\"3710\\\">When to Choose Diploma<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3712\\\" data-end=\\\"3765\\\">If you pursued a diploma instead of regular Class 12.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1qk5dxy\\\" data-start=\\\"3767\\\" data-end=\\\"3795\\\">Details Commonly Required<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3797\\\" data-end=\\\"3888\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"qp7vf2\\\" data-start=\\\"3797\\\" data-end=\\\"3825\\\">Board \\/ institution name<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"4lx9va\\\" data-start=\\\"3826\\\" data-end=\\\"3842\\\">Passing year<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1plf1qs\\\" data-start=\\\"3843\\\" data-end=\\\"3859\\\">Marks \\/ CGPA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5krxlc\\\" data-start=\\\"3860\\\" data-end=\\\"3874\\\">Percentage<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ispjjh\\\" data-start=\\\"3875\\\" data-end=\\\"3888\\\">Course type<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3890\\\" data-end=\\\"3976\\\">All subject marks shown in the marksheet may be considered for percentage calculation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"camk1m\\\" data-start=\\\"3983\\\" data-end=\\\"4030\\\">3. CAT Graduation \\/ Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4032\\\" data-end=\\\"4131\\\">This is one of the most important sections because graduation status is central to CAT eligibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4133\\\" data-end=\\\"4212\\\">Candidates need to select the correct bachelor&rsquo;s degree from the dropdown list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4214\\\" data-end=\\\"4223\\\">Examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4225\\\" data-end=\\\"4326\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1uale4r\\\" data-start=\\\"4225\\\" data-end=\\\"4233\\\">B.A.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1kuwkdh\\\" data-start=\\\"4234\\\" data-end=\\\"4243\\\">B.Com<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ub0l3o\\\" data-start=\\\"4244\\\" data-end=\\\"4252\\\">B.Sc<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"y69ov2\\\" data-start=\\\"4253\\\" data-end=\\\"4263\\\">B.Tech<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16ynlwp\\\" data-start=\\\"4264\\\" data-end=\\\"4271\\\">BBA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16yrbgo\\\" data-start=\\\"4272\\\" data-end=\\\"4279\\\">BCA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16rw3ca\\\" data-start=\\\"4280\\\" data-end=\\\"4287\\\">LLB<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8u4feq\\\" data-start=\\\"4288\\\" data-end=\\\"4299\\\">B.Pharm<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16u26y3\\\" data-start=\\\"4300\\\" data-end=\\\"4326\\\">Other recognized degrees<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3>If You Have Completed Graduation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4369\\\" data-end=\\\"4375\\\">Enter:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4377\\\" data-end=\\\"4488\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1q79z4a\\\" data-start=\\\"4377\\\" data-end=\\\"4409\\\">College \\/ university details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"rdltjm\\\" data-start=\\\"4410\\\" data-end=\\\"4425\\\">Course name<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"4lx9va\\\" data-start=\\\"4426\\\" data-end=\\\"4442\\\">Passing year<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"vqmpqu\\\" data-start=\\\"4443\\\" data-end=\\\"4465\\\">Total marks \\/ CGPA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1xqbqcx\\\" data-start=\\\"4466\\\" data-end=\\\"4488\\\">Aggregate percentage<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4490\\\" data-end=\\\"4540\\\">Use official university norms wherever applicable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"12e1bu1\\\" data-start=\\\"4547\\\" data-end=\\\"4587\\\">If You Are in Final Year of Graduation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4589\\\" data-end=\\\"4652\\\">Candidates currently pursuing the final year may need to enter:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4654\\\" data-end=\\\"4743\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"584naj\\\" data-start=\\\"4654\\\" data-end=\\\"4679\\\">Current academic year<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"twnz5y\\\" data-start=\\\"4680\\\" data-end=\\\"4692\\\">Semester<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"14mu23x\\\" data-start=\\\"4693\\\" data-end=\\\"4743\\\">Marks obtained up to completed semesters \\/ years<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4745\\\" data-end=\\\"4814\\\">This should be updated carefully based on available official results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"kemt95\\\" data-start=\\\"4821\\\" data-end=\\\"4875\\\">Special Provision for 2020 \\/ 2021 Graduation Results<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4877\\\" data-end=\\\"5012\\\">Where officially applicable, candidates promoted\\/passed without marks in those specific years may need to use the provided form option.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1fmoc8q\\\" data-start=\\\"5019\\\" data-end=\\\"5060\\\">4. CAT Second Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5062\\\" data-end=\\\"5149\\\">Candidates having more than one bachelor&rsquo;s degree may need to fill both qualifications.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5151\\\" data-end=\\\"5160\\\">Examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5162\\\" data-end=\\\"5211\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jxh64s\\\" data-start=\\\"5162\\\" data-end=\\\"5177\\\">B.Com + LLB<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1gzczer\\\" data-start=\\\"5178\\\" data-end=\\\"5194\\\">B.A. + B.Ed.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5s4g9a\\\" data-start=\\\"5195\\\" data-end=\\\"5211\\\">B.E. + B.Pharm<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5213\\\" data-end=\\\"5281\\\">Do not hide an additional recognized degree if the form asks for it.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"fnyy36\\\" data-start=\\\"5288\\\" data-end=\\\"5310\\\">5. Dual Degree Cases<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5312\\\" data-end=\\\"5484\\\">If a candidate completed an integrated or dual qualification containing bachelor&rsquo;s and master&rsquo;s components, both sections may need to be filled separately where applicable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5486\\\" data-end=\\\"5495\\\">Examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5497\\\" data-end=\\\"5532\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"in3jgs\\\" data-start=\\\"5497\\\" data-end=\\\"5516\\\">B.Tech + M.Tech<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1k8lshy\\\" data-start=\\\"5517\\\" data-end=\\\"5532\\\">B.Tech + M.Sc<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5534\\\" data-end=\\\"5596\\\">Always enter according to official structure of the programme.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"sm7354\\\" data-start=\\\"5603\\\" data-end=\\\"5635\\\">6. CAT Master&rsquo;s Degree Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5637\\\" data-end=\\\"5715\\\">Candidates with postgraduate qualifications may enter master&rsquo;s degree details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5717\\\" data-end=\\\"5726\\\">Examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5728\\\" data-end=\\\"5812\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1sjqtus\\\" data-start=\\\"5728\\\" data-end=\\\"5736\\\">M.A.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1y4qi96\\\" data-start=\\\"5737\\\" data-end=\\\"5746\\\">M.Com<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1sk0dh7\\\" data-start=\\\"5747\\\" data-end=\\\"5755\\\">M.Sc<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16vahra\\\" data-start=\\\"5756\\\" data-end=\\\"5763\\\">MBA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16v9rnr\\\" data-start=\\\"5764\\\" data-end=\\\"5771\\\">MCA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1leydbl\\\" data-start=\\\"5772\\\" data-end=\\\"5782\\\">M.Tech<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1t2036k\\\" data-start=\\\"5783\\\" data-end=\\\"5812\\\">Other recognized PG degrees<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5814\\\" data-end=\\\"5867\\\">Candidates may need to mention whether the degree is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5869\\\" data-end=\\\"5907\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"19xglo4\\\" data-start=\\\"5869\\\" data-end=\\\"5886\\\">Completed, or<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"6ay0lh\\\" data-start=\\\"5887\\\" data-end=\\\"5907\\\">Currently pursuing<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5909\\\" data-end=\\\"5967\\\">Then fill marks, university, year, and percentage details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"10q6m7o\\\" data-start=\\\"5974\\\" data-end=\\\"6010\\\">7. CAT Professional Degree Details<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6012\\\" data-end=\\\"6104\\\">Candidates with professional qualifications may need to select them from the available list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6106\\\" data-end=\\\"6122\\\">Common examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6124\\\" data-end=\\\"6205\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1j40kga\\\" data-start=\\\"6124\\\" data-end=\\\"6130\\\">CA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1j40w7s\\\" data-start=\\\"6131\\\" data-end=\\\"6137\\\">CS<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"i3y22c\\\" data-start=\\\"6138\\\" data-end=\\\"6152\\\">ICWA \\/ CMA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1yo2k5r\\\" data-start=\\\"6153\\\" data-end=\\\"6161\\\">FIAI<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1f8ms9r\\\" data-start=\\\"6162\\\" data-end=\\\"6205\\\">Other recognized professional credentials<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6207\\\" data-end=\\\"6289\\\">Where multiple qualifications exist, follow official instructions for marks entry.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"nbqzf9\\\" data-start=\\\"6296\\\" data-end=\\\"6329\\\">If No Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree Is Held<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6331\\\" data-end=\\\"6496\\\">In some cases, recognized professional qualifications may be relevant under official eligibility conditions. Candidates should carefully follow the latest CAT rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"13arl8x\\\" data-start=\\\"6503\\\" data-end=\\\"6540\\\">Original Mark Sheets Required Later<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6542\\\" data-end=\\\"6669\\\">Candidates should preserve original documents because mark sheets, certificates, and conversion records may be required during:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6671\\\" data-end=\\\"6746\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"137dqj4\\\" data-start=\\\"6671\\\" data-end=\\\"6691\\\">Interview rounds<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"o227h4\\\" data-start=\\\"6692\\\" data-end=\\\"6718\\\">Admission verification<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"jm25qw\\\" data-start=\\\"6719\\\" data-end=\\\"6746\\\">Institute joining process<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6748\\\" data-end=\\\"6784\\\">Never enter estimated data casually.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"13wmuvo\\\" data-start=\\\"6791\\\" data-end=\\\"6842\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid in CAT Academics Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1nzplgq\\\" data-start=\\\"6844\\\" data-end=\\\"6869\\\">Wrong Percentage Entry<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6871\\\" data-end=\\\"6902\\\">Confusing CGPA with percentage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"127pv2g\\\" data-start=\\\"6904\\\" data-end=\\\"6942\\\">Using Rounded-Off Marks Incorrectly<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6944\\\" data-end=\\\"6974\\\">Use correct decimals if asked.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"15wxmyq\\\" data-start=\\\"6976\\\" data-end=\\\"7001\\\">Incorrect Passing Year<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7003\\\" data-end=\\\"7032\\\">Check certificates carefully.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"spmr0y\\\" data-start=\\\"7034\\\" data-end=\\\"7059\\\">Wrong Degree Selection<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7061\\\" data-end=\\\"7102\\\">Choose exact qualification from dropdown.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1eq3yi9\\\" data-start=\\\"7104\\\" data-end=\\\"7144\\\">Ignoring Backlogs \\/ Incomplete Status<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7146\\\" data-end=\\\"7177\\\">Enter academic status honestly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1xvkgpm\\\" data-start=\\\"7179\\\" data-end=\\\"7202\\\">Fake Marks Inflation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7204\\\" data-end=\\\"7263\\\">This can create serious rejection risk during verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"msoe60\\\" data-start=\\\"7270\\\" data-end=\\\"7333\\\">Best Documents to Keep Ready Before Filling Academics Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7335\\\" data-end=\\\"7343\\\">Prepare:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"7345\\\" data-end=\\\"7610\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ulae2l\\\" data-start=\\\"7345\\\" data-end=\\\"7367\\\">Class 10 marksheet<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1eaztxb\\\" data-start=\\\"7368\\\" data-end=\\\"7390\\\">Class 12 marksheet<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"11bawgc\\\" data-start=\\\"7391\\\" data-end=\\\"7430\\\">Diploma certificate (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"145ztdj\\\" data-start=\\\"7431\\\" data-end=\\\"7465\\\">Graduation semester marksheets<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"j4l32d\\\" data-start=\\\"7466\\\" data-end=\\\"7494\\\">Final degree certificate<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"dmxk3n\\\" data-start=\\\"7495\\\" data-end=\\\"7531\\\">Master&rsquo;s records (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1rkevue\\\" data-start=\\\"7532\\\" data-end=\\\"7568\\\">Professional qualification proof<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"183y0ut\\\" data-start=\\\"7569\\\" data-end=\\\"7610\\\">CGPA conversion certificate (if needed)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"7612\\\" data-end=\\\"7654\\\">This reduces mistakes during form filling.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" WORK EXPERIENCE \",\"name\":\"_work_experience_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"98\\\" data-end=\\\"475\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"102\\\" data-end=\\\"133\\\">CAT Work Experience section<\\/strong> is an important part of the CAT application form for candidates who have worked after completing graduation. Many top management institutes consider work experience during shortlisting, interview calls, profile evaluation, final selection, and classroom diversity. Because of this, candidates should fill this section carefully and honestly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"477\\\" data-end=\\\"825\\\">Many applicants make mistakes such as counting internships, including part-time jobs, adding pre-graduation experience, or calculating incorrect number of days. These errors can create problems during interview verification or admission stages. Therefore, the CAT Work Experience section should be completed using proper records and accurate dates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"827\\\" data-end=\\\"1001\\\">This detailed guide explains how to fill the CAT Work Experience section correctly, what counts as valid experience, what should not be entered, and common mistakes to avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ov2ca9\\\" data-start=\\\"1008\\\" data-end=\\\"1053\\\">Why the CAT Work Experience Section Matters<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1055\\\" data-end=\\\"1124\\\">Work experience may help in multiple ways depending on the institute.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1126\\\" data-end=\\\"1151\\\">It may be considered for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1153\\\" data-end=\\\"1349\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"byqgbz\\\" data-start=\\\"1153\\\" data-end=\\\"1183\\\">Profile-based shortlisting<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"i5jryo\\\" data-start=\\\"1184\\\" data-end=\\\"1211\\\">Interview call criteria<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jhvlmz\\\" data-start=\\\"1212\\\" data-end=\\\"1233\\\">Final merit score<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"nbc8i8\\\" data-start=\\\"1234\\\" data-end=\\\"1264\\\">Academic diversity balance<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bohf9n\\\" data-start=\\\"1265\\\" data-end=\\\"1300\\\">Classroom learning contribution<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1gs0x58\\\" data-start=\\\"1301\\\" data-end=\\\"1349\\\">Leadership and practical exposure assessment<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1351\\\" data-end=\\\"1466\\\">Some institutes give weightage to relevant full-time work experience, while some may use it only during interviews.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"l1hd1c\\\" data-start=\\\"1473\\\" data-end=\\\"1519\\\">Who Should Fill the Work Experience Section?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1521\\\" data-end=\\\"1613\\\">This section is for candidates who have worked in <strong data-start=\\\"1571\\\" data-end=\\\"1612\\\">full-time employment after graduation<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1615\\\" data-end=\\\"1750\\\">If you have never worked in a qualifying full-time role after graduation, you may usually enter zero or leave as per form instructions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1752\\\" data-end=\\\"1825\\\">Freshers can still apply for CAT and admission opportunities remain open.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1v335qk\\\" data-start=\\\"1832\\\" data-end=\\\"1878\\\">What Type of Experience Is Usually Accepted?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1880\\\" data-end=\\\"1971\\\">Only <strong data-start=\\\"1885\\\" data-end=\\\"1942\\\">full-time work experience after completing graduation<\\/strong> should generally be entered.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1973\\\" data-end=\\\"1984\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1986\\\" data-end=\\\"2207\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"evt5dh\\\" data-start=\\\"1986\\\" data-end=\\\"2026\\\">You completed your bachelor&rsquo;s degree<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"tx08tm\\\" data-start=\\\"2027\\\" data-end=\\\"2063\\\">You joined a full-time paid role<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"9xsu2j\\\" data-start=\\\"2064\\\" data-end=\\\"2158\\\">You worked in a company, organization, firm, institution, startup, or recognized workplace<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"n0l910\\\" data-start=\\\"2159\\\" data-end=\\\"2207\\\">Employment dates can be verified if required<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"hkobtx\\\" data-start=\\\"2214\\\" data-end=\\\"2259\\\">What Is NOT Counted as CAT Work Experience?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2261\\\" data-end=\\\"2342\\\">The following are generally not counted as valid work experience in this section:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2344\\\" data-end=\\\"2686\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ucaw1f\\\" data-start=\\\"2344\\\" data-end=\\\"2362\\\">Part-time jobs<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1vama37\\\" data-start=\\\"2363\\\" data-end=\\\"2378\\\">Internships<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16e7ta2\\\" data-start=\\\"2379\\\" data-end=\\\"2418\\\">Project-based temporary assignments<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"12hfzwu\\\" data-start=\\\"2419\\\" data-end=\\\"2434\\\">Articleship<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ksg2cv\\\" data-start=\\\"2435\\\" data-end=\\\"2533\\\">Freelance short assignments (unless officially qualifying as full-time employment under rules)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tkqngo\\\" data-start=\\\"2534\\\" data-end=\\\"2565\\\">Work done before graduation<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1y5ayl2\\\" data-start=\\\"2566\\\" data-end=\\\"2666\\\">Family business support without formal structure (unless officially documentable and acceptable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1g8ebix\\\" data-start=\\\"2667\\\" data-end=\\\"2686\\\">Summer training<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2688\\\" data-end=\\\"2812\\\">Candidates often make the mistake of adding internships to increase profile strength. This can backfire during verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1ok17zo\\\" data-start=\\\"2819\\\" data-end=\\\"2861\\\">CAT Work Experience Calculation: In Days<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2863\\\" data-end=\\\"2971\\\">Candidates may need to enter total work experience <strong data-start=\\\"2914\\\" data-end=\\\"2925\\\">in days<\\/strong> as of the specified cut-off date in the form.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2973\\\" data-end=\\\"3060\\\">This means the total number of qualifying full-time workdays completed up to that date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"2nbowt\\\" data-start=\\\"3067\\\" data-end=\\\"3111\\\">How to Calculate Work Experience Correctly<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3113\\\" data-end=\\\"3117\\\">Use:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3119\\\" data-end=\\\"3295\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dmjrv4\\\" data-start=\\\"3119\\\" data-end=\\\"3142\\\">Joining date of job<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dk11q5\\\" data-start=\\\"3143\\\" data-end=\\\"3200\\\">Last working date (or cut-off date if still employed)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jbo9lv\\\" data-start=\\\"3201\\\" data-end=\\\"3247\\\">Exclude non-qualifying periods if required<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"t1wwi8\\\" data-start=\\\"3248\\\" data-end=\\\"3295\\\">Subtract break periods separately where asked<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1c54mul\\\" data-start=\\\"3297\\\" data-end=\\\"3307\\\">Example<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3309\\\" data-end=\\\"3446\\\">If you joined on 1 August 2023 and valid cut-off is 31 July 2025, then calculate total qualifying days from joining date to cut-off date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3448\\\" data-end=\\\"3492\\\">Use exact dates rather than guessing months.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1sh07gh\\\" data-start=\\\"3499\\\" data-end=\\\"3532\\\">Should Ongoing Job Be Included?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3534\\\" data-end=\\\"3651\\\">Yes, if you are still working and the form asks for experience up to a specific date, calculate only up to that date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3653\\\" data-end=\\\"3715\\\">Do not include future months that have not yet been completed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1b6psav\\\" data-start=\\\"3722\\\" data-end=\\\"3751\\\">Break in Experience Meaning<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3753\\\" data-end=\\\"3808\\\">The form may ask for <strong data-start=\\\"3774\\\" data-end=\\\"3807\\\">Break in Experience (in days)<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3810\\\" data-end=\\\"3894\\\">This means gaps between jobs or periods where you were not in qualifying employment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3896\\\" data-end=\\\"3905\\\">Examples:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3907\\\" data-end=\\\"4055\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"18a6aln\\\" data-start=\\\"3907\\\" data-end=\\\"3946\\\">Resigned and unemployed for 45 days<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"d3c9ef\\\" data-start=\\\"3947\\\" data-end=\\\"3979\\\">Career gap between companies<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"hrib29\\\" data-start=\\\"3980\\\" data-end=\\\"4011\\\">Study break before next job<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1voyl6n\\\" data-start=\\\"4012\\\" data-end=\\\"4055\\\">Personal break before rejoining workforce<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"9erkvl\\\" data-start=\\\"4062\\\" data-end=\\\"4097\\\">What to Enter if No Break Exists?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4099\\\" data-end=\\\"4206\\\">If no gap exists between qualifying jobs and instructions ask for break days, candidates may need to enter:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4208\\\" data-end=\\\"4213\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4208\\\" data-end=\\\"4213\\\">0<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4215\\\" data-end=\\\"4259\\\">Always follow the current form instructions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ye1633\\\" data-start=\\\"4266\\\" data-end=\\\"4304\\\">How to Calculate Break in Experience<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4306\\\" data-end=\\\"4355\\\">Add all qualifying non-working gaps between jobs.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1c54mul\\\" data-start=\\\"4357\\\" data-end=\\\"4367\\\">Example<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4369\\\" data-end=\\\"4424\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15n46ee\\\" data-start=\\\"4369\\\" data-end=\\\"4396\\\">Job 1 ended on 31 March<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jxgfy0\\\" data-start=\\\"4397\\\" data-end=\\\"4424\\\">Job 2 started on 1 June<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4426\\\" data-end=\\\"4451\\\">Approximate gap = 61 days<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4453\\\" data-end=\\\"4519\\\">If multiple gaps exist, total them if required by the form format.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1rac6u0\\\" data-start=\\\"4526\\\" data-end=\\\"4582\\\">Documents to Keep Ready Before Filling Work Experience<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4584\\\" data-end=\\\"4592\\\">Prepare:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4594\\\" data-end=\\\"4739\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"11ia3da\\\" data-start=\\\"4594\\\" data-end=\\\"4610\\\">Offer letter<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"19q8h3o\\\" data-start=\\\"4611\\\" data-end=\\\"4629\\\">Joining letter<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1le0ryv\\\" data-start=\\\"4630\\\" data-end=\\\"4650\\\">Relieving letter<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"hsdns\\\" data-start=\\\"4651\\\" data-end=\\\"4672\\\">Experience letter<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"132rbft\\\" data-start=\\\"4673\\\" data-end=\\\"4689\\\">Salary slips<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1pb6ajw\\\" data-start=\\\"4690\\\" data-end=\\\"4704\\\">HR records<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"u5pocb\\\" data-start=\\\"4705\\\" data-end=\\\"4739\\\">Employment start and end dates<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4741\\\" data-end=\\\"4776\\\">These help avoid incorrect entries.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"pkrxpt\\\" data-start=\\\"4783\\\" data-end=\\\"4829\\\">Why Honest Work Experience Entry Is Critical<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4831\\\" data-end=\\\"4883\\\">Institutes may verify work experience later through:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4885\\\" data-end=\\\"4997\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"oz9fxs\\\" data-start=\\\"4885\\\" data-end=\\\"4912\\\">Experience certificates<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"132rbft\\\" data-start=\\\"4913\\\" data-end=\\\"4929\\\">Salary slips<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"x6c4gb\\\" data-start=\\\"4930\\\" data-end=\\\"4949\\\">HR verification<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"gq5dlb\\\" data-start=\\\"4950\\\" data-end=\\\"4975\\\">Interview questioning<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"2pzueu\\\" data-start=\\\"4976\\\" data-end=\\\"4997\\\">Joining documents<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4999\\\" data-end=\\\"5072\\\">If inflated or false claims are found, it can harm candidature seriously.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"kh35p\\\" data-start=\\\"5079\\\" data-end=\\\"5136\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid in CAT Work Experience Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"sn6uiq\\\" data-start=\\\"5138\\\" data-end=\\\"5174\\\">Counting Internship as Experience<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5176\\\" data-end=\\\"5254\\\">Internships are usually separate and not counted as full-time work experience.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"d43y1o\\\" data-start=\\\"5256\\\" data-end=\\\"5291\\\">Including Work Before Graduation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5293\\\" data-end=\\\"5354\\\">Only qualifying post-graduation experience should be entered.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"79iu2o\\\" data-start=\\\"5356\\\" data-end=\\\"5396\\\">Estimating by Months Instead of Dates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5398\\\" data-end=\\\"5432\\\">Always calculate properly in days.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"l8i2hr\\\" data-start=\\\"5434\\\" data-end=\\\"5457\\\">Ignoring Career Gaps<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5459\\\" data-end=\\\"5506\\\">Break periods should be entered where required.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"11sco8v\\\" data-start=\\\"5508\\\" data-end=\\\"5535\\\">Adding Future Experience<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5537\\\" data-end=\\\"5580\\\">Count only till the specified cut-off date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"6c5tew\\\" data-start=\\\"5582\\\" data-end=\\\"5606\\\">Exaggerating Job Role<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5608\\\" data-end=\\\"5654\\\">Interview panels often detect inconsistencies.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"854c4o\\\" data-start=\\\"5661\\\" data-end=\\\"5704\\\">Does Work Experience Guarantee Admission?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5706\\\" data-end=\\\"5875\\\">No. Work experience can strengthen profile value in some institutes, but CAT score, academics, interviews, written rounds, and overall profile also matter significantly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5877\\\" data-end=\\\"5916\\\">Freshers also get admission every year.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1udsib5\\\" data-start=\\\"5923\\\" data-end=\\\"5977\\\">Best Strategy for Freshers vs Experienced Candidates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"13u5k6j\\\" data-start=\\\"5979\\\" data-end=\\\"5990\\\">Freshers<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5992\\\" data-end=\\\"6078\\\">Focus strongly on CAT percentile, academics, communication, and interview preparation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"ctjwyh\\\" data-start=\\\"6080\\\" data-end=\\\"6105\\\">Experienced Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6107\\\" data-end=\\\"6228\\\">Use work achievements, leadership examples, business understanding, and problem-solving experience to strengthen profile.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" PROGRAMMES\",\"name\":\"_programmes\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"98\\\" data-end=\\\"484\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"102\\\" data-end=\\\"137\\\">CAT Programme Selection section<\\/strong> is one of the most strategic parts of the CAT application form. Many candidates focus only on exam preparation and fill this section quickly without understanding its long-term impact. However, the programmes you select here can directly influence your chances of receiving admission opportunities from participating institutes after CAT results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"486\\\" data-end=\\\"714\\\">This section generally allows candidates to choose management programmes and preferred interview cities for selected programmes. A wrong decision here can limit future options, while a smart selection can increase opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"716\\\" data-end=\\\"915\\\">This complete guide explains how to fill the CAT Programme Selection section properly, how to choose programmes wisely, how interview city preference works, and what mistakes candidates should avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<hr data-start=\\\"917\\\" data-end=\\\"920\\\">\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1eyqgvn\\\" data-start=\\\"922\\\" data-end=\\\"968\\\">What Is the CAT Programme Selection Section?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"970\\\" data-end=\\\"1106\\\">In this section, candidates may be allowed to choose programmes offered through the CAT admission process from participating institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1108\\\" data-end=\\\"1193\\\">Depending on the form year, this may include different management programmes such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1195\\\" data-end=\\\"1349\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16vahra\\\" data-start=\\\"1195\\\" data-end=\\\"1202\\\">MBA<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"12w8o6w\\\" data-start=\\\"1203\\\" data-end=\\\"1233\\\">PGDM-equivalent programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"11bavs0\\\" data-start=\\\"1234\\\" data-end=\\\"1252\\\">PGP programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ny2ptz\\\" data-start=\\\"1253\\\" data-end=\\\"1290\\\">Specialized management programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"swo5f9\\\" data-start=\\\"1291\\\" data-end=\\\"1349\\\">Executive \\/ sector-focused programmes (where applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1351\\\" data-end=\\\"1464\\\">Candidates should choose programmes carefully based on eligibility, interest, profile strength, and career goals.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"v2pqeb\\\" data-start=\\\"1471\\\" data-end=\\\"1501\\\">Select All Programmes Option<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1503\\\" data-end=\\\"1575\\\">The form may provide a <strong data-start=\\\"1526\\\" data-end=\\\"1540\\\">Select All<\\/strong> checkbox above the programme list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1577\\\" data-end=\\\"1657\\\">When selected, this may automatically mark all available programmes in the list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"cyo3nc\\\" data-start=\\\"1664\\\" data-end=\\\"1694\\\">Should You Use &ldquo;Select All&rdquo;?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1696\\\" data-end=\\\"1726\\\">This depends on your strategy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"2btl73\\\" data-start=\\\"1728\\\" data-end=\\\"1760\\\">When Select All Can Be Useful<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1762\\\" data-end=\\\"1922\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"x54tu8\\\" data-start=\\\"1762\\\" data-end=\\\"1796\\\">You want maximum opportunities<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1766j1k\\\" data-start=\\\"1797\\\" data-end=\\\"1836\\\">You are open to multiple institutes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"146tn5p\\\" data-start=\\\"1837\\\" data-end=\\\"1885\\\">You are flexible with specialization choices<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dbfunm\\\" data-start=\\\"1886\\\" data-end=\\\"1922\\\">You want broader admission chances<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1haphju\\\" data-start=\\\"1924\\\" data-end=\\\"1959\\\">When Select All May Not Be Ideal<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1961\\\" data-end=\\\"2154\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bbncxy\\\" data-start=\\\"1961\\\" data-end=\\\"2011\\\">You are interested only in specific programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"vgnb76\\\" data-start=\\\"2012\\\" data-end=\\\"2063\\\">You do not meet eligibility for certain courses<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"htymby\\\" data-start=\\\"2064\\\" data-end=\\\"2101\\\">You have a clear career direction<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"17qdnvw\\\" data-start=\\\"2102\\\" data-end=\\\"2154\\\">You do not want unwanted calls or future confusion<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2156\\\" data-end=\\\"2217\\\">Blindly selecting everything is not always the smartest move.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"vz1sb7\\\" data-start=\\\"2224\\\" data-end=\\\"2258\\\">How to Choose Programmes Smartly<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2260\\\" data-end=\\\"2322\\\">Instead of random selection, evaluate each programme based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2324\\\" data-end=\\\"2564\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"v3akl8\\\" data-start=\\\"2324\\\" data-end=\\\"2340\\\">Career goals<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1q9w8jm\\\" data-start=\\\"2341\\\" data-end=\\\"2369\\\">Preferred specialization<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"e37z7\\\" data-start=\\\"2370\\\" data-end=\\\"2393\\\">Academic background<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1gezcbg\\\" data-start=\\\"2394\\\" data-end=\\\"2421\\\">Work experience profile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ftq93d\\\" data-start=\\\"2422\\\" data-end=\\\"2449\\\">Future salary potential<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1gffeaw\\\" data-start=\\\"2450\\\" data-end=\\\"2478\\\">Brand value of institute<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"6vgvgu\\\" data-start=\\\"2479\\\" data-end=\\\"2502\\\">Location preference<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15n0cob\\\" data-start=\\\"2503\\\" data-end=\\\"2524\\\">Competition level<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1wxiaq\\\" data-start=\\\"2525\\\" data-end=\\\"2541\\\">Fees and ROI<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"k3bggo\\\" data-start=\\\"2542\\\" data-end=\\\"2564\\\">Long-term career fit<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"zptzai\\\" data-start=\\\"2571\\\" data-end=\\\"2609\\\">Examples of Smart Programme Strategy<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"14k8smw\\\" data-start=\\\"2611\\\" data-end=\\\"2645\\\">Candidate Interested in Finance<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2647\\\" data-end=\\\"2704\\\">May prioritize general MBA + finance-friendly institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"j8c2qp\\\" data-start=\\\"2706\\\" data-end=\\\"2737\\\">Candidate with IT Background<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2739\\\" data-end=\\\"2808\\\">May choose analytics, operations, tech-management aligned programmes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"qi2k25\\\" data-start=\\\"2810\\\" data-end=\\\"2830\\\">Fresher Candidate<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2832\\\" data-end=\\\"2882\\\">May prefer flagship general management programmes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"2jh38q\\\" data-start=\\\"2884\\\" data-end=\\\"2908\\\">Experienced Candidate<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2910\\\" data-end=\\\"2987\\\">May also consider executive-style or profile-friendly options where eligible.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"33zo4l\\\" data-start=\\\"2994\\\" data-end=\\\"3025\\\">CAT Interview City Preference<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3027\\\" data-end=\\\"3148\\\">After selecting a programme, candidates may need to choose an <strong data-start=\\\"3089\\\" data-end=\\\"3107\\\">Interview City<\\/strong> for that programme from a dropdown list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3150\\\" data-end=\\\"3229\\\">This city preference may be relevant for later selection stages if shortlisted.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"wezhit\\\" data-start=\\\"3236\\\" data-end=\\\"3276\\\">How to Choose Interview City Correctly<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3278\\\" data-end=\\\"3323\\\">Choose a city based on practical convenience:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3325\\\" data-end=\\\"3499\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1vuwi4r\\\" data-start=\\\"3325\\\" data-end=\\\"3365\\\">Closest major city to your residence<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"az5v7c\\\" data-start=\\\"3366\\\" data-end=\\\"3387\\\">Lower travel cost<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1nl2v1g\\\" data-start=\\\"3388\\\" data-end=\\\"3411\\\">Easier connectivity<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"7obhsv\\\" data-start=\\\"3412\\\" data-end=\\\"3437\\\">Comfortable logistics<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1he5pn2\\\" data-start=\\\"3438\\\" data-end=\\\"3463\\\">Safer travel planning<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5fmp9r\\\" data-start=\\\"3464\\\" data-end=\\\"3499\\\">Backup accommodation availability<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1oc3dsj\\\" data-start=\\\"3506\\\" data-end=\\\"3536\\\">Best Interview City Strategy<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1nkh6k\\\" data-start=\\\"3538\\\" data-end=\\\"3567\\\">If You Live in North India<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3569\\\" data-end=\\\"3618\\\">Choose nearest practical metro or available city.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"po0dzn\\\" data-start=\\\"3620\\\" data-end=\\\"3651\\\">If You Work in Another State<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3653\\\" data-end=\\\"3698\\\">Choose city near current workplace if easier.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1vi824u\\\" data-start=\\\"3700\\\" data-end=\\\"3727\\\">If You Frequently Travel<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3729\\\" data-end=\\\"3789\\\">Choose city with best connectivity rather than nearest only.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"5rs79b\\\" data-start=\\\"3796\\\" data-end=\\\"3830\\\">Important Note on Interview City<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3832\\\" data-end=\\\"4009\\\">Selecting an interview city does not guarantee final allotment there in every situation. Final arrangements depend on official processes, seat availability, and institute rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4011\\\" data-end=\\\"4054\\\">Always check latest official updates later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"fyl5e4\\\" data-start=\\\"4061\\\" data-end=\\\"4124\\\">Why Programme Selection Is More Important Than Students Think<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4126\\\" data-end=\\\"4219\\\">Many candidates assume CAT score alone matters. But programme selection also matters because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4221\\\" data-end=\\\"4422\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"14dx018\\\" data-start=\\\"4221\\\" data-end=\\\"4277\\\">Unselected programmes may close future opportunities<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1wvhncp\\\" data-start=\\\"4278\\\" data-end=\\\"4332\\\">Some candidates forget niche high-value programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bp17a0\\\" data-start=\\\"4333\\\" data-end=\\\"4380\\\">Some select too narrowly and reduce chances<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"10gfrmk\\\" data-start=\\\"4381\\\" data-end=\\\"4422\\\">Some ignore profile-suitable programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4424\\\" data-end=\\\"4487\\\">A good CAT score cannot help in a programme you never selected.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1ypawym\\\" data-start=\\\"4494\\\" data-end=\\\"4545\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid in CAT Programme Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1e67gaq\\\" data-start=\\\"4547\\\" data-end=\\\"4579\\\">Randomly Selecting Everything<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4581\\\" data-end=\\\"4608\\\">Can create confusion later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1negfri\\\" data-start=\\\"4610\\\" data-end=\\\"4640\\\">Selecting Only Famous Names<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4642\\\" data-end=\\\"4684\\\">May miss excellent emerging opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3>Ignoring Career Fit<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4710\\\" data-end=\\\"4753\\\">Prestige alone should not decide selection.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1rp3ddv\\\" data-start=\\\"4755\\\" data-end=\\\"4785\\\">Wrong Interview City Choice<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4787\\\" data-end=\\\"4830\\\">May create travel stress during interviews.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"wki16u\\\" data-start=\\\"4832\\\" data-end=\\\"4861\\\">Not Researching Programmes<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4863\\\" data-end=\\\"4911\\\">Different institutes offer different structures.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"neqs42\\\" data-start=\\\"4913\\\" data-end=\\\"4938\\\">Waiting Until Last Day<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4940\\\" data-end=\\\"4985\\\">Rushed decisions often become poor decisions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"p8f72k\\\" data-start=\\\"4992\\\" data-end=\\\"5033\\\">Should Freshers Select More Programmes?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5035\\\" data-end=\\\"5132\\\">Often yes, because broader options may help maximize chances, depending on eligibility and goals.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5134\\\" data-end=\\\"5189\\\">However, choices should still be thoughtful&mdash;not random.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"jbapp5\\\" data-start=\\\"5196\\\" data-end=\\\"5241\\\">Should Experienced Candidates Be Selective?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5243\\\" data-end=\\\"5384\\\">Often yes. Candidates with work experience may target programmes aligned with career progression, industry switch, leadership growth, or ROI.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1c8hz0n\\\" data-start=\\\"5391\\\" data-end=\\\"5434\\\">Best Approach Before Clicking Save &amp; Next<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5436\\\" data-end=\\\"5454\\\">Before proceeding:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5456\\\" data-end=\\\"5630\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"3bdcut\\\" data-start=\\\"5456\\\" data-end=\\\"5490\\\">Review all selected programmes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"vtkxxk\\\" data-start=\\\"5491\\\" data-end=\\\"5527\\\">Check interview city preferences<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"pz6qz\\\" data-start=\\\"5528\\\" data-end=\\\"5558\\\">Remove unwanted selections<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1pfsqzs\\\" data-start=\\\"5559\\\" data-end=\\\"5592\\\">Confirm eligibility alignment<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1i2ipv4\\\" data-start=\\\"5593\\\" data-end=\\\"5630\\\">Ensure no accidental missed choices<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"azcjo4\\\" data-start=\\\"5637\\\" data-end=\\\"5673\\\">Hidden Risk Most Candidates Ignore<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5675\\\" data-end=\\\"5846\\\">Some candidates realize after result declaration that they forgot to select a desirable programme earlier. By then, correction opportunities may be limited or unavailable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5848\\\" data-end=\\\"5927\\\">This is why programme selection deserves serious attention during form filling.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" TEST CITY \",\"name\":\"_test_city_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"94\\\" data-end=\\\"472\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"98\\\" data-end=\\\"134\\\">CAT Test City Preference section<\\/strong> is one of the most important parts of the CAT application form because it decides where you may be allotted your examination centre. Many candidates ignore this section and randomly select cities, but a poor choice can create travel stress, higher expenses, long-distance movement, late reporting risk, and unnecessary exam-day pressure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"474\\\" data-end=\\\"805\\\">The CAT form generally allows candidates to choose <strong data-start=\\\"525\\\" data-end=\\\"555\\\">five different test cities<\\/strong> in order of preference. After the registration process closes, one city may be allotted based on availability and administrative planning. Because of this, candidates should make smart and practical choices instead of emotional or random selections.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"807\\\" data-end=\\\"984\\\">This complete guide explains how CAT test city preference works, how to choose five cities wisely, common mistakes to avoid, and the best strategy for stress-free exam planning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"15flhph\\\" data-start=\\\"991\\\" data-end=\\\"1038\\\">What Is the CAT Test City Preference Section?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1040\\\" data-end=\\\"1155\\\">In this section, candidates are usually asked to choose <strong data-start=\\\"1096\\\" data-end=\\\"1130\\\">five different CAT exam cities<\\/strong> from the available list.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1157\\\" data-end=\\\"1211\\\">These cities are entered in preference order, meaning:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1213\\\" data-end=\\\"1381\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"b4ixa0\\\" data-start=\\\"1213\\\" data-end=\\\"1251\\\">Preference 1 = Most preferred city<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"19sxosn\\\" data-start=\\\"1252\\\" data-end=\\\"1284\\\">Preference 2 = Second choice<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"lddwxh\\\" data-start=\\\"1285\\\" data-end=\\\"1316\\\">Preference 3 = Third choice<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ovyt5v\\\" data-start=\\\"1317\\\" data-end=\\\"1349\\\">Preference 4 = Fourth choice<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ld3xxh\\\" data-start=\\\"1350\\\" data-end=\\\"1381\\\">Preference 5 = Fifth choice<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1383\\\" data-end=\\\"1480\\\">The final allotment is generally based on seat availability, capacity, and official arrangements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"10nuzvq\\\" data-start=\\\"1487\\\" data-end=\\\"1532\\\">How Many Cities Can You Choose in CAT Form?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1534\\\" data-end=\\\"1587\\\">Candidates may select <strong data-start=\\\"1556\\\" data-end=\\\"1586\\\">five different test cities<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1x60uzx\\\" data-start=\\\"1589\\\" data-end=\\\"1606\\\">Important Rule<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1608\\\" data-end=\\\"1694\\\">The same city usually cannot be selected more than once in different preference slots.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1696\\\" data-end=\\\"1747\\\">That means each preference should be a unique city.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"15vxwvb\\\" data-start=\\\"1754\\\" data-end=\\\"1797\\\">How CAT Exam City Allotment Usually Works<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1799\\\" data-end=\\\"1889\\\">After the registration deadline, one of your selected cities may be allotted depending on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1891\\\" data-end=\\\"2031\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"17iivu\\\" data-start=\\\"1891\\\" data-end=\\\"1912\\\">Seat availability<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tchg5e\\\" data-start=\\\"1913\\\" data-end=\\\"1950\\\">Number of applicants in each city<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1lbqw1j\\\" data-start=\\\"1951\\\" data-end=\\\"1970\\\">Centre capacity<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ebdell\\\" data-start=\\\"1971\\\" data-end=\\\"1998\\\">Administrative planning<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"3oo9r4\\\" data-start=\\\"1999\\\" data-end=\\\"2031\\\">Regional demand distribution<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"qxlgtc\\\" data-start=\\\"2038\\\" data-end=\\\"2090\\\">What If None of My Preferred Cities Are Available?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2092\\\" data-end=\\\"2194\\\">In some cases, if none of the five selected cities can be allotted, a <strong data-start=\\\"2162\\\" data-end=\\\"2177\\\">nearby city<\\/strong> may be assigned.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2196\\\" data-end=\\\"2302\\\">This is why your choices should be geographically practical and not scattered randomly across the country.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"vexjqn\\\" data-start=\\\"2309\\\" data-end=\\\"2352\\\">Best Strategy to Choose 5 CAT Test Cities<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"ytsf7t\\\" data-start=\\\"2354\\\" data-end=\\\"2404\\\">Preference 1: Closest and Most Comfortable City<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2406\\\" data-end=\\\"2488\\\">Choose the city nearest to your home or current residence with easy travel access.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"vkr8ak\\\" data-start=\\\"2490\\\" data-end=\\\"2525\\\">Preference 2: Nearby Backup City<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2527\\\" data-end=\\\"2582\\\">Select another nearby city with good transport options.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"14rey2b\\\" data-start=\\\"2584\\\" data-end=\\\"2622\\\">Preference 3: Strong Alternate City<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2624\\\" data-end=\\\"2686\\\">Choose a city where you have family, friends, or stay options.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"dmqylx\\\" data-start=\\\"2688\\\" data-end=\\\"2730\\\">Preference 4: Practical Regional Option<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2732\\\" data-end=\\\"2803\\\">Select a city in the same state or nearby state with manageable travel.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 data-section-id=\\\"aq834s\\\" data-start=\\\"2805\\\" data-end=\\\"2841\\\">Preference 5: Broad Safety Choice<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2843\\\" data-end=\\\"2913\\\">Choose a city likely to have multiple centres and better availability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1ur63rx\\\" data-start=\\\"2920\\\" data-end=\\\"2959\\\">How to Choose CAT Test Cities Smartly<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2961\\\" data-end=\\\"2989\\\">Evaluate each city based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2991\\\" data-end=\\\"3200\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ikayb6\\\" data-start=\\\"2991\\\" data-end=\\\"3013\\\">Distance from home<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"omyv81\\\" data-start=\\\"3014\\\" data-end=\\\"3051\\\">Train \\/ bus \\/ flight connectivity<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"fdgfr9\\\" data-start=\\\"3052\\\" data-end=\\\"3067\\\">Travel time<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ze3cz\\\" data-start=\\\"3068\\\" data-end=\\\"3090\\\">Hotel availability<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"b9oz1w\\\" data-start=\\\"3091\\\" data-end=\\\"3101\\\">Safety<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1xt4wq8\\\" data-start=\\\"3102\\\" data-end=\\\"3124\\\">Weather conditions<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"19n9bwy\\\" data-start=\\\"3125\\\" data-end=\\\"3143\\\">Cost of travel<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"dfx0iu\\\" data-start=\\\"3144\\\" data-end=\\\"3173\\\">Familiarity with location<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"9bamqc\\\" data-start=\\\"3174\\\" data-end=\\\"3200\\\">Backup stay arrangements<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3386\\\" data-end=\\\"3440\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"87q1jk\\\" data-start=\\\"3447\\\" data-end=\\\"3480\\\">Common Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"aifi7e\\\" data-start=\\\"3482\\\" data-end=\\\"3518\\\">Choosing Only Famous Metro Cities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3520\\\" data-end=\\\"3568\\\">Large demand can increase competition for seats.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1rz1a1e\\\" data-start=\\\"3570\\\" data-end=\\\"3599\\\">Choosing Random Far Cities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3601\\\" data-end=\\\"3626\\\">May create travel burden.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1swipuu\\\" data-start=\\\"3628\\\" data-end=\\\"3654\\\">Ignoring Backup Options<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3656\\\" data-end=\\\"3694\\\">Always include practical alternatives.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"dbpaoe\\\" data-start=\\\"3696\\\" data-end=\\\"3720\\\">Selecting Emotionally<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3722\\\" data-end=\\\"3769\\\">Choose based on logistics, not city popularity.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"mwgsgu\\\" data-start=\\\"3771\\\" data-end=\\\"3802\\\">Ignoring Weather or Distance<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3804\\\" data-end=\\\"3866\\\">Winter fog, traffic, or long travel can affect reporting time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1clc2u7\\\" data-start=\\\"3873\\\" data-end=\\\"3916\\\">Should I Choose All Cities in One Region?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3918\\\" data-end=\\\"3944\\\">Usually yes, if practical.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3946\\\" data-end=\\\"4058\\\">Choosing cities within reachable distance often reduces travel risk if you are allotted a lower preference city.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1lccn9t\\\" data-start=\\\"4065\\\" data-end=\\\"4103\\\">Should I Choose Cities Across India?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4105\\\" data-end=\\\"4165\\\">Usually not unless you have flexibility or specific reasons.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4167\\\" data-end=\\\"4281\\\">Randomly mixing North, South, East, and West India cities can create major travel stress if allotted unexpectedly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1423gtk\\\" data-start=\\\"4288\\\" data-end=\\\"4322\\\">Hidden Risk Most Students Ignore<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4324\\\" data-end=\\\"4507\\\">Many candidates focus only on getting a nearby city but ignore <strong data-start=\\\"4387\\\" data-end=\\\"4405\\\">reporting time<\\/strong>. Even a city 100 km away can be difficult if the exam slot is early morning and transport is limited.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4509\\\" data-end=\\\"4584\\\">Choose cities where same-day travel is realistic or overnight stay is easy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"11ojyap\\\" data-start=\\\"4591\\\" data-end=\\\"4627\\\">What Happens After City Selection?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4629\\\" data-end=\\\"4754\\\">After allotment, the exact exam centre address, reporting time, and slot are generally provided later through the admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4756\\\" data-end=\\\"4814\\\">City preference does not mean you choose the exact centre.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ldfypb\\\" data-start=\\\"4821\\\" data-end=\\\"4854\\\">Can Test City Be Changed Later?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4856\\\" data-end=\\\"5018\\\">Usually changes after final submission are limited or unavailable unless official correction windows are announced. Therefore, choose carefully before submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"z9qaxl\\\" data-start=\\\"5025\\\" data-end=\\\"5070\\\">Final Checklist Before Clicking Save &amp; Next<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5072\\\" data-end=\\\"5270\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"3pvfuv\\\" data-start=\\\"5072\\\" data-end=\\\"5105\\\">All five cities are different<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1eqm3e6\\\" data-start=\\\"5106\\\" data-end=\\\"5141\\\">Preference order is intentional<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dxtk9z\\\" data-start=\\\"5142\\\" data-end=\\\"5168\\\">Travel options checked<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"k00ke7\\\" data-start=\\\"5169\\\" data-end=\\\"5195\\\">Backup cities included<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1cu44s3\\\" data-start=\\\"5196\\\" data-end=\\\"5236\\\">No unrealistic distant city selected<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"woa6bp\\\" data-start=\\\"5237\\\" data-end=\\\"5270\\\">Comfortable options prioritized<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5592\\\" data-end=\\\"5666\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" DECLARATION\",\"name\":\"_declaration\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"111\\\" data-end=\\\"467\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"115\\\" data-end=\\\"146\\\">CAT application fee section<\\/strong> is the final and one of the most important stages of the CAT application form. Many candidates complete all details carefully but make mistakes during payment, preview verification, transaction handling, or confirmation tracking. Even a small error at this stage can delay or interrupt successful application submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"469\\\" data-end=\\\"667\\\">Your CAT registration is generally considered complete only after successful fee payment and final submission. Therefore, candidates should understand the payment process properly before proceeding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"669\\\" data-end=\\\"850\\\">This complete guide explains CAT application fees, category-wise charges, payment steps, confirmation process, transaction issues, helpdesk support, and important mistakes to avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"189jn85\\\" data-start=\\\"857\\\" data-end=\\\"914\\\">CAT Application Fee 2026 (Based on Mentioned Structure)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"916\\\" data-end=\\\"968\\\">The fee structure mentioned in the provided data is:<\\/p>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"TyagGW_tableContainer\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\">\\r\\n<table class=\\\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\\\" data-start=\\\"970\\\" data-end=\\\"1087\\\">\\r\\n<thead data-start=\\\"970\\\" data-end=\\\"1010\\\">\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"970\\\" data-end=\\\"1010\\\">\\r\\n<th class=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"970\\\" data-end=\\\"991\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Candidate Category<\\/th>\\r\\n<th class=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"991\\\" data-end=\\\"1010\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Application Fee<\\/th>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/thead>\\r\\n<tbody data-start=\\\"1021\\\" data-end=\\\"1087\\\">\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"1021\\\" data-end=\\\"1058\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"1021\\\" data-end=\\\"1046\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">General \\/ EWS \\/ NC-OBC<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"1046\\\" data-end=\\\"1058\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Rs. 2600<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"1059\\\" data-end=\\\"1087\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"1059\\\" data-end=\\\"1075\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">SC \\/ ST \\/ PwD<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"1075\\\" data-end=\\\"1087\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Rs. 1300<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<blockquote data-start=\\\"1089\\\" data-end=\\\"1228\\\">\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1091\\\" data-end=\\\"1228\\\">Final fee for future sessions may change officially. Candidates should always verify the latest amount during the live application cycle.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/blockquote>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1sev5ue\\\" data-start=\\\"1235\\\" data-end=\\\"1273\\\">Why CAT Application Fee Is Important<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1275\\\" data-end=\\\"1339\\\">Payment is not just a formal step. It is generally required for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1341\\\" data-end=\\\"1520\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"yvpzfj\\\" data-start=\\\"1341\\\" data-end=\\\"1376\\\">Final submission of application<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"sq4xct\\\" data-start=\\\"1377\\\" data-end=\\\"1404\\\">Registration completion<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"cz9c02\\\" data-start=\\\"1405\\\" data-end=\\\"1442\\\">Admit card generation eligibility<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1yr1tef\\\" data-start=\\\"1443\\\" data-end=\\\"1483\\\">Official application record creation<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"uvu97a\\\" data-start=\\\"1484\\\" data-end=\\\"1520\\\">Candidate dashboard confirmation<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1522\\\" data-end=\\\"1588\\\">Without successful payment, the application may remain incomplete.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1s9tpei\\\" data-start=\\\"1595\\\" data-end=\\\"1614\\\">CAT Payment Modes<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1616\\\" data-end=\\\"1699\\\">Candidates may need to choose a payment mode available through the official portal.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1701\\\" data-end=\\\"1771\\\">The form generally activates the payment gateway after mode selection.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1773\\\" data-end=\\\"1808\\\">Common payment methods may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1810\\\" data-end=\\\"1929\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"124dfgi\\\" data-start=\\\"1810\\\" data-end=\\\"1824\\\">Debit Card<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"4f8o4x\\\" data-start=\\\"1825\\\" data-end=\\\"1840\\\">Credit Card<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"181u65t\\\" data-start=\\\"1841\\\" data-end=\\\"1856\\\">Net Banking<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"rxzq0j\\\" data-start=\\\"1857\\\" data-end=\\\"1879\\\">UPI (if available)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"10g9pmk\\\" data-start=\\\"1880\\\" data-end=\\\"1929\\\">Wallet \\/ gateway-supported methods (if enabled)<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1931\\\" data-end=\\\"1993\\\">Available options depend on the official gateway at that time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1hxu1m4\\\" data-start=\\\"2000\\\" data-end=\\\"2032\\\">CAT Payment Partners Mentioned<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2034\\\" data-end=\\\"2093\\\">The provided information mentions payment partners such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2095\\\" data-end=\\\"2116\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8dyx96\\\" data-start=\\\"2095\\\" data-end=\\\"2107\\\">BillDesk<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"366pw5\\\" data-start=\\\"2108\\\" data-end=\\\"2116\\\">PayU<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2118\\\" data-end=\\\"2201\\\">Depending on selected mode, candidates may be redirected to the respective gateway.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1rozjei\\\" data-start=\\\"2208\\\" data-end=\\\"2242\\\">Step-by-Step CAT Payment Process<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1fd39gj\\\" data-start=\\\"2244\\\" data-end=\\\"2283\\\">Step 1: Preview the Application Form<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2285\\\" data-end=\\\"2369\\\">Before paying, use the <strong data-start=\\\"2308\\\" data-end=\\\"2331\\\">Preview Application<\\/strong> option to verify all entered details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2371\\\" data-end=\\\"2377\\\">Check:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2379\\\" data-end=\\\"2541\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1w9v2i1\\\" data-start=\\\"2379\\\" data-end=\\\"2396\\\">Name spelling<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"y682wg\\\" data-start=\\\"2397\\\" data-end=\\\"2414\\\">Date of birth<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1e0942g\\\" data-start=\\\"2415\\\" data-end=\\\"2427\\\">Category<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"a7xs2m\\\" data-start=\\\"2428\\\" data-end=\\\"2441\\\">Academics<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16ckp93\\\" data-start=\\\"2442\\\" data-end=\\\"2461\\\">Work experience<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"913q6m\\\" data-start=\\\"2462\\\" data-end=\\\"2485\\\">Programmes selected<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"48ekk1\\\" data-start=\\\"2486\\\" data-end=\\\"2511\\\">Test city preferences<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"d6swzf\\\" data-start=\\\"2512\\\" data-end=\\\"2541\\\">Photo and signature uploads<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2543\\\" data-end=\\\"2583\\\">This is one of the most important steps.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1te1su\\\" data-start=\\\"2590\\\" data-end=\\\"2629\\\">Step 2: Confirm Declaration Checkbox<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2631\\\" data-end=\\\"2728\\\">Candidates may need to tick the declaration confirming that the previewed information is correct.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2730\\\" data-end=\\\"2766\\\">Never tick without checking details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"g966ij\\\" data-start=\\\"2773\\\" data-end=\\\"2800\\\">Step 3: Complete CAPTCHA<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2802\\\" data-end=\\\"2848\\\">A CAPTCHA may be shown to verify human access.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2850\\\" data-end=\\\"2893\\\">If unclear, refresh and re-enter correctly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"192olwd\\\" data-start=\\\"2900\\\" data-end=\\\"2930\\\">Step 4: Choose Payment Mode<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2932\\\" data-end=\\\"2979\\\">Select your preferred available payment option.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"yi6lzp\\\" data-start=\\\"2986\\\" data-end=\\\"3017\\\">Step 5: Complete Transaction<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3019\\\" data-end=\\\"3128\\\">You may be redirected to the payment gateway page. Enter payment details carefully and wait for final status.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3130\\\" data-end=\\\"3174\\\">Do not refresh repeatedly during processing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1ifc2cg\\\" data-start=\\\"3181\\\" data-end=\\\"3221\\\">What Happens After Successful Payment?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3223\\\" data-end=\\\"3268\\\">After successful payment, candidates may see:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3270\\\" data-end=\\\"3416\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"wohmp1\\\" data-start=\\\"3270\\\" data-end=\\\"3300\\\">Payment Successful message<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"s8zu7a\\\" data-start=\\\"3301\\\" data-end=\\\"3338\\\">Transaction Number \\/ Reference ID<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"wfulmi\\\" data-start=\\\"3339\\\" data-end=\\\"3382\\\">Redirect back to CAT application portal<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"17obj1f\\\" data-start=\\\"3383\\\" data-end=\\\"3416\\\">Final submission confirmation<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3418\\\" data-end=\\\"3450\\\">Always save transaction details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"152z4u9\\\" data-start=\\\"3457\\\" data-end=\\\"3502\\\">Why Payment Transaction Number Is Important<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3504\\\" data-end=\\\"3561\\\">Keep your transaction number safe because it may help in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3563\\\" data-end=\\\"3655\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1vk2zcb\\\" data-start=\\\"3563\\\" data-end=\\\"3583\\\">Payment disputes<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16edwn7\\\" data-start=\\\"3584\\\" data-end=\\\"3613\\\">Failed confirmation cases<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"wv6pn3\\\" data-start=\\\"3614\\\" data-end=\\\"3634\\\">Helpdesk support<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"6vbtl2\\\" data-start=\\\"3635\\\" data-end=\\\"3655\\\">Future reference<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3657\\\" data-end=\\\"3687\\\">Take a screenshot immediately.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ya78pr\\\" data-start=\\\"3694\\\" data-end=\\\"3735\\\">CAT Confirmation Email After Submission<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3737\\\" data-end=\\\"3821\\\">Candidates may receive a confirmation email after successful application submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3823\\\" data-end=\\\"3846\\\">This email may confirm:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3848\\\" data-end=\\\"3982\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ply0sa\\\" data-start=\\\"3848\\\" data-end=\\\"3886\\\">Application submitted successfully<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"sq4xct\\\" data-start=\\\"3887\\\" data-end=\\\"3914\\\">Registration completion<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"18hoa1b\\\" data-start=\\\"3915\\\" data-end=\\\"3947\\\">Future communication details<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"13r4zii\\\" data-start=\\\"3948\\\" data-end=\\\"3982\\\">Admit card related updates later<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3984\\\" data-end=\\\"3997\\\">Always check:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3999\\\" data-end=\\\"4044\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"tfbo62\\\" data-start=\\\"3999\\\" data-end=\\\"4008\\\">Inbox<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"18bpsmp\\\" data-start=\\\"4009\\\" data-end=\\\"4024\\\">Spam folder<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1dlgfem\\\" data-start=\\\"4025\\\" data-end=\\\"4044\\\">Promotions folder<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1sgia69\\\" data-start=\\\"4051\\\" data-end=\\\"4084\\\">CAT Application Summary Meaning<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4086\\\" data-end=\\\"4159\\\">After login as a registered user, you may see an <strong data-start=\\\"4135\\\" data-end=\\\"4158\\\">Application Summary<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4161\\\" data-end=\\\"4217\\\">This is generally a read-only view of submitted details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4219\\\" data-end=\\\"4282\\\">Use it to verify saved records and keep screenshots\\/PDF copies.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"q35xbz\\\" data-start=\\\"4289\\\" data-end=\\\"4318\\\">Common CAT Payment Problems<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1jghysv\\\" data-start=\\\"4320\\\" data-end=\\\"4365\\\">Amount Debited but Application Not Updated<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4367\\\" data-end=\\\"4441\\\">Sometimes gateway delay happens. Wait some time and recheck portal status.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1qrtv83\\\" data-start=\\\"4443\\\" data-end=\\\"4475\\\">Page Refreshed During Payment<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4477\\\" data-end=\\\"4503\\\">Can interrupt transaction.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"185cmb0\\\" data-start=\\\"4505\\\" data-end=\\\"4528\\\">Wrong Card OTP Delay<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4530\\\" data-end=\\\"4548\\\">May cause timeout.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1o9wvio\\\" data-start=\\\"4550\\\" data-end=\\\"4577\\\">Weak Internet Connection<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4579\\\" data-end=\\\"4618\\\">Can create incomplete payment attempts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"bkte8h\\\" data-start=\\\"4620\\\" data-end=\\\"4648\\\">Multiple Payment Attempts<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4650\\\" data-end=\\\"4698\\\">Avoid repeated payments without checking status.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1muatev\\\" data-start=\\\"4705\\\" data-end=\\\"4735\\\">What to Do If Payment Fails?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4737\\\" data-end=\\\"4754\\\">If payment fails:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol data-start=\\\"4756\\\" data-end=\\\"4911\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jgvc6p\\\" data-start=\\\"4756\\\" data-end=\\\"4779\\\">Check bank message<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1enjmf9\\\" data-start=\\\"4780\\\" data-end=\\\"4809\\\">Re-login after some time<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5pyznl\\\" data-start=\\\"4810\\\" data-end=\\\"4836\\\">Verify payment status<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"k1lkqw\\\" data-start=\\\"4837\\\" data-end=\\\"4877\\\">Avoid panic re-payments immediately<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"rsgrzm\\\" data-start=\\\"4878\\\" data-end=\\\"4911\\\">Contact helpdesk if unresolved<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"7qkywn\\\" data-start=\\\"4918\\\" data-end=\\\"4942\\\">Is CAT Fee Refundable?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4944\\\" data-end=\\\"5094\\\">Application fees are usually non-refundable once successfully processed unless official exceptions are announced. Always verify details before paying.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"8avo1e\\\" data-start=\\\"5101\\\" data-end=\\\"5145\\\">Important Mistakes to Avoid Before Payment<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"188cr4m\\\" data-start=\\\"5147\\\" data-end=\\\"5174\\\">Wrong Category Selection<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5176\\\" data-end=\\\"5221\\\">Can affect fee amount and later verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1e1puc3\\\" data-start=\\\"5223\\\" data-end=\\\"5243\\\">Unchecked Preview<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5245\\\" data-end=\\\"5294\\\">Many candidates notice errors only after payment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"8rdtre\\\" data-start=\\\"5296\\\" data-end=\\\"5323\\\">Last-Minute Payment Rush<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5325\\\" data-end=\\\"5371\\\">Heavy traffic can create issues near deadline.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"bq147v\\\" data-start=\\\"5373\\\" data-end=\\\"5403\\\">Ignoring Email Confirmation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5405\\\" data-end=\\\"5441\\\">Always verify successful submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1lt5u6\\\" data-start=\\\"5443\\\" data-end=\\\"5469\\\">Using Unstable Internet<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5471\\\" data-end=\\\"5504\\\">Risky during gateway redirection.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"zxqb68\\\" data-start=\\\"5511\\\" data-end=\\\"5537\\\">Best Time to Pay CAT Fee<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5539\\\" data-end=\\\"5571\\\">Do not wait until the last date.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5573\\\" data-end=\\\"5587\\\">Best practice:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5589\\\" data-end=\\\"5689\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1h6fc1g\\\" data-start=\\\"5589\\\" data-end=\\\"5612\\\">Complete form early<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"23owx0\\\" data-start=\\\"5613\\\" data-end=\\\"5630\\\">Review calmly<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jc6mn7\\\" data-start=\\\"5631\\\" data-end=\\\"5658\\\">Pay during normal hours<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16b8evf\\\" data-start=\\\"5659\\\" data-end=\\\"5689\\\">Avoid deadline-night traffic<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"ap863j\\\" data-start=\\\"5696\\\" data-end=\\\"5750\\\">CAT Helpdesk Support (As Mentioned in Provided Data)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5752\\\" data-end=\\\"5914\\\">For registration, payment, uploading, and technical issues, candidates may use the grievance portal or official support channels available in the candidate login.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5916\\\" data-end=\\\"5945\\\">The provided details mention:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5947\\\" data-end=\\\"6031\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1oywk19\\\" data-start=\\\"5947\\\" data-end=\\\"6001\\\">Candidate Helpdesk Email: <a class=\\\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\" data-start=\\\"5975\\\" data-end=\\\"5999\\\">cathelpdesk@iimcat.co.in<\\/a><\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ppl821\\\" data-start=\\\"6002\\\" data-end=\\\"6031\\\">Toll Free: 1-800-210-0175<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6033\\\" data-end=\\\"6169\\\">For academic queries such as eligibility, category, or PwD documentation, separate CAT centre contacts may be provided during that year.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6171\\\" data-end=\\\"6242\\\">Always use the latest contact details available on the official portal.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1lhi53j\\\" data-start=\\\"6249\\\" data-end=\\\"6288\\\">Final Checklist Before Paying CAT Fee<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6290\\\" data-end=\\\"6517\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"h7208d\\\" data-start=\\\"6290\\\" data-end=\\\"6322\\\">All personal details correct<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ml6o6\\\" data-start=\\\"6323\\\" data-end=\\\"6343\\\">Category correct<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"z8ahlk\\\" data-start=\\\"6344\\\" data-end=\\\"6366\\\">Academics verified<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1q64is0\\\" data-start=\\\"6367\\\" data-end=\\\"6394\\\">Work experience checked<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"913q6m\\\" data-start=\\\"6395\\\" data-end=\\\"6418\\\">Programmes selected<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16batyu\\\" data-start=\\\"6419\\\" data-end=\\\"6443\\\">Test cities selected<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"rx8lxd\\\" data-start=\\\"6444\\\" data-end=\\\"6474\\\">Photo and signature proper<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1eacc2m\\\" data-start=\\\"6475\\\" data-end=\\\"6494\\\">Internet stable<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bptxeu\\\" data-start=\\\"6495\\\" data-end=\\\"6517\\\">Payment method ready<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', 3, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:51');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(629, 11, ' REGISTRATION  FEES ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" FEES\",\"name\":\"_fees\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates applying for the CAT exam are required to pay the prescribed registration fee during the online application process. The fee amount varies according to the candidate&rsquo;s category. Payment must be completed successfully for the application to be considered valid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Applicants should carefully verify their category, documents, and payment details before making the final transaction, as the registration fee is generally non-refundable once paid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category-Wise CAT Registration Fee<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The applicable registration fee is as follows:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC Category: \\u20b91300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST Category: \\u20b91300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD Category: \\u20b91300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All Other Candidates: \\u20b92600<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This fee structure provides concession benefits to candidates belonging to eligible reserved categories.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Single Fee for Multiple Institute Consideration<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates need to pay the registration fee only once during the CAT application process. Separate payments are not required for each IIM or participating institute selected in the application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One registration fee covers CAT application submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates can select eligible institutes as per the application process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No separate CAT exam fee is charged for each college choice at registration stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, some institutes may have separate admission stages later after CAT results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Documents for Reserved Categories<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates claiming concessional fee under reserved categories must upload valid supporting certificates during registration.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Required categories generally include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important points:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Documents should be clear and readable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name and details should match application form records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Invalid or unclear documents may create verification issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Non-Refundable Fee Policy<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should note that the CAT registration fee is generally non-refundable once paid, regardless of circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Refund is usually not available in cases such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong category selected<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Duplicate application submitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate decides not to appear for exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Incomplete form after payment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal change of plans<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document issues after submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, candidates must review all details carefully before final payment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended Payment Precautions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before making payment, candidates should verify the following:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct name and date of birth<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accurate category selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid mobile number and email ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Proper academic details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct fee amount displayed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stable internet connection during payment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These steps help avoid failed transactions or application errors.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice for Students<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates rush to complete payment and later discover mistakes in category, spelling, or uploaded documents. Since the fee is non-refundable, it is advisable to complete the form carefully, recheck every section, and proceed to payment only after full verification.<\\/p>\"}]', 5, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(630, 11, ' TEST CENTRES ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"CENTRES \",\"name\":\"centres_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam is conducted across a wide network of test centres in multiple cities throughout India to provide candidates with accessible exam locations. The examination is organized in computer-based mode, and candidates are required to appear only at the centre allotted to them through the official admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should understand that selecting preferred cities during registration does not guarantee the same city allotment. Final centre allocation depends on seat availability, administrative planning, and operational requirements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Availability of Test Cities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is generally conducted in approximately 170 test cities across India. These cities are selected to cover major regions and provide broad geographic access to candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important points:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Test centres are spread across multiple states and cities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Both metro and non-metro cities may be included<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final city list is published on the official CAT portal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Number of cities may vary slightly by admission cycle<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This broad network helps reduce travel burden for many applicants.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Test City Preference During Registration<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">At the time of application, candidates are usually asked to select preferred cities for appearing in the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should choose cities that are:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Easily reachable from their residence<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Connected by transport facilities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Practical in case of early morning reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Supported by backup travel options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choosing only distant cities may create avoidable stress later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Test Centre Allotment<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The exact test centre is assigned by the exam authorities after registration closes. Candidates can check the final details only through the admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card typically mentions:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Allotted city<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exact test centre venue<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centre address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam slot<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Important instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should not assume a centre until the admit card is released.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Authority Rights<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The conducting authorities reserve the right to make operational changes whenever required for smooth conduct of the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Adding new test centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Removing certain centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Changing allotted city<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shifting candidates to nearby centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Modifying exam date or slot<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rescheduling due to administrative reasons<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such changes are usually made to manage capacity, security, or unforeseen circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice for Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once the admit card is released, candidates should immediately review all details and make travel arrangements early. Last-minute planning often leads to unnecessary anxiety.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended actions:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download admit card early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify centre location on map<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Estimate travel time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Arrange transport in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep backup route options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the city one day earlier if travelling far<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates face exam-day problems because they ignore centre planning. Avoid these errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Waiting until the last day to check centre details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming the centre will be in preferred city only<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not checking exact address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reaching late due to traffic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carrying incorrect documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring reporting time instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Outstation Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If your allotted centre is outside your hometown, plan accommodation and travel in advance. Reaching calmly and on time can positively impact focus and performance on exam day.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Reminder<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only the test centre mentioned on the official admit card is valid for appearing in CAT. Candidates should follow all centre-specific instructions strictly&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT scorecard is released online through the official CAT website after the declaration of results. Candidates can access their individual scorecards by logging into their registered account using their credentials. In some cases, result updates may also be communicated through SMS or other registered contact channels.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scorecard is an important document used for MBA and management admissions in IIMs and other participating institutes. Candidates should download and securely save multiple copies once it becomes available, as it may be required during shortlisting, interviews, counselling, and admission verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 8, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(631, 11, ' CAT SCORE ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" SCORE\",\"name\":\"_score\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Access the CAT Scorecard<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates can generally obtain their scorecard through the official portal by:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Logging in with registered User ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entering password credentials<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Opening the result or scorecard section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Downloading the PDF copy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Saving a digital and printed version<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It is advisable to download the scorecard early to avoid portal traffic issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Information Mentioned in the Scorecard<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT scorecard usually contains important performance details such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate name and registration details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Section-wise scaled scores<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall scaled score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Section-wise percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Examination details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These metrics are widely used by institutes during the admission process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Validity of CAT Score<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT score remains valid for a limited admission cycle and is generally accepted for management admissions during the specified validity period only. After the validity period ends, the same scorecard is usually not considered for fresh admission cycles.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates planning to apply in later years may need to appear for CAT again.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Admission Use of CAT Score<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The score is commonly used for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">IIM admission shortlisting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MBA \\/ PGDM applications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview call consideration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Merit preparation by participating institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scholarship consideration in some colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, many institutes also evaluate additional factors beyond CAT score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice for Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After downloading the scorecard, candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep multiple PDF backups<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Print copies for future use<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Note percentile carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check college cutoffs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Start interview preparation immediately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Track institute application deadlines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reminder<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A high CAT score improves opportunities, but final admission may also depend on academics, work experience, category, diversity factors, and interview performance.<\\/p>\"}]', 13, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(632, 11, ' ADMISSION PROCESS', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"ADMISSION\",\"name\":\"admission\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam serves as an important gateway for admission to management programmes offered by the Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs) and several other leading institutes. However, candidates should understand that qualifying CAT or obtaining a high percentile alone does not guarantee admission. Final selection is based on a broader evaluation process decided individually by each institute.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Every IIM functions independently and has the authority to design its own admission criteria, shortlisting method, weightage system, and final selection policy. Therefore, admission standards may differ from one institute to another.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Independent Admission Policies of IIMs<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each IIM may set its own rules for selecting candidates after CAT results are declared. This means the same CAT percentile may lead to different outcomes across institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutes may differ in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum sectional cut-offs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall percentile requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic eligibility benchmarks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience preference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Diversity weightage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview evaluation system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final merit list formula<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should review institute-specific policies carefully before applying.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Role of CAT Score in Admission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT performance is one of the most important components in the admission process. Institutes often use CAT percentile to shortlist candidates for the next stage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT score may be used for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Initial shortlist preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional cut-off filtering<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall merit ranking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Comparison among applicants<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final composite score calculation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A strong CAT percentile can significantly improve chances of receiving interview calls.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Other Factors Considered During Selection<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In addition to CAT score, institutes may evaluate the complete profile of the candidate. This helps them select applicants with balanced academic and professional potential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common factors considered include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Relevant work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Professional achievements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gender diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic background diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Extra-curricular accomplishments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is why some candidates with slightly lower percentile may still receive calls from certain institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Shortlisting Stages<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admission process often takes place in multiple stages after CAT results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Typical stages may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT score-based shortlist<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application review<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal Interview<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Written Ability Test or similar assessment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final merit list preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Offer of admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not every institute follows the exact same sequence.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reality Students Should Know<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students focus only on CAT preparation and ignore profile development. This can reduce final admission chances, especially at highly competitive institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even with a high percentile, weak academics or poor interview performance may affect selection. Similarly, candidates with balanced profiles can sometimes outperform higher scorers in final admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Aspirants<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should prepare for the entire admission journey, not only the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended focus areas:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Target strong CAT percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain accurate academic records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Build quality work experience if applicable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Improve communication skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepare for interviews early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Research institute-specific criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Advice<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since each IIM follows its own admission policy, candidates should always check the latest official admission criteria of the institutes they are targeting. Understanding selection rules early helps build a smarter application strategy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 4, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:51'),
(633, 11, ' DISCLAIMER ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" DISCLAIMER\",\"name\":\"_disclaimer\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates appearing for the CAT exam are expected to provide accurate information and strictly follow all rules, instructions, and procedures throughout the examination and admission process. Any violation of rules or submission of false, misleading, or incorrect information can lead to serious consequences, including cancellation of candidature.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Applicants should carefully complete the application form, upload genuine documents, and follow official instructions at every stage to avoid disqualification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Disqualification for Incorrect Information<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If any false statement, incorrect claim, forged document, or misleading information is detected during the selection process, the candidate may face immediate action.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Possible consequences include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediate disqualification from the selection process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection of admission claim<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debarment from appearing in future CAT examinations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of shortlisted status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This applies to academic details, category claims, identity information, and supporting documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Retrospective Action in Later Years<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Sometimes issues may not be detected immediately during the current cycle. If violations are discovered later, action may still be taken even after the process has ended.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of earlier selection benefits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Retrospective disqualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Withdrawal of candidature benefits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Restriction from future participation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, honesty and accuracy are essential from the beginning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Authority to Change Test Centres<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The exam authorities reserve the right to make operational changes whenever required due to administrative, technical, security, or unforeseen circumstances.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Change of exam city<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Change of allotted test centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of a centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shift to another nearby location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Schedule adjustments if necessary<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should regularly check official updates and admit card instructions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Keep Official Documents Safe<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should preserve all important examination documents for future use during the admission cycle.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Documents generally worth retaining include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application confirmation page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fee receipt<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scorecard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category certificates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity proof copies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Important notices and instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These may be required later during verification or counselling.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Legal Jurisdiction<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any dispute relating to the CAT examination process is generally subject to the jurisdiction of the competent courts specified by the exam authorities for that admission cycle.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should understand that legal matters, if any, are handled only under the designated jurisdiction.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice for Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To avoid unnecessary problems, candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fill the form carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Upload only genuine documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Recheck category and marks details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow exam day rules strictly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preserve login credentials and records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Monitor official announcements regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Reminder<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even small mistakes can create major issues during competitive admissions. Accuracy, transparency, and compliance with official rules are as important as exam performance.<\\/p>\"}]', 14, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(634, 11, ' IMPORTANT COMMUNICATION REQUIREMENT', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"REQUIREMENT \",\"name\":\"requirement_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates participating in the CAT examination and admission process must maintain active and accurate contact details throughout the entire selection cycle. Communication from the exam authorities and participating institutes is commonly sent through registered digital channels, making correct contact information extremely important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Failure to maintain accessible contact details may result in missing key updates related to the examination or admission stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mandatory Contact Details<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should declare and continue using:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">A valid and unique email ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">An active mobile phone number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These details should belong to the candidate and remain accessible throughout the complete process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Is Important<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Registered contact details are commonly used for important communications such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration confirmation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result alerts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview shortlisting notices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification messages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission deadlines and instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Missing these updates can directly affect admission opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Meaning of Unique Email ID<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A unique email ID means the candidate should preferably use a personal email address that is not shared with other applicants.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This helps avoid:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Login confusion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missed emails<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Password recovery issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mixing of multiple applications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Security risks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Using someone else&rsquo;s email account can create avoidable problems later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Practices for Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To manage communication smoothly, candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use a personal and frequently checked email ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep the same mobile number active<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check spam or junk mail folders regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Save official emails carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure SMS service remains active<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Update passwords securely<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes to Avoid<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates face issues because of simple communication errors such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entering wrong email address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using inactive mobile number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring important emails<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Losing access to registered number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sharing login credentials with others<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These mistakes can delay or damage the application process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Advice<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Create a dedicated folder in your email for CAT-related communication and check it regularly. Keep screenshots or records of important messages for future reference.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Reminder<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strong exam preparation is valuable, but missing official communication due to inactive contact details can harm the entire admission journey. Always keep your registered email ID and mobile number active until the process is fully completed.<\\/p>\"}]', 11, 1, '2026-04-16 03:31:55', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(702, 19, ' ABOUT MAT ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"INTRODUCTION \",\"name\":\"introduction_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) is one of the most established and widely accepted national-level entrance examinations in India for admission into MBA and allied management programmes. Conducted since 1988, MAT was introduced with the objective of creating a standardized platform to evaluate the aptitude of candidates aspiring for management education across India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Over time, MAT has become a trusted admission gateway for more than 600+ B-Schools, making it one of the largest MBA entrance exams in the country. Its wide acceptance, flexible exam modes, and multiple attempts per year make it a preferred choice among MBA aspirants.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Approved by the Ministry of Education, Government of India in 2003, MAT continues to play a crucial role in providing equal opportunity to students from diverse academic backgrounds, including graduates, final-year students, and working professionals.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What is MAT Exam? (Meaning and Purpose Explained)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT exam is a standardized aptitude test designed to evaluate a candidate&rsquo;s readiness for management education. It assesses key skills required in business and managerial roles, such as logical thinking, data interpretation, language comprehension, and quantitative ability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The core objective of MAT is not just selection, but screening candidates for MBA admissions based on analytical and managerial aptitude rather than academic marks alone.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Primary Objectives of MAT Exam:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provide a common entrance platform for MBA admissions across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Evaluate analytical, verbal, quantitative, and reasoning skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Help B-Schools shortlist suitable candidates efficiently<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure fair and standardized assessment for all applicants<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Support admission into management and allied programmes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Evolution of MAT Exam (1988 to Present)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT has undergone significant transformation since its launch in 1988. Initially conducted in a traditional paper-based format, it has now evolved into a modern, flexible, and technology-driven entrance test.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Changes Over the Years:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Introduction of Computer-Based Test (CBT) mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Option of Paper-Based Test (PBT) and Internet-Based Test (IBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Streamlined exam sections for better clarity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Updated syllabus aligned with modern business requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Faster result processing and improved accessibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This evolution reflects MAT&rsquo;s continuous effort to remain relevant in the changing landscape of management education in India.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why MAT Exam is Important for MBA Admission?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT holds a strong position among MBA entrance exams due to its accessibility, flexibility, and wide acceptance across institutions. It provides multiple opportunities throughout the year, unlike many single-cycle exams.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Key Benefits of MAT Exam:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accepted by 600+ reputed B-Schools across India<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Conducted multiple times a year (Feb, May, Sept, Dec cycles)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Flexible exam modes: PBT, CBT, IBT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Moderate difficulty level suitable for most aspirants<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accepted for MBA, PGDM, and allied management courses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Suitable for fresh graduates and working professionals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 0, 1, '2026-04-16 05:21:25', '2026-04-20 05:53:26');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(716, 11, ' PARTICIPATING COLLAGES / UNIVERSITIES ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" INTRODUCTION \",\"name\":\"_introduction_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam is one of the most important management entrance examinations in India and is widely used for admission into MBA, PGDM, and equivalent postgraduate management programmes. A strong CAT score can open opportunities in the Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs), government universities, autonomous business schools, and many reputed private institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, students must clearly understand one important point: CAT conducts the entrance examination, but it does not centrally allot seats to all colleges. Admission is granted separately by each institute based on its own rules, eligibility criteria, cutoffs, and selection process. This means CAT is a score gateway, while final admission decisions are institute-specific.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Because of this decentralized model, the most authentic information should always be verified from the official CAT website and the official websites of individual colleges.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reality Students Must Understand<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Score Acceptance Does Not Mean Same Admission Rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is where many candidates make mistakes. Just because two colleges accept CAT does not mean both colleges use the same admission formula.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each institute may decide its own:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional cutoff<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience weightage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic marks weightage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Diversity preference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final merit formula<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A candidate rejected by one college may still convert another top college.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden High-Impact Mistake Students Make<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students only focus on CAT percentile and ignore institute applications. Some colleges require separate application forms, additional fees, or separate deadlines. Missing these deadlines can waste even a strong CAT score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always check official websites immediately after CAT result.<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Strategy to Use CAT Score Smartly<\\/h4>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Percentile is Very High<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Target:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Top IIMs<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">FMS<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SPJIMR<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MDI<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Percentile is Good but Not Elite<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Target:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">New IIMs<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">IMT<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">TAPMI<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Great Lakes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strong regional colleges<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Percentile is Moderate<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use CAT with:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tier-2 colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State universities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multi-exam strategy (XAT, CMAT, MAT etc.)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Verify Genuine Participating Colleges<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use this 3-step method:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit official CAT website<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit target college official website<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check &ldquo;Admissions&rdquo; section for CAT acceptance mention<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Never rely blindly on outdated third-party lists.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"IIMs ,Non-IIM Management Colleges , Universities\",\"name\":\"iims_non-iim_management_colleges__universities\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<div class=\\\"relative basis-auto flex-col -mb-(--composer-overlap-px) pb-(--composer-overlap-px) [--composer-overlap-px:28px] grow flex\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"flex flex-col text-sm\\\">\\r\\n<section class=\\\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\\\" dir=\\\"auto\\\" data-turn-id=\\\"request-69e08632-7078-83e8-aef3-a8d56399d105-19\\\" data-testid=\\\"conversation-turn-308\\\" data-scroll-anchor=\\\"false\\\" data-turn=\\\"assistant\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm\\/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg\\/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg\\/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group\\/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\\\" dir=\\\"auto\\\" tabindex=\\\"0\\\" data-message-author-role=\\\"assistant\\\" data-message-id=\\\"0bca00d6-9133-4d42-a142-ef7676a9d5eb\\\" data-message-model-slug=\\\"gpt-5-3\\\" data-turn-start-message=\\\"true\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling\\\">\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-end=\\\"404\\\">CAT scores are accepted by the <strong data-start=\\\"31\\\" data-end=\\\"76\\\">21 Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs)<\\/strong> along with <strong data-start=\\\"88\\\" data-end=\\\"141\\\">hundreds of leading MBA colleges and universities<\\/strong> across India, making CAT one of the most powerful gateways for management aspirants. From top-tier institutions to strong ROI colleges and rising business schools, CAT opens opportunities for students across multiple percentile ranges, career goals, and budgets.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-end=\\\"404\\\">Download Full List of CAT Participating Universities PDF:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-end=\\\"404\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"0\\\" data-end=\\\"404\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"410\\\" data-end=\\\"421\\\">21 IIMs<\\/strong>, including <strong data-start=\\\"433\\\" data-end=\\\"562\\\">IIM Ahmedabad, IIM Bangalore, IIM Calcutta, IIM Lucknow, IIM Kozhikode, IIM Indore, IIM Mumbai, IIM Shillong, and IIM Udaipur<\\/strong>, are among the most prestigious management institutes in India. These institutes are known for excellent faculty, global recognition, top recruiters, leadership-focused curriculum, and strong placement packages. Admission to IIMs is highly competitive and depends on CAT percentile, academics, work experience, and interview performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"902\\\" data-end=\\\"1399\\\">Apart from IIMs, <strong data-start=\\\"919\\\" data-end=\\\"944\\\">200+ Non-IIM colleges<\\/strong> also accept CAT scores and provide excellent MBA opportunities. Some of the most popular names include <strong data-start=\\\"1048\\\" data-end=\\\"1255\\\">FMS Delhi, SPJIMR Mumbai, MDI Gurgaon, IMT Ghaziabad, XIM University, Great Lakes Chennai, FORE School of Management, JBIMS Mumbai, K J Somaiya, Welingkar, BIMTECH, TAPMI, and Goa Institute of Management<\\/strong>. Many of these institutes offer outstanding placements, strong alumni networks, specialized MBA programmes, and lower fee-to-return advantages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1401\\\" data-end=\\\"1683\\\">CAT scores are also accepted by management schools within premier technical institutes such as <strong data-start=\\\"1496\\\" data-end=\\\"1577\\\">IIT Delhi, IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kharagpur, IIT Kanpur, and IIT Roorkee<\\/strong>, giving students another strong path toward quality MBA education with technical and analytical exposure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1685\\\" data-end=\\\"2030\\\">One of the biggest advantages of CAT is that even if a student misses top IIM calls, many excellent colleges remain available across different percentile bands. High scorers may target elite IIMs and premium B-schools, while moderate percentile candidates can still secure admission in reputed colleges with good placements and growth potential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2032\\\" data-end=\\\"2410\\\" data-is-last-node=\\\"\\\" data-is-only-node=\\\"\\\">Every year, the number of participating institutions may change based on programme intake and admission policy, but CAT consistently remains the exam that offers the <strong data-start=\\\"2198\\\" data-end=\\\"2246\\\">widest range of quality MBA options in India<\\/strong>. For serious MBA aspirants, a good CAT score can unlock opportunities in <strong data-start=\\\"2320\\\" data-end=\\\"2372\\\">21 IIMs and hundreds of other respected colleges<\\/strong>, making preparation highly rewarding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/section>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<div id=\\\"thread-bottom-container\\\" class=\\\"sticky bottom-0 z-10 group\\/thread-bottom-container relative isolate w-full basis-auto has-data-has-thread-error:pt-2 has-data-has-thread-error:[box-shadow:var(--sharp-edge-bottom-shadow)] md:border-transparent md:pt-0 dark:border-white\\/20 md:dark:border-transparent print:hidden content-fade single-line\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"relative mx-auto h-0\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"text-base mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm\\/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg\\/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg\\/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 mb-[var(--thread-component-gap,1rem)]\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"pointer-events-auto relative z-1 flex h-(--composer-container-height,100%) max-w-full flex-(--composer-container-flex,1) flex-col\\\"><form class=\\\"group\\/composer w-full\\\" data-type=\\\"unified-composer\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"hidden\\\">&nbsp;<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/form><\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\"}]', 2, 1, '2026-04-17 05:34:29', '2026-04-22 02:36:02'),
(717, 11, ' EXAM SCHEME', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" MODE OF EXAMINATION\",\"name\":\"_mode_of_examination\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is generally conducted as a Computer-Based Test (CBT) at authorized examination centres in multiple cities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Computer-Based Test Means<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates take the exam on a desktop computer at the centre where:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Questions appear on the screen<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Answers are selected or typed digitally<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Section timer runs automatically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rough sheets are provided for calculations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Navigation is controlled through on-screen tools<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This does not mean the exam tests advanced computer skills. Basic mouse handling is usually sufficient.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" CORE OBJECTIVE \",\"name\":\"_core_objective_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The paper is structured to identify candidates who can perform well in demanding management environments. Therefore, CAT tests whether a candidate can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read and interpret complex information quickly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Analyze data logically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Solve numerical problems accurately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Make decisions under pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Manage limited time efficiently<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain accuracy despite stress<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These are the same skills expected in MBA classrooms and corporate environments.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" EXAM STRUCTURE \",\"name\":\"_exam_structure_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is generally divided into three compulsory sections, each testing a different skill domain.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Main Sections<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Quantitative Ability (QA)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All candidates are required to attempt all sections.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section 1: Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section measures language understanding, interpretation ability, reading stamina, and logical comprehension.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Asked<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reading comprehension passages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para jumbles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Odd sentence out<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Summary-based questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Inference questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tone and meaning analysis<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Makes This Section Difficult<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students assume this section is easy because it is language-based. In reality, CAT passages can be dense, abstract, and time-consuming.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The real challenge comes from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Long passages under time pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Similar-looking answer options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Inference-based questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Need for concentration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Truth<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strong grammar alone is not enough. Reading maturity and interpretation ability matter more.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section 2: Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section is often considered one of the most unpredictable parts of CAT. It tests whether candidates can interpret data and solve structured logical problems.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Asked<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tables<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Charts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bar graphs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pie charts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seating arrangements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduling puzzles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Distribution sets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Venn diagrams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Games and tournaments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Caselets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Students Struggle Here<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The difficulty often comes from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multi-step sets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ambiguous-looking data<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Need to identify easiest set first<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time wasted on wrong set selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">DILR is often less about solving speed and more about choosing the right sets.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section 3: Quantitative Ability (QA)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section tests mathematical reasoning based mainly on school-level concepts but in aptitude-oriented form.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Arithmetic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Profit and loss<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ratio and proportion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time, speed and distance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time and work<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Averages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Algebra<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Linear and quadratic equations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Geometry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mensuration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Number systems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Permutation and combination (varies)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why It Feels Tough<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The concepts may be familiar, but CAT questions often require:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smart interpretation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Short methods<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Elimination logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Multi-concept application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time-efficient solving<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Truth<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students weak in basics usually suffer more than students weak in advanced math.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" DURATION OF EXAM\",\"name\":\"_duration_of_exam\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In recent standard formats, CAT has generally been conducted for 120 minutes total.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Typical Sectional Distribution<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">VARC &ndash; 40 minutes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">DILR &ndash; 40 minutes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">QA &ndash; 40 minutes<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The sequence and timing are managed by the system.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Sectional Time Limits<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT usually follows a sectional timing model.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Meaning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates receive fixed time for each section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time cannot normally be carried forward<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Once section time ends, system shifts automatically<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Why This Is Critical<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A student who is excellent in Quant but weak in VARC cannot simply spend extra time later to compensate.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Impact<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Balanced preparation becomes necessary because every section influences final percentile and many institutes also apply sectional cutoffs.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" QUESTION TYPES AND NUMBERS \",\"name\":\"_question_types_and_numbers_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT generally uses two major formats.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Four or more options may be given<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate selects the correct option<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. TITA \\/ Non-MCQ Questions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">(Type In The Answer)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No options given<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate types final answer manually<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why TITA Questions Matter<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These questions often reduce random guessing and reward genuine understanding.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" MARKING SCHEME\",\"name\":\"_marking_scheme\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The commonly used recent marking model has generally been:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">+3 marks for correct answer<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">-1 mark for wrong MCQ answer<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No negative marking for TITA questions<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final yearly rules should always be verified officially.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Number of Questions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The total question count may vary across exam cycles. CAT authorities may adjust paper length, question distribution, or section composition when required.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Student Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Never depend on one old fixed question count while preparing. Focus on adaptability.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" LANGUAGE \",\"name\":\"_language_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam is generally conducted in<span style=\\\"background-color: #fbeeb8;\\\"> <span style=\\\"background-color: #f1c40f;\\\"><strong>English language only<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/span>. All sections of the examination&mdash;Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC), Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR), and Quantitative Ability (QA)&mdash;are presented in English.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means candidates receive:<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Questions in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Instructions in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">On-screen interface primarily in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reading passages in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Number of Languages<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is typically held in <span style=\\\"background-color: #f1c40f;\\\"><strong>1 language only: English.<\\/strong><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unlike some entrance examinations that offer multiple regional language options, CAT is usually not conducted in Hindi or other Indian languages.<strong id=\\\"docs-internal-guid-b64806ac-7fff-520a-7384-d84298fb1a71\\\"><\\/strong><\\/p>\"}]', 6, 1, '2026-04-17 05:34:29', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(865, 11, ' SYLLABUS ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" SYLLABUS STRUCTURE \",\"name\":\"_syllabus_structure_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT preparation is generally divided into three sections:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Quantitative Ability (QA)<\\/h4>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each section tests aptitude and analytical skills rather than rote learning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC) Syllabus<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section evaluates reading ability, language understanding, logic in written communication, and interpretation skills.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Major Topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reading Comprehension Passages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para Jumbles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para Completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Odd Sentence Out<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sentence Arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Summary-Based Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Inference-Based Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tone and Central Idea Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Vocabulary in Context<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Grammar through usage logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Students Must Understand<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">VARC is less about memorizing grammar rules and more about understanding meaning, tone, arguments, and structure.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden High-Impact Skill<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Daily reading habit often gives larger returns than grammar cramming.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR) Syllabus<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section checks structured thinking, analytical reasoning, and interpretation of data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Interpretation Topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tables<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pie Charts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bar Graphs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Line Graphs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Caselets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mixed Graph Sets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Comparison<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Logical Reasoning Topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seating Arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blood Relations (varies)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Distribution Puzzles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scheduling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Games &amp; Tournaments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Arrangement Sets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Binary Logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Routes \\/ Network Logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selection Based Puzzles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Students Must Understand<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">DILR success depends heavily on set selection, patience, and practice&mdash;not memorization.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Quantitative Ability (QA) Syllabus<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section evaluates mathematical reasoning using school-level concepts in aptitude format.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Arithmetic Topics (Most Important for Many Students)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Profit and Loss<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ratio and Proportion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Averages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mixtures and Alligation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Simple Interest \\/ Compound Interest<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time and Work<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time, Speed and Distance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pipes and Cisterns<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Algebra Topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Linear Equations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Quadratic Equations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Inequalities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Functions (basic level)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Progressions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Logs (varies)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Geometry \\/ Mensuration<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Lines and Angles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Triangles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Circles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Polygons<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Coordinate Basics (varies)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Area and Volume<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Number System<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Divisibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Factors and Multiples<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Remainders<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">HCF \\/ LCM<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Units Digit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Base Concepts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Modern Math (Variable Presence)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Permutation &amp; Combination<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Probability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Set Theory Basics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Students Must Understand<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strong arithmetic + algebra basics often provide the highest return for many candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Reality About CAT Syllabus<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT does not guarantee that every topic appears every year. Some chapters may dominate one year and reduce next year.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, Students Should Prepare For:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Concept clarity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mixed practice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Adaptability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Question selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not chapter prediction.<\\/p>\"}]', 7, 1, '2026-04-17 06:32:02', '2026-04-20 01:23:43');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(866, 11, ' ADMIT CARD ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" HOW TO DOWNLOAD ADMIT CARD \",\"name\":\"_how_to_download_admit_card_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Detailed Step-by-Step Process to Download CAT Admit Card<\\/h3>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Visit the Official CAT Website<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Open your browser and visit the official CAT website:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/iimcat.ac.in\\\">https:\\/\\/iimcat.ac.in<\\/a><\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use only the official website to avoid fake links or outdated portals.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Find the Candidate Login Section<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">On the homepage, look for the login area generally meant for registered candidates. It may appear with names such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Login<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate Login<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registered User Login<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applicant Login<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Click the login option.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3: Enter Login Credentials<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use the same details created during CAT registration.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Usually required:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">User ID \\/ Registered Email ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Password<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Enter details carefully with correct uppercase\\/lowercase characters where applicable.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 4: Complete Security Verification<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Sometimes the portal may ask for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Captcha code<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OTP verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Security check<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Complete the required step and proceed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 5: Open Candidate Dashboard<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After successful login, you will enter your candidate dashboard. This is the account area where exam-related options are usually available.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You may see options such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application form<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Updates \\/ notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 6: Click on Admit Card Download Link<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Find and click the option named:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download Admit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hall Ticket<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download Hall Ticket<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This will open your admit card in PDF format.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 7: Check All Details Before Saving<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before downloading, carefully review the information shown on screen:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Slot timing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Test centre name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centre address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If anything appears incorrect, contact official support immediately.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 8: Download the PDF File<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Click the download icon or save option and store the admit card on your device.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best places to save:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Desktop<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile phone<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Google Drive \\/ Email backup<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pen drive<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Keep more than one backup copy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 9: Print the Admit Card<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Take clear printouts of the downloaded admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Print 2 to 3 copies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ensure photo and text are visible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid torn or blurry print copies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A readable printed copy helps during verification.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS\",\"name\":\"_important_instructions\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If You Forgot Password<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Most portals generally provide options such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgot Password<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reset Password<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Recover Login<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use your registered email ID or mobile number to reset access.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do this early to avoid last-minute panic.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Admit Card Is Not Showing<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Possible reasons may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Application incomplete<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment pending<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong login credentials<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Temporary server traffic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Browser issue<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Try:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Refreshing page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Using another browser<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Logging in later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Checking payment\\/application status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Things to Verify After Downloading<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should carefully confirm:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct spelling of name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Clear photograph<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct exam city<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct centre address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct date and timing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Matching application number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mistakes should be reported quickly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Precautions<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download early, do not wait till last day<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use stable internet connection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use official website only<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep login credentials safe<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Print multiple copies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preserve admit card after exam also<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgetting password at last moment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Printing unreadable copy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring centre location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Checking admit card too late<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not reading instructions printed on admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', 10, 1, '2026-04-17 06:32:02', '2026-04-20 01:23:43'),
(867, 11, ' EXAM DAY GUIDELINES ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" GUIDELINES \",\"name\":\"_guidelines_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam day is one of the most important stages of the entire admission process. Even well-prepared candidates can face unnecessary problems if they ignore reporting instructions, document requirements, timing discipline, or test centre rules. Therefore, candidates should not focus only on preparation and must also understand exam-day procedures carefully.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT authorities generally publish exam-day instructions through the official CAT website and admit card. Candidates are expected to follow all instructions strictly at the test centre.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before Leaving Home<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should prepare all required items in advance to avoid last-minute stress.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Keep Ready<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Printed CAT admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid original photo ID proof<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Passport size photo (if instructed)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Transparent water bottle (only if allowed)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Basic stationery only if officially permitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended Checks<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirm reporting time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirm exam centre address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check travel route<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Estimate traffic\\/travel delay<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep emergency contact numbers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reporting Time and Entry Rules<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should reach the centre well before the reporting time mentioned on the admit card. Late arrival may create entry issues depending on official policy and centre procedures.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Early Arrival Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Security screening takes time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ID verification may involve queues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric checks may be conducted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Centre gates may close before exam start<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stress reduces when you arrive early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reaching late can negatively affect mental focus before the exam even begins.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Documents Required at Centre<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are generally expected to carry:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Printed admit card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Original valid photo identity proof<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common ID proofs may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aadhaar Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PAN Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Passport<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Driving Licence<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Voter ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The name on the ID proof should closely match the admit card details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Security and Verification Procedures<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT authorities may use security measures to protect exam integrity. Depending on centre arrangements, candidates may undergo:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph matching<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric attendance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Metal detector screening<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Frisking\\/security checks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document inspection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should cooperate calmly with staff.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Items Usually Restricted Inside Centre<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are generally advised not to carry prohibited items.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Commonly restricted items may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile phones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Smart watches<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bluetooth devices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Earphones<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Calculators<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Notes \\/ books<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wallets (varies by centre rules)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bags (varies by centre rules)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Electronic gadgets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always check the latest admit card instructions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Inside the Exam Hall<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After entering the lab\\/hall, candidates are usually guided to their allotted seat or computer terminal.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates Should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sit only at assigned system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check name\\/roll details if displayed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Listen to invigilator instructions carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read on-screen instructions before test begins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Raise hand if technical issue occurs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not touch systems unnecessarily before instructed.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">During the Examination<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is a computer-based test with timed sections. Candidates should remain disciplined throughout the test.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Conduct Rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain silence<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not communicate with others<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not attempt unfair means<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow invigilator instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use rough sheets only as allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Manage sectional time carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any violation may lead to disciplinary action.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If Technical Issue Happens<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In rare cases, computer or system issues may occur.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay calm<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediately inform invigilator<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not panic or leave seat without permission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam staff generally handle genuine technical disruptions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time Management on Exam Day<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students lose marks due to panic rather than lack of preparation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Mental Approach<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Start calmly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read each question carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Avoid rushing first five minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Skip traps and difficult questions wisely<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain accuracy over random attempts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stay composed if one section feels hard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Remember: if the paper feels difficult, it may feel difficult for others too.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After Completing Exam<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Once the exam ends:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Follow exit instructions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submit rough sheets if required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leave centre in orderly manner<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Keep admit card safely for future reference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admit card may be useful later for result or selection stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common High-Impact Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Reaching Late<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Creates panic and may risk entry trouble.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Forgetting Admit Card or ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Can create serious verification issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Carrying Prohibited Items<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Leads to delays or inconvenience.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Arguing with Staff<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Wastes energy and focus.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Panicking After Tough Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Destroys performance in remaining paper.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" MALPRACTICE DISQUALIFICATION & BREACH \",\"name\":\"_malpractice_disqualification__breach_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam unfair means rules define all activities that are strictly prohibited during the Common Admission Test. These rules are designed to maintain fairness, transparency, and equal opportunity for all candidates appearing in this highly competitive national-level management entrance exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since CAT is used for admission to top institutes such as the Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs) and other prestigious business schools, even a small violation of exam rules can lead to serious consequences like cancellation of result, disqualification, or rejection from the admission process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding these rules is not just about avoiding cheating&mdash;it is about ensuring that candidates do not unintentionally violate any regulation that could affect their future<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1 What is Unfair Means in CAT Exam?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In the context of CAT, unfair means refers to any action that gives a candidate an unjust advantage over others or violates examination regulations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is not limited to direct cheating alone. Even actions like carrying restricted items, misrepresentation of identity, or not following instructions properly may be treated as unfair means.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The core idea behind these rules is to ensure that every candidate competes under the same conditions, without external assistance or manipulation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2 CAT Exam Malpractice Rules Explained in Detail<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Impersonation in CAT Exam<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Impersonation is one of the most serious violations in CAT. It occurs when someone other than the registered candidate appears for the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may involve fake identity substitution, forged documents, or manipulated verification details. Since CAT uses biometric verification and strict identity checks, impersonation is treated as a severe offence.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate is found involved in impersonation, the candidature can be cancelled immediately, and strict action may be taken against both individuals involved.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Cheating During CAT Examination<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Cheating refers to any attempt to gain answers or assistance through unauthorized means during the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since CAT is a computer-based test conducted under strict surveillance, cheating attempts are monitored closely. Still, violations may include copying from another candidate&rsquo;s screen, communicating silently through gestures, or using hidden notes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even attempting to communicate with another candidate during the exam can be treated as misconduct.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such actions are considered a violation because CAT is designed to test individual analytical and problem-solving ability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Carrying Prohibited Items Inside Exam Hall<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the most common and serious mistakes candidates make is carrying restricted items into the examination centre.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Items such as mobile phones, smart watches, Bluetooth devices, calculators (if not allowed), earphones, or written notes are strictly prohibited.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if these items are not used, simply possessing them inside the examination hall can be treated as a violation. This rule exists to prevent any possibility of external assistance or communication.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are always advised to carefully check admit card instructions before reaching the exam centre.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Misconduct at Examination Centre<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Misconduct refers to any behaviour that disrupts the smooth conduct of the examination or disobeys invigilator instructions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may include refusing to follow security checks, arguing with staff, disturbing other candidates, or moving without permission inside the exam hall.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such behaviour is taken seriously because it affects the discipline and fairness of the entire examination environment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if a candidate is not cheating, misconduct alone can lead to disciplinary action.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Tampering with Computer-Based Test System<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT is conducted as a computer-based test, and all systems are securely locked during the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Any attempt to interfere with the computer system, access unauthorized screens, or manipulate software is considered a serious violation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Such actions are treated as an attempt to compromise the integrity of the examination process and may result in strict penalties.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6. False Information or Fraudulent Documents<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates are required to provide accurate information during registration and admission stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If any candidate submits fake academic details, incorrect category certificates, or false identity information, it may be treated as misconduct.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even if such issues are discovered after the exam or during admission, the candidature or admission offer may be cancelled.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This rule ensures transparency and authenticity in the entire selection process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">7. CAT Exam Breach of Examination Rules (Beyond Cheating)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not all violations involve intentional cheating. Many candidates face issues due to negligence or lack of awareness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A breach of examination rules may include arriving late at the centre, ignoring instructions from invigilators, carrying restricted items unknowingly, or moving without permission inside the exam hall.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These actions may appear minor, but in a high-security exam like CAT, even small violations can be recorded as rule breaches.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3 Consequences ans strictness<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The consequences of violating CAT rules are strict because the exam is used for high-stakes admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Depending on the severity of the violation, candidates may face:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Immediate removal from the exam centre<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cancellation of CAT candidature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Disqualification from the examination process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Withholding or cancellation of result<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Rejection from admission process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debarment from future attempts (in serious cases)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The authorities have full discretion to decide the final action based on evidence and severity<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Exam Security and Monitoring System<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">To prevent unfair practices, CAT uses multiple security layers such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CCTV surveillance in exam centres<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Biometric verification of candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity document checks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Secure computer-based testing platform<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strict invigilator monitoring<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These measures ensure that every candidate is evaluated fairly and without external interference.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why CAT Exam Rules Are So Strict<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam is used by highly reputed institutes such as Indian Institutes of Management for MBA admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since competition is extremely high and even a small advantage can impact selection, strict rules are necessary to maintain fairness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These rules ensure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Equal opportunity for all candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Transparent evaluation process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Integrity of exam results<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Trust in the admission system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', 12, 1, '2026-04-17 06:32:02', '2026-04-20 01:23:43');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(868, 11, ' DECLARATION OF RESULTS ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" RESULT \",\"name\":\"_result_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT result is one of the most significant stages of the examination process because it determines a candidate&rsquo;s next step toward admission into MBA, PGDM, and other management programmes offered by the Indian Institutes of Management (IIMs) and many participating institutions. However, candidates should clearly understand that the CAT result is generally a scorecard-based outcome, not a direct admission letter. It reflects performance in the examination and is later used by institutes for shortlisting candidates for further rounds such as Personal Interview (PI), Written Ability Test (WAT), Group Discussion (GD), or profile-based selection, depending on institute policy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unlike many traditional entrance examinations that release simple marks or ranks, CAT usually reports performance through scaled scores and percentiles. This system is designed to compare candidate performance fairly across multiple sessions of the examination.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT result is generally released online through the official CAT portal. Candidates are usually required to log in using their registered User ID and password to view and download their scorecard.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The result is not commonly sent in printed form by post. Therefore, candidates must actively check the website and download the scorecard themselves.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">General Process to Check Result<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Visit the official CAT website.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Open the candidate login section.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Enter registered credentials.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Access the result or scorecard tab.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download the PDF scorecard.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Save digital and printed copies for future admission use.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Downloading the scorecard early is advisable so that candidates do not face website traffic issues later.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What the CAT Scorecard Usually Contains<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT scorecard is an official record of the candidate&rsquo;s performance in the examination. It generally includes personal identification details along with section-wise and overall performance data.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidate Details<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scorecard may contain:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category details, where applicable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photograph or identification references<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Performance Details<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The scorecard generally shows:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension (VARC) score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning (DILR) score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Quantitative Ability (QA) score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall scaled score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Section-wise percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Percentile Is Important<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Percentile indicates comparative performance against other candidates. For example, a high percentile usually means the candidate performed better than a large percentage of test-takers. Many institutes use percentile cutoffs rather than raw marks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Answer Key<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT authorities may release an official answer key after the examination. This allows candidates to estimate probable performance before the final result is announced.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The answer key generally serves as a reference document that can be compared with the candidate response sheet.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">It May Include<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Official correct answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Question identifiers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate marked responses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Comparison for score estimation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Objection Opportunity<\\/h4>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If officially announced, candidates may be allowed to raise objections against specific answers within a limited period and as per prescribed rules. Candidates should monitor official notices carefully because objection windows are usually time-bound.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" RE-CHECKING \\/ RE-VALUATION\",\"name\":\"_re-checking__re-valuation\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Traditional rechecking or revaluation of CAT results is generally not available.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since CAT is a standardized computer-based examination where responses are digitally recorded and scores are statistically processed, candidates usually cannot request the type of rechecking commonly seen in board or university exams.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h4 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Generally Not Available<\\/h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Manual rechecking of answer sheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marks recounting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Re-evaluation of answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Post-result re-totaling requests<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should therefore make full use of the response sheet and answer key stage, if released, because that is usually the appropriate transparency mechanism.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" SCORING AND EQUATING \",\"name\":\"_scoring_and_equating_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"87\\\" data-end=\\\"462\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"91\\\" data-end=\\\"120\\\">CAT normalisation process<\\/strong> is one of the most searched and misunderstood topics among MBA aspirants. Since the CAT exam is conducted in multiple sessions on the same day, candidates often worry whether one slot was easier or harder than another. To maintain fairness, the CAT authorities use a scientific <strong data-start=\\\"399\\\" data-end=\\\"430\\\">score normalisation process<\\/strong> before preparing final results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"464\\\" data-end=\\\"665\\\">This means your raw score is not always the final score shown in the CAT result. Instead, scores are adjusted statistically so that candidates across different sessions are evaluated on an equal basis.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"667\\\" data-end=\\\"853\\\">Understanding the <strong data-start=\\\"685\\\" data-end=\\\"761\\\">CAT score normalisation system, scaled score, and percentile calculation<\\/strong> helps students interpret results more accurately and plan realistic admission expectations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1codvv6\\\" data-start=\\\"1194\\\" data-end=\\\"1222\\\">Why CAT Uses Normalisation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1224\\\" data-end=\\\"1368\\\">CAT is usually conducted in <strong data-start=\\\"1252\\\" data-end=\\\"1281\\\">multiple sessions (slots)<\\/strong>. Different candidates appear in different time slots and receive different test forms.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1370\\\" data-end=\\\"1462\\\">Even when exam setters maintain similar standards, there can still be slight differences in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1464\\\" data-end=\\\"1577\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1sw9t1p\\\" data-start=\\\"1464\\\" data-end=\\\"1484\\\">Difficulty level<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"15vecw6\\\" data-start=\\\"1485\\\" data-end=\\\"1507\\\">Question selection<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"6rmf3a\\\" data-start=\\\"1508\\\" data-end=\\\"1536\\\">Time pressure experience<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1rufpdz\\\" data-start=\\\"1537\\\" data-end=\\\"1556\\\">Section balance<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1w87xry\\\" data-start=\\\"1557\\\" data-end=\\\"1577\\\">Attempt patterns<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1579\\\" data-end=\\\"1668\\\">If raw marks alone were used, one slot might get an unintended advantage or disadvantage.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1670\\\" data-end=\\\"1757\\\">That is why CAT uses <strong data-start=\\\"1691\\\" data-end=\\\"1708\\\">normalisation<\\/strong> to create a fair comparison across all sessions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"12k1g1q\\\" data-start=\\\"1764\\\" data-end=\\\"1805\\\">CAT Exam Conducted in Multiple Sessions<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1807\\\" data-end=\\\"1937\\\">As per the provided information, CAT is conducted in <strong data-start=\\\"1860\\\" data-end=\\\"1878\\\">three sessions<\\/strong>, and separate test forms are administered in each session.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1939\\\" data-end=\\\"1960\\\">This generally means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1962\\\" data-end=\\\"2110\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"oxitpd\\\" data-start=\\\"1962\\\" data-end=\\\"2014\\\">Morning session candidates receive one test form<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tbwtqs\\\" data-start=\\\"2015\\\" data-end=\\\"2063\\\">Afternoon session candidates receive another<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1wg1k5k\\\" data-start=\\\"2064\\\" data-end=\\\"2110\\\">Evening session candidates receive another<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2112\\\" data-end=\\\"2169\\\">The pattern remains similar, but actual questions differ.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"rrulsj\\\" data-start=\\\"2176\\\" data-end=\\\"2200\\\">What Is CAT Raw Score?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2202\\\" data-end=\\\"2275\\\">Before understanding normalisation, students must know raw score meaning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"yfes2v\\\" data-start=\\\"2277\\\" data-end=\\\"2296\\\">Raw Score Means:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2298\\\" data-end=\\\"2331\\\">The score obtained directly from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2333\\\" data-end=\\\"2422\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"88a995\\\" data-start=\\\"2333\\\" data-end=\\\"2352\\\">Correct answers<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"ceona5\\\" data-start=\\\"2353\\\" data-end=\\\"2389\\\">Negative marking (if applicable)<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"wi4o0\\\" data-start=\\\"2390\\\" data-end=\\\"2422\\\">Unattempted questions impact<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2424\\\" data-end=\\\"2486\\\">This is your direct performance before statistical adjustment.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2488\\\" data-end=\\\"2576\\\">However, CAT results usually focus on <strong data-start=\\\"2526\\\" data-end=\\\"2555\\\">scaled score + percentile<\\/strong>, not only raw marks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1y8c9yb\\\" data-start=\\\"2583\\\" data-end=\\\"2617\\\">What Is CAT Score Normalisation?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2619\\\" data-end=\\\"2740\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"2623\\\" data-end=\\\"2652\\\">CAT normalisation process<\\/strong> is a statistical method used to adjust candidate scores across different exam sessions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2742\\\" data-end=\\\"2822\\\">Its purpose is to remove unfair differences caused by slot difficulty variation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"2824\\\" data-end=\\\"2977\\\">If one slot was slightly harder and another slightly easier, normalisation helps balance those effects so no candidate is unfairly rewarded or penalized.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1prcvsq\\\" data-start=\\\"2984\\\" data-end=\\\"3034\\\">How CAT Normalisation Works (Simple Explanation)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3036\\\" data-end=\\\"3081\\\">The official process mentions adjustment for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3083\\\" data-end=\\\"3181\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1ppncv8\\\" data-start=\\\"3083\\\" data-end=\\\"3133\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3085\\\" data-end=\\\"3109\\\">Location differences<\\/strong> in score distribution<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"113xi01\\\" data-start=\\\"3134\\\" data-end=\\\"3181\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3136\\\" data-end=\\\"3157\\\">Scale differences<\\/strong> in score distribution<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3183\\\" data-end=\\\"3308\\\">In simpler terms, CAT compares how candidates performed within each slot and aligns scores statistically across all sessions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3310\\\" data-end=\\\"3431\\\">This means the system does not simply &ldquo;add marks&rdquo; or &ldquo;subtract marks&rdquo; randomly. It uses performance distribution methods.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"siv6hv\\\" data-start=\\\"3438\\\" data-end=\\\"3464\\\">CAT Scaled Score Meaning<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3466\\\" data-end=\\\"3524\\\">After normalisation, candidates receive <strong data-start=\\\"3506\\\" data-end=\\\"3523\\\">Scaled Scores<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3526\\\" data-end=\\\"3608\\\">A scaled score is the adjusted score after applying the CAT normalisation formula.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3610\\\" data-end=\\\"3628\\\">This score may be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3630\\\" data-end=\\\"3723\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1083v2u\\\" data-start=\\\"3630\\\" data-end=\\\"3664\\\">Slightly higher than raw score<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"lkxai4\\\" data-start=\\\"3665\\\" data-end=\\\"3698\\\">Slightly lower than raw score<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tqhiji\\\" data-start=\\\"3699\\\" data-end=\\\"3723\\\">Similar to raw score<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3725\\\" data-end=\\\"3762\\\">depending on slot performance trends.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1c7tkya\\\" data-start=\\\"3769\\\" data-end=\\\"3817\\\">CAT Percentile Calculation After Normalisation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3819\\\" data-end=\\\"3891\\\">Once scaled scores are prepared, CAT converts them into <strong data-start=\\\"3875\\\" data-end=\\\"3890\\\">percentiles<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3>What Percentile Means<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"3919\\\" data-end=\\\"4009\\\">Percentile indicates the percentage of candidates who scored equal to or below your level.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4011\\\" data-end=\\\"4023\\\">For example:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4025\\\" data-end=\\\"4184\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1tf28ws\\\" data-start=\\\"4025\\\" data-end=\\\"4108\\\">99 percentile means you performed better than approximately 99% of test takers.<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"13wny0g\\\" data-start=\\\"4109\\\" data-end=\\\"4184\\\">90 percentile means you performed better than around 90% of candidates.<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4186\\\" data-end=\\\"4256\\\">This is why percentile matters more than raw marks for MBA admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1u2syny\\\" data-start=\\\"4263\\\" data-end=\\\"4304\\\">Section-Wise CAT Scores Also Normalised<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4306\\\" data-end=\\\"4388\\\">CAT does not publish only total score. Section-wise performance is also important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4390\\\" data-end=\\\"4447\\\">Scaled scores and percentiles are generally reported for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1uiqr3k\\\" data-start=\\\"4449\\\" data-end=\\\"4468\\\">Section I &ndash; VARC<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4470\\\" data-end=\\\"4514\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4470\\\" data-end=\\\"4514\\\">Verbal Ability and Reading Comprehension<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4516\\\" data-end=\\\"4598\\\">Measures reading ability, language understanding, comprehension, verbal reasoning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1178ei4\\\" data-start=\\\"4600\\\" data-end=\\\"4620\\\">Section II &ndash; DILR<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4622\\\" data-end=\\\"4667\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4622\\\" data-end=\\\"4667\\\">Data Interpretation and Logical Reasoning<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4669\\\" data-end=\\\"4738\\\">Measures analytical reasoning, sets, charts, puzzles, decision logic.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1le6z6u\\\" data-start=\\\"4740\\\" data-end=\\\"4759\\\">Section III &ndash; QA<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4761\\\" data-end=\\\"4785\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4761\\\" data-end=\\\"4785\\\">Quantitative Ability<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4787\\\" data-end=\\\"4858\\\">Measures arithmetic, algebra, geometry, numbers, mathematical aptitude.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"bbx7o2\\\" data-start=\\\"4865\\\" data-end=\\\"4913\\\">Total Score + Sectional Percentile Both Matter<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4915\\\" data-end=\\\"4983\\\">Many candidates focus only on overall percentile. This is a mistake.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"4985\\\" data-end=\\\"5014\\\">Most top institutes consider:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5016\\\" data-end=\\\"5109\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1yrt9ze\\\" data-start=\\\"5016\\\" data-end=\\\"5042\\\">Overall CAT percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"16k5pxg\\\" data-start=\\\"5043\\\" data-end=\\\"5068\\\">Sectional percentiles<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"tonc47\\\" data-start=\\\"5069\\\" data-end=\\\"5109\\\">Balanced performance across sections<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5111\\\" data-end=\\\"5202\\\">A high total percentile with weak sectional percentile can still create shortlist problems.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1fgzwj0\\\" data-start=\\\"5209\\\" data-end=\\\"5277\\\">Why Two Students with Same Raw Score May Get Different Percentiles<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5279\\\" data-end=\\\"5353\\\">This happens because CAT admissions use scaled scores after normalisation.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5355\\\" data-end=\\\"5379\\\">Two candidates may have:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5381\\\" data-end=\\\"5490\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1p7ftm8\\\" data-start=\\\"5381\\\" data-end=\\\"5399\\\">Same raw marks<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"b9ahga\\\" data-start=\\\"5400\\\" data-end=\\\"5419\\\">Different slots<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1d4eu2n\\\" data-start=\\\"5420\\\" data-end=\\\"5456\\\">Different slot difficulty levels<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1s6o7vw\\\" data-start=\\\"5457\\\" data-end=\\\"5490\\\">Different score distributions<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5492\\\" data-end=\\\"5548\\\">Therefore, final scaled scores or percentile may differ.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5550\\\" data-end=\\\"5600\\\">This is normal in multi-session competitive exams.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"q3rusd\\\" data-start=\\\"5607\\\" data-end=\\\"5635\\\">Is CAT Normalisation Fair?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5637\\\" data-end=\\\"5732\\\">The CAT authority uses an established statistical process similar to other large exams such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5734\\\" data-end=\\\"5771\\\"><span class=\\\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline\\\"><span class=\\\"whitespace-normal\\\">Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering<\\/span><\\/span><\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5773\\\" data-end=\\\"5865\\\">The goal is to ensure fairness across large candidate pools appearing in different sessions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"5867\\\" data-end=\\\"6001\\\">No system is perfect in public opinion, but normalisation is widely accepted as the most practical method for multi-slot examinations.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1h25g0v\\\" data-start=\\\"6008\\\" data-end=\\\"6046\\\">Common Myths About CAT Normalisation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1und24\\\" data-start=\\\"6048\\\" data-end=\\\"6096\\\">Myth 1: Easy Slot Always Gives Low Percentile<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6098\\\" data-end=\\\"6157\\\">Not always. It depends on overall performance distribution.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"6stgz\\\" data-start=\\\"6159\\\" data-end=\\\"6197\\\">Myth 2: Hard Slot Gives Bonus Marks<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6199\\\" data-end=\\\"6230\\\">No fixed bonus marks are given.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"4h6nw1\\\" data-start=\\\"6232\\\" data-end=\\\"6276\\\">Myth 3: Raw Score Alone Decides Admission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6278\\\" data-end=\\\"6317\\\">Incorrect. Percentile matters far more.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"1257ep3\\\" data-start=\\\"6319\\\" data-end=\\\"6353\\\">Myth 4: Sectionals Don&rsquo;t Matter<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6355\\\" data-end=\\\"6400\\\">Wrong. Many institutes use sectional cutoffs.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"pgqrki\\\" data-start=\\\"6407\\\" data-end=\\\"6438\\\">What Students Should Focus On<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6440\\\" data-end=\\\"6504\\\">Instead of worrying excessively about slot difficulty, focus on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6506\\\" data-end=\\\"6656\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"r0fbnu\\\" data-start=\\\"6506\\\" data-end=\\\"6543\\\">Maximizing attempts with accuracy<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"5r4dm9\\\" data-start=\\\"6544\\\" data-end=\\\"6588\\\">Strong performance in all three sections<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"hxcczt\\\" data-start=\\\"6589\\\" data-end=\\\"6615\\\">Balanced score profile<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"qnrfo9\\\" data-start=\\\"6616\\\" data-end=\\\"6656\\\">Percentile targets based on colleges<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6658\\\" data-end=\\\"6720\\\">Normalisation is beyond candidate control. Preparation is not.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1hd7irm\\\" data-start=\\\"6727\\\" data-end=\\\"6753\\\">CAT Result Usually Shows<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6755\\\" data-end=\\\"6784\\\">Candidates typically receive:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"6786\\\" data-end=\\\"6893\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"lfmbfn\\\" data-start=\\\"6786\\\" data-end=\\\"6816\\\">Section-wise scaled scores<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"2vpoq4\\\" data-start=\\\"6817\\\" data-end=\\\"6845\\\">Section-wise percentiles<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"2i4nzn\\\" data-start=\\\"6846\\\" data-end=\\\"6870\\\">Overall scaled score<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1cqhcd8\\\" data-start=\\\"6871\\\" data-end=\\\"6893\\\">Overall percentile<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"6895\\\" data-end=\\\"6952\\\">This scorecard is used during shortlisting by institutes.&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 15, 1, '2026-04-17 06:32:02', '2026-04-20 01:04:57'),
(874, 5, 'New Section 16', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" 2\",\"name\":\"_2\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\"}]', 15, 1, '2026-04-17 07:24:00', '2026-04-17 07:24:00');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(900, 11, ' SELECTION PROCESS ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" CAT 2025 RESULTS AND SHORTLISTING \",\"name\":\"_cat_2025_results_and_shortlisting_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT result section is one of the most awaited stages for every management aspirant because it converts months of preparation into measurable performance. However, many candidates misunderstand what the CAT result actually means. A CAT scorecard is important, but it is not the final admission offer. After results are declared, institutes begin their own shortlisting and selection processes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students believe that one high percentile guarantees admission everywhere. In reality, each institute may apply different criteria such as CAT percentile, sectional performance, academics, work experience, diversity factors, written rounds, interviews, and profile strength. Therefore, understanding the CAT result stage properly is extremely important.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This detailed guide explains CAT result declaration, how to download the scorecard, what happens after results, IIM shortlisting process, interview calls, merit logic, and mistakes candidates should avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When CAT Result Is Usually Released<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Based on the provided information, CAT results were tentatively expected from the first week of January on the official website.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">For future sessions, exact dates may vary every year. Candidates should rely only on official announcements.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where to Check CAT Result<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT results are generally published on the official CAT website.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates usually need:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">User ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Password<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Login credentials<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After login, scorecard access may be available.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How to Download CAT Scorecard<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Typical process may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Visit official CAT portal.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Login using registered credentials.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Open result \\/ scorecard section.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 4<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Download PDF scorecard.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 5<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Save multiple copies for future use.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is Included in CAT Scorecard?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A CAT scorecard generally contains performance indicators such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional percentiles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scaled score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Exam year information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Percentile vs Score: Important Difference<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students confuse raw score with percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Raw \\/ Scaled Score<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Represents performance marks after normalization methods.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Shows how many candidates you performed better than comparatively.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Example:<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">99 percentile means you performed better than approximately 99% of test takers.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Result Does NOT Mean Final Admission<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the biggest misconceptions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT result is mainly an entrance performance indicator. Admission decisions usually happen later through institute-specific selection rounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">That means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">High percentile helps strongly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">But admission still depends on later stages<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Happens After CAT Result?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After results, participating institutes may begin shortlisting for next stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These next stages can include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal Interview (PI)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Written Ability Test (WAT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Group Discussion (where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Profile review<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">IIM Shortlisting Process Explained<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The provided information states that shortlisted candidates for the next level of selection may be listed on respective IIM websites, and interview communication may be sent directly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means each IIM may run its own admission process after CAT.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Different IIMs Have Different Criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Every institute may design its own shortlisting model. Criteria can vary based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT overall percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional percentile cutoffs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gender diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reservation norms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">So two candidates with the same CAT percentile may get different outcomes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why 99 Percentile May Not Guarantee All Calls<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Because some institutes value:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strong academics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Balanced profile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience quality<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category-wise competition<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Composite score models<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is why overall profile matters, not percentile alone.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT Merit List Explained<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">There is generally no single universal CAT admission merit list for all institutes. Instead:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each institute may prepare its own shortlist<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Each institute may create its own final merit list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final offers depend on that institute&rsquo;s process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is a crucial concept many candidates miss.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">How Interview Calls Usually Reach Candidates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Shortlisted candidates may receive updates through:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institute website notifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidate dashboard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission portals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always monitor registered email inbox and spam folder regularly after results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Steps Immediately After CAT Result<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Download Scorecard<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Save multiple copies.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Track Institute Websites<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Especially institutes you are targeting.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Start Interview Preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not wait for official call letters.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Gather Documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Prepare marksheets, certificates, work-ex proofs, ID proof, category documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Improve Current Affairs and Communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Useful for interview rounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What If CAT Percentile Is Lower Than Expected?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not assume the journey is over.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Depending on percentile and profile, opportunities may still exist through:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">New IIMs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other top B-schools accepting CAT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tier-2 quality institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Profile-based selections<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Repeat attempt next year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart strategy matters more than panic.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes After CAT Result<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Waiting Without Research<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students lose deadlines.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ignoring Sectional Percentiles<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some institutes require section-wise cutoffs.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only Targeting Old IIMs<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">May miss excellent alternatives.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not Preparing for Interview<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Calls can come quickly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Comparing Blindly With Others<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Every profile is different.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Rechecking \\/ Revaluation of CAT Result<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CAT results are generally released after a standardized evaluation process. Formal rechecking or revaluation opportunities are usually very limited or not commonly available in the traditional board-exam sense. Candidates should always follow official announcements for any objection windows related to answer keys before final results.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" ADMISSION PROCESS \",\"name\":\"_admission_process_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT admission process is one of the most misunderstood stages among MBA aspirants. Many students believe that scoring well in CAT automatically guarantees admission to top IIMs. In reality, CAT percentile is extremely important, but it is only one part of the complete selection process. After results are declared, institutes begin their own multi-stage admission process to identify the most suitable candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Every IIM may use its own shortlisting model, evaluation weightage, academic filters, and final merit formula. This means two candidates with similar CAT percentiles may receive very different outcomes depending on profile strength, academics, interview performance, work experience, diversity factors, and institute-specific policies.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This detailed guide explains the complete CAT admission process, IIM shortlisting stages, WAT, GD, PI rounds, ranking factors, final selection logic, and how candidates should prepare strategically.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is the CAT Admission Process?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT exam is primarily the entrance gateway for admission to management programmes. After CAT results, participating institutes may start selecting candidates for further rounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The admission journey generally includes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT result declaration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Shortlisting for next stage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">WAT \\/ GD \\/ PI rounds (where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Composite score calculation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final merit list<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Offer letter<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Document verification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission confirmation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Truth: CAT Score Alone Is Not Enough<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A strong CAT percentile can help secure attention, but final admission usually depends on multiple factors.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutes may consider:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT overall percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional percentile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gender diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Written round performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Interview performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category norms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall profile suitability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Different IIMs Have Different Admission Criteria<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The provided information states that IIMs shortlist candidates based on their own criteria, which may be independent of each other.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No single universal formula applies to all IIMs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One IIM may emphasize CAT more<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Another may value academics strongly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Another may reward work experience more<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Another may prioritize diversity balance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, candidates should not judge all calls using one institute&rsquo;s logic.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Stage 1: CAT Result and Initial Screening<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After results are declared, institutes may begin filtering candidates based on minimum eligibility and performance benchmarks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This can include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Overall percentile thresholds<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sectional cutoffs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category-wise cutoffs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Basic academic eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Only candidates meeting required standards may move further.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Stage 2: Shortlisting for Interview Rounds<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Shortlisted candidates may be invited for further evaluation rounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This shortlist may depend on a composite profile score, not percentile alone.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Example:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A candidate with slightly lower percentile but excellent academics may receive a call over someone with higher percentile but weaker profile.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Stage 3: WAT (Writing Ability Test)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some institutes may conduct a Writing Ability Test.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Happens in WAT?<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may be asked to write on topics related to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Current affairs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Social issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Business themes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Abstract topics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Policy questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is Evaluated?<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Clarity of thought<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Structure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Grammar<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Awareness<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Communication ability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Stage 4: GD (Group Discussion)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some institutes may include Group Discussion rounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Happens in GD?<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates discuss a topic in a group setting.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is Evaluated?<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Listening ability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leadership<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Team behavior<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Analytical thinking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confidence under pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Not all institutes use GD in every cycle.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Stage 5: PI (Personal Interview)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Personal Interview is often one of the most decisive stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Questions May Cover:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation subjects<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Why MBA?<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Career goals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Current affairs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Hobbies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ethical situations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personal profile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Panel Looks For<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maturity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confidence<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Honesty<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Clarity of goals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Intellectual depth<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Personality fit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Work Experience in CAT Admission Process<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Relevant work experience may strengthen candidature in many institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutes may value:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leadership exposure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Responsibility handled<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Promotions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Industry understanding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Problem-solving maturity<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, poor or inflated experience claims can hurt during interviews.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Academic Performance Importance<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Previous academic performance may be used at different stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates often ignore this factor until results season.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Gender and Academic Diversity Explained<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many institutes aim for balanced classrooms.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Gender Diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional weightage may be considered in some cases to improve gender balance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Academic Diversity<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Non-engineering or varied academic backgrounds may be valued in some selection systems to create richer classroom discussions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Merit List: How Admission Offers Are Decided<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After all rounds, institutes may calculate a final composite score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This may combine:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">WAT score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">GD score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PI score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Diversity factors<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Then final offers may be released.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why High CAT Percentile Sometimes Fails to Convert<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common reasons:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Weak interview performance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Poor academics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Low sectional score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No clarity of goals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Weak communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Stronger competition pool<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institute-specific weighting model<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Moderate Percentile Can Still Convert<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some candidates succeed with moderate percentile because they offer:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Strong academics<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Excellent interview skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Good work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Balanced profile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">High composite scor<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes Candidates Make<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Preparing Only for CAT, Not Interviews<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many lose conversions after good scores.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Ignoring Academics Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Past records can matter.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Copy-Paste MBA Answers<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Panels easily detect rehearsed responses.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No Knowledge of Work Experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should know their own role deeply.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Applying Emotionally<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Every institute uses different criteria.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy After CAT Result<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Research Each Institute Separately<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not assume same rules for all.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Prepare Interview Answers Early<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Start before calls arrive.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Build Current Affairs Awareness<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important for WAT\\/PI.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Gather Documents<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Keep all certificates ready.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practice Communication<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mock interviews can help significantly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" ELIGIBILITY VERIFICATION \",\"name\":\"_eligibility_verification_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The CAT eligibility verification process begins after a candidate gets shortlisted for interview rounds by an IIM or participating institute. Many students focus only on CAT score and interview preparation, but document verification is equally important. Even a high percentile candidate may face rejection, provisional hold, or admission cancellation if eligibility documents are incomplete, incorrect, or not submitted on time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility verification is used to confirm that the candidate truly meets academic qualifications, category claims, graduation status, and admission requirements declared during application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This detailed guide explains CAT eligibility verification for shortlisted candidates, required documents, category certificate rules, final year candidate conditions, provisional admission, deadlines, and critical mistakes to avoid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is CAT Eligibility Verification?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility verification is the process where shortlisted candidates must prove that the information entered in the CAT application form is genuine and valid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutes may verify:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Academic qualifications<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation completion status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marks criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category reservation claims<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identity consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Uploaded application details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This stage usually happens during interview rounds and final admission stages.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Eligibility Verification Is Extremely Important<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates assume interview performance alone decides admission. That is incorrect.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even after selection, admission may be delayed or cancelled if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Marksheets are missing<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Degree certificate unavailable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong category certificate submitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final year proof invalid<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentage criteria not met<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">False claims detected<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submission deadlines missed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mark Sheets and Degree Certificate Requirements<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If shortlisted for interview, candidates may need to show academic proof documents.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Generally required documents include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All semester\\/year marksheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation marksheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Degree certificate (if completed)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attested copies where required<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If finally selected, original degree certificate and marksheets may again be required at the time of joining.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why All Marksheets Matter<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some students think only final semester marksheet is enough. Usually institutes may ask for complete academic progression records.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This helps verify:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Course completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aggregate marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Backlogs status (where relevant)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authenticity of qualification<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What If Degree Certificate Is Not Yet Issued?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">In some universities, final degree certificates take time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may need provisional certificates, consolidated marksheets, or official completion proof as permitted by the institute. Final acceptance depends on institute rules.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation Category Verification Rules<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates claiming reservation benefits under categories such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NC-OBC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">may need to produce original supporting certificates during interview\\/document verification.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Photocopies may also be required for submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Rule: Wrong Category Claim Can Create Serious Problems<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a candidate selects a reserved category in the application but cannot produce valid documents later, benefits may be denied and candidature may be affected according to institute policy.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always claim category only when fully eligible.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NC-OBC and EWS Candidates: Common Mistake<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students upload outdated or incorrect format certificates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always ensure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct authority issued it<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Current validity requirements met<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Proper format used<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name\\/details match application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwD Candidates Verification<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PwD candidates may need disability certificates as per prescribed norms.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institutes may verify:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Benchmark disability eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct category mention<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authentic medical authority issuance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Year Graduation Candidates: Special Rules<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates appearing for Class 12 is not relevant here because CAT is for graduation-level eligibility. Instead, final year graduation candidates are the relevant group.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates in the final year of bachelor&rsquo;s degree or awaiting results may be shortlisted, but they usually need additional proof.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">They may need a certificate from:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Principal<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registrar<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Director<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Authorized university authority<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This certificate may state academic status and latest marks\\/eligibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Marks Requirement for Final Year Candidates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">As provided in the source, final year candidates may need to show eligibility based on latest available grades\\/marks.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">General benchmark mentioned:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">50% marks or equivalent for eligible categories generally<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">45% for SC \\/ ST \\/ PwD categories where applicable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Is Provisional Admission?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a final year candidate is selected before final results are officially available, admission may be granted on a provisional basis.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seat may be temporarily offered<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final confirmation depends on completion of degree requirements<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Required proof must be submitted later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">When Can Provisional Admission Be Cancelled?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Provisional admission may be cancelled if:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Degree not completed in time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final marks below required eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Required certificate not submitted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Submitted proof found incorrect<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Deadlines missed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the biggest risks for final year candidates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Deadline Importance<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The source mentions a deadline for submission of qualifying degree\\/equivalent proof. Exact dates can vary by institute and year.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must check the respective IIM admission policy carefully because institute-specific timelines may differ.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Never assume one common deadline for all institutes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Documents Candidates Should Keep Ready<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Academic Documents<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 marksheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 marksheet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All graduation semester marksheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Degree certificate \\/ provisional certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Identity Documents<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government photo ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CAT application details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Category Documents (if applicable)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC\\/ST certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">NC-OBC certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Year Candidates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registrar\\/Principal certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Latest marksheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes That Cause Trouble<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mismatch in Name Spelling<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Across marksheets, ID, and application.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Old Category Certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">May become invalid.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Missing Semester Marksheets<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Often ignored by students.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Waiting Until Last Minute<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Document issuance can take time.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Assuming Interview Call Means Final Admission<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verification still matters.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Smart Strategy for Shortlisted Candidates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">As soon as CAT results are declared:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Arrange all originals<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Get photocopies attested if needed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scan soft copies clearly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify name\\/date\\/category consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Request university certificates early<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Track institute-specific instructions regularly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 16, 1, '2026-04-20 00:31:50', '2026-04-20 01:04:57');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(909, 11, ' IMPORTANT DATES', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" DATES \",\"name\":\"_dates_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<h2 data-start=\\\"94\\\" data-end=\\\"197\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"165\\\" data-end=\\\"196\\\">CAT exam<\\/strong>.<\\/h2>\\r\\n<div class=\\\"TyagGW_tableContainer\\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\">\\r\\n<table class=\\\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\\\" data-start=\\\"199\\\" data-end=\\\"503\\\">\\r\\n<thead data-start=\\\"199\\\" data-end=\\\"225\\\">\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"199\\\" data-end=\\\"225\\\">\\r\\n<th class=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"199\\\" data-end=\\\"207\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Event<\\/th>\\r\\n<th class=\\\"\\\" data-start=\\\"207\\\" data-end=\\\"225\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Important Date<\\/th>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/thead>\\r\\n<tbody data-start=\\\"236\\\" data-end=\\\"503\\\">\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"236\\\" data-end=\\\"287\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"236\\\" data-end=\\\"258\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Registration Starts<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\" data-start=\\\"258\\\" data-end=\\\"287\\\">01 August 2025 (10:00 AM)<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"288\\\" data-end=\\\"344\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"288\\\" data-end=\\\"313\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Registration Last Date<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\" data-start=\\\"313\\\" data-end=\\\"344\\\">13 September 2025 (5:00 PM)<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"345\\\" data-end=\\\"402\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"345\\\" data-end=\\\"367\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Admit Card Download<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\" data-start=\\\"367\\\" data-end=\\\"402\\\">05 November to 30 November 2025<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"403\\\" data-end=\\\"439\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"403\\\" data-end=\\\"419\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">CAT Exam Date<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\" data-start=\\\"419\\\" data-end=\\\"439\\\">30 November 2025<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr data-start=\\\"440\\\" data-end=\\\"503\\\">\\r\\n<td data-start=\\\"440\\\" data-end=\\\"461\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\">Result Declaration<\\/td>\\r\\n<td data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\" data-start=\\\"461\\\" data-end=\\\"503\\\">First Week of January 2026 (Tentative)<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"505\\\" data-end=\\\"542\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"1k4n7ln\\\" data-start=\\\"549\\\" data-end=\\\"594\\\">Detailed Explanation of CAT Important Dates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"32idna\\\" data-start=\\\"596\\\" data-end=\\\"626\\\">CAT Registration Start Date<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"628\\\" data-end=\\\"814\\\">The CAT application process opened on <strong data-start=\\\"666\\\" data-end=\\\"683\\\">1 August 2025<\\/strong>. From this date, eligible candidates could create login credentials, fill the form, upload documents, and pay the application fee.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"ldv8d8\\\" data-start=\\\"816\\\" data-end=\\\"845\\\">CAT Registration Last Date<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"847\\\" data-end=\\\"1059\\\">The last date mentioned was <strong data-start=\\\"875\\\" data-end=\\\"909\\\">13 September 2025 till 5:00 PM<\\/strong>. Candidates usually should not wait until the final day because heavy traffic, payment issues, or document upload errors may occur near the deadline.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"9lnchb\\\" data-start=\\\"1061\\\" data-end=\\\"1091\\\">CAT Admit Card Release Date<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1093\\\" data-end=\\\"1258\\\">Admit cards were available from <strong data-start=\\\"1125\\\" data-end=\\\"1164\\\">5 November 2025 to 30 November 2025<\\/strong>. Candidates had to download the hall ticket from the official portal using login credentials.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"5v9mae\\\" data-start=\\\"1260\\\" data-end=\\\"1276\\\">CAT Exam Date<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1278\\\" data-end=\\\"1417\\\">CAT 2025 was scheduled for <strong data-start=\\\"1305\\\" data-end=\\\"1325\\\">30 November 2025<\\/strong> in three sessions. Candidates must check exact reporting time and slot on their admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 data-section-id=\\\"12jytwu\\\" data-start=\\\"1419\\\" data-end=\\\"1437\\\">CAT Result Date<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1439\\\" data-end=\\\"1585\\\">Results were tentatively expected in the <strong data-start=\\\"1480\\\" data-end=\\\"1510\\\">first week of January 2026<\\/strong>. After result declaration, IIM shortlisting and interview processes begin.<\\/p>\"}]', 1, 1, '2026-04-20 00:55:22', '2026-04-20 01:05:02'),
(1027, 19, ' APPLICATION PROCESS ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" PROCESS\",\"name\":\"_process\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) application process is conducted online through the official portal. Candidates must complete registration, upload documents, select management institutes, make payment, fill academic details, and submit the final form within the deadline.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students assume the MAT form is simple and rush through it. In reality, small mistakes in photo upload, qualification details, institute selection, or payment completion can create avoidable problems later. A careful and strategic application approach can save time, money, and admission opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Application Process 2026 &ndash; Quick Overview<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates generally need to complete these stages:<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"73\\\"><col width=\\\"330\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step No.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose Test Mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Upload Photo &amp; Signature<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Select Management Institutes (MI)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Make Payment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Fill Personal, Qualification &amp; Experience Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">6<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Final Submission &amp; Print Application<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 1: Choose Test Mode Details<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must first choose how they want to appear for the MAT exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Available Options:<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"195\\\"><col width=\\\"55\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Fee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PBT \\/ CBT (Single Mode)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\u20b92300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PBT + CBT (Double Mode)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\u20b94000<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Meaning of Options<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PBT = Paper Based Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CBT = Computer Based Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PBT + CBT = Both exam modes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose double mode only if you are prepared seriously and want additional score-reporting benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 2: Upload Photograph &amp; Signature<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is one of the most common rejection\\/error areas. Candidates should follow image rules carefully.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Photograph Guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The photograph should be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Recent passport-size colour photo<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Light coloured background (preferably white)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Face clearly visible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No harsh shadows<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Eyes clearly visible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No reflections on glasses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Both ears visible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Caps, hats, dark glasses not allowed<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Religious headwear allowed if face remains visible<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Photo File Rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"113\\\"><col width=\\\"83\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Requirement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">.jpg \\/ .jpeg<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Size<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10 KB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Maximum Size<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">50 KB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Signature Guidelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sign on white paper<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Use black ink pen<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scan signature area only<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Do not upload full page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Signature File Rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"113\\\"><col width=\\\"83\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Requirement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">.jpg \\/ .jpeg<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Size<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5 KB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Maximum Size<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">20 KB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Warning<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This signature may appear on the admit card. If it does not match the signature during exam\\/interview verification, candidature may face issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 3: Choose Management Institutes (MI)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates can select institutes to which MAT scores will be sent.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Standard Selection:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Up to 5 Management Institutes generally included<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Double Test Mode Benefit:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates choosing double test mode can select:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">7 Institutes total (5 standard + 2 extra)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Extra Institute Charges:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional MI choices may require:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">\\u20b9118 per extra MI (including GST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Do not select institutes randomly. Choose based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MBA specialization<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Placement record<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ROI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Location<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Approval status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Past MAT cut-offs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 4: Make Payment<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After selecting institute choices, candidates are redirected to the payment page.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Payment Modes Usually Available:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Credit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">UPI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Net Banking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wallet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After payment, wait for confirmation page. Closing the browser too early can create incomplete transactions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 5: Fill Personal, Qualification &amp; Experience Details<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must carefully enter all required details.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Information Usually Required:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Personal Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Date of Birth<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Gender<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Contact details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Address<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Qualification Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 10 details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Class 12 details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduation details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final year status (if applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Work Experience (if any)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Employer details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Duration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Role information<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Critical Warning<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligibility may be screened based on entered data. Wrong entries can cause future verification issues.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Step 6: Final Submission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Before submitting:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preview complete form<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check spelling mistakes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify marks\\/percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify uploaded images<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify selected exam mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Verify selected institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confirm payment status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After submission:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download confirmation page<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Take printout \\/ PDF copy for records<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Options After Registration<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Successfully registered candidates may receive certain dashboard options.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Update Details<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may edit some details after review.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Usually Non-Editable Fields:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">DOB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Email ID<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mobile Number<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Upgrade Exam Mode<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may upgrade already selected mode to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CBT + PBT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CBT + CBT (if available)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Fee:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">\\u20b91700 (subject to official availability)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Additional MI Choices<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates may add more institute choices by paying:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">\\u20b9118 per MI (including GST)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Admit Card Process<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">All provisionally registered candidates must download admit card from the applicant dashboard.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Notes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card is not sent by post<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card is not sent by email<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Download only from official dashboard<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Check the website regularly for admit card release updates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistakes Students Make While Filling MAT Form<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates lose time or create issues through careless submission.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong email\\/mobile number entered<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blurry photo upload<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signature mismatch<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wrong graduation percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Random institute selection<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leaving payment incomplete<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not downloading final form copy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Waiting until last date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Checklist Before Final Submission<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verify These Items:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct name spelling<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct DOB<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid email &amp; mobile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Photo within size limits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Signature clear<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct academic marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Preferred test mode selected<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Correct institute choices<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Payment successful<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 4, 1, '2026-04-20 05:22:43', '2026-04-21 00:03:03'),
(1028, 19, ' APPLICATION FEE ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" FEES\",\"name\":\"_fees\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) application fee is officially published by AIMA (All India Management Association) on the MAT registration portal. Candidates must pay the prescribed fee online while submitting the application form.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the fee structure is important because MAT offers single mode and double mode registration options, and the total amount depends on the test mode selected.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Application Fee&nbsp; &ndash; Official Structure<\\/h2>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"198\\\"><col width=\\\"123\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Test Mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Application Fee<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Paper Based Test (PBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\u20b92300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Computer Based Test (CBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\u20b92300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PBT + CBT (Both Modes)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">\\u20b94000<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What These Options Mean<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Single Mode Registration &ndash; \\u20b92300<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates choosing only one exam mode need to pay \\u20b92300.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You can choose:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PBT (Paper Based Test)<br>or<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CBT (Computer Based Test)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is suitable for candidates who want one attempt in one selected mode.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Dual Mode Registration &ndash; \\u20b94000<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates choosing both PBT + CBT need to pay \\u20b94000.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This option allows candidates to appear in:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One Paper Based Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One Computer Based Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates selecting dual mode generally get the benefit of selecting 2 extra Management Institutes, in addition to the standard institute choices.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Payment Methods (Officially Mentioned)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT website states that payment can usually be made through:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Credit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Debit Card<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Net Banking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">UPI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Wallet \\/ Paytm wallet<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Which MAT Fee Option Is Better?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose \\u20b92300 Single Mode If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want one serious attempt<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Budget is limited<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are confident in one exam mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose \\u20b94000 Dual Mode If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want more opportunities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want both PBT and CBT exposure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want extra institute selection benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want to maximize admission chances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistakes Students Make<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Paying without deciding mode properly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting dual mode without preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring extra institute advantage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Waiting till last date and facing payment issues<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming fee is refundable<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Professional Note<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Application fee policies may change by session\\/year. Always verify the latest active session fee on the official portal before payment.<\\/p>\"}]', 5, 1, '2026-04-20 05:22:43', '2026-04-21 00:03:03');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1030, 19, ' EXAMINATION SCHEMES', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" EXAM PATTERN\",\"name\":\"_exam_pattern\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) follows a structured and balanced exam pattern designed to evaluate a candidate&rsquo;s readiness for MBA and allied management programmes. Understanding the MAT exam pattern is one of the most important parts of preparation because many candidates study topics extensively but fail to build the right exam strategy. Knowing how the paper is divided, how marks are awarded, and how sections should be attempted can significantly improve final performance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT exam pattern focuses on testing five major skill areas: language ability, reasoning, mathematical aptitude, analytical interpretation, and business awareness. Since each section carries equal number of questions, candidates need balanced preparation rather than over-focusing on one subject.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Exam Pattern 2026 &ndash; Quick Overview<\\/h2>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"186\\\"><col width=\\\"366\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Particulars<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Management Aptitude Test (MAT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Level<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">National Level MBA Entrance Exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Paper-Based Test (PBT) \\/ Computer-Based Test (CBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Question Type<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total Sections<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">150<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Questions Per Section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Negative Marking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Yes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Penalty for Wrong Answer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">-0.25 mark<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Correct Answer Marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">+1 mark<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Exam Pattern 2026 &ndash; Section-Wise Distribution<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT paper is divided into five sections with equal weightage in terms of number of questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"92\\\"><col width=\\\"255\\\"><col width=\\\"127\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section No.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No. of Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">I<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Language Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">II<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">III<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">IV<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Analysis and Sufficiency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">V<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Economic and Business Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Structure Matters<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since every section contains 30 questions, no section should be ignored. Many students focus only on Quantitative Aptitude or Reasoning and neglect General Awareness or English. This creates an unbalanced score profile and can reduce overall competitiveness.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Detailed Explanation of Each Section<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Language Comprehension<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section evaluates communication ability, grammar understanding, vocabulary, and reading skills.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Covered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reading comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Vocabulary usage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Grammar correction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para jumbles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sentence completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Synonyms and antonyms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strong performance in this section helps candidates score quickly if reading speed and vocabulary are strong.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section measures logical decision-making, pattern recognition, and analytical thinking.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Covered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seating arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blood relations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Coding-decoding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Syllogism<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Series<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Statement-based reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Puzzles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section is highly scoring for candidates who practice regularly. Accuracy matters more than guesswork.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Mathematical Skills<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section tests quantitative aptitude and numerical problem-solving ability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Covered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ratio and proportion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Profit and loss<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Time and work<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Algebra<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Geometry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Average<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Number system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students fear this section unnecessarily. In MAT, concept clarity and speed in arithmetic topics often produce better returns than advanced mathematics.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Data Analysis and Sufficiency<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section checks interpretation of numerical data and decision-making based on information.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Covered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tables<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pie charts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Line graphs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Bar charts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Caselets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data sufficiency sets<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who master approximation techniques and percentage conversions can score strongly here.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5. Economic and Business Environment<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section evaluates awareness of business trends, economy, current affairs, and corporate developments.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Areas Covered:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Business news<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Economic updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Appointments<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Budget highlights<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">National and international current affairs<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Importance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section is often underestimated. However, it can help overall score profile and is useful during GD-PI rounds after exam results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Marking Scheme 2026<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT exam includes negative marking, which means careless attempts can reduce your score.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"126\\\"><col width=\\\"60\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Response Type<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Marks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Correct Answer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">+1<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Incorrect Answer<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">-0.25<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Unattempted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">0<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Attempting all questions randomly is a poor strategy. Smart selection and calculated attempts generally outperform blind maximum attempts.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Time Management Strategy for MAT Exam<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Even strong candidates lose marks due to poor time allocation. Balanced time usage is critical.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended Time Split<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"245\\\"><col width=\\\"122\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Suggested Time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Language Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">20&ndash;25 mins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 mins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 mins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Analysis<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 mins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Economic &amp; Business Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10&ndash;15 mins<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Guidance<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a question takes too long, move ahead and return later. MAT rewards speed with consistency.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistakes Students Make in MAT Exam Pattern Strategy<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many aspirants know the syllabus but still underperform due to execution mistakes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring negative marking<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Spending too much time on difficult Quant questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Leaving easier sections for later<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guessing too many answers at the end<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring Economic &amp; Business Environment completely<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Never practicing full mock papers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Success in MAT depends not only on knowledge but on paper-handling skill.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">High-Score Attempt Strategy for MAT<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A strong attempt sequence can improve confidence and momentum.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Recommended Order (Flexible by Strength)<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Language Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Analysis<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Economic and Business Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Works<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Starting with familiar and moderately quick sections builds rhythm early in the exam.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" EXAM MODE \",\"name\":\"_exam_mode_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) offers multiple exam modes to provide flexibility and convenience to candidates. This is one of the major advantages of MAT compared to many other entrance examinations, as students can choose the mode that best suits their comfort level, exam strategy, and preparation style.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates can appear for MAT through Paper Based Test (PBT), Computer Based Test (CBT), or choose both modes (PBT+CBT) by paying an additional fee. This flexible system allows aspirants to maximize opportunities and improve admission chances by selecting the most suitable testing format.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Understanding the differences between these modes is important because choosing the right exam mode can directly affect performance, comfort, and score outcomes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Exam Modes 2026 &ndash; Available Options<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates can take the MAT exam in any of the following modes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Paper Based Test (PBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Computer Based Test (CBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Paper Based Test + Computer Based Test (PBT+CBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Each mode is valid for admission consideration, but the exam experience and flexibility may differ.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Paper Based Test (PBT)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Paper Based Test is the traditional offline examination mode where candidates answer questions using an OMR sheet or printed answer format at the allotted exam centre.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Suitable For:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates comfortable with written exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Students who prefer reading questions on paper<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aspirants less comfortable with computer screens<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Advantages:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Familiar exam environment for many students<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Easier for those who prefer handwritten rough work<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduced screen fatigue during exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Consideration:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates must be careful while marking answers because mistakes in OMR marking can affect results.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Computer Based Test (CBT)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Computer Based Test is conducted through a computer interface at designated test centres. Candidates answer questions digitally using the on-screen system.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Suitable For:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Candidates comfortable using computers<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Students who prefer digital interfaces<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Aspirants who regularly practice online mock tests<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Advantages:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Modern exam environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Faster navigation between questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Similar experience to many other national-level computer-based exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Consideration:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students unfamiliar with screen-based exams should practice CBT mock tests in advance.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Paper Based Test + Computer Based Test (PBT+CBT)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates also have the option to appear in both PBT and CBT modes by paying an additional fee. This is a strategic option for students who want more opportunities and wider score submission benefits.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Fee Structure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Standard MAT fee: \\u20b92300<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional mode fee: \\u20b91700<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Total for PBT + CBT: \\u20b94000<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Major Benefits:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Opportunity to appear in two test modes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Better chances to secure a stronger score profile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional selection options for management institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Greater flexibility in admissions strategy<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Additional Institute Selection Benefit<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates opting for the additional test mode receive an extra advantage in score reporting.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Institute Selection Options:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Standard registration: Select 5 Management Institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PBT + CBT option: Select 7 Management Institutes total<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means candidates choosing both modes can send scores to 2 additional institutes, increasing admission opportunities without separate score-reporting effort.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Which MAT Exam Mode Should You Choose?<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choosing the right mode should depend on comfort level, preparation strategy, and admission goals.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose PBT If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You perform better on paper-based exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You prefer physical reading and rough calculations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are less comfortable with digital testing systems<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose CBT If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are comfortable with online exams<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You regularly practice on computer-based mocks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You prefer faster question navigation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Choose PBT + CBT If:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want maximum admission opportunities<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want to improve chances through multiple attempts<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You want score reporting to 7 institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">You are serious about maximizing MBA options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistakes Students Make While Choosing MAT Mode<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates select exam mode casually without strategic thinking.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choosing CBT without any computer-based practice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Choosing PBT only because friends selected it<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring the extra value of PBT+CBT option<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Selecting both modes without sufficient preparation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Not considering institute selection benefits<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Advice:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Your exam mode should match your performance style, not popularity trends.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Strategy for Serious Aspirants<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates targeting better admission chances often consider PBT+CBT because:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">It increases opportunity exposure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Provides additional institute selection options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduces dependency on one test sitting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Helps serious aspirants diversify admission chances<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">However, this option should be chosen only if preparation level supports multiple attempts.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" EXAM DURATION\",\"name\":\"_exam_duration\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) is designed to evaluate a candidate&rsquo;s aptitude under a controlled time environment. Understanding the MAT exam duration is extremely important because many students focus only on syllabus preparation and ignore the time-pressure aspect of the examination. In reality, strong subject knowledge alone does not guarantee a high score if time is not managed efficiently.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT contains five sections with thirty questions each, making a total of 150 questions that must be attempted within 120 minutes. This means candidates need to maintain both speed and accuracy throughout the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The exam duration is intentionally compact to test decision-making, concentration, and performance under pressure&mdash;skills that are highly relevant for management education and future leadership roles.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Exam Duration 2026 &ndash;&nbsp;<\\/h2>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"192\\\"><col width=\\\"193\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Particulars<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Details<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total Sections<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">5<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Questions in Each Section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">150<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Total Exam Duration<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">120 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Average Time Per Question<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Less than 1 Minute<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Exam Type<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time-Bound Objective Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Total Duration Explained<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates receive 120 minutes (2 hours) to complete all 150 questions. Since the number of questions is relatively high compared to available time, MAT is considered a speed-based aptitude exam where efficient question selection becomes critical.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Duration Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students assume two hours is enough, but when divided across 150 questions, the average available time per question is limited. This creates pressure in sections such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Data Analysis and Sufficiency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These sections may require calculations or deeper thinking, which is why time planning is essential.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section-Wise Question Distribution and Time Logic<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since MAT has five sections with equal number of questions, candidates should ideally create a balanced time plan rather than spending excessive time on one area.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"255\\\"><col width=\\\"83\\\"><col width=\\\"122\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Suggested Time<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Language Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">20&ndash;25 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Analysis and Sufficiency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Economic and Business Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">10&ndash;15 Minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is not an official sectional time restriction. It is a strategic recommendation to help candidates complete the paper efficiently.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Average Time Per Question in MAT<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">With 150 questions in 120 minutes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Average time available per question = 48 seconds approximately<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What This Means Practically<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">You cannot afford to solve every difficult question in detail. Candidates who try to fully solve every problem often run out of time before completing easier scoring questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT rewards candidates who can:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Identify easy questions quickly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Skip time-consuming traps<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Return later if time remains<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Maintain accuracy under speed pressure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Best Time Management Strategy for MAT Exam<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Start with Your Strongest Section<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Beginning with a section where you are comfortable helps build momentum and confidence early in the exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Avoid Getting Stuck<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If a question takes too long, move forward immediately. One difficult question can cost the time needed for three easy ones.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">3. Maintain a Checkpoint System<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">A smart benchmark can be:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">30 minutes completed: Around 35&ndash;40 questions attempted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">60 minutes completed: Around 75 questions attempted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">90 minutes completed: Around 115 questions attempted<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Final 30 minutes: Finish remaining + review marked questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">4. Keep Final Minutes for Smart Review<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Use the last few minutes to revisit doubtful but manageable questions instead of random guessing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistakes Students Make in MAT Duration Handling<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates lose marks not because of low knowledge, but because of poor pacing.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Spending too much time on Quantitative Aptitude<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reading long RC passages too slowly<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Guessing rapidly in final minutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring clock tracking during exam<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempting difficult questions first<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Panicking after one tough section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Time pressure affects everyone. The difference between average and high scorers is how calmly they manage it.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" EXAM MEDIUM \",\"name\":\"_exam_medium_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p data-start=\\\"53\\\" data-end=\\\"297\\\">The <strong data-start=\\\"57\\\" data-end=\\\"91\\\">Management Aptitude Test (MAT)<\\/strong> is generally conducted in <strong data-start=\\\"118\\\" data-end=\\\"136\\\">English medium<\\/strong>. This means the question paper, examination instructions, online interface (for CBT mode), and most official exam-related communication are provided in English.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"299\\\" data-end=\\\"621\\\">For candidates appearing in <strong data-start=\\\"327\\\" data-end=\\\"353\\\">Paper Based Test (PBT)<\\/strong> or <strong data-start=\\\"357\\\" data-end=\\\"386\\\">Computer Based Test (CBT)<\\/strong> mode, the questions are typically available in English only. MAT is a national-level MBA entrance examination, and English is used as the common language because management education in many institutes is largely conducted in English.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"299\\\" data-end=\\\"621\\\">Is Regional Language Available in MAT?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"670\\\" data-end=\\\"822\\\">As per the standard MAT exam format, <strong data-start=\\\"707\\\" data-end=\\\"764\\\">regional language options are generally not available<\\/strong>. The exam is not commonly conducted in languages such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"824\\\" data-end=\\\"932\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"nxa5sa\\\" data-start=\\\"824\\\" data-end=\\\"833\\\">Hindi<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1sefhkz\\\" data-start=\\\"834\\\" data-end=\\\"845\\\">Punjabi<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1cagkdx\\\" data-start=\\\"846\\\" data-end=\\\"855\\\">Tamil<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"kkgoxe\\\" data-start=\\\"856\\\" data-end=\\\"866\\\">Telugu<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"51iwma\\\" data-start=\\\"867\\\" data-end=\\\"878\\\">Bengali<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"28qule\\\" data-start=\\\"879\\\" data-end=\\\"890\\\">Marathi<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"88u05b\\\" data-start=\\\"891\\\" data-end=\\\"903\\\">Gujarati<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"idv17c\\\" data-start=\\\"904\\\" data-end=\\\"932\\\">Other regional languages<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"934\\\" data-end=\\\"1011\\\">Candidates are usually required to attempt the examination in English medium.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"5a1be5\\\" data-start=\\\"1018\\\" data-end=\\\"1053\\\">Why English Medium is Used in MAT<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1055\\\" data-end=\\\"1142\\\">English is used as the exam medium because MBA and management programmes often involve:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1144\\\" data-end=\\\"1317\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"94rer\\\" data-start=\\\"1144\\\" data-end=\\\"1180\\\">English-based classroom learning<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1mxw4gr\\\" data-start=\\\"1181\\\" data-end=\\\"1215\\\">Case studies and presentations<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1jtm87i\\\" data-start=\\\"1216\\\" data-end=\\\"1242\\\">Business communication<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"l2llud\\\" data-start=\\\"1243\\\" data-end=\\\"1279\\\">Interviews and group discussions<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1bybjg1\\\" data-start=\\\"1280\\\" data-end=\\\"1317\\\">Corporate workplace communication<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1319\\\" data-end=\\\"1413\\\">Using one common medium also helps maintain a standardized national-level examination process.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 data-section-id=\\\"d19i3l\\\" data-start=\\\"1420\\\" data-end=\\\"1453\\\">Important Advice for Candidates<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p data-start=\\\"1455\\\" data-end=\\\"1646\\\">Candidates from regional language or non-English backgrounds should not be discouraged. Many students successfully clear MAT every year through proper preparation. Focus areas should include:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul data-start=\\\"1648\\\" data-end=\\\"1788\\\">\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"bjvn4\\\" data-start=\\\"1648\\\" data-end=\\\"1680\\\">Basic vocabulary improvement<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"1xaplzz\\\" data-start=\\\"1681\\\" data-end=\\\"1715\\\">Reading comprehension practice<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"8etesi\\\" data-start=\\\"1716\\\" data-end=\\\"1757\\\">Familiarity with English instructions<\\/li>\\r\\n<li data-section-id=\\\"uk6sid\\\" data-start=\\\"1758\\\" data-end=\\\"1788\\\">Regular mock test practice<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\"}]', 3, 1, '2026-04-20 05:22:43', '2026-04-21 00:03:07');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1031, 19, ' ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" BASIC REQUIREMENT\",\"name\":\"_basic_requirement\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates who wish to appear for the MAT exam must meet the following primary academic condition:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Graduates in any discipline are eligible to apply.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means candidates who have completed a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university can apply, irrespective of stream.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Eligible academic backgrounds generally include:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Commerce<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Science<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Arts \\/ Humanities<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Engineering<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Management<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Computer Applications<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pharmacy<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Law<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Agriculture<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other recognized undergraduate programmes<\\/h3>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Insight<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">One of the major strengths of MAT is that it does not restrict applicants to a specific stream. This creates equal opportunity for students from varied educational backgrounds.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" QUALIFICATION CRITERIA \",\"name\":\"_qualification_criteria_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The qualification requirement is based on completion of an undergraduate degree.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Accepted Qualification Standard:<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should have completed a Bachelor&rsquo;s degree in any discipline from a recognized institution or university.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Clarification<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT exam itself is an entrance test. Final admission into MBA programmes depends on the institute selected, and some colleges may require:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minimum graduation percentage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Recognized degree status<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Valid final-year result submission<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Additional selection rounds such as GD\\/PI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Therefore, exam eligibility and college admission eligibility should not be treated as identical.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Can Final Year Students Apply for MAT?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Yes. Final year students of graduate courses can also apply for the MAT exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means candidates who are currently pursuing the last year \\/ final semester of their bachelor&rsquo;s degree and are awaiting final results are generally eligible to register.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This is Important<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This allows students to appear for MAT without waiting for graduation completion, helping them save one academic year and move directly toward MBA admission planning.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Practical Advice for Final Year Students<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates applying in final year status should ensure:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">They will complete graduation within the required admission timeline<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Mark sheets and provisional results can be produced when demanded by colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">No backlog delays affect final admission eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students qualify in the entrance exam but face admission problems later due to pending graduation formalities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Is MAT Open to All Streams?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Yes. MAT is considered a multi-discipline management entrance exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates from all major streams can apply, such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">B.Com \\/ BBA graduates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">B.Sc \\/ BCA graduates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">BA graduates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">B.Tech \\/ BE graduates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Pharmacy or Agriculture graduates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Other recognized undergraduate degrees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Strategic Advantage<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Students from technical or non-commerce backgrounds often perform strongly in MAT because reasoning and aptitude sections reward skill, not degree stream.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Minimum Marks Requirement in Graduation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT exam eligibility itself is broadly graduation-based, but minimum marks may vary by participating institute.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some colleges may ask for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">50% marks in graduation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Relaxation for reserved categories<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Different academic cut-offs depending on programme level<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always check the admission criteria of the specific B-School you are targeting, not only MAT exam eligibility.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">NIOS and Recognized Board Candidates Eligibility<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates from NIOS or other recognized boards are generally eligible, provided their subsequent graduation degree is from a recognized university\\/institution<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why This Matters<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students wrongly assume open schooling backgrounds create restrictions. In most cases, recognized academic progression is what matters.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" AGE LIMIT \",\"name\":\"_age_limit_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Generally, there is no strict upper age limit specified for appearing in the MAT exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This makes MAT suitable for:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><strong>Fresh graduates<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"font-weight: bold;\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><strong>Gap year students<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"font-weight: bold;\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><strong>Working professionals<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"font-weight: bold;\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><strong>Career switch candidates<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"font-weight: bold;\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\"><strong>Experienced candidates planning MBA growth<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Insight<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Because there is usually no narrow age barrier, MAT becomes a practical option for candidates returning to academics after work experience.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><strong>Common Mistakes Students Make Regarding MAT Eligibility<\\/strong><\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many aspirants misunderstand basic rules and lose time or opportunities.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Errors:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assuming only commerce students can apply<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Believing MBA entrance exams require work experience<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Ignoring institute-specific graduation percentage rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applying in final year without planning result timelines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confusing exam eligibility with college admission eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Expert Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Always check both:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MAT exam eligibility<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Target college admission criteria<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ol>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These are related but not always the same.<\\/p>\"},{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" RESERVATION\",\"name\":\"_reservation\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) is an entrance examination used by multiple MBA colleges and management institutes across India. Because MAT functions as a score-based admission gateway rather than a single centralized seat-allotment system, many students are confused about whether reservation applies directly in the MAT exam.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The correct understanding is important: reservation in MAT is different from reservation in college admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Is There Reservation in MAT Exam Itself?<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Direct Exam-Level Reservation<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Generally, the MAT exam itself does not operate like a centralized counselling exam with a common reservation-based seat allotment system. It is primarily an entrance test where candidates receive scores that are used by participating institutes for admissions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means MAT mainly provides:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Entrance test score<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Performance evaluation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission eligibility route to institutes<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The exam score process itself is not usually structured as a central category-based seat allotment model.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where Reservation Usually Applies &ndash; At Institute Level<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation policies are commonly applied by the individual colleges \\/ universities \\/ institutes that accept MAT scores, depending on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Government regulations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">University rules<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State policies<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Institution type (government\\/private\\/deemed)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minority or special category norms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This means one MAT-accepting college may follow a different reservation structure than another.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Categories Commonly Considered by Institutes (Varies by College)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Depending on the institution, reservation may be available for categories such as:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">SC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ST<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">OBC<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">EWS<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PwD<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State domicile quota (in some universities)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Minority category (where applicable)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Availability, percentage, and documentation rules vary by institute.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why Students Get Confused About MAT Reservation<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates assume:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">MAT scorecard itself grants reserved seats<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">All MAT colleges follow one reservation system<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Every institute offers the same quota structure<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">These assumptions are usually incorrect.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Since MAT is accepted by many institutions, admission policies are decentralized.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What Candidates Should Do Practically<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">If reservation benefits are important for your admission planning:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Check These Before Applying to Colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category quota availability<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Required caste\\/category certificate format<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Validity date of certificate<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">State vs central certificate acceptance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cut-off differences by category<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Separate counselling rounds if any<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Hidden Mistake Many Students Make<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Some students prepare only for the exam and check category rules after results. By then, deadlines or document issues may create problems.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Better Approach:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Check institute-wise reservation policy before selecting colleges.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Guidance for MAT Aspirants<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After getting MAT scores, shortlist colleges based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Category reservation benefit<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fees<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Placement record<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Accreditation<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">ROI<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admission process<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reservation should be one factor, not the only factor.<\\/p>\"}]', 2, 1, '2026-04-20 05:22:43', '2026-04-21 00:03:07'),
(1032, 19, ' IMPORTANT DATES ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" DATES \",\"name\":\"_dates_\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) is conducted multiple times each year, giving candidates several opportunities to improve scores and secure admission into MBA and allied management programmes. MAT is typically held in February, May, September, and December sessions. Because different modes such as Paper Based Test (PBT) and Computer Based Test (CBT) may have separate schedules, candidates must carefully track official dates.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Checking important dates regularly is essential because late applications, missed admit card downloads, or confusion between PBT and CBT schedules can directly affect your attempt.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Important Dates 2026 &ndash; Latest Official Update (May 2026 Session)<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Based on the official MAT portal, the May 2026 session application schedule is active.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3>Registration Last Dates<\\/h3>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"198\\\"><col width=\\\"143\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mode of Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Last Date to Apply<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Paper Based Test (PBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">25 May 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Computer Based Test (CBT)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">8 June 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Exam Dates 2026 (May Session)<\\/h3>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"103\\\"><col width=\\\"360\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mode of Test<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expected \\/ Announced Exam Date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">PBT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After registration closure (as per admit card schedule)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">CBT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">After registration closure (as per official portal)<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should verify exact exam city, reporting time, and shift details through the admit card.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Admit Card Dates 2026<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The MAT admit card is usually released a few days before the examination date. Candidates must log in to the official website and download the admit card using their credentials.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Guidance:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card is mandatory for exam entry<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Carry printed copy for PBT mode<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Check name, exam date, centre, and reporting time carefully<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Read exam day instructions in advance<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Sessions Conducted Every Year<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT is generally conducted four times annually, which makes it one of the most flexible MBA entrance exams in India<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Usual Sessions:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">February<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">May<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">September<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">December<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This allows candidates to:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Attempt multiple times in one year<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Improve score profile<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Apply strategically to colleges<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Reduce pressure of one single exam attempt<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expected MAT 2026 Full-Year Timeline<\\/h2>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"119\\\"><col width=\\\"196\\\"><col width=\\\"152\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Session<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Likely Registration Period<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Likely Exam Period<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">February 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Dec 2025 &ndash; Feb 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Feb \\/ Mar 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">May 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Apr &ndash; Jun 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">May \\/ Jun 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">September 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Jul &ndash; Sep 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Sep 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">December 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Oct &ndash; Dec 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Dec 2026<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Note<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Future sessions (September and December 2026) are based on the usual annual MAT cycle. Exact dates should be checked on the official website once announced.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Why MAT Important Dates Matter<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many candidates prepare well but lose opportunities due to poor deadline management.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Common Mistakes:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Waiting until last date to apply<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Confusing PBT and CBT deadlines<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Forgetting admit card download<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Missing result updates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Applying late and losing preferred test city options<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Professional Advice<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Apply early whenever registration opens. Early application often gives better city availability and reduces technical issues near deadlines.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">What to Track in Every MAT Session<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Candidates should monitor these date categories:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Registration opening date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Last date to apply<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Admit card release date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">PBT exam date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">CBT exam date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Result declaration date<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Scorecard download window<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p>&nbsp;<\\/p>\"}]', 1, 1, '2026-04-20 05:22:43', '2026-04-21 00:02:44');
INSERT INTO `dynamic_exam_sections` (`id`, `dynamic_exam_id`, `heading`, `content`, `order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1033, 19, ' SYLLABUS ', '[{\"type\":\"input\",\"inputType\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\" SYLLABUS INFORMATION\",\"name\":\"_syllabus_information\",\"required\":true,\"options\":\"\",\"value\":\"<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The Management Aptitude Test (MAT) syllabus is structured to assess whether a candidate possesses the aptitude, reasoning ability, communication skills, numerical understanding, analytical thinking, and business awareness required for management education. Unlike subject-specific entrance exams, MAT is an aptitude-based examination, which means it evaluates practical skills rather than testing only academic memorization.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">According to the official MAT examination structure published by AIMA (All India Management Association), the exam consists of five major sections, each designed to test a different competency relevant for MBA and allied management programmes.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students make the mistake of searching only for a short topic list. In reality, MAT preparation should be based on understanding the section-wise pattern, commonly asked concepts, scoring areas, and strategic preparation methods. A deep understanding of the syllabus gives a major advantage over candidates who study randomly.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">MAT Official Syllabus Structure&nbsp;<\\/h2>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">The official MAT exam pattern confirms five sections with equal number of questions.<\\/p>\\r\\n<div dir=\\\"ltr\\\" align=\\\"left\\\">\\r\\n<table><colgroup><col width=\\\"92\\\"><col width=\\\"255\\\"><col width=\\\"127\\\"><\\/colgroup>\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Section No.<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Official Section Name<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">No. of Questions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">I<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Language Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">II<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">III<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Mathematical Skills<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">IV<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Data Analysis and Sufficiency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">V<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Economic and Business Environment<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">30<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/td>\\r\\n<\\/tr>\\r\\n<\\/tbody>\\r\\n<\\/table>\\r\\n<\\/div>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Where This Is Mentioned on Official Website<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Then check:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">About MAT<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Information to Candidates<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Test Structure \\/ Exam Pattern Section<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This is where the official section names and distribution are provided.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h2 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Detailed Section-Wise MAT Syllabus 2026<\\/h2>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">1. Language Comprehension<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section evaluates a candidate&rsquo;s ability to understand written English, interpret information, apply grammar rules, and process language accurately. Since management education involves presentations, reports, communication, and case-study reading, this section is highly relevant.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Topics:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Reading Comprehension<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Passages followed by questions based on:<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Main idea<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tone of passage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Inference<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fact vs opinion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Vocabulary in context<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Vocabulary<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Synonyms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Antonyms<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Word usage<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">One word substitution<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Foreign words used in English<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Grammar<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Tenses<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Subject-verb agreement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Prepositions<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Articles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sentence correction<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Error spotting<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verbal Ability<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Para jumbles<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Fill in the blanks<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Sentence completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Odd sentence out<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Expert Preparation Advice<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Many students memorize vocabulary lists but ignore comprehension. This is a mistake because comprehension often carries practical scoring value. Improve daily reading speed and editorial analysis.<\\/p>\\r\\n<h3 dir=\\\"ltr\\\">2. Intelligence and Critical Reasoning<\\/h3>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">This section tests logical decision-making, structured thinking, and pattern recognition. It reflects managerial problem-solving ability.<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Important Topics:<\\/p>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Logical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Seating arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Linear arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Circular arrangement<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Blood relations<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Direction sense<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Analytical Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Statement and assumption<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Statement and conclusion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Cause and effect<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Decision making logic<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Verbal Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Syllogism<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Assertion and reason<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Logical consistency<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<\\/ul>\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\">Non-Verbal Reasoning<\\/p>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Series completion<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Analogy patterns<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li dir=\\\"ltr\\\" aria-level=\\\"1\\\">\\r\\n<p dir=\\\"ltr\\\" role=\\\"presentation\\\">Coding-decoding<\\/p>\\r\\n<\\/li>\\r\\n<li d