er_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(399, 75, '6fd01ea2-14cc-41d7-8c10-a94807550f1c', 'acc96fe9-f3b0-4239-abbb-1366ebb6aff4', 322, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 02:10:27', '2026-06-17 00:22:56', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1099\">The syllabus introduces learners to important concepts, traditions, and philosophical ideas associated with Hinduism and Indian civilization.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1101\" data-end=\"1104\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1xhszhm\" data-start=\"1106\" data-end=\"1137\">Salient Features of Hinduism</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1139\" data-end=\"1276\">This module introduces the foundational characteristics and unique aspects of Hinduism as one of the world&rsquo;s oldest spiritual traditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1278\" data-end=\"1299\">Students learn about:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1301\" data-end=\"1451\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"19x94av\" data-start=\"1301\" data-end=\"1334\">Core philosophical principles</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"me4r0t\" data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1372\">Diversity within Hindu traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"olfoy\" data-start=\"1373\" data-end=\"1409\">Spiritual and cultural practices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ucj4b9\" data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1451\">The role of dharma and ethics in life</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1453\" data-end=\"1543\">The module provides an overview of Hindu thought and its influence on Indian civilization.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1545\" data-end=\"1548\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"ayswdi\" data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1588\">The Heritage of Scriptures in India</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1590\" data-end=\"1684\">This section focuses on the rich scriptural heritage of India and its intellectual traditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1686\" data-end=\"1703\">Students explore:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1705\" data-end=\"1844\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ergoso\" data-start=\"1705\" data-end=\"1729\">Vedas and Upanishads</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sm73b9\" data-start=\"1730\" data-end=\"1751\">Epics and Puranas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ceft3p\" data-start=\"1752\" data-end=\"1791\">Importance of scriptural traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2iqan\" data-start=\"1792\" data-end=\"1844\">Role of knowledge transmission in Indian culture</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1846\" data-end=\"1950\">The module helps learners understand how ancient texts shaped Indian philosophy and spiritual practices.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1952\" data-end=\"1955\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"17h7tj7\" data-start=\"1957\" data-end=\"1978\">The Idea of Iswarā</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"2105\">This topic explains the philosophical understanding of <strong data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2087\">Iswarā (Supreme Reality or Divine Consciousness)</strong> in Hindu thought.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2107\" data-end=\"2128\">Students learn about:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2130\" data-end=\"2274\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1exgmxw\" data-start=\"2130\" data-end=\"2166\">Concepts of divinity in Hinduism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1g90en9\" data-start=\"2167\" data-end=\"2210\">Different philosophical interpretations</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1g4yca8\" data-start=\"2211\" data-end=\"2274\">Relationship between individual and universal consciousness</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2276\" data-end=\"2356\">The module introduces spiritual perspectives on existence and divine principles.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2358\" data-end=\"2361\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1xn3o2h\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2377\">Puruṣārthās</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"2379\" data-end=\"2457\">This module focuses on the four major goals of human life in Hindu philosophy:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2459\" data-end=\"2567\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1q2ej99\" data-start=\"2459\" data-end=\"2485\">Dharma (righteousness)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"g4uwyi\" data-start=\"2486\" data-end=\"2508\">Artha (prosperity)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12xmjx5\" data-start=\"2509\" data-end=\"2543\">Kāma (desires and fulfillment)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j9mhlj\" data-start=\"2544\" data-end=\"2567\">Moksha (liberation)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2569\" data-end=\"2662\">Students understand how these principles guide balanced personal, social, and spiritual life.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2664\" data-end=\"2667\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"cap6ws\" data-start=\"2669\" data-end=\"2691\">The Theory of Karma</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"2693\" data-end=\"2781\">The concept of karma is one of the most important philosophical foundations in Hinduism.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2783\" data-end=\"2800\">Students explore:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2802\" data-end=\"2959\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1g7r6er\" data-start=\"2802\" data-end=\"2835\">Law of action and consequence</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qm2dfv\" data-start=\"2836\" data-end=\"2882\">Ethical responsibility and decision-making</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"13ud3pa\" data-start=\"2883\" data-end=\"2912\">Karma and personal growth</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1r4jzuo\" data-start=\"2913\" data-end=\"2959\">Spiritual perspectives on life experiences</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2961\" data-end=\"3051\">This module helps learners understand the philosophical and practical dimensions of karma.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3053\" data-end=\"3056\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"123y1lx\" data-start=\"3058\" data-end=\"3095\">Sanyasa &ndash; Pinnacle of Selflessness</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"3097\" data-end=\"3217\">This topic introduces the concept of <strong data-start=\"3134\" data-end=\"3145\">Sanyasa</strong>, which represents renunciation, selflessness, and spiritual dedication.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3219\" data-end=\"3240\">Students learn about:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3242\" data-end=\"3366\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"j84f46\" data-start=\"3242\" data-end=\"3280\">Stages of life in Hindu philosophy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yyfwxl\" data-start=\"3281\" data-end=\"3324\">Importance of detachment and discipline</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qhfc7e\" data-start=\"3325\" data-end=\"3366\">Spiritual growth and self-realization</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3368\" data-end=\"3466\">The module explains how selflessness and simplicity are viewed within Indian spiritual traditions.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3468\" data-end=\"3471\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"nb1afg\" data-start=\"3473\" data-end=\"3500\">Sādhanā in Personal Life</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"3502\" data-end=\"3577\">This module focuses on spiritual discipline and self-development practices.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3579\" data-end=\"3596\">Students explore:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3598\" data-end=\"3752\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tzi52x\" data-start=\"3598\" data-end=\"3632\">Meditation and self-reflection</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ojr8jo\" data-start=\"3633\" data-end=\"3662\">Daily spiritual practices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12wwv8s\" data-start=\"3663\" data-end=\"3700\">Mental discipline and mindfulness</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4el0j\" data-start=\"3701\" data-end=\"3752\">Role of personal growth in spiritual traditions</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3754\" data-end=\"3840\">The module highlights practical applications of spiritual principles in everyday life.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3842\" data-end=\"3845\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"jdw6ld\" data-start=\"3847\" data-end=\"3881\">Temples &ndash; The Cradle of Culture</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"3883\" data-end=\"4001\">Temples are explored not only as places of worship but also as centers of art, education, culture, and community life.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4003\" data-end=\"4023\">Students understand:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4025\" data-end=\"4182\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17si78s\" data-start=\"4025\" data-end=\"4061\">Cultural significance of temples</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hb74ye\" data-start=\"4062\" data-end=\"4100\">Temple architecture and traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"e3d3bx\" data-start=\"4101\" data-end=\"4142\">Social and spiritual roles of temples</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12z6oqj\" data-start=\"4143\" data-end=\"4182\">Preservation of heritage and values</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"4184\" data-end=\"4187\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"xujapz\" data-start=\"4189\" data-end=\"4197\">Yaj&ntilde;a</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"4199\" data-end=\"4320\">This module explains the concept of <strong data-start=\"4235\" data-end=\"4244\">Yaj&ntilde;a</strong>, traditionally associated with sacrifice, offering, and collective welfare.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4322\" data-end=\"4343\">Students learn about:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4345\" data-end=\"4465\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1082vlq\" data-start=\"4345\" data-end=\"4388\">Symbolic and spiritual meaning of yaj&ntilde;a</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jq9jvn\" data-start=\"4389\" data-end=\"4417\">Role in Vedic traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a1kt2e\" data-start=\"4418\" data-end=\"4465\">Importance of selflessness and contribution</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"4467\" data-end=\"4470\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ljqmsm\" data-start=\"4472\" data-end=\"4503\">Guru Tattva &amp; Avatāra Tattva</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"4505\" data-end=\"4541\">This topic explores the concepts of:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4543\" data-end=\"4616\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qgla70\" data-start=\"4543\" data-end=\"4581\">Guru (spiritual teacher and guide)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"x9wo7m\" data-start=\"4582\" data-end=\"4616\">Avatāra (divine manifestation)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4618\" data-end=\"4719\">Students understand the importance of guidance, wisdom, and spiritual leadership in Hindu traditions.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"4721\" data-end=\"4724\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1360gnn\" data-start=\"4726\" data-end=\"4763\">Dharmic Moorings of Modern Science</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"4765\" data-end=\"4868\">This module examines the relationship between Indian philosophical thought and modern scientific ideas.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4870\" data-end=\"4887\">Students explore:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4889\" data-end=\"5042\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15ogied\" data-start=\"4889\" data-end=\"4934\">Ethical foundations of scientific inquiry</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"q48twx\" data-start=\"4935\" data-end=\"4997\">Interdisciplinary perspectives on science and spirituality</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bobi2i\" data-start=\"4998\" data-end=\"5042\">Dharmic principles and knowledge systems</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5044\" data-end=\"5047\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1tglcgi\" data-start=\"5049\" data-end=\"5061\">Symbology</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"5063\" data-end=\"5134\">The module focuses on symbolism used in Hindu traditions and practices.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5136\" data-end=\"5157\">Students learn about:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5159\" data-end=\"5253\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fcw03j\" data-start=\"5159\" data-end=\"5193\">Spiritual symbols and meanings</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1r0iqzy\" data-start=\"5194\" data-end=\"5214\">Ritual symbolism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4vnepm\" data-start=\"5215\" data-end=\"5253\">Cultural interpretation of symbols</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5255\" data-end=\"5353\">This helps learners understand the deeper philosophical significance behind traditional practices.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5355\" data-end=\"5358\">\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"xdhn61\" data-start=\"5360\" data-end=\"5395\">Other Heterodox Systems in India</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"5397\" data-end=\"5502\">The course also introduces learners to other philosophical and spiritual systems that developed in India.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5504\" data-end=\"5531\">Students gain awareness of:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5533\" data-end=\"5658\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jgrfy9\" data-start=\"5533\" data-end=\"5563\">Diverse schools of thought</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ebxrhz\" data-start=\"5564\" data-end=\"5604\">Philosophical debates and traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14h5vvc\" data-start=\"5605\" data-end=\"5658\">Intellectual diversity within Indian civilization</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(400, 75, '6fd01ea2-14cc-41d7-8c10-a94807550f1c', 'acc96fe9-f3b0-4239-abbb-1366ebb6aff4', 323, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 02:16:04', '2026-06-17 00:23:10', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"727\">The Hindu Studies Program is designed to provide learners with a structured understanding of Hindu philosophy, scriptures, Indian knowledge systems, cultural traditions, and social thought. The program introduces foundational concepts of Hinduism while also exploring Indian philosophical systems, literature, spiritual traditions, and cultural diversity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"729\" data-end=\"895\">The course is suitable for students, researchers, educators, spiritual learners, and individuals interested in Indian civilization, philosophy, and cultural heritage.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"900\">\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"skmusw\" data-start=\"902\" data-end=\"935\">Hindu Studies Program Structure</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"1095\">The program is divided into multiple interdisciplinary courses that provide comprehensive understanding of Hindu thought, literature, philosophy, and culture.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1097\" data-end=\"1100\">\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"16r56ew\" data-start=\"1102\" data-end=\"1176\">Course 1 &ndash; Introduction to Hindu Studies Certificate Program (3 Credits)</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1273\">This course introduces learners to the foundations of Hinduism and its philosophical worldview.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1275\" data-end=\"1298\">Topics covered include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1300\" data-end=\"1542\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1robguy\" data-start=\"1300\" data-end=\"1328\">Introduction to Hinduism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dx89sz\" data-start=\"1329\" data-end=\"1368\">Definition, Synonyms, and Etymology</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o5eyy2\" data-start=\"1369\" data-end=\"1392\">History of Hinduism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9qrxfd\" data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1412\">Hindu Worldview</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"mx4j5j\" data-start=\"1413\" data-end=\"1431\">Dharma and Rta</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"8rwgel\" data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1470\">Fundamental Philosophical Concepts</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"5uldsm\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1495\">Creation and Creator</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1aro2r0\" data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1512\">Purusharthas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"orivcw\" data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1542\">Karma, Janma, and Samsara</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1544\" data-end=\"1789\">Students learn about the origins, evolution, and philosophical foundations of Hindu thought. The course also explains important concepts such as dharma (righteous living), karma (action and consequence), and samsara (cycle of birth and rebirth).</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1791\" data-end=\"1916\">The module helps learners understand how Hindu philosophy approaches ethics, life purpose, spirituality, and human existence.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1918\" data-end=\"1921\">\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"1q2ct57\" data-start=\"1923\" data-end=\"2005\">Course 2 &ndash; Hindu Literature I for Online Hindu Studies Certification (3 Credits)</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"2007\" data-end=\"2078\">This course focuses on the literary and scriptural traditions of India.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2080\" data-end=\"2103\">Topics covered include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2105\" data-end=\"2272\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"171ylau\" data-start=\"2105\" data-end=\"2130\">Introduction to Vedas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1x6k7gk\" data-start=\"2131\" data-end=\"2151\">Vedic Literature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"lkq6a6\" data-start=\"2152\" data-end=\"2169\">Dharmasastras</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"18x8wg\" data-start=\"2170\" data-end=\"2216\">Purpose and Nature of Puranas and Itihasas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1gkvd8n\" data-start=\"2217\" data-end=\"2243\">Puranas and Upapuranas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zarxcf\" data-start=\"2244\" data-end=\"2272\">Introduction to Itihasas</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2274\" data-end=\"2413\">Students gain understanding of ancient Indian scriptures and literary traditions that shaped Indian civilization and philosophical thought.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2415\" data-end=\"2580\">The course explains the significance of texts such as the Vedas, Puranas, and Itihasas in preserving cultural values, spiritual teachings, and historical narratives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2582\" data-end=\"2693\">Learners also understand how these texts influenced ethics, rituals, education, governance, and social systems.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2695\" data-end=\"2698\">\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"1gid8gl\" data-start=\"2700\" data-end=\"2753\">Course 3 &ndash; Indian Philosophical Systems (3 Credits)</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"2755\" data-end=\"2853\">This course introduces learners to major Indian philosophical schools and intellectual traditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2855\" data-end=\"2878\">Topics covered include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2880\" data-end=\"3045\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nqk60p\" data-start=\"2880\" data-end=\"2917\">Introduction to Indian Philosophy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cf6l2f\" data-start=\"2918\" data-end=\"2935\">Shaddarshanas</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"5prfmm\" data-start=\"2936\" data-end=\"2963\">Introduction to Vedanta</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11aypy8\" data-start=\"2964\" data-end=\"2976\">Buddhism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ctcktv\" data-start=\"2977\" data-end=\"2988\">Jainism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1c93m7a\" data-start=\"2989\" data-end=\"3000\">Sikhism</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hg7bo7\" data-start=\"3001\" data-end=\"3012\">Ajivaka</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"u3qmb1\" data-start=\"3013\" data-end=\"3025\">Charvaka</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ga2ipj\" data-start=\"3026\" data-end=\"3045\">Tribal Cultures</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3047\" data-end=\"3186\">Students explore both orthodox and heterodox systems of Indian philosophy and understand the diversity of intellectual traditions in India.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3188\" data-end=\"3314\">The course helps learners compare different perspectives on consciousness, ethics, spirituality, reality, and human existence.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3316\" data-end=\"3407\">This interdisciplinary understanding promotes broader cultural and philosophical awareness.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3409\" data-end=\"3412\">\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"evq85w\" data-start=\"3414\" data-end=\"3476\">Course 4 &ndash; Hinduism: Cultural and Social Aspects (3 Credits)</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"3478\" data-end=\"3557\">This course focuses on the social, cultural, and global dimensions of Hinduism.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3559\" data-end=\"3582\">Topics covered include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3584\" data-end=\"3737\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w2x7eu\" data-start=\"3584\" data-end=\"3625\">Varnashrama Dharma and Social Aspects</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ke9mzp\" data-start=\"3626\" data-end=\"3655\">Hinduism Across the World</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"op51h7\" data-start=\"3656\" data-end=\"3691\">Interaction with Modern Science</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1h4fix4\" data-start=\"3692\" data-end=\"3737\">Diversity in Hindu Traditions and Culture</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3739\" data-end=\"3836\">Students understand how Hindu cultural traditions evolved across different regions and societies.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3838\" data-end=\"3863\">The course also explores:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3865\" data-end=\"4080\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xefxy7\" data-start=\"3865\" data-end=\"3908\">Social organization and cultural values</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dd8e8\" data-start=\"3909\" data-end=\"3946\">Global spread of Hindu traditions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"u6ujst\" data-start=\"3947\" data-end=\"4018\">Relationship between Hindu philosophy and modern scientific thought</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yf1amy\" data-start=\"4019\" data-end=\"4080\">Cultural diversity within Hindu practices and communities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4082\" data-end=\"4219\">This module encourages learners to appreciate cultural heritage while understanding the evolving role of Hindu thought in modern society.</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(401, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 68, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 02:59:42', '2026-05-15 02:59:42', '<p data-start=\"30\" data-end=\"296\">The BBA admission process is designed to make student enrollment simple, transparent, and convenient. Candidates must complete the online application process, submit the required documents, and fulfill the eligibility criteria to secure admission into the program.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"298\" data-end=\"589\">Before applying, students should carefully review the course details, fee structure, specialization options, and admission requirements. Submitting accurate information and documents is important because incorrect or incomplete applications may delay the verification and approval process.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"591\" data-end=\"769\">Most universities follow an online admission system where students can register, upload documents, pay fees digitally, and track their admission status from the student portal.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1is0rul\" data-start=\"771\" data-end=\"808\">Step-by-Step BBA Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"fj55iv\" data-start=\"810\" data-end=\"865\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"867\" data-end=\"1114\">Candidates need to visit the university admission portal and create an account using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After successful registration, login credentials are generated for accessing the application dashboard.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1m3uwh1\" data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1169\">Step 2: Fill and Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1384\">Students must complete the online admission form carefully by entering academic, personal, and contact details. It is important to select the correct BBA program or specialization during the application process.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1515\">Applicants should double-check all information before final submission to avoid mistakes in documentation or admission records.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1ff8ob\" data-start=\"1517\" data-end=\"1554\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1556\" data-end=\"1751\">Candidates are required to upload the necessary supporting documents for verification. These documents are generally needed to confirm identity, academic qualifications, and eligibility status.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1753\" data-end=\"1793\">Commonly required documents may include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1795\" data-end=\"1945\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hithjx\" data-start=\"1795\" data-end=\"1818\">Class 10 mark sheet</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dmcj4v\" data-start=\"1819\" data-end=\"1842\">Class 12 mark sheet</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1871\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1872\" data-end=\"1885\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1886\" data-end=\"1904\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"1945\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1947\" data-end=\"2164\">Students appearing for Class 12 examinations can also apply by submitting available academic documents as per university guidelines. NIOS board candidates are generally eligible if their qualification is recognized.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1ioie5o\" data-start=\"2166\" data-end=\"2221\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2415\">After submission, the university reviews the application form and verifies uploaded documents. The eligibility criteria, academic records, and supporting details are checked before approval.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2417\" data-end=\"2612\">Applications with incomplete details, unclear documents, or incorrect information may face delays or rejection, so students should ensure proper document quality and accuracy during submission.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"xtyzc\" data-start=\"2614\" data-end=\"2645\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2647\" data-end=\"2896\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the applicable BBA program fee through the online payment system. After successful payment, the university generates the registration or enrollment number confirming admission into the program.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2898\" data-end=\"3004\">Students should keep payment receipts and admission confirmation details safely for future academic use.</p>', 1, '<p data-start=\"29\" data-end=\"407\">Candidates seeking admission to the Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA) program must have completed their Class 12 education from a recognized board in any stream such as Commerce, Science, or Arts. Students who are currently appearing for Class 12 examinations are also eligible to apply, subject to fulfilling the final admission requirements after result declaration.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"409\" data-end=\"755\">The program is designed for students who want to build a strong foundation in business management, marketing, finance, entrepreneurship, and corporate operations. Since BBA is a career-oriented management course, candidates should have basic communication skills, analytical thinking ability, and interest in business and leadership activities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"757\" data-end=\"1030\">Students from recognized boards including CBSE, ISC, State Boards, and NIOS are generally eligible for admission. Some universities may also specify minimum qualifying marks in Class 12, while others may offer admission based on merit or entrance examination performance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1032\" data-end=\"1244\">Before applying, candidates should carefully check the university&rsquo;s admission rules, specialization options, fee structure, and placement support to choose the right BBA program according to their career goals.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"158yw77\" data-start=\"1246\" data-end=\"1270\">Important Highlights</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1272\" data-end=\"1599\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yibqw\" data-start=\"1272\" data-end=\"1315\">Passed Class 12 from a recognized board</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"l9pogq\" data-start=\"1316\" data-end=\"1366\">Students appearing for Class 12 can also apply</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1a4kan1\" data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1408\">Students from any stream are eligible</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"d24fz0\" data-start=\"1409\" data-end=\"1447\">NIOS board candidates are eligible</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qj6s7j\" data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1526\">Admission may be merit-based or entrance-based depending on the university</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1r9mdyi\" data-start=\"1527\" data-end=\"1599\">Basic interest in business, management, and leadership is beneficial</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p data-start=\"26\" data-end=\"284\">The BBA fee structure is designed to provide flexible payment options for students pursuing management education. Students can either choose the lump sum payment option for overall cost savings or pay semester-wise according to their financial convenience.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"648\">The overall course fee includes academic charges and a non-refundable registration fee applicable during the first semester. Apart from tuition fees, students should also keep in mind additional academic expenses such as examination fees, project costs, study materials, internet access for online learning (if applicable), and optional certification programs.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"650\" data-end=\"901\">Choosing the right payment option depends on a student&rsquo;s financial planning, budget, and long-term educational goals. Many students prefer semester-wise payments for flexibility, while lump sum payment options may help reduce the total program cost.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"j7wzoz\" data-start=\"903\" data-end=\"943\">BBA Fee Structure for Indian Students</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"1226\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"977\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"977\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"962\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Payment Option</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"977\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1226\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1018\">\r\n<td data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1007\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1018\">₹72,661</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1019\" data-end=\"1049\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1019\" data-end=\"1038\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1049\">₹12,661</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1097\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1073\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1097\">₹12,000 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1177\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1117\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1177\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1226\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1206\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1206\" data-end=\"1226\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1253\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1452\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1290\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1290\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1270\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1290\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1301\" data-end=\"1452\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1301\" data-end=\"1333\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1301\" data-end=\"1322\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1322\" data-end=\"1333\">₹72,661</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1386\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1357\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Average Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1357\" data-end=\"1386\">Approx. ₹12,000 &ndash; ₹12,661</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1452\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1418\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Additional Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1452\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject if applicable</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', 'Medium', '<h2 data-section-id=\"1wbu27o\" data-start=\"1059\" data-end=\"1085\">BBA Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1087\" data-end=\"1318\">The first semester focuses on introducing students to the basics of business management, accounting, communication, and organizational structure. It helps students build a strong academic foundation for advanced management studies.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"2236\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1345\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1345\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1330\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1345\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"2236\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"1465\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"1379\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial Accounting</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1379\" data-end=\"1465\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of accounting, financial statements, bookkeeping, and business transactions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1583\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1493\" data-col-size=\"md\">Principles of Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1493\" data-end=\"1583\" data-col-size=\"md\">Introduction to management functions, leadership, planning, and organizational control</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1687\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1608\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Organisation</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1608\" data-end=\"1687\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding business structures, ownership forms, and business operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1688\" data-end=\"1782\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1688\" data-end=\"1715\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Mathematics &ndash; I</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1782\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fundamental mathematical concepts used in business calculations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1783\" data-end=\"1888\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1783\" data-end=\"1826\" data-col-size=\"md\">Biochemical Insights into the Human Body</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1826\" data-end=\"1888\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basic understanding of human health and biological systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1889\" data-end=\"2009\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1889\" data-end=\"1943\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language and Communication Skills (Level-I)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"2009\" data-col-size=\"md\">Development of communication, grammar, and presentation skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2127\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2010\" data-end=\"2050\" data-col-size=\"md\">Office and Spreadsheet Tools Learning</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2050\" data-end=\"2127\" data-col-size=\"md\">Practical learning of MS Office, spreadsheets, and business documentation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2128\" data-end=\"2236\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2128\" data-end=\"2154\" data-col-size=\"md\">Human Values and Ethics</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2154\" data-end=\"2236\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding ethical behavior, social responsibility, and professional values</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"pupjiv\" data-start=\"2238\" data-end=\"2264\">BBA Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2412\">The second semester strengthens analytical, economic, and organizational understanding while improving professional communication and soft skills.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2414\" data-end=\"3218\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2414\" data-end=\"2439\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2414\" data-end=\"2439\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2414\" data-end=\"2424\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2424\" data-end=\"2439\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2450\" data-end=\"3218\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2450\" data-end=\"2540\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2450\" data-end=\"2472\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Statistics</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2472\" data-end=\"2540\" data-col-size=\"md\">Statistical methods, data analysis, and business decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2541\" data-end=\"2630\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2541\" data-end=\"2564\" data-col-size=\"md\">Managerial Economics</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2564\" data-end=\"2630\" data-col-size=\"md\">Economic concepts applied to business and management decisions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2631\" data-end=\"2732\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2631\" data-end=\"2657\" data-col-size=\"md\">Organizational Behavior</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2657\" data-end=\"2732\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of employee behavior, motivation, teamwork, and workplace culture</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2733\" data-end=\"2822\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2733\" data-end=\"2761\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Mathematics &ndash; II</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2761\" data-end=\"2822\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced business mathematics and quantitative techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2823\" data-end=\"2905\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2823\" data-end=\"2847\" data-col-size=\"md\">Biochemistry &amp; Health</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2847\" data-end=\"2905\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding health, nutrition, and wellness concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2906\" data-end=\"3019\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2906\" data-end=\"2961\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language and Communication Skills (Level-II)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2961\" data-end=\"3019\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced communication and professional writing skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3020\" data-end=\"3116\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3020\" data-end=\"3034\" data-col-size=\"md\">Soft Skills</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3034\" data-end=\"3116\" data-col-size=\"md\">Personality development, teamwork, leadership, and interpersonal communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3218\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3141\" data-col-size=\"md\">Environmental Studies</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3141\" data-end=\"3218\" data-col-size=\"md\">Awareness of environmental issues, sustainability, and ecological balance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"9gkz1y\" data-start=\"3220\" data-end=\"3246\">BBA Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"3248\" data-end=\"3415\">The third semester introduces functional areas of management such as marketing, accounting, and human resource management while focusing on professional communication.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"3417\" data-end=\"4264\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"3417\" data-end=\"3442\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3417\" data-end=\"3442\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3417\" data-end=\"3427\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3427\" data-end=\"3442\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"3453\" data-end=\"4264\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3453\" data-end=\"3548\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3453\" data-end=\"3477\" data-col-size=\"md\">Managerial Accounting</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3477\" data-end=\"3548\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial analysis, budgeting, and management accounting techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3549\" data-end=\"3641\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3549\" data-end=\"3572\" data-col-size=\"md\">Marketing Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3572\" data-end=\"3641\" data-col-size=\"md\">Marketing strategies, consumer behavior, branding, and promotions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3642\" data-end=\"3743\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3642\" data-end=\"3670\" data-col-size=\"md\">Human Resource Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3670\" data-end=\"3743\" data-col-size=\"md\">Recruitment, training, employee relations, and performance management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3744\" data-end=\"3822\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3744\" data-end=\"3766\" data-col-size=\"md\">Disaster Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3766\" data-end=\"3822\" data-col-size=\"md\">Planning and management of emergencies and disasters</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3823\" data-end=\"3913\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3823\" data-end=\"3860\" data-col-size=\"md\">Biochemistry of Lifestyle Diseases</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3860\" data-end=\"3913\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding lifestyle-related health conditions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3914\" data-end=\"4025\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3914\" data-end=\"3970\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language and Communication Skills (Level-III)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3970\" data-end=\"4025\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business communication and advanced language skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4026\" data-end=\"4138\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4026\" data-end=\"4063\" data-col-size=\"md\">Communication in Professional Life</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4063\" data-end=\"4138\" data-col-size=\"md\">Workplace communication, corporate interaction, and presentation skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4139\" data-end=\"4264\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4139\" data-end=\"4203\" data-col-size=\"md\">Event Management / Security Analysis and Portfolio Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4203\" data-end=\"4264\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of event planning or financial investment analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1v11yoh\" data-start=\"4266\" data-end=\"4292\">BBA Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"4294\" data-end=\"4405\">The fourth semester focuses on research, business environment, financial markets, and professional development.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"4407\" data-end=\"5129\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"4407\" data-end=\"4432\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"4407\" data-end=\"4432\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"4407\" data-end=\"4417\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"4417\" data-end=\"4432\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"4443\" data-end=\"5129\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"4443\" data-end=\"4528\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4443\" data-end=\"4461\" data-col-size=\"md\">Capital Markets</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4461\" data-end=\"4528\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding stock markets, securities, and investment systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4529\" data-end=\"4620\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4529\" data-end=\"4557\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Research Methods</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4557\" data-end=\"4620\" data-col-size=\"md\">Research techniques, data collection, and business analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4712\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4644\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Environment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4644\" data-end=\"4712\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of economic, political, legal, and social business factors</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4713\" data-end=\"4795\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4713\" data-end=\"4744\" data-col-size=\"md\">Consumer Protection in India</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4744\" data-end=\"4795\" data-col-size=\"md\">Consumer rights, laws, and grievance mechanisms</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4796\" data-end=\"4918\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4796\" data-end=\"4851\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language and Communication Skills (Level-IV)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4851\" data-end=\"4918\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced corporate communication and business language training</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"4919\" data-end=\"5006\">\r\n<td data-start=\"4919\" data-end=\"4940\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial Literacy</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"4940\" data-end=\"5006\" data-col-size=\"md\">Personal finance, budgeting, savings, and investment awareness</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5007\" data-end=\"5129\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5007\" data-end=\"5064\" data-col-size=\"md\">International English Language Proficiency Development</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5064\" data-end=\"5129\" data-col-size=\"md\">Improving global communication and English proficiency skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"180g2sw\" data-start=\"5131\" data-end=\"5157\">BBA Semester 5 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"5159\" data-end=\"5308\">The fifth semester introduces advanced corporate and international business concepts while providing practical industry exposure through internships.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"5310\" data-end=\"5895\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"5310\" data-end=\"5335\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"5310\" data-end=\"5335\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"5310\" data-end=\"5320\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"5320\" data-end=\"5335\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"5346\" data-end=\"5895\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"5346\" data-end=\"5434\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5346\" data-end=\"5366\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Corporate Finance</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5366\" data-end=\"5434\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial planning, capital management, and investment decisions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5435\" data-end=\"5537\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5435\" data-end=\"5460\" data-col-size=\"sm\">International Business</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5460\" data-end=\"5537\" data-col-size=\"md\">Global trade, international markets, and cross-border business operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5538\" data-end=\"5630\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5538\" data-end=\"5554\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Business Laws</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5554\" data-end=\"5630\" data-col-size=\"md\">Legal aspects related to contracts, companies, and commercial activities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5631\" data-end=\"5728\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5631\" data-end=\"5665\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Corporate Secretarial Practices</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5665\" data-end=\"5728\" data-col-size=\"md\">Corporate compliance, documentation, and company procedures</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5729\" data-end=\"5796\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5729\" data-end=\"5742\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Internship</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5742\" data-end=\"5796\" data-col-size=\"md\">Practical industry training and corporate exposure</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5797\" data-end=\"5895\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5797\" data-end=\"5826\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Creativity and Advertising</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"5826\" data-end=\"5895\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advertising concepts, creative campaigns, and branding techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1jbk43\" data-start=\"5897\" data-end=\"5923\">BBA Semester 6 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"5925\" data-end=\"6092\">The final semester focuses on entrepreneurship, financial analysis, e-commerce, and practical business applications to prepare students for careers and higher studies.</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"6094\" data-end=\"6690\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"6094\" data-end=\"6119\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"6094\" data-end=\"6119\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"6094\" data-end=\"6104\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"6104\" data-end=\"6119\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"6130\" data-end=\"6690\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"6130\" data-end=\"6220\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6130\" data-end=\"6165\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Analysis of Financial Statements</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6165\" data-end=\"6220\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial performance evaluation and ratio analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6221\" data-end=\"6321\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6221\" data-end=\"6252\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Entrepreneurship Development</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6252\" data-end=\"6321\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business startup planning, innovation, and entrepreneurial skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6322\" data-end=\"6413\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6322\" data-end=\"6348\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Comprehensive Viva-Voce</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6348\" data-end=\"6413\" data-col-size=\"md\">Final assessment of overall business and management knowledge</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6414\" data-end=\"6502\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6414\" data-end=\"6427\" data-col-size=\"sm\">E-Commerce</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6427\" data-end=\"6502\" data-col-size=\"md\">Online business models, digital transactions, and e-business operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6503\" data-end=\"6605\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6503\" data-end=\"6538\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Advertising and Personal Selling</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6538\" data-end=\"6605\" data-col-size=\"md\">Sales techniques, promotion strategies, and customer engagement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6690\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6625\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Event Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"6625\" data-end=\"6690\" data-col-size=\"md\">Planning, organizing, and managing business and social events</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 72661.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 