>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2462\" data-end=\"2550\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2462\" data-end=\"2499\" data-col-size=\"md\">Communication in Professional Life</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2499\" data-end=\"2550\">Workplace communication and presentation skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"5ecnw3\" data-start=\"2552\" data-end=\"2577\">BA Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2979\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2604\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2604\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2589\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2589\" data-end=\"2604\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2615\" data-end=\"2979\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2615\" data-end=\"2698\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2615\" data-end=\"2653\" data-col-size=\"md\">Core Courses Selected in Semester I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2653\" data-end=\"2698\">Continued advanced study of core subjects</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2699\" data-end=\"2804\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2699\" data-end=\"2756\" data-col-size=\"md\">International English Language Proficiency Development</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2756\" data-end=\"2804\">Improves global English communication skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2805\" data-end=\"2908\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2805\" data-end=\"2860\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language and Communication Skills (Level-IV)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2860\" data-end=\"2908\">Advanced professional communication training</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2909\" data-end=\"2979\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2909\" data-end=\"2930\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial Literacy</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2930\" data-end=\"2979\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of budgeting, savings, and investments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"4o02xe\" data-start=\"2981\" data-end=\"3006\">BA Semester 5 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"3008\" data-end=\"3211\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"3008\" data-end=\"3033\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3008\" data-end=\"3033\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3008\" data-end=\"3018\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3018\" data-end=\"3033\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"3044\" data-end=\"3211\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3044\" data-end=\"3129\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3044\" data-end=\"3082\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Core Courses Selected in Semester I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3082\" data-end=\"3129\">Continued specialization in chosen subjects</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3130\" data-end=\"3211\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3130\" data-end=\"3159\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Creativity and Advertising</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3159\" data-end=\"3211\">Basics of advertising and creative communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1yvx35d\" data-start=\"3213\" data-end=\"3238\">BA Semester 6 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"3240\" data-end=\"3493\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"3240\" data-end=\"3265\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3240\" data-end=\"3265\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3240\" data-end=\"3250\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"3250\" data-end=\"3265\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"3276\" data-end=\"3493\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3276\" data-end=\"3361\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3276\" data-end=\"3314\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Core Courses Selected in Semester I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3314\" data-end=\"3361\">Final-stage study of selected core subjects</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3362\" data-end=\"3431\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3362\" data-end=\"3382\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Digital Marketing</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3382\" data-end=\"3431\">Introduction to online marketing and branding</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3432\" data-end=\"3493\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3432\" data-end=\"3451\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Event Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3451\" data-end=\"3493\">Basics of planning and managing events</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"rylnlw\" data-start=\"3495\" data-end=\"3529\">&nbsp;</h2>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 72661.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(404, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 76, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 04:23:09', '2026-05-15 04:23:09', '<p data-start=\"30\" data-end=\"340\">The MBA admission process is designed to be simple, transparent, and fully online, allowing students and working professionals to complete their enrollment with ease. Candidates must complete registration, submit the application form, upload documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"342\" data-end=\"543\">Before applying, students should carefully check the eligibility criteria, specialization options, fee structure, and required documents to ensure a smooth admission process without delays or errors.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"zj15v6\" data-start=\"545\" data-end=\"582\">Step-by-Step MBA Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"fj55iv\" data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"639\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"640\" data-end=\"892\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After successful registration, login credentials are generated for accessing the application form and dashboard.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1hhaxep\" data-start=\"894\" data-end=\"938\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"939\" data-end=\"1116\">Students need to fill out the online admission form for the selected MBA program carefully. The form includes personal details, academic qualifications, and program selection.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1253\">Applicants should ensure all details are accurate before final submission, as incorrect information may cause delays in verification.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1ff8ob\" data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1292\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1293\" data-end=\"1392\">Candidates must upload all necessary supporting documents for verification and eligibility check.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1394\" data-end=\"1419\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1596\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iil7g4\" data-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1461\">Graduation mark sheet and certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1493\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1494\" data-end=\"1522\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1523\" data-end=\"1536\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1555\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1556\" data-end=\"1596\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1598\" data-end=\"1713\">Students in their final year of graduation can also apply, subject to completing their degree requirements later.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1ioie5o\" data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1770\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1771\" data-end=\"1870\">After submission, the university verifies all uploaded documents and checks eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1872\" data-end=\"2029\">Applications with missing, incorrect, or unclear documents may face delays or rejection, so students should ensure proper document submission and accuracy.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"xtyzc\" data-start=\"2031\" data-end=\"2062\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2063\" data-end=\"2264\">Once the application is approved, students must pay the applicable MBA program fee online. After successful payment, the university issues a registration number confirming admission into the program.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2365\">Students should save the payment receipt and admission confirmation details for future reference.</p>', 1, '<p data-start=\"33\" data-end=\"354\">Candidates seeking admission to the Master of Business Administration (MBA) program must have completed 10+2 education and hold a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university. The graduation degree can be from any stream such as Commerce, Arts, Science, Engineering, or Management, depending on university guidelines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"356\" data-end=\"702\">The MBA program is designed for students and working professionals who want to build careers in management, leadership, finance, marketing, human resources, business analytics, operations, and entrepreneurship. It develops strong decision-making, communication, analytical, and managerial skills required in corporate and business environments.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"704\" data-end=\"997\">Students who are in the final year of their bachelor&rsquo;s degree are also eligible to apply in most universities, provided they complete their degree as per admission requirements. Some universities may also consider entrance exams, academic performance, or work experience for final selection.</p>\r\n<h2 data-start=\"999\" data-end=\"1028\" data-section-id=\"3lr0zp\">MBA Eligibility Highlights</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1030\" data-end=\"1439\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1030\" data-end=\"1082\" data-section-id=\"1vndt6d\">Must have completed 10+2 from a recognized board</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1083\" data-end=\"1145\" data-section-id=\"dq6j0q\">Bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university is required</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1146\" data-end=\"1195\" data-section-id=\"pj7yjx\">Final-year graduation students can also apply</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1196\" data-end=\"1269\" data-section-id=\"1pnpt0x\">Students from any stream are eligible (Commerce, Arts, Science, etc.)</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1320\" data-section-id=\"cwbb4d\">Admission may be entrance-based or merit-based</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1321\" data-end=\"1375\" data-section-id=\"10ixwrx\">Some institutes may require minimum marks criteria</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1376\" data-end=\"1439\" data-section-id=\"lffnde\">Work experience may be preferred for executive MBA programs</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p data-start=\"26\" data-end=\"402\">The MBA fee structure is designed to offer flexible payment options for both Indian and international students. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option depending on their financial planning and convenience. The total fee generally includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"404\" data-end=\"605\">Apart from tuition fees, students should also consider additional academic costs such as examination fees, project work, certification courses, and other learning-related expenses during the program.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"6nqp5k\" data-start=\"607\" data-end=\"627\">MBA Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"916\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"655\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"655\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"629\" data-end=\"640\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Category</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"640\" data-end=\"655\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"666\" data-end=\"916\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"666\" data-end=\"696\">\r\n<td data-start=\"666\" data-end=\"685\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"685\" data-end=\"696\">₹25,500</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"744\">\r\n<td data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"720\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"720\" data-end=\"744\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹25,500 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"787\">\r\n<td data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"774\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"774\" data-end=\"787\">₹1,02,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"788\" data-end=\"867\">\r\n<td data-start=\"788\" data-end=\"807\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"867\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"868\" data-end=\"916\">\r\n<td data-start=\"868\" data-end=\"896\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"896\" data-end=\"916\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"943\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"1121\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"980\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"980\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"960\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"980\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1121\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1025\">\r\n<td data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1012\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1012\" data-end=\"1025\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹1,02,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1064\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1053\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Average Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1064\">₹25,500</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1065\" data-end=\"1121\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1065\" data-end=\"1085\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1085\" data-end=\"1121\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"10a0g6z\" data-start=\"1123\" data-end=\"1152\">MBA Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1154\" data-end=\"1415\">The MBA program offers a clear and structured fee system where students can select a payment method that suits their budget. Semester-wise payment allows flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete payments in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1417\" data-end=\"1665\">The first semester fee includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the same fee structure continues. Re-appear examination fees are charged separately in case a student needs to retake any subject exam.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"34\" data-end=\"388\">The MBA syllabus is designed to develop strong managerial, analytical, leadership, and decision-making skills required in modern business environments. The course combines core management subjects, business fundamentals, financial knowledge, marketing concepts, and research-based learning to prepare students for corporate and entrepreneurial careers.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"390\" data-end=\"614\">The program is divided into four semesters, where the first two semesters focus on core management subjects and the last two semesters allow students to specialize through elective subjects based on their career interests.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1xd206z\" data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"642\">MBA Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"644\" data-end=\"1293\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"644\" data-end=\"669\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"644\" data-end=\"669\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"644\" data-end=\"654\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"654\" data-end=\"669\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"1293\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"806\">\r\n<td data-start=\"680\" data-end=\"730\" data-col-size=\"md\">Management Process and Organizational Behaviour</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"730\" data-end=\"806\">Study of management functions, leadership styles, and workplace behavior</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"925\">\r\n<td data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"858\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fundamentals of Statistics for Business Decision</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"925\">Statistical tools used in business decision-making and analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"1009\">\r\n<td data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"949\" data-col-size=\"md\">Managerial Economics</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"1009\">Application of economic principles in business decisions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1094\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1033\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial Accounting</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1094\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of accounting, financial statements, and reporting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1095\" data-end=\"1184\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1095\" data-end=\"1120\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business Communication</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1184\">Professional communication skills for corporate environments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1185\" data-end=\"1293\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1185\" data-end=\"1227\" data-col-size=\"md\">Indian Economy and Business Environment</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1227\" data-end=\"1293\">Overview of India&rsquo;s economic structure and business conditions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1r35sig\" data-start=\"1295\" data-end=\"1321\">MBA Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1915\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1348\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1348\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1333\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1348\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1359\" data-end=\"1915\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1359\" data-end=\"1449\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1359\" data-end=\"1387\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Human Resource Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1449\" data-col-size=\"md\">Employee recruitment, training, and performance management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1450\" data-end=\"1548\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1450\" data-end=\"1488\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Computer Applications in Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1488\" data-end=\"1548\" data-col-size=\"md\">Use of software and digital tools in business operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1629\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1572\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Marketing Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1572\" data-end=\"1629\">Marketing strategies, branding, and consumer behavior</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1630\" data-end=\"1721\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1630\" data-end=\"1653\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Financial Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1653\" data-end=\"1721\">Financial planning, investment decisions, and capital management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1722\" data-end=\"1815\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1722\" data-end=\"1750\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Business Research Methods</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1750\" data-end=\"1815\" data-col-size=\"md\">Research techniques for business analysis and decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1816\" data-end=\"1915\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1816\" data-end=\"1855\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Production and Operations Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1855\" data-end=\"1915\">Managing production processes and operational efficiency</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1rtidh5\" data-start=\"1917\" data-end=\"1943\">MBA Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1945\" data-end=\"2053\">In the third semester, students choose an elective specialization based on their career interests and goals.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2055\" data-end=\"2352\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17pwog0\" data-start=\"2055\" data-end=\"2120\">Students select one MBA elective as per specialization choice</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"172x14n\" data-start=\"2121\" data-end=\"2181\">Focus shifts toward advanced industry-specific knowledge</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"wo6go0\" data-start=\"2182\" data-end=\"2296\">Subjects depend on chosen stream such as Finance, Marketing, HR, Business Analytics, or International Business</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ge24ta\" data-start=\"2297\" data-end=\"2352\">Emphasis on practical and applied business learning</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"lwzcny\" data-start=\"2354\" data-end=\"2380\">MBA Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"2382\" data-end=\"2468\">The final semester continues with elective-based specialization and advanced learning.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2703\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tk7b38\" data-start=\"2470\" data-end=\"2524\">Continuation of chosen MBA elective specialization</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12k7qiq\" data-start=\"2525\" data-end=\"2577\">Advanced topics in the selected management field</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zos1hp\" data-start=\"2578\" data-end=\"2635\">Focus on practical application and industry readiness</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qd8jz6\" data-start=\"2636\" data-end=\"2703\">Includes project work, case studies, or research-based learning</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"32\",\"33\",\"34\",\"38\",\"50\"]', 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 102000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(405, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 104, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 04:36:34', '2026-05-15 04:36:34', '<p data-start=\"47\" data-end=\"362\">The admission process for MA Political Science is designed to be simple, transparent, and fully online, allowing students to complete their application without difficulty. Candidates must complete registration, submit the application form, upload documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"364\" data-end=\"566\">Before applying, students should carefully review the eligibility criteria, specialization structure, fee details, and required documents to ensure a smooth admission process without errors or delays.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1i1fc8d\" data-start=\"568\" data-end=\"622\">Step-by-Step MA Political Science Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"8q329j\" data-start=\"624\" data-end=\"681\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"682\" data-end=\"934\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After successful registration, login credentials are generated for accessing the application form and dashboard.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1u4bokh\" data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"982\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"1121\">Students need to fill out the MA Political Science admission form carefully with correct personal, academic, and course-related details.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1123\" data-end=\"1272\">It is important to verify all information before final submission, as incorrect details may cause issues during verification or admission approval.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1rwoaln\" data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1313\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1314\" data-end=\"1445\">Candidates must upload all necessary supporting documents in the prescribed format for verification and eligibility confirmation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1447\" data-end=\"1474\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1475\" data-end=\"1658\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dlzfxc\" data-start=\"1475\" data-end=\"1523\">Graduation mark sheet and degree certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1524\" data-end=\"1555\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1556\" data-end=\"1584\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1585\" data-end=\"1598\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1617\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1618\" data-end=\"1658\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1660\" data-end=\"1790\">Students in the final year of graduation can also apply, subject to completing their degree before final admission confirmation.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"nk09bg\" data-start=\"1792\" data-end=\"1849\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1850\" data-end=\"1957\">After submission, the university verifies academic records, uploaded documents, and eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1959\" data-end=\"2168\">Incomplete applications, incorrect information, or unclear document uploads may delay the process or lead to rejection. Students should regularly check their admission portal or registered email for updates.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t02fyw\" data-start=\"2170\" data-end=\"2203\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2204\" data-end=\"2423\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the applicable MA Political Science program fee online. After successful payment, the university issues a registration number confirming admission into the course.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2425\" data-end=\"2525\">Students should keep the payment receipt and admission confirmation details safely for future use</p>', 1, '<p data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"333\">Candidates seeking admission to the Master of Arts (MA) in Political Science program must hold a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university. The degree can be in Political Science or any other related or non-related discipline, depending on the university&rsquo;s admission policies.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"680\">The program is designed for students who want to deepen their understanding of political theory, public administration, international relations, governance systems, public policy, and comparative politics. It is suitable for graduates aiming for careers in teaching, research, civil services, policy-making, journalism, and political analysis.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"682\" data-end=\"982\">Students who are in the final year of their bachelor&rsquo;s degree are also eligible to apply in many universities, provided they complete their graduation before final admission confirmation. Candidates from recognized universities and institutions approved by regulatory bodies are generally eligible.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1157\">Some universities may also consider minimum qualifying marks, entrance examinations, or interview-based selection depending on the admission process and competition level.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1dsszyy\" data-start=\"1159\" data-end=\"1205\">MA Political Science Eligibility Highlights</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1207\" data-end=\"1577\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"43qoql\" data-start=\"1207\" data-end=\"1269\">Must have a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1sbzmdv\" data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1334\">Students from any stream may apply (Arts, Commerce, Science)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pj7yjx\" data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1384\">Final-year graduation students can also apply</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fjbzql\" data-start=\"1385\" data-end=\"1435\">Admission may be merit-based or entrance-based</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6rjjq3\" data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1497\">Some universities may require minimum percentage criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"18gkoob\" data-start=\"1498\" data-end=\"1577\">Suitable for students interested in politics, governance, and public policy</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p data-start=\"43\" data-end=\"376\">The MA Political Science fee structure is designed to offer affordable and flexible payment options for students pursuing advanced studies in political science, governance, and international relations. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option based on their financial convenience and planning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"378\" data-end=\"689\">The total program fee includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester. In addition to tuition fees, students should also consider other academic expenses such as examination fees, study materials, research work, and competitive exam preparation support.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1cb1ern\" data-start=\"691\" data-end=\"748\">MA Political Science Fee Structure for Indian Students</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"1041\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"782\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"782\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"767\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Payment Option</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"767\" data-end=\"782\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"793\" data-end=\"1041\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"793\" data-end=\"823\">\r\n<td data-start=\"793\" data-end=\"812\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"812\" data-end=\"823\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"824\" data-end=\"871\">\r\n<td data-start=\"824\" data-end=\"847\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"847\" data-end=\"871\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"872\" data-end=\"912\">\r\n<td data-start=\"872\" data-end=\"901\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"901\" data-end=\"912\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"992\">\r\n<td data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"932\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"992\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"993\" data-end=\"1041\">\r\n<td data-start=\"993\" data-end=\"1021\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1021\" data-end=\"1041\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1068\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1236\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1105\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1105\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1070\" data-end=\"1085\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1085\" data-end=\"1105\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1236\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1148\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1137\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1137\" data-end=\"1148\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1149\" data-end=\"1179\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1149\" data-end=\"1168\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1168\" data-end=\"1179\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1180\" data-end=\"1236\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1180\" data-end=\"1200\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1200\" data-end=\"1236\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1eusvdw\" data-start=\"1238\" data-end=\"1284\">MA Political Science Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1598\">The MA Political Science program provides a clear and structured fee system suitable for students from different financial backgrounds. Semester-wise payment allows flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete the payment in advance and avoid semester-wise transactions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1600\" data-end=\"1892\">The first semester fee includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the same fee structure continues throughout the program. If a student fails or needs to reappear in any subject examination, additional charges of ₹500 per subject are applicable.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"51\" data-end=\"398\">The MA Political Science syllabus is designed to provide advanced knowledge of political theory, governance systems, public administration, international relations, comparative politics, and public policy. The program helps students develop analytical thinking, research skills, and a deep understanding of national and global political systems.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"688\">The course is structured across four semesters, combining core political science subjects, research methodology, and specialized electives. It is highly useful for students aiming for careers in civil services, teaching, research, policy-making, journalism, and international relations.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"cwlv5w\" data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"733\">MA Political Science Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"735\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"735\" data-end=\"760\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"735\" data-end=\"760\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"735\" data-end=\"745\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"760\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"771\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"771\" data-end=\"861\">\r\n<td data-start=\"771\" data-end=\"799\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Western Political Thought</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"799\" data-end=\"861\">Study of major Western political philosophers and theories</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"862\" data-end=\"964\">\r\n<td data-start=\"862\" data-end=\"897\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Indian Government and Politics-I</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"964\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of Indian political system, constitution, and governance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"1057\">\r\n<td data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"998\" data-col-size=\"sm\">International Relations Theory</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"998\" data-end=\"1057\">Introduction to global political theories and diplomacy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1141\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1084\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Public Administration-I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1084\" data-end=\"1141\">Fundamentals of administration and governance systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1221\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1167\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Research Methodology-I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1221\">Basics of research techniques and academic writing</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1222\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1222\" data-end=\"1244\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Political Geography</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1298\">Study of geographical factors influencing politics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"j6i2uf\" data-start=\"1300\" data-end=\"1343\">MA Political Science Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1988\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1370\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1370\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1355\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1355\" data-end=\"1370\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1381\" data-end=\"1988\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1381\" data-end=\"1465\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1381\" data-end=\"1408\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Indian Political Thought</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1408\" data-end=\"1465\">Study of Indian political philosophers and ideologies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1564\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1502\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Indian Government and Politics-II</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1502\" data-end=\"1564\">Advanced study of Indian political system and institutions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1565\" data-end=\"1653\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1565\" data-end=\"1598\" data-col-size=\"sm\">International Relations-Issues</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1598\" data-end=\"1653\">Contemporary global issues and diplomatic relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1654\" data-end=\"1738\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1654\" data-end=\"1681\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Public Administration-II</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1681\" data-end=\"1738\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced administrative systems and governance models</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1739\" data-end=\"1812\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1739\" data-end=\"1765\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Research Methodology-II</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1765\" data-end=\"1812\">Advanced research methods and data analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1910\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1846\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Geo-Politics and World Affairs</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1846\" data-end=\"1910\">Study of global power structures and international relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1911\" data-end=\"1988\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1911\" data-end=\"1932\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Financial Literacy</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1988\">Basics of finance, budgeting, and economic awareness</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"ig5hvq\" data-start=\"1990\" data-end=\"2033\">MA Political Science Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2921\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2060\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2060\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2045\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2045\" data-end=\"2060\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2071\" data-end=\"2921\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2071\" data-end=\"2148\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2071\" data-end=\"2092\" data-col-size=\"md\">Political Theory-I</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2092\" data-end=\"2148\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced political theories and ideological concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2149\" data-end=\"2226\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2149\" data-end=\"2174\" data-col-size=\"md\">Comparative Politics-I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2174\" data-end=\"2226\">Comparison of political systems across countries</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2227\" data-end=\"2330\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2227\" data-end=\"2276\" data-col-size=\"md\">India&rsquo;s Foreign Policy &amp; Relations-I (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2276\" data-end=\"2330\">Study of India&rsquo;s international relations framework</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2414\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2363\" data-col-size=\"md\">International Law-I (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2414\">Basics of international legal systems and rules</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2415\" data-end=\"2529\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2415\" data-end=\"2481\" data-col-size=\"md\">International Organization and Global Order Studies-I (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2481\" data-end=\"2529\">Study of global institutions and world order</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2530\" data-end=\"2631\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2530\" data-end=\"2580\" data-col-size=\"md\">Political Sociology: Indian Context-I (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2580\" data-end=\"2631\">Study of society-politics relationship in India</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2632\" data-end=\"2740\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2632\" data-end=\"2686\" data-col-size=\"md\">State Politics in India (Haryana focus)-I (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2686\" data-end=\"2740\">Regional political systems and governance in India</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2741\" data-end=\"2832\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2741\" data-end=\"2774\" data-col-size=\"md\">Democracy in India-I (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2774\" data-end=\"2832\">Study of democratic structure and functioning in India</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2833\" data-end=\"2921\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2833\" data-end=\"2868\" data-col-size=\"md\">Open Elective: Retail Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2868\" data-end=\"2921\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of retail industry and management concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ocoiox\" data-start=\"2923\" data-end=\"2966\">MA Political Science Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2968\" data-end=\"3740\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2968\" data-end=\"2993\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2968\" data-end=\"2993\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2968\" data-end=\"2978\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2978\" data-end=\"2993\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"3004\" data-end=\"3740\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"3004\" data-end=\"3082\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3004\" data-end=\"3026\" data-col-size=\"md\">Political Theory-II</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3026\" data-end=\"3082\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced concepts in political philosophy and theory</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3083\" data-end=\"3154\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3083\" data-end=\"3109\" data-col-size=\"md\">Comparative Politics-II</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3109\" data-end=\"3154\" data-col-size=\"md\">Further study of global political systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3155\" data-end=\"3254\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3155\" data-end=\"3205\" data-col-size=\"md\">India&rsquo;s Foreign Policy &amp; Relations-II (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3205\" data-end=\"3254\">Advanced analysis of India&rsquo;s global relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3255\" data-end=\"3331\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3255\" data-end=\"3288\" data-col-size=\"md\">International Law-II (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3288\" data-end=\"3331\">Advanced international legal frameworks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3332\" data-end=\"3437\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3332\" data-end=\"3399\" data-col-size=\"md\">International Organization and Global Order Studies-II (Group A)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3399\" data-end=\"3437\">Study of global governance systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3438\" data-end=\"3540\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3438\" data-end=\"3489\" data-col-size=\"md\">Political Sociology: Indian Context-II (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3489\" data-end=\"3540\">Advanced study of politics and society in India</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3541\" data-end=\"3652\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3541\" data-end=\"3596\" data-col-size=\"md\">State Politics in India (Haryana focus)-II (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3596\" data-end=\"3652\">Regional governance and political structure analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3653\" data-end=\"3740\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3653\" data-end=\"3687\" data-col-size=\"md\">Democracy in India-II (Group B)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3687\" data-end=\"3740\">Advanced understanding of Indian democracy system</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 60000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(406, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 327, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 04:45:05', '2026-05-15 05:13:25', '<p data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"366\">The MA Mass Communication admission process is designed to be simple, transparent, and fully online, allowing students to complete their enrollment without difficulty. Candidates must complete registration, fill the application form, upload required documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"562\">Before applying, students should carefully review eligibility criteria, course structure, specialization options, and fee details to ensure a smooth admission process without errors or delays.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1r7g0fw\" data-start=\"564\" data-end=\"619\">Step-by-Step MA Mass Communication Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"8q329j\" data-start=\"621\" data-end=\"678\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"679\" data-end=\"931\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After successful registration, login credentials are generated for accessing the application form and dashboard.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1u4bokh\" data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"979\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"980\" data-end=\"1120\">Students need to fill out the MA Mass Communication admission form carefully with accurate personal, academic, and course-related details.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1122\" data-end=\"1267\">It is important to review all information before final submission, as incorrect details may cause delays in verification or admission approval.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1rwoaln\" data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1308\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1309\" data-end=\"1423\">Candidates must upload all necessary supporting documents in the prescribed format for eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1425\" data-end=\"1452\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1453\" data-end=\"1636\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dlzfxc\" data-start=\"1453\" data-end=\"1501\">Graduation mark sheet and degree certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1502\" data-end=\"1533\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1534\" data-end=\"1562\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1576\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1595\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1596\" data-end=\"1636\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1638\" data-end=\"1768\">Students in the final year of graduation can also apply, subject to completing their degree before final admission confirmation.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"nk09bg\" data-start=\"1770\" data-end=\"1827\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1828\" data-end=\"1935\">After submission, the university verifies academic records, uploaded documents, and eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1937\" data-end=\"2084\">Applications with incomplete, incorrect, or unclear documents may face delays or rejection, so students should ensure proper document submission.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t02fyw\" data-start=\"2086\" data-end=\"2119\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2120\" data-end=\"2340\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the applicable MA Mass Communication program fee online. After successful payment, the university issues a registration number confirming admission into the course.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2342\" data-end=\"2445\">Students should keep payment receipts and admission confirmation details safely for future reference.</p>', 1, '<h1 data-section-id=\"1hb7bsu\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"49\">MA Mass Communication Eligibility Criteria 2026</h1>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1aexq0b\" data-start=\"51\" data-end=\"76\">Eligibility Highlights</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"477\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dq6j0q\" data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"140\">Bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university is required</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jrh6yy\" data-start=\"141\" data-end=\"205\">Students from any stream (Arts, Commerce, Science) can apply</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jk4tp4\" data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"279\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible in many universities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fjbzql\" data-start=\"280\" data-end=\"330\">Admission may be merit-based or entrance-based</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6rjjq3\" data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"392\">Some universities may require minimum percentage criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3rpo40\" data-start=\"393\" data-end=\"477\">Suitable for students interested in media, journalism, and communication careers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ui3lje\" data-start=\"479\" data-end=\"501\">Eligibility Details</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"729\">Candidates applying for MA Mass Communication must have completed a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university. The degree can be in any discipline, as the program is open to students from different academic backgrounds.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"956\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible to apply in most universities, provided they complete their degree before final admission confirmation. This allows students to apply early without waiting for final results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1164\">In some institutions, admission may also depend on entrance exams, interviews, or portfolio evaluation. Certain universities may also set minimum marks criteria depending on competition and course demand.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1166\" data-end=\"1402\">The course is ideal for students interested in journalism, media production, advertising, public relations, digital media, and communication industries. It focuses on building strong writing, reporting, storytelling, and media skills.</p>', '<p data-start=\"44\" data-end=\"438\">The MA Mass Communication fee structure is designed to provide flexible payment options for both Indian and international students. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option depending on their financial planning and convenience. The total program fee includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"654\">Apart from tuition fees, students should also consider additional academic expenses such as practical production work, project assignments, media tools, and examination-related charges during the course duration.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1d42as6\" data-start=\"656\" data-end=\"694\">MA Mass Communication Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"981\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"722\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"722\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"707\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Category</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"707\" data-end=\"722\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"733\" data-end=\"981\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"733\" data-end=\"763\">\r\n<td data-start=\"733\" data-end=\"752\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"752\" data-end=\"763\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"811\">\r\n<td data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"787\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"787\" data-end=\"811\">₹15,000 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"812\" data-end=\"852\">\r\n<td data-start=\"812\" data-end=\"841\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"852\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"932\">\r\n<td data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"872\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"872\" data-end=\"932\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"981\">\r\n<td data-start=\"933\" data-end=\"961\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"981\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"1008\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1176\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1045\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1045\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1025\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1045\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1056\" data-end=\"1176\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1056\" data-end=\"1088\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1056\" data-end=\"1077\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1077\" data-end=\"1088\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1089\" data-end=\"1119\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1089\" data-end=\"1108\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1108\" data-end=\"1119\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1176\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1140\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1140\" data-end=\"1176\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"pqmo6t\" data-start=\"1178\" data-end=\"1225\">MA Mass Communication Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1227\" data-end=\"1500\">The MA Mass Communication program offers a clear and structured fee system that helps students manage their academic expenses easily. Semester-wise payment allows flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete the payment in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1502\" data-end=\"1760\">The first semester fee includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the same fee structure continues. If a student needs to reappear in any subject examination, an additional fee of ₹500 per subject is applicable.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"52\" data-end=\"404\">The MA Mass Communication syllabus is designed to provide students with strong knowledge of journalism, media production, advertising, public relations, and digital communication. The course focuses on both theoretical understanding and practical media skills needed for careers in news, television, radio, digital media, and corporate communication.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"406\" data-end=\"693\">The program is structured across four semesters and gradually moves from basic communication concepts to advanced media production, reporting, editing, and industry-focused specializations. It helps students build professional skills in writing, reporting, editing, and media handling.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1aa88tx\" data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"739\">MA Mass Communication Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"1201\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"766\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"766\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"751\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"751\" data-end=\"766\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"1201\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"877\">\r\n<td data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"816\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Theory and Practice of Communication</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"816\" data-end=\"877\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of communication models, principles, and processes</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"959\">\r\n<td data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"895\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Writing Skills</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"959\" data-col-size=\"md\">Development of writing, editing, and content creation skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"1049\">\r\n<td data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"989\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Introduction to Mass Media</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"989\" data-end=\"1049\" data-col-size=\"md\">Overview of print, electronic, and digital media systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1120\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1068\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Media &amp; Society</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1120\" data-col-size=\"md\">Relationship between media and social structures</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1121\" data-end=\"1201\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1121\" data-end=\"1145\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Computer Applications</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1145\" data-end=\"1201\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basic computer tools used in media and communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1f3fal2\" data-start=\"1203\" data-end=\"1247\">MA Mass Communication Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1249\" data-end=\"1740\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1249\" data-end=\"1274\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1249\" data-end=\"1274\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1249\" data-end=\"1259\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1259\" data-end=\"1274\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1285\" data-end=\"1740\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1285\" data-end=\"1354\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1285\" data-end=\"1297\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Reporting</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1297\" data-end=\"1354\">News reporting techniques and field journalism skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1355\" data-end=\"1428\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1355\" data-end=\"1369\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Advertising</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1369\" data-end=\"1428\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fundamentals of advertising and marketing communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1508\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1429\" data-end=\"1448\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Radio Journalism</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1508\" data-col-size=\"md\">Radio production, scripting, and broadcasting techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1509\" data-end=\"1585\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1509\" data-end=\"1528\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Photo Journalism</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1528\" data-end=\"1585\">Basics of photography for news and media storytelling</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1663\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1614\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Media Laws and Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1663\" data-col-size=\"md\">Legal framework and media industry management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1664\" data-end=\"1740\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1664\" data-end=\"1680\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Indian Polity</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1680\" data-end=\"1740\">Understanding Indian political system for media coverage</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ftrvjr\" data-start=\"1742\" data-end=\"1786\">MA Mass Communication Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"2247\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1813\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1813\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1788\" data-end=\"1798\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1798\" data-end=\"1813\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1824\" data-end=\"2247\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1824\" data-end=\"1884\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1824\" data-end=\"1834\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Editing</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1834\" data-end=\"1884\" data-col-size=\"md\">News editing techniques and content refinement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1885\" data-end=\"1948\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1885\" data-end=\"1901\" data-col-size=\"sm\">TV Journalism</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1901\" data-end=\"1948\" data-col-size=\"md\">Television news production and broadcasting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1949\" data-end=\"2021\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1949\" data-end=\"1968\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Public Relations</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1968\" data-end=\"2021\">Managing public image and corporate communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2022\" data-end=\"2107\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2022\" data-end=\"2047\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Communication Research</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2047\" data-end=\"2107\">Research methods used in media and communication studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2182\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2135\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Communication Technology</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2135\" data-end=\"2182\">Tools and technologies used in modern media</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2183\" data-end=\"2247\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2183\" data-end=\"2199\" data-col-size=\"sm\">India &amp; World</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2199\" data-end=\"2247\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of national and global current affairs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"l8hogg\" data-start=\"2249\" data-end=\"2293\">MA Mass Communication Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2708\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2320\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2320\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2305\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2305\" data-end=\"2320\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2708\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2404\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2356\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Print Media Production</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2356\" data-end=\"2404\" data-col-size=\"md\">Newspaper and magazine production techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2405\" data-end=\"2470\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2405\" data-end=\"2435\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Electronic Media Production</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2435\" data-end=\"2470\" data-col-size=\"md\">TV and radio content production</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2471\" data-end=\"2539\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2471\" data-end=\"2490\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Cyber Journalism</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2490\" data-end=\"2539\">Digital journalism and online media reporting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2540\" data-end=\"2620\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2540\" data-end=\"2568\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Development Communication</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2568\" data-end=\"2620\">Media&rsquo;s role in social development and awareness</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2621\" data-end=\"2708\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2621\" data-end=\"2655\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Film and Entertainment Industry</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2655\" data-end=\"2708\">Basics of film production and entertainment media</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 60000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(407, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 102, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 05:23:06', '2026-05-15 05:23:06', '<p data-start=\"37\" data-end=\"313\">The MA English admission process is simple, structured, and fully online, allowing students to complete their application easily. Candidates need to complete registration, submit the application form, upload documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"315\" data-end=\"508\">Before applying, students should carefully check eligibility criteria, course structure, specialization options, and fee details to ensure a smooth admission process without errors or delays.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1hvsg2\" data-start=\"510\" data-end=\"554\">Step-by-Step MA English Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"8q329j\" data-start=\"556\" data-end=\"613\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"614\" data-end=\"839\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After registration, login credentials are created for accessing the application form.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1u4bokh\" data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"887\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"888\" data-end=\"1005\">Students must fill out the MA English admission form carefully with correct personal, academic, and course details.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1157\">It is important to verify all information before final submission, as incorrect details may create issues during verification or admission approval.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1rwoaln\" data-start=\"1159\" data-end=\"1198\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1199\" data-end=\"1304\">Candidates need to upload all necessary supporting documents in the prescribed format for verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1306\" data-end=\"1333\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1517\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dlzfxc\" data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1382\">Graduation mark sheet and degree certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1383\" data-end=\"1414\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1415\" data-end=\"1443\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1444\" data-end=\"1457\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1458\" data-end=\"1476\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1477\" data-end=\"1517\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"1649\">Students in the final year of graduation can also apply, subject to completing their degree before final admission confirmation.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"nk09bg\" data-start=\"1651\" data-end=\"1708\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1709\" data-end=\"1807\">After submission, the university verifies academic records, documents, and eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1809\" data-end=\"1947\">Applications with incorrect, incomplete, or unclear documents may face delays or rejection, so students should ensure proper submission.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t02fyw\" data-start=\"1949\" data-end=\"1982\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1983\" data-end=\"2167\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the MA English program fee online. After successful payment, the university provides a registration number confirming admission.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2169\" data-end=\"2272\">Students should keep payment receipts and admission confirmation details safely for future reference.</p>', 1, '<h2 data-section-id=\"1aexq0b\" data-start=\"40\" data-end=\"65\">Eligibility Highlights</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"458\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dq6j0q\" data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"129\">Bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university is required</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jrh6yy\" data-start=\"130\" data-end=\"194\">Students from any stream (Arts, Commerce, Science) can apply</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jk4tp4\" data-start=\"195\" data-end=\"268\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible in many universities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fjbzql\" data-start=\"269\" data-end=\"319\">Admission may be merit-based or entrance-based</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"izhkbp\" data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"376\">Some universities may require minimum marks criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1k8ad09\" data-start=\"377\" data-end=\"458\">Suitable for students interested in literature, language, and writing careers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ui3lje\" data-start=\"460\" data-end=\"482\">Eligibility Details</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"484\" data-end=\"691\">Candidates applying for MA English must have completed a bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university. The degree can be in English or any other discipline, depending on the university&rsquo;s admission rules.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"693\" data-end=\"912\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible to apply in most universities, provided they complete their degree before final admission is confirmed. This allows students to apply without waiting for final results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"914\" data-end=\"1120\">Some institutions may conduct entrance exams, interviews, or academic screening depending on competition and course requirements. A few universities may also set minimum percentage criteria for admission.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1122\" data-end=\"1347\">The course is suitable for students interested in English literature, linguistics, writing, teaching, research, and communication-based careers. It helps improve critical thinking, writing ability, and language proficiency</p>', '<p data-start=\"33\" data-end=\"304\">The MA English fee structure is designed to provide flexible and affordable payment options for both Indian and international students. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option depending on their financial convenience and planning.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"306\" data-end=\"597\">The total fee includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester. Apart from tuition fees, students should also consider additional academic expenses such as study materials, assignments, and examination-related costs during the course.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"q8d8y0\" data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"626\">MA English Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"913\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"654\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"654\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"639\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Category</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"639\" data-end=\"654\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"913\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"695\">\r\n<td data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"684\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"695\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"743\">\r\n<td data-start=\"696\" data-end=\"719\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"719\" data-end=\"743\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"784\">\r\n<td data-start=\"744\" data-end=\"773\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"773\" data-end=\"784\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"864\">\r\n<td data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"804\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"804\" data-end=\"864\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"913\">\r\n<td data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"893\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"913\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"940\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"942\" data-end=\"1108\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"942\" data-end=\"977\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"942\" data-end=\"977\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"942\" data-end=\"957\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"957\" data-end=\"977\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1108\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1020\">\r\n<td data-start=\"988\" data-end=\"1009\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1009\" data-end=\"1020\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1021\" data-end=\"1051\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1021\" data-end=\"1040\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1051\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1108\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1072\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1108\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"9bzo2z\" data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1146\">MA English Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1148\" data-end=\"1414\">The MA English program offers a clear and structured fee system that helps students manage their academic expenses easily. Semester-wise payment provides flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete their payment in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1416\" data-end=\"1693\">The first semester includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the same fee structure continues throughout the program. If a student needs to reappear in any subject examination, an additional fee of ₹500 per subject is applicable.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"41\" data-end=\"360\">The MA English syllabus is designed to provide deep knowledge of English literature, language studies, critical theory, and literary analysis. It covers classical to modern literature along with electives that allow students to explore fiction, drama, poetry, gender studies, philosophy, and post-colonial literature.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"362\" data-end=\"624\">The course is structured across four semesters and helps students develop strong reading, writing, interpretation, and analytical skills. It is highly useful for careers in teaching, research, content writing, publishing, media, and civil services preparation.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1r5kcvf\" data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"659\">MA English Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"1315\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"686\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"686\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"671\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"671\" data-end=\"686\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"1315\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"796\">\r\n<td data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"741\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1550&ndash;1660 (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"796\">Study of early English literature and major writers</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"797\" data-end=\"896\">\r\n<td data-start=\"797\" data-end=\"841\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1660&ndash;1798 (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"896\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature from restoration and neoclassical period</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"986\">\r\n<td data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"941\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1798&ndash;1914 (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"941\" data-end=\"986\" data-col-size=\"md\">Romantic and Victorian literature studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"987\" data-end=\"1077\">\r\n<td data-start=\"987\" data-end=\"1031\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1914&ndash;2000 (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1077\">Modern and contemporary English literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1078\" data-end=\"1157\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1078\" data-end=\"1115\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Fiction (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1115\" data-end=\"1157\">Basics of fiction writing and analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1158\" data-end=\"1231\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1158\" data-end=\"1193\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Drama (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1193\" data-end=\"1231\">Study of drama structure and plays</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1232\" data-end=\"1315\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1232\" data-end=\"1268\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Poetry (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1268\" data-end=\"1315\">Introduction to poetry forms and techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"2pk3t4\" data-start=\"1317\" data-end=\"1350\">MA English Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"2071\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1377\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1377\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1352\" data-end=\"1362\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1362\" data-end=\"1377\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"2071\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1479\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1388\" data-end=\"1433\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1550&ndash;1660 (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1479\">Advanced study of early English literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1577\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1525\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1660&ndash;1798 (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1525\" data-end=\"1577\">Advanced neoclassical and restoration literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1578\" data-end=\"1669\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1578\" data-end=\"1623\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1798&ndash;1914 (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1623\" data-end=\"1669\">Deep study of romantic and Victorian works</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1760\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1670\" data-end=\"1715\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature in English: 1914&ndash;2000 (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1715\" data-end=\"1760\">Modern and postmodern literature analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1761\" data-end=\"1847\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1761\" data-end=\"1799\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Fiction (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1799\" data-end=\"1847\">Advanced fiction analysis and interpretation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1848\" data-end=\"1925\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1848\" data-end=\"1884\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Drama (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1884\" data-end=\"1925\">Detailed study of dramatic literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1926\" data-end=\"1991\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1926\" data-end=\"1963\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of a Genre: Poetry (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1963\" data-end=\"1991\">Advanced poetry analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1992\" data-end=\"2071\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1992\" data-end=\"2028\" data-col-size=\"md\">Open Elective: Financial Literacy</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2028\" data-end=\"2071\">Basic financial knowledge and awareness</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ezvdd5\" data-start=\"2073\" data-end=\"2106\">MA English Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2830\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2133\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2133\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2108\" data-end=\"2118\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2118\" data-end=\"2133\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2144\" data-end=\"2830\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2144\" data-end=\"2222\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2144\" data-end=\"2171\" data-col-size=\"md\">Critical Theory (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2171\" data-end=\"2222\">Introduction to literary criticism and theories</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2299\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2254\" data-col-size=\"md\">American Literature (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2254\" data-end=\"2299\">Study of major American writers and texts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2300\" data-end=\"2378\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2300\" data-end=\"2337\" data-col-size=\"md\">Indian Writing in English (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2337\" data-end=\"2378\" data-col-size=\"md\">Indian English literature and authors</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2379\" data-end=\"2448\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2379\" data-end=\"2407\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2407\" data-end=\"2448\">Advanced language structure and usage</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2449\" data-end=\"2514\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2449\" data-end=\"2482\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature and Gender (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"2514\">Gender studies in literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2515\" data-end=\"2600\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2515\" data-end=\"2561\" data-col-size=\"md\">Colonial and Post-Colonial Studies (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2561\" data-end=\"2600\">Impact of colonialism in literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2601\" data-end=\"2689\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2601\" data-end=\"2638\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature and Philosophy (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2638\" data-end=\"2689\">Link between literature and philosophical ideas</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2690\" data-end=\"2756\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2690\" data-end=\"2717\" data-col-size=\"md\">New Literatures (Part-I)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2717\" data-end=\"2756\">Study of emerging global literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2757\" data-end=\"2830\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2757\" data-end=\"2792\" data-col-size=\"md\">Open Elective: Retail Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2792\" data-end=\"2830\">Basics of retail business concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"136n2q6\" data-start=\"2832\" data-end=\"2865\">MA English Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"3694\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2892\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2892\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2877\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2877\" data-end=\"2892\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"3694\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2971\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2903\" data-end=\"2931\" data-col-size=\"md\">Critical Theory (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2931\" data-end=\"2971\">Advanced literary criticism concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2972\" data-end=\"3045\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2972\" data-end=\"3004\" data-col-size=\"md\">American Literature (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3004\" data-end=\"3045\" data-col-size=\"md\">Deep study of American literary works</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3046\" data-end=\"3130\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3046\" data-end=\"3084\" data-col-size=\"md\">Indian Writing in English (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3084\" data-end=\"3130\">Advanced Indian English literature studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3206\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3160\" data-col-size=\"md\">English Language (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3160\" data-end=\"3206\">Advanced language and communication skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3207\" data-end=\"3284\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3207\" data-end=\"3241\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature and Gender (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3241\" data-end=\"3284\">Advanced gender-based literary analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3375\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3332\" data-col-size=\"md\">Colonial and Post-Colonial Studies (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3332\" data-end=\"3375\">Advanced post-colonial literary studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3376\" data-end=\"3469\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3376\" data-end=\"3414\" data-col-size=\"md\">Literature and Philosophy (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3414\" data-end=\"3469\">Advanced philosophical interpretation of literature</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3470\" data-end=\"3544\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3470\" data-end=\"3498\" data-col-size=\"md\">New Literatures (Part-II)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"3498\" data-end=\"3544\" data-col-size=\"md\">Global and contemporary literature studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3545\" data-end=\"3615\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3545\" data-end=\"3573\" data-col-size=\"md\">Western Political Thought</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3573\" data-end=\"3615\">Basics of Western political philosophy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"3616\" data-end=\"3694\">\r\n<td data-start=\"3616\" data-end=\"3651\" data-col-size=\"md\">Indian Government and Politics-I</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"3651\" data-end=\"3694\">Introduction to Indian political system</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 60000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(408, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 75, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 05:36:00', '2026-05-15 05:36:00', '<p data-start=\"30\" data-end=\"333\">The MCA admission process is designed to be simple, structured, and fully online, allowing students to complete their enrollment without difficulty. Candidates must complete registration, fill out the application form, upload required documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"526\">Before applying, students should carefully check eligibility criteria, course structure, specialization focus, and fee details to ensure a smooth admission process without errors or delays.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"f7mx77\" data-start=\"528\" data-end=\"565\">Step-by-Step MCA Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"8q329j\" data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"624\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"625\" data-end=\"864\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After registration, login credentials are created for accessing the application form and dashboard.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1u4bokh\" data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"912\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"1034\">Students need to fill out the MCA admission form carefully with correct personal, academic, and course-related details.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1036\" data-end=\"1186\">It is important to verify all details before final submission, as incorrect information may create issues during verification or admission approval.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1rwoaln\" data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1227\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1342\">Candidates must upload all necessary supporting documents in the prescribed format for eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1371\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1555\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dlzfxc\" data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1420\">Graduation mark sheet and degree certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1421\" data-end=\"1452\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1453\" data-end=\"1481\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1495\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1514\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1555\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1557\" data-end=\"1677\">Final-year graduation students can also apply, subject to completing their degree before final admission confirmation.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"nk09bg\" data-start=\"1679\" data-end=\"1736\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1835\">After submission, the university verifies academic records, documents, and eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1837\" data-end=\"1969\">Incomplete or incorrect documents may delay the admission process or lead to rejection, so students must ensure proper submission.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t02fyw\" data-start=\"1971\" data-end=\"2004\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2005\" data-end=\"2197\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the MCA program fee online. After successful payment, the university issues a registration number confirming admission into the program.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2199\" data-end=\"2296\">Students should keep payment receipts and admission confirmation details safely for future use.</p>', 1, '<h1 data-section-id=\"1h2qv2p\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"31\">MCA Eligibility Criteria 2026</h1>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1aexq0b\" data-start=\"33\" data-end=\"58\">Eligibility Highlights</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"549\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1irsuzv\" data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"133\">Graduation in any discipline from a recognized university is required</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"edd5yn\" data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"216\">Minimum 50% marks in graduation (47.5% for SC/ST/Differently abled candidates)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"smf5hz\" data-start=\"217\" data-end=\"299\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible to apply in many universities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vz7uhv\" data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"371\">Some universities may prefer candidates with Mathematics background</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"is63g2\" data-start=\"372\" data-end=\"449\">Admission may be entrance-based or merit-based depending on the institute</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1edvxhp\" data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"549\">Suitable for students interested in computer applications, software development, and IT careers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ui3lje\" data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"573\">Eligibility Details</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"575\" data-end=\"837\">Candidates applying for the Master of Computer Applications (MCA) program must have completed graduation from a recognized university. A minimum of 50% marks is required, while relaxation is provided to SC/ST and differently abled candidates as per guidelines.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"839\" data-end=\"1055\">Final-year graduation students are also eligible in many universities, provided they complete their degree before final admission confirmation. This allows students to apply early without waiting for final results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1057\" data-end=\"1243\">Some institutions may prefer candidates who have studied Mathematics at the 10+2 or graduation level. However, this requirement may vary depending on the university&rsquo;s admission policy.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1245\" data-end=\"1522\">The MCA program is designed for students who want to build careers in software development, programming, data science, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and IT services. It focuses on technical knowledge, programming skills, and practical software development training.</p>', '<p data-start=\"26\" data-end=\"284\">The MCA fee structure is designed to offer flexible and affordable payment options for both Indian and international students. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option based on their financial planning and convenience.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"598\">The total program fee includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester. Apart from tuition fees, students should also consider additional academic expenses such as lab work, projects, certification courses, and examination-related costs during the course.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1cxsk8p\" data-start=\"600\" data-end=\"620\">MCA Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"907\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"648\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"648\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"633\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Category</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"633\" data-end=\"648\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"907\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"689\">\r\n<td data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"678\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"678\" data-end=\"689\">₹19,947</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"737\">\r\n<td data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"713\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"713\" data-end=\"737\">₹18,900 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"778\">\r\n<td data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"767\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"767\" data-end=\"778\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹76,647</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"779\" data-end=\"858\">\r\n<td data-start=\"779\" data-end=\"798\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"798\" data-end=\"858\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"907\">\r\n<td data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"887\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"887\" data-end=\"907\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"909\" data-end=\"934\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"1119\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"971\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"971\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"951\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"951\" data-end=\"971\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"982\" data-end=\"1119\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"982\" data-end=\"1014\">\r\n<td data-start=\"982\" data-end=\"1003\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1003\" data-end=\"1014\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹76,647</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1062\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1041\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Fee (Avg.)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1041\" data-end=\"1062\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹18,900 &ndash; ₹19,947</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1119\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1063\" data-end=\"1083\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1083\" data-end=\"1119\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1atu2ey\" data-start=\"1121\" data-end=\"1150\">MCA Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1152\" data-end=\"1416\">The MCA program offers a structured and transparent fee system that helps students manage their education expenses effectively. Semester-wise payment allows flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete payments in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1673\">The first semester fee includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the fee remains consistent as per the structure. In case a student needs to reappear for any subject, a fee of ₹500 per subject is applicable.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"34\" data-end=\"349\">The MCA syllabus is designed to provide strong technical knowledge in computer applications, programming, software development, and emerging technologies. The course focuses on building practical skills in coding, system design, data management, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and modern computing tools.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"537\">The program is divided into four semesters, combining core computer science subjects, practical labs, internships, and project-based learning to prepare students for IT industry roles.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1d0yahm\" data-start=\"539\" data-end=\"565\">MCA Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"1117\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"592\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"592\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"567\" data-end=\"577\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"577\" data-end=\"592\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"1117\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"683\">\r\n<td data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"630\" data-col-size=\"md\">Operating System &amp; Linux</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"630\" data-end=\"683\">Basics of operating systems and Linux environment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"758\">\r\n<td data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"702\" data-col-size=\"md\">Data Structures</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"702\" data-end=\"758\" data-col-size=\"md\">Concepts of organizing and managing data efficiently</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"838\">\r\n<td data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"788\" data-col-size=\"md\">Client Side Web Technology</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"788\" data-end=\"838\" data-col-size=\"md\">Web design using HTML, CSS, and frontend tools</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"839\" data-end=\"903\">\r\n<td data-start=\"839\" data-end=\"861\" data-col-size=\"md\">Programming in Java</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"861\" data-end=\"903\" data-col-size=\"md\">Object-oriented programming using Java</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"904\" data-end=\"1006\">\r\n<td data-start=\"904\" data-end=\"958\" data-col-size=\"md\">Computer Fundamentals and Problem Solving Through C</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"1006\">Basics of computer systems and C programming</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1057\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1017\" data-col-size=\"md\">Seminar</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1017\" data-end=\"1057\">Presentation-based academic learning</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1117\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1058\" data-end=\"1080\" data-col-size=\"md\">Practical - 1, 2, 3</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1080\" data-end=\"1117\" data-col-size=\"md\">Hands-on programming and lab work</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"e4gik9\" data-start=\"1119\" data-end=\"1145\">MCA Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1756\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1172\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1172\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1147\" data-end=\"1157\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1157\" data-end=\"1172\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1183\" data-end=\"1756\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1183\" data-end=\"1256\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1183\" data-end=\"1213\" data-col-size=\"md\">Database Management Systems</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1213\" data-end=\"1256\">Managing and organizing structured data</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1257\" data-end=\"1322\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1257\" data-end=\"1286\" data-col-size=\"md\">Server Side Web Technology</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1322\">Backend web development concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1389\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1323\" data-end=\"1349\" data-col-size=\"md\">Artificial Intelligence</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1389\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of AI and intelligent systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1390\" data-end=\"1488\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1390\" data-end=\"1438\" data-col-size=\"md\">Mathematical Foundations for Computer Science</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1438\" data-end=\"1488\" data-col-size=\"md\">Logic, mathematics, and computational concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1489\" data-end=\"1557\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1489\" data-end=\"1508\" data-col-size=\"md\">Computer Network</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1557\">Networking concepts and communication systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1558\" data-end=\"1602\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1558\" data-end=\"1571\" data-col-size=\"md\">Internship</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1571\" data-end=\"1602\" data-col-size=\"md\">Practical industry exposure</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1603\" data-end=\"1696\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1603\" data-end=\"1653\" data-col-size=\"md\">Constitutional, Human and Moral Values, and IPR</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1653\" data-end=\"1696\">Ethics and intellectual property rights</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1697\" data-end=\"1756\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1697\" data-end=\"1719\" data-col-size=\"md\">Practical - 4, 5, 6</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1719\" data-end=\"1756\" data-col-size=\"md\">Lab-based technical practice work</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"10v9azc\" data-start=\"1758\" data-end=\"1784\">MCA Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"2258\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"1811\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"1811\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1786\" data-end=\"1796\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1811\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"2258\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"1895\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"1851\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Machine Learning in Python</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1895\">Introduction to ML concepts using Python</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1896\" data-end=\"1976\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1896\" data-end=\"1932\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Design and Analysis of Algorithms</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1976\">Algorithm design and efficiency analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1977\" data-end=\"2045\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1977\" data-end=\"1995\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Ethical Hacking</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1995\" data-end=\"2045\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of cybersecurity and hacking techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2046\" data-end=\"2122\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2046\" data-end=\"2075\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Data Analytics using Excel</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2075\" data-end=\"2122\">Data analysis and visualization using Excel</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2123\" data-end=\"2197\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2123\" data-end=\"2156\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Big Data &amp; Pattern Recognition</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2156\" data-end=\"2197\">Introduction to big data technologies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2198\" data-end=\"2258\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2198\" data-end=\"2217\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Practical - 7, 8</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2217\" data-end=\"2258\">Advanced programming and lab practice</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1eljhhb\" data-start=\"2260\" data-end=\"2286\">MCA Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2701\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2313\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2313\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2288\" data-end=\"2298\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2298\" data-end=\"2313\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2324\" data-end=\"2701\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2324\" data-end=\"2397\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2324\" data-end=\"2348\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Blockchain Technology</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2348\" data-end=\"2397\">Basics of blockchain systems and applications</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2398\" data-end=\"2478\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2398\" data-end=\"2436\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Principles of Programming Languages</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2436\" data-end=\"2478\">Study of programming language concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2479\" data-end=\"2550\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2479\" data-end=\"2512\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Object Oriented Design and UML</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2512\" data-end=\"2550\">Software design using UML modeling</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2551\" data-end=\"2625\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2551\" data-end=\"2581\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Cyber Security Fundamentals</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2581\" data-end=\"2625\" data-col-size=\"md\">Introduction to cybersecurity principles</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2626\" data-end=\"2701\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2626\" data-end=\"2651\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Dissertation / Project</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2651\" data-end=\"2701\">Final project based on real-world applications</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 76647.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(409, 76, '5d035506-ff90-47c0-b5e1-c80c3f178807', '58ccd349-6761-4944-9739-809ff0ece2f3', 75, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 06:02:12', '2026-05-15 06:02:12', '<p data-start=\"32\" data-end=\"325\">The M.Com admission process is simple, structured, and fully online, allowing students to complete their application without difficulty. Candidates are required to complete registration, fill out the application form, upload documents, and pay the program fee after eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"518\">Before applying, students should carefully check eligibility criteria, course structure, specialization areas, and fee details to ensure a smooth admission process without errors or delays.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1vtv96m\" data-start=\"520\" data-end=\"559\">Step-by-Step M.Com Admission Process</h2>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"8q329j\" data-start=\"561\" data-end=\"618\">Step 1: Register on the University Admission Portal</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"619\" data-end=\"844\">Candidates must first register on the official university admission portal using basic details such as name, email ID, and mobile number. After registration, login credentials are created for accessing the application form.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1u4bokh\" data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"892\">Step 2: Submit the Online Admission Form</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"1013\">Students must fill out the M.Com admission form carefully with correct personal, academic, and course-related details.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1169\">It is important to review all information before final submission, as incorrect details may lead to verification issues or delays in admission approval.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1rwoaln\" data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1210\">Step 3: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1211\" data-end=\"1328\">Candidates need to upload all necessary supporting documents in the prescribed format for eligibility verification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1357\">Common documents include:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1358\" data-end=\"1541\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dlzfxc\" data-start=\"1358\" data-end=\"1406\">Graduation mark sheet and degree certificate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ara2fa\" data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1438\">Class 10 and 12 mark sheets</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11yc9fs\" data-start=\"1439\" data-end=\"1467\">Passport-size photograph</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yra9zg\" data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1481\">Signature</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l6qwl6\" data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1500\">Identity proof</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14qiub2\" data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1541\">Category certificate (if applicable)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1543\" data-end=\"1673\">Students in the final year of graduation can also apply, subject to completing their degree before final admission confirmation.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"nk09bg\" data-start=\"1675\" data-end=\"1732\">Step 4: Document Verification and Eligibility Check</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"1733\" data-end=\"1840\">After submission, the university verifies academic records, uploaded documents, and eligibility criteria.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1842\" data-end=\"1978\">Applications with incorrect or incomplete documents may face delays or rejection, so students must ensure proper and clear submission.</p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t02fyw\" data-start=\"1980\" data-end=\"2013\">Step 5: Pay the Program Fee</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"2014\" data-end=\"2209\">Once the application is approved, candidates must pay the M.Com program fee online. After successful payment, the university provides a registration number confirming admission into the course.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2211\" data-end=\"2314\">Students should keep payment receipts and admission confirmation details safely for future reference.</p>', 1, '<h2 data-section-id=\"1aexq0b\" data-start=\"35\" data-end=\"60\">Eligibility</h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"62\" data-end=\"499\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"89p2yk\" data-start=\"62\" data-end=\"122\">A B.Com degree from a recognized university is preferred</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qzcltw\" data-start=\"123\" data-end=\"206\">Graduates in any discipline with Economics and/or Mathematics are also eligible</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1yi8m12\" data-start=\"207\" data-end=\"268\">Degree must be from a recognized or equivalent university</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"eb83c2\" data-start=\"269\" data-end=\"334\">Final-year graduation students can apply in many universities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nblri7\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"414\">Admission may be merit-based or entrance-based depending on the institution</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"135x5w7\" data-start=\"415\" data-end=\"499\">Suitable for students interested in commerce, finance, accounting, and economics</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ui3lje\" data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"523\">Eligibility Details</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"525\" data-end=\"807\">Candidates applying for the Master of Commerce (M.Com) program must have completed graduation from a recognized university. A B.Com degree is the most preferred qualification, but students from other disciplines are also eligible if they have studied Economics and/or Mathematics.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"809\" data-end=\"1022\">Final-year graduation students can also apply in many universities, provided they complete their degree before final admission confirmation. This allows students to apply early without waiting for final results.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1234\">Some universities may conduct entrance exams or consider academic performance during admission. A few institutions may also set minimum marks criteria depending on competition and specialization requirements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1236\" data-end=\"1468\">The M.Com program is suitable for students who want to build careers in accounting, finance, banking, taxation, economics, and business analysis. It also helps in higher studies like PhD, teaching, and professional certifications.</p>', '<p data-start=\"28\" data-end=\"290\">The M.Com fee structure is designed to provide flexible and affordable payment options for both Indian and international students. Students can choose between semester-wise payment or a lump sum payment option based on their financial planning and convenience.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"590\">The total program fee includes academic charges along with a non-refundable registration fee applicable in the first semester. Apart from tuition fees, students should also consider additional academic expenses such as project work, examination fees, and research-related costs during the course.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1578ro4\" data-start=\"592\" data-end=\"614\">M.Com Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"901\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"642\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"642\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"616\" data-end=\"627\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Category</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"627\" data-end=\"642\" data-col-size=\"md\">Fee Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"653\" data-end=\"901\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"653\" data-end=\"683\">\r\n<td data-start=\"653\" data-end=\"672\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1st Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"672\" data-end=\"683\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"731\">\r\n<td data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"707\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2nd Semester Onwards</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"707\" data-end=\"731\">₹15,000 per semester</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"772\">\r\n<td data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"761\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Lump Sum Payment (Popular)</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"772\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"773\" data-end=\"852\">\r\n<td data-start=\"773\" data-end=\"792\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"792\" data-end=\"852\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹1,000 (Included in 1st Semester Fee and Non-Refundable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"901\">\r\n<td data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"881\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"881\" data-end=\"901\" data-col-size=\"md\">₹500 per subject</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"7w02bk\" data-start=\"903\" data-end=\"928\">Average Cost Breakdown</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"930\" data-end=\"1096\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"930\" data-end=\"965\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"930\" data-end=\"965\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"930\" data-end=\"945\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Expense Type</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"945\" data-end=\"965\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Estimated Amount</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"1096\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"1008\">\r\n<td data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"997\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Program Cost</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"997\" data-end=\"1008\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹60,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1009\" data-end=\"1039\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1009\" data-end=\"1028\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Per Semester Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1039\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹15,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1096\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1060\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Re-Appear Charges</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1060\" data-end=\"1096\" data-col-size=\"sm\">₹500 per subject (if applicable)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1l8eenr\" data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1129\">M.Com Fee Structure Overview</h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"1131\" data-end=\"1380\">The M.Com program offers a structured fee system that helps students manage their academic expenses easily. Semester-wise payment provides flexibility, while the lump sum option is preferred by students who want to complete the payment in advance.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1382\" data-end=\"1659\">The first semester includes a non-refundable registration fee of ₹1,000. From the second semester onwards, the same fee structure continues throughout the program. If a student needs to reappear in any subject examination, an additional fee of ₹500 per subject is applicable</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"36\" data-end=\"374\">The M.Com syllabus is designed to provide advanced knowledge of commerce, finance, accounting, taxation, marketing, and business management. The course focuses on building analytical skills, financial expertise, and business decision-making abilities required for careers in banking, corporate finance, taxation, auditing, and research.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"376\" data-end=\"552\">The program is structured across four semesters, combining core commerce subjects, specialization papers, case studies, and practical learning through projects and viva-voce.</p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"lm5rcn\" data-start=\"554\" data-end=\"582\">M.Com Semester 1 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"1066\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"609\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"609\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"594\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"594\" data-end=\"609\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"1066\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"691\">\r\n<td data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"647\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Organizational Behaviour</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"691\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of human behavior in organizations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"692\" data-end=\"771\">\r\n<td data-start=\"692\" data-end=\"715\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Business Environment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"771\" data-col-size=\"md\">Understanding internal and external business factors</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"772\" data-end=\"845\">\r\n<td data-start=\"772\" data-end=\"795\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Managerial Economics</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"795\" data-end=\"845\" data-col-size=\"md\">Application of economics in business decisions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"912\">\r\n<td data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"860\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Company Law</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"860\" data-end=\"912\" data-col-size=\"md\">Legal framework governing companies and business</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"995\">\r\n<td data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"951\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Accounting for Managerial Decisions</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"951\" data-end=\"995\" data-col-size=\"md\">Accounting tools for managerial planning</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"996\" data-end=\"1066\">\r\n<td data-start=\"996\" data-end=\"1019\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Marketing Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1019\" data-end=\"1066\" data-col-size=\"md\">Basics of marketing strategies and concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"w79k9g\" data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1096\">M.Com Semester 2 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1712\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1123\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1123\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1108\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1108\" data-end=\"1123\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1712\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1209\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1162\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Human Resource Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1209\" data-col-size=\"md\">Employee management and workplace relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1210\" data-end=\"1296\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1210\" data-end=\"1247\" data-col-size=\"sm\">International Business Environment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1247\" data-end=\"1296\" data-col-size=\"md\">Global business systems and trade environment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1297\" data-end=\"1363\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1297\" data-end=\"1319\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Strategic Marketing</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1319\" data-end=\"1363\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced marketing planning and strategy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1364\" data-end=\"1440\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1364\" data-end=\"1396\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Financial Management &amp; Policy</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1440\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial planning and corporate finance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1441\" data-end=\"1497\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1441\" data-end=\"1464\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Corporate Accounting</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1497\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced accounting practices</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1498\" data-end=\"1563\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1498\" data-end=\"1520\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Business Statistics</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1520\" data-end=\"1563\" data-col-size=\"md\">Statistical tools for business analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1636\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1580\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Indian Polity</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1636\">Understanding Indian political and governance system</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1637\" data-end=\"1712\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1637\" data-end=\"1664\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Viva-Voce cum Case Study</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1664\" data-end=\"1712\">Practical evaluation and case-based learning</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"9ggrud\" data-start=\"1714\" data-end=\"1742\">M.Com Semester 3 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1744\" data-end=\"2410\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1744\" data-end=\"1769\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1744\" data-end=\"1769\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1744\" data-end=\"1754\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"1754\" data-end=\"1769\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"2410\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1858\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1816\" data-col-size=\"md\">Computer Applications in Business</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1816\" data-end=\"1858\" data-col-size=\"md\">Use of software in business operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1859\" data-end=\"1942\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1859\" data-end=\"1891\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advanced Financial Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1891\" data-end=\"1942\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial decision-making and corporate finance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"2038\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1943\" data-end=\"1989\" data-col-size=\"md\">Security Analysis and Investment Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1989\" data-end=\"2038\">Investment planning and stock market analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2039\" data-end=\"2125\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2039\" data-end=\"2076\" data-col-size=\"md\">Financial Institutions and Markets</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2076\" data-end=\"2125\">Banking system and financial market structure</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2126\" data-end=\"2193\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2126\" data-end=\"2151\" data-col-size=\"md\">Advertising Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2151\" data-end=\"2193\">Principles of advertising and branding</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2194\" data-end=\"2272\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2194\" data-end=\"2225\" data-col-size=\"md\">Entrepreneurship Development</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2225\" data-end=\"2272\" data-col-size=\"md\">Business startup and entrepreneurial skills</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2335\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2294\" data-col-size=\"md\">Marketing Research</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2294\" data-end=\"2335\" data-col-size=\"md\">Market analysis and consumer research</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2336\" data-end=\"2410\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2336\" data-end=\"2358\" data-col-size=\"md\">India and the World</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2358\" data-end=\"2410\" data-col-size=\"md\">Study of global economic and political relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"k1kkcy\" data-start=\"2412\" data-end=\"2440\">M.Com Semester 4 Subjects</h2>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"2442\" data-end=\"3019\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"2442\" data-end=\"2467\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2442\" data-end=\"2467\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2442\" data-end=\"2452\" data-col-size=\"md\">Subject</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"2452\" data-end=\"2467\" data-col-size=\"md\">Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"2478\" data-end=\"3019\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"2478\" data-end=\"2546\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2478\" data-end=\"2498\" data-col-size=\"md\">IT and E-Commerce</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2498\" data-end=\"2546\">Digital business and online commerce systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"2633\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"2587\" data-col-size=\"md\">Corporate Tax Planning and Management</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2587\" data-end=\"2633\">Tax laws and corporate taxation strategies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2634\" data-end=\"2712\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2634\" data-end=\"2665\" data-col-size=\"md\">Project Planning and Control</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2665\" data-end=\"2712\" data-col-size=\"md\">Project management and execution techniques</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2713\" data-end=\"2804\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2713\" data-end=\"2759\" data-col-size=\"md\">International Financial Reporting Standards</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2759\" data-end=\"2804\">Global accounting standards and reporting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2805\" data-end=\"2872\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2805\" data-end=\"2824\" data-col-size=\"md\">Sales Management</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2824\" data-end=\"2872\" data-col-size=\"md\">Sales strategies and distribution management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2873\" data-end=\"2944\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2873\" data-end=\"2896\" data-col-size=\"md\">Corporate Governance</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2896\" data-end=\"2944\">Business ethics and corporate responsibility</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2945\" data-end=\"3019\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2945\" data-end=\"2972\" data-col-size=\"md\">Viva-Voce cum Case Study</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2972\" data-end=\"3019\">Final practical evaluation and case studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 60000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(410, 77, '7f5fd513-96c0-4a34-baea-573948e1ee78', '4809357d-d380-4637-bc50-4f4e2ccb4790', 52, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-05-15 06:50:45', '2026-05-15 06:52:16', '<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"28\">Admission Process Overview</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"30\" data-end=\"320\">The admission process is designed to be simple, fully online, and student-friendly, allowing applicants to complete all required steps from registration to final submission without any physical paperwork. The process ensures smooth verification and quick enrollment for eligible candidates.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"354\">Step-by-Step Admission Process</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"356\" data-end=\"704\">Registration<br data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"371\">The first step in the admission process is registration on the official admission portal. Candidates are required to create their user profile by providing basic personal details such as name, contact information, and academic background. Once registered, login credentials are generated for further access to the application system.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"706\" data-end=\"1125\">Fill Online Application Form<br data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"737\">After successful registration, applicants must proceed to fill out the online application form. In this stage, students need to carefully enter their personal information, educational qualifications, and course preferences. It is important to ensure that all details are accurate and match official documents, as incorrect information may lead to verification issues later in the process.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1506\">Complete Your Form<br data-start=\"1145\" data-end=\"1148\">Once the application form is filled, candidates must review all entered details carefully before final submission. After verification, the form should be submitted online along with any required supporting documents. This step confirms the applicant&rsquo;s intention to apply for the programme and initiates the eligibility verification process by the university.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1508\" data-end=\"1920\">Admission Process Explained<br data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1538\">The entire admission process is structured to ensure ease, transparency, and efficiency. It eliminates complex paperwork and allows students to complete the application from anywhere. After submission, the university reviews the application and verifies the eligibility based on submitted documents. Once approved, candidates proceed to the next stage of enrollment and fee payment.</p>', 1, '<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"34\">Eligibility Criteria for Admission</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"36\" data-end=\"548\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9f0kfh\" data-start=\"36\" data-end=\"111\">Intermediate (10+2) or equivalent qualification from a recognized board</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14beole\" data-start=\"112\" data-end=\"176\">Candidates appearing for Class 12 are also eligible to apply</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"kxpkw\" data-start=\"177\" data-end=\"237\">Two-year ITI qualification from a recognized institution</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dd0x75\" data-start=\"238\" data-end=\"298\">APOS (Open Schooling) or equivalent open board education</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nyoeb1\" data-start=\"299\" data-end=\"360\">NIOS (National Institute of Open Schooling) qualification</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1tgd0l\" data-start=\"361\" data-end=\"399\">Polytechnic Diploma after Class 10</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"124pqrv\" data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"458\">Veterinary, Agriculture, or related diploma programmes</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9zsmtf\" data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"548\">Any other qualification equivalent to 10+2 years of study approved by the institution</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"550\" data-end=\"1032\">Eligibility Criteria Explained<br data-start=\"580\" data-end=\"583\">The admission eligibility is based on completion of 10+2 level education or an equivalent qualification. This includes students who have completed Intermediate from any recognized board as well as those who are currently appearing for their Class 12 examinations. Candidates from different learning backgrounds such as vocational training, open schooling, and diploma education are also considered eligible, making the system flexible and inclusive.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1034\" data-end=\"1333\">Students who have completed a two-year ITI programme are eligible if their qualification is recognized as equivalent to 10+2 education. Similarly, candidates from APOS and NIOS boards are fully accepted, as these open schooling systems are treated as equivalent to formal higher secondary education.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1692\">Polytechnic diploma holders after Class 10 can also apply, along with students who have completed diplomas in fields such as Veterinary Science or Agriculture, provided their qualification meets equivalency standards. In addition, any other recognized qualification that matches the 10+2 level of education is accepted after verification by the institution.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1694\" data-end=\"1942\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Overall, the eligibility structure is designed to provide multiple entry pathways for students from academic, technical, and vocational backgrounds, ensuring wider access to higher education opportunities while maintaining basic academic standards.</p>', '<p data-start=\"231\" data-end=\"656\">The Online BA programme in History, Economics, and Political Science follows a structured and transparent fee system spread across the academic duration. It includes registration, examination, and tuition components, ensuring students clearly understand the total financial requirement before admission. The fee remains stable across years, making it easier for students to plan their education without financial uncertainty.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"658\" data-end=\"682\">Detailed Fee Structure</p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"1005\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"741\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"741\">\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"700\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Fee Component</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"700\" data-end=\"713\" data-col-size=\"sm\">First Year</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"713\" data-end=\"727\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Second Year</th>\r\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" data-start=\"727\" data-end=\"741\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Third Year</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"800\" data-end=\"1005\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"800\" data-end=\"840\">\r\n<td data-start=\"800\" data-end=\"819\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"819\" data-end=\"831\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 1,000</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"831\" data-end=\"835\" data-col-size=\"sm\">&ndash;</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"835\" data-end=\"840\" data-col-size=\"sm\">&ndash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"896\">\r\n<td data-start=\"841\" data-end=\"859\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Examination Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"859\" data-end=\"871\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 2,000</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"883\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 2,000</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"883\" data-end=\"896\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 2,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"948\">\r\n<td data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"911\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"911\" data-end=\"923\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 5,250</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"923\" data-end=\"935\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 5,250</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"935\" data-end=\"948\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 5,250</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"1005\">\r\n<td data-start=\"949\" data-end=\"968\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Total Annual Fee</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"968\" data-end=\"980\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 8,250</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"980\" data-end=\"992\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 7,250</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1005\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Rs. 7,250</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p data-start=\"1007\" data-end=\"1281\">Total Programme Fee<br data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1029\">The <strong>total cost</strong> of the complete programme is Rs. <strong>22,750</strong>, which covers all three academic years including tuition and examination charges. This makes the programme financially accessible while maintaining academic quality and structured learning support.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1283\" data-end=\"1613\">Fee Structure Explained<br data-start=\"1306\" data-end=\"1309\">The fee system is designed to be simple and predictable. A one-time registration fee is charged at the time of admission, while examination fees are applicable each year for assessment purposes. The tuition fee remains constant throughout the course duration, ensuring financial consistency for students.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1615\" data-end=\"1782\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Overall, the structure provides clarity, affordability, and stability, allowing learners to focus on their studies without worrying about unexpected financial changes.</p>', 'Medium', '<p data-start=\"30\" data-end=\"514\">The programme is structured across six semesters and is designed to build a strong academic foundation in humanities, social sciences, economics, political studies, communication skills, and computer fundamentals. The curriculum follows a progressive learning approach, starting with basic foundation subjects and gradually moving toward advanced and specialized areas of study. This ensures that students develop both conceptual clarity and analytical thinking throughout the course.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"516\" data-end=\"549\">Semester-wise Program Structure</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"551\" data-end=\"563\">Semester I</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"564\" data-end=\"690\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11iesgc\" data-start=\"564\" data-end=\"583\">General English</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pwfqqc\" data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"637\">Telugu / Hindi / Sanskrit / Communicative English</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nnm7a2\" data-start=\"638\" data-end=\"660\">Contemporary India</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f97gh3\" data-start=\"661\" data-end=\"690\">Introduction to Computers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"692\" data-end=\"705\">Semester II</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"706\" data-end=\"854\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1wh25nd\" data-start=\"706\" data-end=\"750\">History &amp; Culture of India up to 1526 AD</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jnfj1x\" data-start=\"751\" data-end=\"796\">History &amp; Culture of India (1526 to 1950)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ka3ham\" data-start=\"797\" data-end=\"834\">Introduction to Political Science</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gkconi\" data-start=\"835\" data-end=\"854\">Micro Economics</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"870\">Semester III</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"1012\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11iesgc\" data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"890\">General English</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1sqodde\" data-start=\"891\" data-end=\"945\">Telugu / Hindi / Sanskrit / Business Communication</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1taqm84\" data-start=\"946\" data-end=\"986\">Science and Technology &amp; Development</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"g9d8hl\" data-start=\"987\" data-end=\"1012\">Environmental Studies</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1014\" data-end=\"1027\">Semester IV</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1130\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1gtwb8n\" data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1054\">Macroeconomic Analysis</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1lakp9t\" data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1089\">Basic Organs of the Government</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"i04who\" data-start=\"1090\" data-end=\"1111\">Political Thought</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"87tpkh\" data-start=\"1112\" data-end=\"1130\">Indian Economy</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1144\">Semester V</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1145\" data-end=\"1358\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1x1dz4a\" data-start=\"1145\" data-end=\"1205\">History &amp; Culture of Andhra (1512 to 1956 AD) &ndash; Part One</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"19shzrg\" data-start=\"1206\" data-end=\"1263\">Public Finance and International Economics &ndash; Part One</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"uwpvxg\" data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1298\">Indian Government and Politics</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pugj7y\" data-start=\"1299\" data-end=\"1358\">History of Modern World (1453 AD to 1945 AD) &ndash; Part One</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1373\">Semester VI</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1598\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1xmotpe\" data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1434\">History &amp; Culture of Andhra (1512 to 1956 AD) &ndash; Part Two</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1aaz9gk\" data-start=\"1435\" data-end=\"1492\">Public Finance and International Economics &ndash; Part Two</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"e2vbz5\" data-start=\"1493\" data-end=\"1538\">Government and Politics of Andhra Pradesh</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qa4812\" data-start=\"1539\" data-end=\"1598\">History of Modern World (1453 AD to 1945 AD) &ndash; Part Two</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1600\" data-end=\"2007\">Program Overview Explained<br data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1629\">This programme offers a well-structured academic journey that integrates language development, historical studies, political science, economics, and environmental awareness. In the initial phase, students are introduced to foundational subjects that strengthen communication skills, basic computing knowledge, and an understanding of contemporary social and historical contexts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2009\" data-end=\"2295\">As the course progresses, students move toward more analytical subjects such as macroeconomic analysis, political theory, governance systems, and economic development. These subjects help in developing a deeper understanding of how societies function at both national and global levels.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2297\" data-end=\"2574\">In the later stage of the programme, students engage with advanced topics related to regional history, public finance, international economics, and modern world developments. This stage enhances critical thinking and provides broader exposure to political and economic systems.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2576\" data-end=\"2817\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">Overall, the programme structure is designed to create a balanced academic foundation that supports higher studies, competitive examinations, and diverse career opportunities in administration, education, research, and public policy domains.</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 22750.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
