er_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(468, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 340, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 00:50:32', '2026-06-01 00:50:32', NULL, 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy Eligibility Criteria&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is designed for students and professionals who aspire to build expertise in <strong>international relations, foreign policy, diplomacy, strategic studies, security studies, geopolitical analysis, conflict resolution, intelligence assessment, and global governance</strong>. The program welcomes applicants from diverse academic backgrounds, recognizing that contemporary global challenges require interdisciplinary perspectives and analytical thinking.</p>\r\n<p>Whether you are interested in diplomacy, international organizations, policy research, defense and security analysis, strategic consulting, or public affairs, the program provides a strong academic foundation for understanding the complex dynamics shaping world politics and international security.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.A. International Relations, Security and Strategy</h2>\r\n<p>To apply for admission to the OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy program, candidates must meet the following requirements:</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants must hold an <strong>undergraduate degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university in India or abroad.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Students from Humanities, Social Sciences, Commerce, Management, Science, Engineering, Law, Journalism, and other academic backgrounds are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>The program encourages applications from candidates with a strong interest in international affairs, diplomacy, public policy, strategic studies, and global security.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must submit valid identification documents during the admission process:</p>\r\n<p><strong>For Indian Applicants</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Aadhaar Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>PAN Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Voter ID Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Any other government-issued identity proof as accepted by the university</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>For International Applicants</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Process</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the program follows a holistic review process that evaluates both academic credentials and the applicant\'s ability to engage with contemporary international issues.</p>\r\n<h3>Document Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions committee conducts a comprehensive review of the applicant\'s academic records, supporting documents, and overall profile. This evaluation helps assess the candidate\'s academic preparedness, intellectual curiosity, and potential for success in a rigorous postgraduate environment.</p>\r\n<h3>Short Essay Requirement</h3>\r\n<p>As part of the selection process, applicants are required to submit a short essay addressing the following topic:</p>\r\n<p><strong>\"How has a major global event shaped your understanding of international relations and influenced your career goals? How will the M.A. in International Relations, Security, and Strategy programme help you achieve these goals?\"</strong></p>\r\n<p>The essay serves as an opportunity for candidates to demonstrate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of global affairs and international developments</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analytical and critical thinking abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in diplomacy, foreign policy, or security studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication and academic writing skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Long-term career objectives</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Motivation for pursuing the program</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility and Selection Criteria Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Minimum Qualification</td>\r\n<td>Undergraduate Degree in Any Discipline</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Eligible Academic Backgrounds</td>\r\n<td>All Streams</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Indian Applicant Requirement</td>\r\n<td>Government-Issued ID Proof</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>International Applicant Requirement</td>\r\n<td>Valid Passport</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Selection Method</td>\r\n<td>Document Review</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Additional Requirement</td>\r\n<td>Short Essay Submission</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Admission Basis</td>\r\n<td>Academic Profile and Essay Evaluation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The <strong>OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy eligibility criteria</strong> are designed to attract motivated learners who are passionate about global affairs, diplomacy, security studies, strategic analysis, and international policy. Through a profile-based admission process and a future-focused curriculum, the program offers an excellent pathway for students seeking careers in international relations, foreign policy, global security, and strategic leadership.</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for students seeking careers in <strong>international relations, diplomacy, foreign policy, security studies, strategic affairs, intelligence analysis, geopolitical risk assessment, conflict resolution, and global governance</strong>. The program combines academic rigor with practical insights into contemporary international challenges, helping students develop the analytical and strategic skills required in today\'s interconnected world.</p>\r\n<p>For students evaluating postgraduate education options, understanding the fee structure is an important step in assessing the overall academic value, career opportunities, and long-term return on investment offered by the program.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. International Relations, Security and Strategy Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹50,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 February 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹3,00,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Fee Overview</h3>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹3,00,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹50,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Option</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based Fee Structure</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Areas</td>\r\n<td>International Relations, Security Studies, Diplomacy, Strategic Affairs &amp; Global Governance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the Fee Cover?</h2>\r\n<p>The fee supports a comprehensive learning experience that combines international relations theory with practical training in diplomacy, security analysis, foreign policy, intelligence studies, and conflict management. Students gain exposure to some of the most relevant issues shaping contemporary global politics and international security.</p>\r\n<p>Major academic areas covered within the program include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Relations Theory</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Diplomatic Practices and Negotiation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Foreign Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Intelligence and Strategic Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Terrorism and Counterterrorism</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Maritime Security and Naval Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Geopolitical Risk Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Law and Ethics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Conflict Resolution and Peacebuilding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Security and Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Decision-Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research and Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in International Relations, Security and Strategy Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Master of Arts (M.A.) in International Relations, Security and Strategy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for students interested in global affairs, diplomacy, national security, strategic studies, foreign policy, intelligence analysis, conflict resolution, and international governance. The program provides an interdisciplinary understanding of the political, military, economic, and strategic factors shaping the contemporary international system.</p>\r\n<p>With growing demand for professionals in <strong>international relations, foreign policy analysis, security studies, geopolitical risk assessment, strategic intelligence, diplomacy, and global governance</strong>, this program equips students with both theoretical knowledge and practical analytical skills required to navigate complex global challenges.</p>\r\n<p>Unlike traditional political science programs, the curriculum combines international relations theory with real-world security issues, intelligence studies, maritime strategy, terrorism studies, conflict management, and strategic decision-making, preparing graduates for careers in government, international organizations, think tanks, research institutions, consulting firms, and security-focused industries.</p>\r\n<h2>M.A. International Relations, Security and Strategy Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum is divided into four terms, gradually moving from foundational concepts of international relations to advanced security studies, strategic analysis, intelligence assessment, and specialized pathways through either a dissertation or elective-based track.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 1: Foundations of International Relations and Security Studies</h2>\r\n<p>The first term establishes a strong foundation in international affairs, diplomatic engagement, intelligence operations, and strategic thinking. Students learn how states interact, how foreign policy decisions are shaped, and how security challenges influence global politics.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>International Relations Theory</td>\r\n<td>Major theories, global power structures, international systems, and state behavior</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Diplomatic Practices</td>\r\n<td>Diplomacy, negotiations, international communication, and diplomatic institutions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Intelligence, War and Weapons</td>\r\n<td>Intelligence systems, military strategy, warfare studies, and security dynamics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Key Skills Developed</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Relations Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Diplomatic Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Security Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Geopolitical Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Intelligence Awareness</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 2: Foreign Policy, Security Threats and Maritime Strategy</h2>\r\n<p>The second term focuses on the strategic decisions of major and emerging powers while examining contemporary security challenges affecting international stability.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Foreign Policies of Great, Middle and Small Powers</td>\r\n<td>Comparative foreign policy analysis and strategic decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Terrorism, Counterterrorism and Unconventional Threats</td>\r\n<td>Terrorism studies, security responses, insurgency, and emerging threats</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Maritime Security and Naval Strategy</td>\r\n<td>Naval power, maritime disputes, sea routes, and Indo-Pacific security</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Key Skills Developed</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Foreign Policy Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Counterterrorism Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Maritime Security Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Risk Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>National Security Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Threat Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 3: Intelligence, Ethics and Conflict Resolution</h2>\r\n<p>The third term develops advanced analytical skills required to assess security risks, understand international legal frameworks, and manage conflicts between states and non-state actors.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Intelligence Analysis and Risk Assessment</td>\r\n<td>Intelligence gathering, strategic forecasting, and geopolitical risk evaluation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Law and Ethics in International Relations</td>\r\n<td>International law, ethics, global norms, and governance frameworks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Negotiating and Resolving International Conflicts</td>\r\n<td>Conflict management, peacebuilding, mediation, and negotiation strategies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Key Skills Developed</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Intelligence Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Risk Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Conflict Resolution</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Forecasting</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Law Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Negotiation and Mediation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 4: Specialization Pathways</h2>\r\n<p>In the final term, students can choose between two academic pathways based on their career goals and interests.</p>\r\n<h3>Pathway 1: Dissertation Track</h3>\r\n<p>Students interested in research, policy analysis, academia, or doctoral studies can pursue an independent dissertation under faculty supervision.</p>\r\n<p>The dissertation pathway includes:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research Thinking, Methodology and Design</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Independent Research Project</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Advanced Policy and Security Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic Writing and Research Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Dissertation Eligibility Criteria</h3>\r\n<p>To pursue the dissertation pathway, students must meet specific academic requirements:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Maintain the required academic performance after the first semester.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Demonstrate consistent academic progress throughout the program.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Successfully meet all university requirements for dissertation eligibility.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Students with pending academic deficiencies may not be eligible for the dissertation track.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The dissertation option is ideal for students planning careers in policy research, think tanks, academia, strategic studies, and international affairs research.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3>Pathway 2: Elective-Based Track</h3>\r\n<p>Students choosing the non-dissertation pathway can specialize through a selection of advanced electives aligned with contemporary global challenges and security issues.</p>\r\n<h3>Available Electives</h3>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Elective Courses</th>\r\n<th>Focus Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Domestic Politics and their Impact on Foreign Policy</td>\r\n<td>Political systems and foreign policy behavior</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Nuclear, Space and Cyber Security</td>\r\n<td>Emerging domains of strategic competition</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Climate Change, Migration and Human Security</td>\r\n<td>Environmental security and humanitarian challenges</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Military Conflict and Deterrence in the 21st Century</td>\r\n<td>Modern warfare and strategic deterrence</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>The China-US New Cold War and the Indo-Pacific</td>\r\n<td>Great power rivalry and regional security</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Multilateral Institutions and Global Security</td>\r\n<td>International organizations and global governance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>India\'s Rise in World Affairs</td>\r\n<td>India\'s strategic role in global politics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Statistical Methods and Data Analysis</td>\r\n<td>Quantitative research and policy analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Democratic Governance</td>\r\n<td>Governance systems and political institutions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>These electives allow students to customize their learning experience based on specific interests within international relations, security studies, strategic affairs, and public policy.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 300000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(469, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 216, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 01:04:38', '2026-06-01 01:04:38', NULL, 1, '<h2>Online MBA in Business Analytics Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online MBA in Business Analytics</strong> is designed for graduates and working professionals who want to develop expertise in <strong>Business Analytics, Data Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, Business Intelligence, Data Visualization, Digital Transformation, and Strategic Decision-Making</strong>. The program combines management education with modern analytical tools, preparing learners for leadership roles in today\'s data-driven business environment.</p>\r\n<p>Whether you are a recent graduate looking to build a career in analytics or a professional aiming to upskill in business intelligence and AI-powered decision-making, the program provides a strong foundation for career growth across multiple industries.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for Online MBA in Business Analytics</h2>\r\n<p>To apply for admission, candidates must satisfy the following eligibility requirements:</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants must hold a <strong>Bachelor\'s degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>A minimum <strong>50% aggregate score in graduation</strong> is required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Candidates from Commerce, Management, Engineering, Science, Arts, Computer Applications, Economics, Statistics, and other academic backgrounds are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The multidisciplinary nature of Business Analytics allows students from diverse educational streams to successfully pursue the program and build careers in analytics, consulting, technology, finance, marketing, and operations.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit valid identity documents as part of the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<p>Candidates must provide:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Aadhaar Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>One additional Government-Issued ID Proof such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>PAN Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Voter ID Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Driving License</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passport</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and admission processing.</p>\r\n<h2>Selection Criteria for Online MBA in Business Analytics</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the program is based on a profile-based evaluation process designed to assess the applicant\'s academic qualifications and professional background.</p>\r\n<h3>Document Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions team evaluates all documents submitted by applicants, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic qualifications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduation records</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Identity documents</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professional credentials, where applicable</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The document review helps assess academic preparedness and suitability for a postgraduate business analytics program.</p>\r\n<h3>Relevant Work Experience</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates with relevant professional experience may strengthen their application profile.</p>\r\n<p>Work experience in areas such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Information Technology</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Banking and Finance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Marketing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Operations Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Consulting</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Project Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Intelligence</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Transformation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>can provide valuable practical perspectives that enhance classroom learning and peer collaboration.</p>\r\n<h2>Who Should Apply for an Online MBA in Business Analytics?</h2>\r\n<p>This program is ideal for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Fresh graduates seeking careers in analytics and business intelligence.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Working professionals looking to transition into data-driven roles.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Managers who want to improve decision-making using analytics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>IT professionals aiming to move into business leadership positions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Entrepreneurs seeking to leverage data for business growth.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professionals interested in Artificial Intelligence and Digital Transformation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is specifically designed to help learners understand how businesses use data, analytics, and emerging technologies to improve performance and gain competitive advantages.</p>\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n<h2>Eligibility &amp; Selection Criteria Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Program Name</td>\r\n<td>Online MBA in Business Analytics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Minimum Qualification</td>\r\n<td>Bachelor\'s Degree in Any Discipline</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Minimum Marks Required</td>\r\n<td>50% Aggregate in Graduation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Eligible Academic Streams</td>\r\n<td>All Disciplines</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Indian Applicant Requirement</td>\r\n<td>Aadhaar Card + One Additional Government-Issued ID Proof</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>International Applicant Requirement</td>\r\n<td>Valid Passport</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Selection Process</td>\r\n<td>Document Review</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Additional Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Relevant Work Experience</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Admission Basis</td>\r\n<td>Academic Profile and Professional Background</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online MBA in Business Analytics eligibility criteria</strong> are designed to identify motivated learners who want to build expertise in analytics, artificial intelligence, business intelligence, and strategic management. Through its flexible admission requirements and industry-focused curriculum, the program provides an excellent pathway for professionals and graduates seeking high-growth careers in the analytics and digital business ecosystem.</p>', '<h2>Online MBA in Business Analytics Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online MBA in Business Analytics</strong> is a future-focused management program designed for professionals and graduates who want to build expertise in <strong>Business Analytics, Data Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, Business Intelligence, Data Visualization, Digital Transformation, Predictive Analytics, and Strategic Decision-Making</strong>. As organizations increasingly rely on data-driven strategies, the demand for professionals with analytical and managerial capabilities continues to grow across industries.</p>\r\n<p>Understanding the fee structure is an important step for students evaluating the affordability, flexibility, and long-term value of an Online MBA. The program offers a structured payment plan that allows learners to invest in advanced business and analytics education while managing their financial commitments effectively.</p>\r\n<h2>Online MBA in Business Analytics Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹75,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,00,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 November 2026</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Program Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,00,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Program Name</td>\r\n<td>Online MBA in Business Analytics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Program Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,00,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Flexible Payment Option</td>\r\n<td>Available</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Mode</td>\r\n<td>Online</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Specialization</td>\r\n<td>Business Analytics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>2 Years</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the Online MBA in Business Analytics Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The program fee supports a comprehensive learning experience that combines business management education with advanced analytics and emerging technologies. Students gain access to a curriculum designed to develop expertise in both managerial decision-making and data-driven business strategy.</p>\r\n<p>Major learning areas include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Artificial Intelligence</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Generative AI for Business</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Intelligence</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Visualization</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Financial Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Marketing Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Predictive and Prescriptive Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Business Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Operations and Supply Chain Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is aligned with current industry requirements and focuses on practical applications of analytics in business environments.</p>\r\n<h2>Online MBA in Business Analytics Fee Summary</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Program Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,00,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,00,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Mode</td>\r\n<td>Online</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Program Duration</td>\r\n<td>2 Years</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Specialization</td>\r\n<td>Business Analytics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Core Learning Areas</td>\r\n<td>Business Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, Data Analytics, Business Intelligence</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Career Domains</td>\r\n<td>Analytics, Consulting, Technology, Finance, Marketing, Operations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>For students seeking a management degree that combines <strong>business strategy, analytics, artificial intelligence, data visualization, and digital transformation</strong>, the <strong>Online MBA in Business Analytics</strong> offers a strong balance of academic value, industry relevance, and career advancement potential, making it a worthwhile investment for future-focused professionals.</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>Online MBA in Business Analytics Syllabus &amp; Curriculum</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online MBA in Business Analytics</strong> is designed for professionals and graduates who want to develop expertise in both <strong>business management and data-driven decision-making</strong>. The curriculum combines core management subjects with advanced analytics, artificial intelligence, data visualization, business intelligence, and emerging digital technologies to prepare students for leadership roles in the modern business environment.</p>\r\n<p>What makes this program particularly relevant in today\'s market is its focus on <strong>Business Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, Generative AI, Data Analytics, Predictive Modeling, and Digital Transformation</strong>. Students learn how to convert business data into actionable insights, improve strategic decision-making, and drive organizational growth through analytics.</p>\r\n<p>A major highlight of the curriculum is the inclusion of innovative AI-focused courses such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Generative AI for Business Strategy &amp; Innovation</strong> &ndash; Learn how AI can be used to generate business insights, create intelligent dashboards, automate reporting, and support strategic decision-making.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>AI Tools for Decision-Making and Productivity</strong> &ndash; Explore practical AI tools that improve business productivity, streamline workflows, and enhance managerial efficiency.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The program follows a progressive learning approach, beginning with business fundamentals and gradually advancing toward analytics, artificial intelligence, and strategic business leadership.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 1: Building Foundations in Business and Analytics</h2>\r\n<p>The first term introduces students to core business concepts while establishing a strong foundation in analytical thinking and data-driven decision-making.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Course</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Business Economics</td>\r\n<td>Economic principles, market behavior, business environment, and strategic decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Marketing Management</td>\r\n<td>Consumer behavior, branding, marketing strategies, and customer value creation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Introduction to Business Analytics using R</td>\r\n<td>Data analysis fundamentals, analytics tools, and business applications using R</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Statistical Methods for Decision Making</td>\r\n<td>Business statistics, forecasting, probability, and quantitative decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Business Communication (Experiential Learning)</td>\r\n<td>Professional communication, leadership communication, presentations, and workplace collaboration</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Statistical Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Marketing Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Decision-Making Frameworks</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 2: Business Intelligence and Data Visualization</h2>\r\n<p>The second term focuses on financial understanding, operational excellence, and business intelligence tools that help organizations make informed strategic decisions.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Course</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Financial Accounting</td>\r\n<td>Financial statements, accounting principles, and financial reporting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Operations &amp; Supply Chain Management</td>\r\n<td>Supply chain optimization, operational efficiency, and process management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Data Visualization</td>\r\n<td>Dashboard creation, storytelling with data, and business reporting</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Business Decision Modeling with Spreadsheets</td>\r\n<td>Business forecasting, scenario analysis, and data-driven planning</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Design Thinking</td>\r\n<td>Innovation, problem-solving, user-centric business solutions, and creative thinking</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Intelligence</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Visualization</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Financial Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Operational Planning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Problem Solving</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 3: Advanced Analytics and Artificial Intelligence</h2>\r\n<p>The third term introduces advanced analytical techniques and emerging technologies that are transforming modern businesses. Students learn how organizations use AI, predictive analytics, and digital technologies to gain competitive advantages.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Course</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Managing People &amp; Organizations</td>\r\n<td>Leadership, organizational behavior, talent management, and team performance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Financial Management</td>\r\n<td>Investment decisions, capital budgeting, risk-return analysis, and financial strategy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Prescriptive Analytics</td>\r\n<td>Optimization techniques, decision modeling, and business recommendations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Text Analytics</td>\r\n<td>Natural language processing, sentiment analysis, and unstructured data analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Emerging Technologies &amp; Digital Business</td>\r\n<td>Digital transformation, innovation, and technology-driven business models</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Artificial Intelligence</td>\r\n<td>AI applications in business, machine learning concepts, and intelligent decision systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 3</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Artificial Intelligence for Business</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Predictive and Prescriptive Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Business Forecasting</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Transformation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Leadership</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data-Driven Decision Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Key Highlights of the Online MBA in Business Analytics Curriculum</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Industry-focused Online MBA with specialization in Business Analytics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strong blend of management education and analytical skills.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Hands-on exposure to business intelligence and data visualization tools.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Dedicated courses in Artificial Intelligence and Digital Business.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Generative AI and AI productivity tools integrated into the curriculum.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Focus on predictive, prescriptive, and text analytics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Practical learning through experiential business communication modules.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Curriculum aligned with current industry demand for analytics professionals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Suitable for professionals seeking careers in data-driven leadership roles.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 200000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
