(470, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 341, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 01:19:56', '2026-06-01 01:19:56', NULL, 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is designed for students and professionals who want to build expertise in <strong>global health, public health, healthcare policy, epidemiology, health equity, international development, health program management, and sustainable development</strong>. The program welcomes applicants from diverse academic backgrounds who are passionate about addressing contemporary health and development challenges at local, national, and global levels.</p>\r\n<p>With growing demand for professionals in public health organizations, international development agencies, NGOs, healthcare institutions, policy think tanks, and global research organizations, the program provides a strong foundation for students seeking impactful careers in the health and development sector.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development</h2>\r\n<p>To apply for admission to the OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development program, candidates must meet the following eligibility requirements:</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants must hold a <strong>Bachelor&rsquo;s degree from a recognized university</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from any academic discipline are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Students from Science, Arts, Commerce, Management, Social Sciences, Public Policy, Healthcare, Nursing, Pharmacy, Life Sciences, Engineering, and related fields are encouraged to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The multidisciplinary nature of global health and human development allows students from varied educational backgrounds to contribute diverse perspectives while developing expertise in health systems, policy, and development practices.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to provide valid identification documents during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and admission processing.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Process</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development program follows a comprehensive evaluation process designed to assess academic preparedness, professional potential, leadership qualities, and commitment to global health and development.</p>\r\n<h3>Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit a Statement of Purpose outlining:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic background and achievements</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in global health and human development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career goals and professional aspirations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Motivation for pursuing the program</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Reasons for choosing OP Jindal University</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Areas of interest within public health, healthcare policy, development studies, or global governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A well-written SOP helps the admissions committee understand the applicant\'s passion, vision, and commitment to making a positive impact in the health and development sector.</p>\r\n<h3>Curriculum Vitae (CV)</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates must submit an updated Curriculum Vitae (CV) highlighting:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Educational qualifications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research experience</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Internships and projects</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professional experience</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Leadership activities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Volunteering and community engagement</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Relevant certifications and achievements</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The CV provides a comprehensive overview of the applicant\'s academic and professional journey.</p>\r\n<h3>Aptitude Test</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are also assessed through an Aptitude Test designed to evaluate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analytical thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Problem-solving abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Quantitative reasoning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Critical thinking capabilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic readiness for postgraduate study</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The aptitude assessment helps identify candidates who can successfully engage with the interdisciplinary and research-oriented curriculum.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a multidisciplinary postgraduate program designed for students who want to build expertise in <strong>global health, public health, epidemiology, healthcare policy, health equity, international development, program management, and sustainable development</strong>. The program combines academic rigor with practical learning to prepare graduates for leadership and research roles in healthcare, development organizations, NGOs, policy institutions, and international agencies.</p>\r\n<p>As global health challenges continue to evolve, there is increasing demand for professionals who can understand healthcare systems, design effective interventions, analyze health policies, and contribute to sustainable human development. The program\'s fee structure reflects its specialized curriculum, research-driven learning approach, and global perspective on health and development.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. Global Health and Human Development Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 January 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,75,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Focus</td>\r\n<td>Global Health, Public Health, Human Development &amp; Health Policy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the M.Sc. Global Health and Human Development Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports an advanced academic experience that combines public health knowledge with development studies, healthcare governance, epidemiology, and policy analysis. Students gain exposure to contemporary global health challenges while developing research, analytical, and leadership skills.</p>\r\n<p>Major learning areas covered in the program include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Health and Human Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Epidemiology and Biostatistics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Health Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Health Equity and Social Determinants of Health</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Health Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Healthcare Policy and Systems</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Program Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Burden of Diseases</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Health Ethics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Planetary Health</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Dissertation or Capstone Research Project</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to address real-world health and development challenges through an interdisciplinary and globally relevant approach.</p>\r\n<h2>Why Students Choose OP Jindal University for Global Health Studies</h2>\r\n<p>The OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development stands out because of its unique integration of <strong>global health, public health, healthcare systems, development studies, health governance, sustainability, and research</strong>. The curriculum is designed to help students understand the interconnected factors that influence health outcomes at local, national, and global levels.</p>\r\n<p>By combining theoretical knowledge with practical research and policy analysis, the program prepares graduates to contribute meaningfully to healthcare improvement, development initiatives, and evidence-based policymaking.</p>\r\n<p>.</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Global Health and Human Development</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is an interdisciplinary postgraduate program designed to address some of the most pressing health and development challenges facing societies worldwide. The curriculum combines public health, global health policy, epidemiology, health equity, healthcare systems, program management, research methods, and sustainable development to prepare students for impactful careers in the health and development sector.</p>\r\n<p>As global challenges such as pandemics, health inequities, climate change, migration, healthcare accessibility, and sustainable development continue to shape public policy, there is a growing demand for professionals who can understand the complex relationship between health, human development, governance, and social systems. This program equips students with the analytical, research, and leadership skills needed to contribute to global health initiatives, international development programs, public health organizations, NGOs, and policy institutions.</p>\r\n<p>Unlike traditional public health programs, the curriculum integrates <strong>Global Health Governance, Health Equity, Epidemiology, Program Management, Planetary Health, Globalization of Healthcare, and Development Studies</strong>, providing students with a broader understanding of health challenges from both local and global perspectives.</p>\r\n<h2>M.Sc. Global Health and Human Development Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum follows a trimester-based structure that gradually builds expertise in public health foundations, health policy, research methodologies, healthcare systems, and global development challenges.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 1: Foundations of Global Health and Human Development</h2>\r\n<p>The first trimester introduces students to the fundamental concepts of global health, public health systems, health equity, epidemiology, and international health governance. Students develop a strong understanding of how health outcomes are influenced by social, economic, environmental, and political factors.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Foundations in Global Health and Human Development</td>\r\n<td>Core concepts of public health, global development, and health systems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Basics of Epidemiology and Biostatistics</td>\r\n<td>Disease patterns, population health analysis, and health data interpretation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Social Determinants of Health Equity</td>\r\n<td>Social, economic, and environmental factors affecting health outcomes</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Global Health Governance</td>\r\n<td>International health organizations, global health policies, and governance frameworks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Health Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Epidemiological Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Health Data Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Health Policy Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Health Awareness</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Evidence-Based Decision Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 2: Public Health Research and Program Management</h2>\r\n<p>The second trimester focuses on research methodologies, disease burden analysis, health program implementation, and ethical challenges within global health systems. Students gain practical knowledge of how public health interventions are designed, managed, and evaluated.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Research Methods</td>\r\n<td>Quantitative and qualitative research techniques, data collection, and analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Global Burden of Diseases</td>\r\n<td>Disease trends, global health challenges, and population health priorities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Program Management</td>\r\n<td>Planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of health programs</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Decolonizing Global Health and Global Health Ethics</td>\r\n<td>Ethical frameworks, equity issues, and inclusive approaches to global health</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Health Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Program Planning and Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Health Project Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Ethical Decision Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Health Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 3: Planetary Health, Global Health Systems, and Applied Research</h2>\r\n<p>The final trimester explores the impact of globalization and environmental change on health systems while providing students with an opportunity to apply their learning through a dissertation or capstone project.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Planetary Health</td>\r\n<td>Climate change, environmental sustainability, and their impact on human health</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Globalization of Health and Health Care</td>\r\n<td>Global healthcare systems, international health policies, and cross-border health challenges</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dissertation/Capstone</td>\r\n<td>Independent research project addressing a real-world global health or development issue</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Dissertation and Capstone Experience</h3>\r\n<p>The dissertation or capstone project enables students to apply theoretical knowledge to practical health and development challenges. Under faculty guidance, students conduct research, evaluate policies, and propose solutions to contemporary public health issues.</p>\r\n<p>This hands-on academic experience strengthens analytical, research, and policy-making capabilities while preparing students for professional and academic advancement.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 275000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(471, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 342, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 01:39:28', '2026-06-01 01:39:28', NULL, 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in India Studies Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.A. in India Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a distinctive interdisciplinary postgraduate program designed for students who wish to explore India\'s history, civilization, culture, philosophy, politics, society, international relations, and global influence through an academic and research-oriented lens. The program welcomes learners from diverse educational backgrounds who are interested in understanding India\'s evolving role in the twenty-first century and its growing significance in global affairs.</p>\r\n<p>As interest in <strong>India Studies, Indian Civilization, Indian Culture, Indian Philosophy, South Asian Studies, Public Policy, International Relations, and Global India</strong> continues to rise worldwide, the program offers a unique opportunity to develop specialized knowledge and analytical skills that are increasingly valued across academia, policy institutions, think tanks, cultural organizations, and international organizations.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.A. in India Studies</h2>\r\n<p>Applicants seeking admission to the OP Jindal University M.A. in India Studies program must meet the following eligibility requirements:</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Candidates must possess a <strong>Bachelor\'s degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from Arts, Humanities, Commerce, Science, Management, Engineering, Law, Social Sciences, Media, and other academic streams are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>The program encourages applications from individuals interested in Indian history, culture, society, governance, philosophy, diplomacy, and public affairs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The multidisciplinary nature of India Studies ensures that students from varied educational backgrounds can successfully engage with the curriculum and contribute diverse perspectives to classroom discussions.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit valid identification documents during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<p>Any one of the following Government-Issued ID Proofs:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Aadhaar Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>PAN Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Voter ID Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and admission processing.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Process</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the M.A. in India Studies program follows a holistic evaluation process that assesses a candidate\'s academic preparedness, intellectual curiosity, research potential, and interest in India\'s civilizational and contemporary development.</p>\r\n<h3>Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit a <strong>Statement of Purpose (500&ndash;700 words)</strong> as part of the admission process.</p>\r\n<p>The SOP should address the following questions:</p>\r\n<h3>Question 1</h3>\r\n<p><strong>What aspect of India\'s history, culture, or philosophy inspires you the most, and why?</strong></p>\r\n<p>This question helps applicants demonstrate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Intellectual engagement with India\'s civilizational heritage</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of Indian culture and traditions</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Ability to critically reflect on historical and philosophical ideas</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Personal motivations and academic interests</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Question 2</h3>\r\n<p><strong>Which one aspect of India, according to you, has the potential to make a positive impact in shaping the 21st century?</strong></p>\r\n<p>This question allows candidates to showcase:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Awareness of contemporary India</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of global challenges and opportunities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Critical thinking and analytical abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Vision for India\'s future role in the world</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A strong SOP should present thoughtful arguments, demonstrate originality, and clearly connect the applicant\'s interests with the objectives of the India Studies program.</p>\r\n<h3>Document Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions committee conducts a comprehensive review of the submitted documents and academic records. The review process evaluates:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic background and achievements</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Quality of the Statement of Purpose</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Intellectual curiosity and research interests</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication and analytical skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Overall suitability for the program</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This holistic approach ensures that applicants are assessed beyond academic scores alone.</p>\r\n<h3>Rolling Admissions Process</h3>\r\n<p>Applications for the M.A. in India Studies program are accepted on a <strong>rolling basis</strong>. This allows candidates to apply throughout the admission cycle rather than waiting for a single deadline.</p>\r\n<p>Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications early, as seats may be allocated progressively during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h2>What Makes a Strong Applicant?</h2>\r\n<p>The admissions team values candidates who demonstrate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Genuine interest in India and its global significance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Curiosity about Indian history, culture, philosophy, and society</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strong communication and writing skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analytical and critical thinking abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research aptitude</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in interdisciplinary learning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Motivation to contribute to academic, policy, cultural, or development sectors</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Students with a passion for understanding India\'s past, present, and future often find the program particularly rewarding.</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in India Studies Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.A. in India Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a unique interdisciplinary postgraduate program that offers an in-depth exploration of <strong>Indian history, culture, philosophy, politics, society, international relations, strategic thought, and contemporary India</strong>. Designed for students, researchers, policy enthusiasts, and professionals interested in understanding India\'s growing global influence, the program combines academic rigor with practical research and analytical training.</p>\r\n<p>As India continues to play an increasingly important role in global politics, economics, culture, and diplomacy, specialized programs such as India Studies are gaining significant relevance. The fee structure reflects the program\'s multidisciplinary curriculum, research-focused learning approach, and opportunities for intellectual and professional development.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in India Studies Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 January 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,75,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.A. in India Studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Focus</td>\r\n<td>Indian History, Culture, Society, Politics, Philosophy &amp; International Relations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the M.A. India Studies Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports a comprehensive academic experience that enables students to examine India through multiple disciplinary perspectives. The curriculum explores the country\'s civilizational heritage, democratic institutions, cultural traditions, social transformations, strategic thinking, and international engagement.</p>\r\n<p>Key areas of study include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Civilization and History</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Politics and Democracy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Philosophy and Religions</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>India\'s International Relations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Gender, Caste, and Social Justice</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Cinema, Theatre, and Cultural Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Yoga, Mindfulness, and Contemporary Spiritual Traditions</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>India\'s Business, Innovation, Science, and Technology Ecosystem</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Strategic Thought</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Indian Literature and Cultural Narratives</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research Methodology and Academic Writing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Dissertation and Advanced Research Opportunities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The program is designed to provide a holistic understanding of India\'s past, present, and future while developing strong analytical and research capabilities</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in India Studies Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.A. in India Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a unique interdisciplinary postgraduate program that explores India\'s rich civilizational heritage, democratic institutions, philosophy, religion, society, culture, international relations, strategic thought, and economic transformation. Designed for students who want to develop a deeper understanding of India from historical, political, sociological, cultural, and global perspectives, the program combines academic rigor with contemporary relevance.</p>\r\n<p>As India continues to emerge as a major global power, there is increasing interest in understanding its history, governance, culture, diplomacy, business environment, and strategic influence. The curriculum provides students with a comprehensive understanding of India\'s evolution while developing advanced research, analytical, and critical thinking skills.</p>\r\n<p>Unlike traditional history, political science, or cultural studies programs, the M.A. in India Studies integrates multiple disciplines to provide a holistic perspective on India&rsquo;s past, present, and future.</p>\r\n<h2>M.A. India Studies Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum is organized across four terms and gradually builds knowledge of Indian civilization, democracy, society, culture, global engagement, and strategic thinking. Students can further customize their learning through electives or pursue an advanced dissertation pathway.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 1: Understanding India\'s Civilizational Foundations</h2>\r\n<p>The first term introduces students to India\'s historical evolution, philosophical traditions, democratic development, and academic research skills. It provides the intellectual foundation necessary for understanding contemporary India.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Ancient Civilisation, Rising Power: Indian Histories</td>\r\n<td>Evolution of Indian civilization, historical developments, and India\'s journey as a global power</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Understanding the World\'s Largest Democracy: India\'s Domestic Politics since Independence</td>\r\n<td>Indian political institutions, governance systems, electoral politics, and public policy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Between the City and the Forest: The Evolution of Indic Philosophy and Religions</td>\r\n<td>Indian philosophical traditions, religious movements, and intellectual heritage</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Gateway to Writing and Research-I: Mastering Academic Writing Basics</td>\r\n<td>Academic writing, research techniques, critical reading, and scholarly communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Historical Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Political Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Critical Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Writing and Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interpretation of Cultural and Religious Traditions</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 2: Contemporary India and Social Transformation</h2>\r\n<p>The second term examines India\'s role in global affairs while exploring important social, cultural, and academic dimensions that shape modern Indian society.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>India\'s Rise on the Global Stage: An Introduction to its International Relations</td>\r\n<td>Foreign policy, diplomacy, global partnerships, and India\'s international influence</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Understanding Gender, Caste, and Social Justice in Contemporary India: A Sociological Perspective</td>\r\n<td>Social structures, inequality, inclusion, and social change</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>The Stage, the Screen, and All That Drama!: Understanding Theatre, Cinema and Entertainment in India</td>\r\n<td>Indian cinema, performing arts, popular culture, and media studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Gateway to Writing and Research-II: Bridging Disciplines, Theories, and Methods in India Studies</td>\r\n<td>Advanced research methodologies and interdisciplinary approaches</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Why This Term Matters</h3>\r\n<p>Modern India cannot be understood solely through history or politics. Social justice, cultural expression, media influence, and international engagement play critical roles in shaping contemporary Indian society. This term helps students develop a multidimensional understanding of India\'s transformation in the twenty-first century.</p>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Relations Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sociological Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Cultural Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interdisciplinary Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Affairs Awareness</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 3: Spiritual Traditions, Innovation, and Cultural Influence</h2>\r\n<p>The third term explores India\'s living traditions, growing innovation ecosystem, and global cultural influence. Students examine how ancient practices continue to shape contemporary society while understanding India\'s emergence as a major economic and technological power.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Sacred India Alive: Yoga, Mindfulness, Bhakti and the Lived Religions in Contemporary Contexts</td>\r\n<td>Contemporary religious practices, spirituality, yoga, and cultural traditions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>India Innovates: An Introduction to Business, Science, and Technology in the World\'s Fastest-Growing Market</td>\r\n<td>Innovation, entrepreneurship, economic development, science, and technology ecosystems</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Appreciating Indian Music and Dance: Traditions, Evolution, and Global Influence</td>\r\n<td>Indian performing arts, cultural heritage, and global cultural impact</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 3</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Cultural Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Innovation Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Religious and Philosophical Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Heritage Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Global Cultural Awareness</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 4: Specialization and Advanced Research Pathways</h2>\r\n<p>In the final term, students can choose between an elective-based pathway or a dissertation-focused academic track depending on their interests and career goals.</p>\r\n<h3>Pathway 1: Elective-Based Learning</h3>\r\n<p>Students can deepen their understanding of specialized areas within India Studies through advanced elective courses.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Elective Courses</th>\r\n<th>Focus Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>The Great Indian Diaspora: A Global Perspective</td>\r\n<td>Migration, diaspora communities, and India\'s global influence</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>India Through its Literatures: Crossing the Ocean of Stories</td>\r\n<td>Indian literary traditions and cultural narratives</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Karma, Kursi, and Kurukshetra: An Introduction to Indian Strategic Thought</td>\r\n<td>Strategic thinking, statecraft, and Indian geopolitical traditions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Pathway 2: Dissertation and Research Track</h3>\r\n<p>Students interested in academic research, policy studies, doctoral education, or advanced scholarship can pursue a dissertation pathway.</p>\r\n<p>The dissertation track includes:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Dissertation Seminar: An Exploration of Imagination and Voice in Academic Writing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Independent Research Project</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>One Elective from the Available Elective Basket</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This pathway enables students to conduct original research on topics related to Indian society, culture, politics, history, religion, diplomacy, development, or strategic studies.</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 275000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(472, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 343, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 02:04:02', '2026-06-01 02:04:02', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication Admission Process 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The admission process for the <strong>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</strong> is designed to evaluate applicants based on their academic qualifications, professional background, and overall suitability for the program. The process is straightforward and allows students from diverse academic and professional backgrounds to apply.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 1: Complete the Online Application Form</h3>\r\n<p>Visit the university\'s admission portal and fill out the application form with accurate personal, academic, and professional details.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 2: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must submit the necessary documents, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Bachelor\'s degree certificates and academic transcripts</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof (for Indian applicants)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passport (for international applicants)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Recent passport-size photograph</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Any supporting documents related to work experience, if applicable</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Step 3: Profile and Document Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions team reviews the submitted application, academic qualifications, and supporting documents to assess the candidate\'s eligibility and suitability for the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 4: Evaluation of Academic Background and Experience</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are evaluated based on:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Undergraduate academic performance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Educational background</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Relevant professional experience (if applicable)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Overall profile strength</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Candidates with communication, media, marketing, public relations, journalism, branding, or related professional experience may bring additional value to their application.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 5: Admission Decision</h3>\r\n<p>After successful evaluation, eligible candidates receive an admission offer from the university.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 6: Accept the Offer Letter</h3>\r\n<p>Selected candidates must formally accept the admission offer within the specified timeline.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 7: Pay the Registration Fee</h3>\r\n<p>To confirm their seat in the program, candidates are required to pay the registration fee as mentioned in the offer letter.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 8: Complete Enrollment Formalities</h3>\r\n<p>After fee payment and document verification, students complete the enrollment process and gain access to academic resources, orientation details, and program information.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for graduates and professionals who want to build expertise in <strong>strategic communication, corporate communication, public relations, digital media, brand communication, content strategy, media management, marketing communication, and public affairs</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>As organizations increasingly rely on digital communication, reputation management, audience engagement, and data-driven communication strategies, there is a growing demand for professionals who can combine creativity, analytical thinking, and communication leadership. This program provides learners with the knowledge and practical skills required to succeed in today\'s rapidly evolving media and communication landscape.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</h2>\r\n<p>Applicants seeking admission to the OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication program must meet the following eligibility requirements.</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Candidates must hold a <strong>Bachelor&rsquo;s degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants should have secured a minimum of <strong>50% marks in their undergraduate degree</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from Arts, Commerce, Science, Management, Engineering, Journalism, Media Studies, Humanities, Social Sciences, Law, and other academic backgrounds are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The interdisciplinary nature of strategic communication allows students from diverse educational streams to pursue the program and develop specialized expertise in communication strategy and media leadership.</p>\r\n<h3>Professional Experience</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates with <strong>relevant work experience</strong> may also strengthen their application profile.</p>\r\n<p>Professional exposure in areas such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Corporate Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Relations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Marketing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media and Journalism</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Advertising</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Content Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Brand Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Media Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Affairs</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Marketing Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>can provide additional value and practical perspectives during the learning experience.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to provide valid identification documents as part of the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and admission processing.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Criteria</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the M.Sc. in Strategic Communication program is based on academic eligibility and profile evaluation.</p>\r\n<h3>Selection Requirement</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The admissions team reviews academic qualifications and supporting documents to determine the applicant\'s suitability for the program.</p>\r\n<h2>Who Should Apply for the M.Sc. Strategic Communication Program?</h2>\r\n<p>This program is ideal for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Fresh graduates interested in media and communication careers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professionals seeking leadership roles in corporate communication.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public relations and branding professionals looking to upskill.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital marketing specialists aiming to strengthen communication expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Content creators and storytellers interested in strategic communication.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media professionals seeking advanced academic qualifications.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Individuals interested in communication strategy and audience engagement.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to develop strategic thinking, communication leadership, and media management capabilities that are highly valued across industries.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for students and professionals seeking expertise in <strong>strategic communication, corporate communication, public relations, digital media, brand management, content strategy, media analytics, marketing communication, and reputation management</strong>. As organizations increasingly prioritize effective communication and digital engagement, professionals with advanced communication skills are becoming highly valuable across industries.</p>\r\n<p>The program combines communication theory, media strategy, digital storytelling, public affairs, marketing communication, and data-driven audience engagement to prepare graduates for leadership roles in the modern communication ecosystem.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 January 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,75,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Mode</td>\r\n<td>Higher Education Postgraduate Program</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the M.Sc. Strategic Communication Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports an advanced learning experience focused on developing expertise in modern communication practices, digital engagement, audience analysis, and strategic messaging. The curriculum is designed to help students understand how communication influences organizations, brands, governments, and society.</p>\r\n<p>Major learning areas include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Corporate Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Relations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Media Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Marketing Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media Ethics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Big Data and Communication Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Visual Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Multimedia Storytelling</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media Advocacy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Change Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>New Media Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Students also gain opportunities to apply their knowledge through research projects, simulations, capstone projects, or thesis work.</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Strategic Communication Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a future-focused postgraduate program designed for students who want to build expertise in <strong>strategic communication, digital media, corporate communication, public relations, media strategy, content creation, marketing communication, brand storytelling, data-driven communication, and public advocacy</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>In today\'s digital-first world, organizations, governments, businesses, media houses, and non-profit institutions rely heavily on effective communication strategies to engage audiences, shape public opinion, manage brand reputation, and drive meaningful impact. This program equips students with the analytical, creative, and strategic skills required to thrive in the rapidly evolving communication industry.</p>\r\n<p>Unlike traditional mass communication programs, the curriculum combines <strong>strategic communication, media analytics, big data, digital storytelling, social change communication, public discourse, media ethics, marketing strategy, and new media technologies</strong>, ensuring graduates are prepared for leadership roles in modern communication ecosystems.</p>\r\n<h2>M.Sc. Strategic Communication Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to help students understand how communication influences business, society, policy, and culture. Through a blend of theory, practical application, and research, learners gain expertise in crafting effective communication strategies across multiple platforms and audiences.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 1: Foundations of Strategic Communication</h2>\r\n<p>The first trimester introduces students to the principles of strategic communication, media ethics, data interpretation, and visual storytelling. Students learn how communication strategies are developed and how organizations use data and media to influence audiences.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Critical Approaches to Strategic Communication</td>\r\n<td>Strategic communication theories, audience engagement, communication planning, and message design</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Comprehending Big Data</td>\r\n<td>Data-driven communication, analytics, audience insights, and information interpretation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Media Ethics</td>\r\n<td>Ethical decision-making, media responsibility, transparency, and communication standards</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Visual Communication Strategies</td>\r\n<td>Visual storytelling, design thinking, content presentation, and audience impact</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Communication Planning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Visual Storytelling</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Ethical Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Audience Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 2: Media Strategy, Advocacy and Campaign Management</h2>\r\n<p>The second trimester focuses on communication campaigns, multimedia storytelling, public engagement, policy advocacy, and understanding the changing media ecosystem.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Multimedia Storytelling</td>\r\n<td>Cross-platform storytelling, digital content creation, and narrative development</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Marketing Strategies and Campaigning</td>\r\n<td>Brand communication, campaign planning, consumer engagement, and marketing strategy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Media Advocacy in Policy, Public Discourse and Social Change</td>\r\n<td>Public awareness campaigns, advocacy communication, social impact initiatives, and policy engagement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Navigating the Media Landscape</td>\r\n<td>Media industries, emerging platforms, communication trends, and audience behavior</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Why This Trimester Matters</h3>\r\n<p>Organizations today communicate across multiple channels including social media, digital platforms, traditional media, and community networks. This trimester helps students understand how strategic communication can influence public opinion, support organizational goals, and create social impact.</p>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Campaign Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Brand Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Relations Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Content Marketing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Advocacy Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Multimedia Production</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 3: Digital Media, Society and Advanced Communication Practice</h2>\r\n<p>The final trimester explores the relationship between communication, technology, and society while providing students with an opportunity to apply their learning through an advanced research or industry-focused project.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>New Media Communication</td>\r\n<td>Digital platforms, social media communication, online engagement, and emerging communication technologies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Understanding Social Structure</td>\r\n<td>Society, culture, social behavior, and communication within diverse communities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Thesis / Capstone / Simulation</td>\r\n<td>Independent research, communication strategy development, industry simulation, or applied project work</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Thesis, Capstone and Simulation Experience</h3>\r\n<p>The final project component allows students to apply strategic communication concepts to real-world challenges. Depending on their interests, students can pursue:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic research through a thesis.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Industry-oriented problem solving through a capstone project.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Practical communication planning through simulations and case-based learning.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This experience helps students develop advanced analytical, research, and professional communication capabilities.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2>Skills You Will Gain</h2>\r\n<p>Graduates of the program develop expertise in:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Corporate Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Relations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Brand Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Media Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Media Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media Analytics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data-Driven Communication</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Content Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Multimedia Storytelling</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Advocacy and Public Affairs</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Career Scope After M.Sc. in Strategic Communication</h2>\r\n<p>The demand for communication professionals continues to grow across corporate, media, government, consulting, technology, and development sectors.</p>\r\n<h3>Popular Career Opportunities</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strategic Communication Specialist</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Corporate Communication Manager</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Relations Consultant</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Brand Communication Manager</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Digital Marketing Strategist</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Content Strategy Manager</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Media Analyst</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Media Manager</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Affairs Specialist</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication Consultant</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Campaign Manager</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Corporate Reputation Specialist</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 275000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(473, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 344, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 02:16:05', '2026-06-01 02:16:05', '<h2>OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy Admission Process 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The admission process for the <strong>Online M.A. in Public Policy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is designed to identify motivated learners with an interest in <strong>public policy, governance, public administration, economic policy, development studies, public affairs, and policy research</strong>. The process follows a profile-based evaluation approach, ensuring that candidates are assessed on their academic background, written communication skills, and overall suitability for the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 1: Submit the Online Application</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates must complete the online application form by providing their personal, academic, and professional details through the university\'s admission portal.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 2: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to upload the necessary documents for verification, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Bachelor\'s degree certificate and academic transcripts</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof (Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, or Voter ID) for Indian applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passport for international applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Recent passport-size photograph</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Any additional supporting documents, if applicable</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Step 3: Submit the Short Essay</h3>\r\n<p>As part of the admission process, applicants must submit a short essay addressing the prescribed topic related to their career goals and public policy interests.</p>\r\n<p>The essay helps the admissions committee evaluate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of public policy issues</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Critical thinking and analytical abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Written communication skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career aspirations and motivation for the program</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Step 4: Application and Profile Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions team conducts a comprehensive review of:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic qualifications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Submitted documents</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Short essay response</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Overall applicant profile</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This holistic evaluation helps assess the candidate\'s readiness for postgraduate study in public policy and governance.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 5: Admission Decision</h3>\r\n<p>Based on the profile evaluation and essay assessment, eligible candidates are shortlisted and offered admission to the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 6: Receive and Accept the Offer Letter</h3>\r\n<p>Selected applicants receive an official admission offer from the university. Candidates must confirm their acceptance within the specified timeline.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 7: Pay the Registration Fee</h3>\r\n<p>To secure admission, students are required to pay the registration fee as mentioned in the offer letter.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 8: Complete Enrollment Formalities</h3>\r\n<p>After successful fee payment and document verification, candidates complete the enrollment process and gain access to the program, academic resources, and orientation details.</p>\r\n<h2>Admission Process Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Admission Stage</th>\r\n<th>Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Online Application</td>\r\n<td>Submit the application form</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Document Upload</td>\r\n<td>Upload academic and identity documents</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Short Essay Submission</td>\r\n<td>Complete the mandatory essay requirement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Profile Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Review of academic and personal profile</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Admission Decision</td>\r\n<td>Selection based on overall assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Offer Letter Acceptance</td>\r\n<td>Confirm admission offer</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee Payment</td>\r\n<td>Secure seat in the program</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Final Enrollment</td>\r\n<td>Complete admission formalities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The <strong>OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy admission process</strong> is structured to ensure a smooth and transparent admission experience while identifying candidates who demonstrate strong academic potential, policy awareness, and a commitment to contributing to governance, public policy, and social impact initiatives.</p>', 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online M.A. in Public Policy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is designed for graduates, working professionals, policy enthusiasts, development practitioners, government officials, researchers, and aspiring public leaders who want to develop expertise in <strong>public policy, governance, public administration, policy analysis, public affairs, development studies, economics, and evidence-based policymaking</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>As governments, international organizations, think tanks, NGOs, and consulting firms increasingly seek professionals capable of analyzing complex policy challenges and designing effective solutions, the demand for qualified public policy specialists continues to grow. This program provides learners with the academic foundation and analytical skills required to understand, evaluate, and influence policy decisions that shape societies and economies.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for Online M.A. in Public Policy</h2>\r\n<p>Candidates seeking admission to the OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy program must fulfill the following eligibility requirements.</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants must possess an <strong>undergraduate degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university in India or abroad.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from Arts, Commerce, Science, Management, Engineering, Law, Social Sciences, Journalism, Public Administration, Economics, and other academic fields are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>The program welcomes applicants from diverse educational backgrounds who are interested in governance, policy research, public leadership, and social impact.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The interdisciplinary nature of public policy allows students from various academic streams to contribute unique perspectives while developing policy analysis and governance expertise.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must provide valid identification documents during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<p>Any one of the following Government-Issued ID Proofs:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Aadhaar Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>PAN Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Voter ID Card</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and enrollment purposes.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Criteria</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the Online M.A. in Public Policy program follows a holistic profile-based assessment process designed to evaluate the applicant\'s academic readiness, analytical thinking, communication skills, and interest in public policy and governance.</p>\r\n<h3>Short Essay Requirement</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit a short essay addressing the following topic:</p>\r\n<p><strong>\"What are your long-term career goals and aspirations, and how will this degree support you in achieving them? Additionally, given your interest in public policy, briefly describe a policy implemented in your country in the past five years that has had a lasting impact, and explain why you find it significant.\"</strong></p>\r\n<p>This essay plays an important role in the selection process and helps the admissions committee assess the applicant\'s:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of public policy issues</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analytical and critical thinking abilities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Communication and writing skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career aspirations and professional goals</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Awareness of governance and policy developments</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Motivation for pursuing a career in public policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>What Makes a Strong Essay?</h3>\r\n<p>A strong submission typically demonstrates:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Clear career objectives</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Thoughtful understanding of policy challenges</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Ability to evaluate policy outcomes</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Evidence-based reasoning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Awareness of current governance issues</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in public service and policy innovation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strong written communication skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The essay allows applicants to showcase their intellectual curiosity, leadership potential, and commitment to creating positive social impact through policy and governance.</p>\r\n<h2>Who Should Apply for the Online M.A. in Public Policy?</h2>\r\n<p>This program is ideal for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates interested in policy and governance careers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government and public sector professionals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>NGO and development sector practitioners.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public affairs and policy consultants.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Researchers and policy analysts.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social entrepreneurs and changemakers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Working professionals seeking policy expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Individuals preparing for leadership roles in governance and public administration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The online format provides flexibility for learners who want to advance their education while balancing professional and personal commitments.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>Online M.A. in Public Policy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for students and working professionals who aspire to build expertise in <strong>public policy, governance, public administration, policy analysis, public affairs, development studies, economic policy, public sector leadership, and evidence-based policymaking</strong>. The program combines academic rigor with practical policy insights, helping learners understand how governments, institutions, and international organizations design and implement policies that impact society.</p>\r\n<p>As public policy becomes increasingly data-driven and interdisciplinary, professionals with expertise in governance, policy evaluation, economic analysis, and public leadership are in high demand across government departments, think tanks, NGOs, consulting firms, international organizations, and development agencies.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Online M.A. in Public Policy Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹50,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 February 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹3,00,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>Online M.A. in Public Policy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹3,00,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹50,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Mode</td>\r\n<td>Online</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the Online M.A. in Public Policy Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports a comprehensive learning experience that combines public policy theory, governance frameworks, economics, policy design, public finance, policy analytics, and development studies. Students gain access to an interdisciplinary curriculum designed to address real-world governance and public policy challenges.</p>\r\n<p>Key academic areas covered in the program include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Governance and Public Administration</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Finance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Economic Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Law and Public Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Economics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Design and Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Analytics for Public Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Machine Learning and AI in Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Organizations and Policy Regimes</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Impact Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research and Dissertation Opportunities</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to prepare students for policy leadership roles in both domestic and international contexts</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.A. in Public Policy Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.A. in Public Policy</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a multidisciplinary postgraduate program designed to prepare future policy professionals, governance experts, development practitioners, policy analysts, economists, and public sector leaders. The curriculum combines <strong>public policy, economics, governance, data analytics, public finance, development studies, policy evaluation, artificial intelligence, and evidence-based decision-making</strong> to address complex social, economic, and governance challenges.</p>\r\n<p>As governments, international organizations, think tanks, consulting firms, and development institutions increasingly rely on data-driven policymaking, the demand for professionals with expertise in <strong>public policy analysis, policy design, public administration, governance, impact evaluation, and policy analytics</strong> continues to grow. This program equips students with the analytical, research, and strategic skills required to shape public policy in the twenty-first century.</p>\r\n<p>A unique feature of the curriculum is the opportunity to choose between a <strong>Data Analytics Track</strong> and a <strong>Policy Design Track</strong>, allowing students to align their studies with specific career goals and professional interests.</p>\r\n<h2>M.A. Public Policy Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum progresses from foundational concepts in economics and public policy to advanced specialization in policy analytics, governance, public finance, policy design, and program evaluation. Students can further customize their learning through elective courses and a dissertation pathway.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 1: Foundations of Public Policy and Economic Analysis</h2>\r\n<p>The first term introduces students to the core principles of economics, policy formulation, research design, and public decision-making. Students learn how governments and institutions develop policies that address social and economic challenges.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Microeconomics: Foundation and Insights</td>\r\n<td>Economic behavior, market structures, incentives, and resource allocation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Theories of Public Policy</td>\r\n<td>Public policy frameworks, policy formulation, and governance processes</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Qualitative Analysis and Survey Design</td>\r\n<td>Research methods, survey techniques, stakeholder analysis, and policy research</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Economic Reasoning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Qualitative Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Survey Design</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Evidence-Based Decision Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 2: Governance, Law and Quantitative Policy Analysis</h2>\r\n<p>The second term focuses on governance systems, legal frameworks, macroeconomic policy, and quantitative analytical tools that support effective policymaking.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Law, Governance and Public Policy</td>\r\n<td>Regulatory systems, governance structures, and policy implementation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Macroeconomics: Foundation and Insights</td>\r\n<td>Economic growth, inflation, employment, and fiscal policy</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Statistical Methods and Data Analysis</td>\r\n<td>Data interpretation, statistical techniques, and policy analytics</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Why This Term Matters</h3>\r\n<p>Modern policymakers increasingly rely on data and evidence to design effective public interventions. This term develops the analytical capabilities required to evaluate policy outcomes and understand large-scale economic and governance issues.</p>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Governance Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Legal and Regulatory Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Statistical Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Sector Decision-Making</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Economic Policy Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 3: Specialization Pathways</h2>\r\n<p>In the third term, students choose between two specialized pathways based on their interests and career aspirations.</p>\r\n<h3>Data Analytics Track</h3>\r\n<p>This pathway is designed for students interested in data-driven policymaking, policy analytics, artificial intelligence, and quantitative policy research.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Econometrics Theory and Practice</td>\r\n<td>Quantitative policy analysis, forecasting, and causal inference</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Introduction to Data Science</td>\r\n<td>Data analytics, predictive modeling, and policy intelligence</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 1</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Policy Design Track</h3>\r\n<p>This pathway focuses on policy formulation, international governance, public finance, and institutional decision-making.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>International Organizations and Policy Regimes</td>\r\n<td>Global governance, international institutions, and policy cooperation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Public Finance</td>\r\n<td>Government expenditure, taxation, budgeting, and fiscal management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 1</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 4: Advanced Specialization and Applied Learning</h2>\r\n<p>The final term allows students to deepen their expertise through advanced coursework and electives while preparing for leadership roles in public policy and governance.</p>\r\n<h3>Data Analytics Track</h3>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Machine Learning, AI and Public Policy</td>\r\n<td>Artificial intelligence applications in governance and policy decision-making</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 2</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 3</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Policy Design Track</h3>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Program Design and Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Public program planning, monitoring, and impact assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 2</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Elective 3</td>\r\n<td>Specialized area of interest</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Elective Courses</h2>\r\n<p>Students can personalize their academic journey by selecting electives from a wide range of public policy, governance, economics, development, and international affairs subjects.</p>\r\n<h3>Public Policy and Governance Electives</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Complexity and Public Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Democratic Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Economics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Econometrics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Economics of Reforms and Regulations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Issues, Policies and Practice</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Gender and Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Identity and Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Introduction to Health Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Urbanisation and Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Foundations of Public Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Methods of Impact Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Cross-Disciplinary Electives</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>International Relations Theory</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Law and Ethics in International Relations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Change, Migration and Human Security</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Negotiating and Resolving International Conflicts</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Foreign Policy of Great, Middle and Small Powers</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These electives help students develop expertise in emerging policy areas while building interdisciplinary knowledge.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Dissertation Opportunity</h2>\r\n<p>Students interested in advanced research can choose to undertake a dissertation during the final phase of the program.</p>\r\n<p>The dissertation enables students to:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Conduct independent policy research.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analyze real-world governance and development challenges.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Apply theoretical and analytical frameworks to practical policy issues.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Develop advanced research and academic writing skills.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Work closely with faculty mentors on specialized policy topics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The dissertation pathway is particularly valuable for students considering careers in research, academia, think tanks, international organizations, and doctoral studies.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 300000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `organisation_courses` (`id`, `organisation_id`, `campus_id`, `department_id`, `course_id`, `academic_unit_name`, `slug`, `entrance_exam_id`, `entrance_exam_ids`, `entrance_exam_category`, `mode`, `fees`, `duration`, `status`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `admission_process`, `provisional_admission`, `eligibility`, `fees_structure`, `roi`, `curriculum`, `career_prospects`, `placement_details`, `program_level_id`, `stream_offered_id`, `discipline_id`, `specialization_id`, `specialization_ids`, `rating`, `industrial_collaboration`, `internship_ranking`, `course_languages`, `total_fees`, `school_type`, `education_board`, `board_affiliation_number`, `affiliation_valid_from`, `affiliation_valid_to`, `medium_of_instruction`, `grade_range`, `streams_offered`, `student_strength`, `total_teachers`, `trained_teachers_percentage`, `student_teacher_ratio`, `special_educator_available`, `school_counsellor_available`, `average_class_size`, `assessment_pattern`, `homework_policy`, `parent_teacher_meet_frequency`, `remedial_classes_available`, `board_result_classes`, `average_board_result_percentage`, `highest_score`, `distinction_percentage`, `olympiad_participation`, `competitive_exam_preparation_support`, `annual_fee_range`, `admission_fee`, `transport_fee`, `hostel_fee`, `fee_payment_frequency`, `parent_app_available`, `attendance_tracking_available`, `sports_offered`, `arts_music_programs_available`, `clubs_and_societies`, `annual_events`, `delivery_mode`, `integrated_schooling_available`, `total_batches`, `average_batch_size`, `min_batch_size`, `max_batch_size`, `separate_batches_for_droppers`, `merit_based_batching`, `total_faculty_count`, `senior_faculty_count`, `average_faculty_experience_years`, `full_time_faculty_percentage`, `visiting_faculty_available`, `doubt_solving_mode`, `personal_mentorship_available`, `extra_classes_for_weak_students`, `parent_counselling_available`, `study_material_type`, `dpp_provided`, `test_series_available`, `tests_per_month`, `full_syllabus_tests_count`, `online_test_platform_available`, `results_years_available`, `total_selections_all_time`, `selections_last_year`, `highest_rank_achieved`, `average_selection_rate`, `result_verification_status`, `average_course_fee_range`, `installment_available`, `scholarship_available`, `refund_policy_available`, `verified_reviews_only`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`) VALUES
(474, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 345, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 02:31:22', '2026-06-01 02:31:22', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Admission Process 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The admission process for the <strong>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</strong> is designed to identify students and professionals who are passionate about <strong>climate change, sustainability, environmental policy, ESG, renewable energy, sustainable development, environmental governance, and climate action</strong>. The process follows a holistic evaluation approach that considers the applicant\'s academic background, career aspirations, and motivation for pursuing the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 1: Complete the Online Application Form</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must fill out the online application form by providing their personal, academic, and professional details through the university\'s admission portal.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 2: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates are required to submit the necessary documents for verification, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Bachelor\'s degree certificate and academic transcripts</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof for Indian applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passport for international applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Recent passport-size photograph</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Additional supporting documents, if applicable</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Step 3: Submit the Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must submit a <strong>Statement of Purpose (Maximum 800 Words)</strong> explaining:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Their interest in environmental change and sustainability</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Short-term and long-term career goals</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professional aspirations in sustainability-related fields</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>How the program will contribute to their academic, professional, and personal growth</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The SOP is a key component of the admission process and helps the university evaluate the applicant\'s motivation and suitability for the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 4: Application and Profile Evaluation</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions committee conducts a detailed review of:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic qualifications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Submitted documents</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Statement of Purpose</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career objectives and overall profile</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The evaluation focuses on identifying candidates who demonstrate strong interest in sustainability, climate action, environmental management, and sustainable development.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 5: Admission Decision</h3>\r\n<p>Based on the overall profile assessment and SOP evaluation, shortlisted candidates are offered admission to the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 6: Receive and Accept the Offer Letter</h3>\r\n<p>Selected applicants receive an official admission offer from the university. Candidates must confirm their acceptance within the specified timeline.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 7: Pay the Registration Fee</h3>\r\n<p>To secure admission, candidates must pay the registration fee mentioned in the offer letter.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 8: Complete Enrollment Formalities</h3>\r\n<p>After successful fee payment and document verification, students complete the enrollment process and gain access to academic resources, orientation information, and program details.</p>\r\n<h2>Admission Process Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Admission Stage</th>\r\n<th>Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Online Application</td>\r\n<td>Submit the application form</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Document Upload</td>\r\n<td>Upload academic and identity documents</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>SOP Submission</td>\r\n<td>Submit Statement of Purpose</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Profile Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Review of academic and professional profile</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Admission Decision</td>\r\n<td>Selection based on overall assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Offer Letter Acceptance</td>\r\n<td>Confirm admission offer</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee Payment</td>\r\n<td>Secure admission seat</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Final Enrollment</td>\r\n<td>Complete enrollment formalities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The <strong>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability admission process</strong> is designed to ensure a smooth and transparent admission experience while selecting candidates who are committed to creating meaningful impact in the fields of sustainability, climate change, environmental policy, ESG, and sustainable development.</p>', 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a future-oriented postgraduate program designed for students and professionals who want to build expertise in <strong>climate change, sustainability, environmental management, ESG, environmental policy, renewable energy, sustainable development, climate governance, environmental compliance, and green business practices</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>As governments, multinational corporations, international organizations, and sustainability-focused institutions continue to invest in climate action and environmental responsibility, the demand for professionals with specialized knowledge in sustainability and environmental management is growing rapidly. This program prepares students to understand environmental challenges, evaluate sustainability strategies, and contribute to building a more sustainable future.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</h2>\r\n<p>Candidates seeking admission to the OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability program must fulfill the following eligibility requirements.</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants must hold a <strong>Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from Science, Engineering, Commerce, Management, Humanities, Social Sciences, Environmental Studies, Agriculture, Economics, Public Policy, and other academic backgrounds are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>The program welcomes learners from diverse disciplines who are interested in sustainability, environmental governance, climate action, and sustainable development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The interdisciplinary nature of environmental studies allows students from multiple academic streams to develop expertise in sustainability and climate-related fields.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must provide valid identification documents during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and enrollment purposes.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Criteria</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability program follows a profile-based evaluation process designed to assess the applicant\'s motivation, career aspirations, and interest in sustainability and environmental leadership.</p>\r\n<h3>Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit a <strong>Statement of Purpose (Maximum 800 Words)</strong> as part of the admission process.</p>\r\n<p>The SOP should explain:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Why the applicant wants to pursue the M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Short-term career goals and professional aspirations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Long-term career objectives in sustainability, climate action, environmental policy, ESG, or related sectors.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>How the program will contribute to personal growth and professional development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in environmental challenges and sustainable development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The Statement of Purpose provides applicants with an opportunity to demonstrate their passion for sustainability and their commitment to contributing to environmental solutions.</p>\r\n<h2>What Does the Admissions Team Evaluate?</h2>\r\n<p>During the selection process, the university evaluates:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic background</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Quality of the Statement of Purpose</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in sustainability and environmental issues</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career objectives and professional vision</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analytical and communication skills</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Potential to contribute to sustainability-focused initiatives</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The admissions process follows a holistic approach rather than relying solely on academic scores.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a specialized postgraduate program designed for students and professionals who want to build expertise in <strong>climate change, sustainability management, ESG, environmental policy, renewable energy, carbon markets, environmental governance, sustainable development, and climate risk management</strong>. The program combines scientific knowledge, policy perspectives, technological innovation, and sustainability-focused leadership skills to prepare graduates for emerging green economy careers.</p>\r\n<p>As organizations worldwide prioritize net-zero goals, ESG compliance, sustainable business practices, and environmental responsibility, professionals with expertise in sustainability and climate action are among the most sought-after talent globally. The program equips learners with the knowledge and practical skills needed to contribute to environmental transformation across industries, governments, and international organizations.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 January 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,75,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Focus</td>\r\n<td>Sustainability, Climate Change, ESG &amp; Environmental Management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the M.Sc. Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports a comprehensive postgraduate learning experience that combines environmental science, sustainability strategy, climate policy, ESG frameworks, and emerging technologies. Students gain exposure to global sustainability challenges and practical solutions used by governments, businesses, and international institutions.</p>\r\n<p>Major learning areas include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Change and Sustainability</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>ESG and Sustainability Reporting</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Carbon Markets and Climate Finance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Renewable Energy and Energy Transition</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Policy and Regulation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>AI and Machine Learning for Sustainability</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Compliance and Risk Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Data Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainability Research and Capstone Projects</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to prepare students for leadership roles in sustainability-focused sectors while addressing real-world environmental challenges.</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a future-focused postgraduate program designed for students and professionals who want to develop expertise in <strong>climate change, sustainability, environmental management, environmental policy, carbon markets, ESG, renewable energy, sustainable development, environmental governance, and green business practices</strong>.</p>\r\n<p>As organizations, governments, and international institutions increasingly prioritize sustainability and climate action, the demand for professionals skilled in <strong>environmental sustainability, climate risk management, carbon accounting, environmental compliance, ESG reporting, sustainability consulting, and sustainable development planning</strong> continues to grow. This program equips students with the scientific, analytical, technological, and policy-oriented skills needed to address complex environmental challenges in the 21st century.</p>\r\n<p>The curriculum combines environmental science, climate studies, sustainability solutions, policy frameworks, artificial intelligence, environmental governance, and industry-focused applications, preparing graduates for careers across environmental consulting, sustainability management, climate policy, research, and corporate ESG functions.</p>\r\n<h2>M.Sc. Environmental Change &amp; Sustainability Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to provide a comprehensive understanding of environmental systems, climate change impacts, sustainability frameworks, environmental regulations, and emerging technologies used in sustainability management.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 1: Foundations of Environmental Change and Sustainable Development</h2>\r\n<p>The first term introduces students to the science behind environmental change and its impact on ecosystems, public health, and global development. Students gain a strong understanding of sustainability principles and global environmental challenges.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Fundamentals of Environmental Change</td>\r\n<td>Climate systems, environmental transformations, ecological challenges, and sustainability concepts</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Pollution and Health</td>\r\n<td>Environmental pollution, public health impacts, environmental risk assessment, and mitigation strategies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Planetary Boundaries and Sustainable Development Goals</td>\r\n<td>Global sustainability frameworks, SDGs, resource management, and environmental governance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainability Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Change Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Health Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development Planning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Ecological Risk Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 2: Climate Science, Carbon Markets and Sustainability Solutions</h2>\r\n<p>The second term focuses on climate systems, carbon management, renewable transitions, and practical sustainability strategies used by governments and organizations worldwide.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Energy-Carbon Market</td>\r\n<td>Carbon trading, emissions management, energy transition, and climate finance</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Climate Modelling</td>\r\n<td>Climate forecasting, environmental simulations, and climate risk assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Sustainability Solutions</td>\r\n<td>Sustainable business practices, environmental innovation, and climate adaptation strategies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Carbon Market Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Risk Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainability Strategy Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Planning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Adaptation Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Green Economy Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 3: Industry Sustainability and Environmental Innovation</h2>\r\n<p>The third term explores environmental compliance, sustainable industry practices, and the role of advanced technologies in addressing environmental challenges.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Environment Compliances in Industry</td>\r\n<td>Environmental regulations, compliance frameworks, ESG standards, and corporate sustainability</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>AI and Machine Learning in Sustainability</td>\r\n<td>Artificial intelligence applications in environmental monitoring and sustainability management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Environmental Policy or Green Markets</td>\r\n<td>Environmental governance, sustainability regulations, green business models, and market-based solutions</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Term 3</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Compliance Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>ESG and Sustainability Reporting</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Artificial Intelligence Applications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Policy Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Green Business Strategy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainability Innovation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Term 4: Advanced Sustainability Governance and Research</h2>\r\n<p>The final term allows students to specialize further through advanced electives while applying their knowledge through a capstone project or research thesis.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Environmental Data Analysis or Sustainable Governance</td>\r\n<td>Sustainability analytics, governance frameworks, environmental decision-making, and policy evaluation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Capstone / Thesis</td>\r\n<td>Independent research, sustainability projects, environmental consulting studies, or policy-focused investigations</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Capstone and Thesis Experience</h3>\r\n<p>The capstone or thesis component enables students to work on real-world environmental and sustainability challenges. Students may explore areas such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Climate Change Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>ESG and Corporate Sustainability</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Carbon Management</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Renewable Energy Systems</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Environmental Impact Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Green Economy Strategies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This practical experience strengthens research, analytical, and problem-solving skills while preparing students for professional and academic advancement.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 275000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(475, 84, '79639da0-12e5-4abe-a2a7-90acfa099a40', '47933c11-475d-4ee4-ab70-4bb32e29c731', 346, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ONLINE', NULL, NULL, 1, 0, '2026-06-01 02:45:13', '2026-06-01 02:45:13', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies Admission Process 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The admission process for the <strong>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies</strong> is designed to identify students and professionals who are passionate about <strong>development studies, public policy, sustainable development, social impact, governance, poverty alleviation, human development, and policy research</strong>. The university follows a holistic admission approach that evaluates applicants based on their academic qualifications, career aspirations, and motivation to contribute to development and social change.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 1: Complete the Online Application Form</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must submit the online application form through the university admission portal by providing their personal, academic, and professional details.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 2: Upload Required Documents</h3>\r\n<p>Candidates are required to upload the necessary documents for verification, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Bachelor\'s degree certificate and academic transcripts</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof for Indian applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passport for international applicants</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Recent passport-size photograph</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Additional supporting documents, if applicable</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Step 3: Submit the Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>As part of the admission process, applicants must submit a <strong>Statement of Purpose (Maximum 800 Words)</strong> explaining:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Their interest in Development Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Short-term and long-term career goals</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Personal and professional aspirations</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>How the program will support their academic and career growth</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in public policy, governance, social impact, sustainability, or development sectors</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The SOP is a key component of the admission process and helps the admissions committee evaluate the applicant\'s motivation and suitability for the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 4: Profile and Application Review</h3>\r\n<p>The admissions team conducts a comprehensive assessment of:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic qualifications</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Submitted documents</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Statement of Purpose</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Career objectives and overall profile</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>This review helps determine the applicant\'s readiness for postgraduate study and their potential contribution to the learning environment.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 5: Admission Decision</h3>\r\n<p>Based on the overall profile evaluation and SOP assessment, eligible candidates are shortlisted and offered admission to the program.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 6: Receive and Accept the Offer Letter</h3>\r\n<p>Selected applicants receive an official admission offer from the university. Candidates must confirm their acceptance within the timeline specified by the university.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 7: Pay the Registration Fee</h3>\r\n<p>To secure their admission, candidates must pay the registration fee mentioned in the offer letter.</p>\r\n<h3>Step 8: Complete Enrollment Formalities</h3>\r\n<p>After successful fee payment and document verification, students complete the enrollment process and gain access to academic resources, orientation information, and course-related updates.</p>\r\n<h2>Admission Process Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Admission Stage</th>\r\n<th>Description</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Online Application</td>\r\n<td>Complete and submit the application form</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Document Upload</td>\r\n<td>Upload academic and identity documents</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>SOP Submission</td>\r\n<td>Submit Statement of Purpose</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Profile Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Review of academic profile and SOP</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Admission Decision</td>\r\n<td>Selection based on holistic assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Offer Letter Acceptance</td>\r\n<td>Confirm admission offer</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee Payment</td>\r\n<td>Secure admission seat</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Final Enrollment</td>\r\n<td>Complete admission and onboarding formalities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The <strong>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies admission process</strong> is designed to ensure a transparent and student-friendly admission experience while selecting candidates who demonstrate strong academic potential, leadership qualities, and a commitment to creating positive social and developmental impact.</p>', 1, '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Development Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a multidisciplinary postgraduate program designed for students and professionals who want to develop expertise in <strong>development studies, public policy, sustainable development, poverty alleviation, social impact, governance, human development, economic development, and social change</strong>. The program prepares learners to understand and address some of the most pressing development challenges facing societies today through research, policy analysis, and evidence-based decision-making.</p>\r\n<p>As governments, international organizations, NGOs, development agencies, and policy institutions increasingly focus on inclusive growth, sustainability, and social development, there is growing demand for professionals with specialized knowledge of development issues and solutions. This program provides a strong academic foundation for careers in the development sector, public policy, research, and social impact organizations.</p>\r\n<h2>Eligibility Criteria for M.Sc. in Development Studies</h2>\r\n<p>Applicants seeking admission to the OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies program must meet the following eligibility requirements.</p>\r\n<h3>Academic Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Candidates must hold a <strong>Bachelor&rsquo;s degree in any discipline</strong> from a recognized university.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Applicants should have secured a minimum of <strong>50% marks in graduation</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates from Arts, Commerce, Science, Management, Engineering, Social Sciences, Economics, Public Policy, Law, Humanities, and related fields are eligible to apply.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The interdisciplinary nature of Development Studies allows students from diverse educational backgrounds to contribute different perspectives while developing expertise in development policy, governance, and social transformation.</p>\r\n<h3>Identity Verification Requirements</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must provide valid identification documents during the admission process.</p>\r\n<h4>For Indian Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government-Issued ID Proof</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>For International Applicants</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Valid Passport (Mandatory)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These documents are required for identity verification and admission processing.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University Selection Criteria</h2>\r\n<p>Admission to the M.Sc. in Development Studies program follows a profile-based evaluation process that focuses on the applicant\'s academic background, motivation, and commitment to development-related issues.</p>\r\n<h3>Statement of Purpose (SOP)</h3>\r\n<p>Applicants are required to submit a <strong>Statement of Purpose (Maximum 800 Words)</strong> as part of the selection process.</p>\r\n<p>The SOP should discuss:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>The applicant\'s short-term career goals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Long-term professional aspirations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Personal growth objectives.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in development studies and social impact.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>How the M.Sc. in Development Studies program will support these goals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Motivation for pursuing a career in development, policy, research, governance, or related fields.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The Statement of Purpose helps the admissions committee assess the applicant\'s vision, intellectual curiosity, career direction, and commitment to addressing development challenges.</p>\r\n<h2>What Makes a Strong Application?</h2>\r\n<p>Successful applicants typically demonstrate:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Clear academic and professional goals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Interest in sustainable development and social change.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Understanding of development challenges.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Strong communication and analytical skills.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Passion for public policy, governance, and development work.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Commitment to creating positive social impact.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>A thoughtful and well-structured SOP can significantly strengthen an applicant\'s overall profile.</p>\r\n<h2>Who Should Apply for the M.Sc. in Development Studies?</h2>\r\n<p>This program is ideal for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Graduates interested in development and public policy careers.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Professionals working in NGOs and social impact organizations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Researchers and policy enthusiasts.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Individuals interested in poverty reduction and human development.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development practitioners seeking advanced academic training.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Government and public sector professionals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social entrepreneurs and community development leaders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to develop both theoretical understanding and practical problem-solving capabilities needed in the development sector.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies Fees 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Development Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is a multidisciplinary postgraduate program that equips students with advanced knowledge of <strong>development policy, sustainable development, governance, poverty alleviation, social impact, human development, public policy, and development economics</strong>. The program is designed for learners who want to understand the challenges of inclusive growth and contribute to policy solutions that create meaningful social and economic change.</p>\r\n<p>With increasing global focus on sustainability, social justice, economic development, and evidence-based policymaking, professionals trained in Development Studies are highly valued across governments, international organizations, NGOs, consulting firms, think tanks, and research institutions. The program combines academic rigor, research training, and practical development perspectives to prepare graduates for leadership roles in the development sector.</p>\r\n<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies Fee Structure</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Fee Component</th>\r\n<th>Amount</th>\r\n<th>Due Date</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Amount</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n<td>Upon Acceptance of Offer Letter</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 1</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>Before Batch Commencement</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Instalment 2</td>\r\n<td>₹1,25,000</td>\r\n<td>By 15 January 2027</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Total Tuition Fee</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>₹2,75,000</strong></td>\r\n<td>&mdash;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>Fee Overview</h2>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Particulars</th>\r\n<th>Details</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Course Name</td>\r\n<td>M.Sc. in Development Studies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>University</td>\r\n<td>OP Jindal University</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Duration</td>\r\n<td>1 Year</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Total Tuition Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹2,75,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registration Fee</td>\r\n<td>₹25,000</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Payment Structure</td>\r\n<td>Instalment-Based</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Learning Focus</td>\r\n<td>Development Studies, Public Policy, Governance &amp; Sustainable Development</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2>What Does the M.Sc. Development Studies Fee Include?</h2>\r\n<p>The tuition fee supports a comprehensive learning experience focused on understanding and solving complex development challenges. Students gain exposure to development theory, policy analysis, governance systems, research methodologies, sustainable development practices, and social impact evaluation.</p>\r\n<p>Key learning areas covered in the program include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Studies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Policy and Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Economics</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Poverty and Inequality Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Human Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Quantitative and Qualitative Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Project Management and Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Change and Democratic Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Research and Academic Writing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Dissertation and Independent Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The curriculum is designed to help students build analytical, research, and policy-oriented skills required in today\'s development sector.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'Medium', '<h2>OP Jindal University M.Sc. in Development Studies Syllabus &amp; Curriculum 2026</h2>\r\n<p>The <strong>M.Sc. in Development Studies</strong> at <strong>OP Jindal University</strong> is an interdisciplinary postgraduate program designed for students who want to understand the complex social, economic, political, and institutional factors that influence development across societies. The program combines <strong>development economics, public policy, social change, poverty studies, sustainable development, research methods, governance, and project management</strong> to prepare graduates for impactful careers in development organizations, policy institutions, international agencies, NGOs, research centers, and government bodies.</p>\r\n<p>As issues such as <strong>poverty alleviation, inequality, human development, social justice, sustainable development, governance, and inclusive growth</strong> continue to shape global and national policy agendas, there is increasing demand for professionals who can analyze development challenges and design effective solutions. This program equips students with the analytical, research, and practical skills needed to contribute meaningfully to development initiatives and policymaking processes.</p>\r\n<p>The curriculum combines theoretical foundations with hands-on research and project-based learning, helping students develop a comprehensive understanding of contemporary development issues.</p>\r\n<h2>M.Sc. Development Studies Course Structure</h2>\r\n<p>The curriculum is organized across three trimesters and progressively builds expertise in development theory, quantitative and qualitative research, public policy, social change, sustainable development, and project evaluation.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 1: Foundations of Development Studies</h2>\r\n<p>The first trimester introduces students to the major theories, concepts, and debates that shape the field of development studies. Students also begin building essential research and academic writing skills.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Theoretical Perspectives on Development</td>\r\n<td>Development theories, economic growth models, modernization, globalization, and development debates</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Introduction to Quantitative Research</td>\r\n<td>Statistical thinking, research techniques, survey methods, and data collection</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Political Economy of India&rsquo;s Development</td>\r\n<td>Economic reforms, governance, public institutions, and India\'s development trajectory</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Research Design and Academic Writing</td>\r\n<td>Research planning, academic writing, literature review, and scholarly communication</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 1</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Quantitative Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Academic Writing</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Policy Understanding</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Critical Thinking</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Research Design</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 2: Human Development, Inequality and Sustainability</h2>\r\n<p>The second trimester focuses on contemporary development challenges including poverty, inequality, human development, sustainability, and social exclusion. Students gain expertise in qualitative research and data interpretation used in development planning and policy evaluation.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Poverty, Inequality &amp; Human Development</td>\r\n<td>Human development indicators, poverty reduction, social inclusion, and welfare policies</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Introduction to Qualitative Research</td>\r\n<td>Field research, interviews, case studies, and qualitative data analysis</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Data Analysis</td>\r\n<td>Research data interpretation, evidence-based decision-making, and policy evaluation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Sustainable Development: Technology and Exclusion</td>\r\n<td>Sustainability, technological change, digital inclusion, and development challenges</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Why This Trimester Matters</h3>\r\n<p>Modern development challenges require professionals who can evaluate social and economic inequalities while understanding how technology, sustainability, and public policy influence development outcomes. This trimester provides students with practical analytical tools used across development organizations and policy institutions.</p>\r\n<h3>Skills Developed in Trimester 2</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Poverty Analysis</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Qualitative Research</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Data Interpretation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development Planning</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Social Impact Assessment</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development Policy Evaluation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2>Trimester 3: Governance, Social Change and Applied Research</h2>\r\n<p>The final trimester emphasizes project implementation, governance systems, democratic institutions, and social transformation while providing students with an opportunity to conduct independent research through a dissertation.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Courses</th>\r\n<th>Key Learning Areas</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Project Management and Evaluation</td>\r\n<td>Development project planning, monitoring, implementation, and impact assessment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>State, Democracy and Social Change</td>\r\n<td>Governance systems, democratic institutions, citizenship, and social transformation</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dissertation</td>\r\n<td>Independent research on a development-related issue under faculty supervision</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3>Dissertation and Research Experience</h3>\r\n<p>A major highlight of the program is the dissertation component, which allows students to conduct in-depth research on a development issue of their choice. Students work closely with faculty mentors to develop research questions, analyze data, and generate evidence-based insights.</p>\r\n<p>Research areas may include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Poverty and Inequality</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Rural Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Urban Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Public Policy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Education and Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Gender and Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Sustainable Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Governance and Social Change</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Technology and Inclusion</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Human Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The dissertation strengthens analytical, research, and policy-writing skills while preparing students for professional and academic advancement.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4.0, NULL, NULL, '[\"1\"]', 275000.00, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '0', '0', NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
